France 24 (EN),Western Europe,en,"US proposed Ukraine cedes Donbas in exchange for joining NATO, Zelensky says","US proposed Ukraine cedes Donbas in exchange for joining NATO, Zelensky says","US proposed Ukraine cedes Donbas in exchange for joining NATO, Zelensky says President Zelensky said the US had proposed ceding Ukraine's eastern city of Donbas to Russia, in exchange for Ukrainian membership of NATO, following the latest round of peace talks in Abu Dhabi this week. He reiterated that Kyiv was not willing to retreat from its territory and warned that the Kremlin's bid to change the continent's security architecture could lead to more wars. President Zelensky said the US had proposed ceding Ukraine's eastern city of Donbas to Russia, in exchange for Ukrainian membership of NATO, following the latest round of peace talks in Abu Dhabi this week. He reiterated that Kyiv was not willing to retreat from its territory and warned that the Kremlin's bid to change the continent's security architecture could lead to more wars. Issued on:14/11/2026 - 11:30Modified:14/11/2026 - 11:42 Ukraine's PresidentVolodymyr Zelenskysaid that the United States proposed Ukraine cede land toRussiain exchange for joiningNATOand thathis government was in talkson ""specific"" security guarantees from the West. He said that US negotiators had floated a question about Ukraine's potential withdrawal from its eastern region of Donbas in exchange for ‌joining the alliance, following the ⁠latest round ofpeace talks with Russia in ‌Abu Dhabi. Zelensky reiterated his position that ⁠Kyiv was not willing to retreat from its territory. He said that if Ukraine received a ‌comprehensive security package, that includes security guarantees, a strong and well-funded Ukrainian ‌army and funds to rebuild, he would put the question to a referendum. ""The Americans raised a question: ""What if Ukraine joins NATO? Would Ukraine withdraw from Donbas?"" This was the first time this had been raised,"" Zelensky told reporters in remarks released by his office on Saturday. He said the EU and NATO are Europe's only ""real security"", warning the Kremlin's bid to change the co","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:30:04 GMT",https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-us-negotiators-suggest-ukraine-cedes-territory-in-exchange-for-nato-membership,2026-11-15 03:26:17
France 24 (EN),Western Europe,en,'Climate action is alive': Triumphant Democrats attend COP31 summit shunned by Trump,'Climate action is alive': Triumphant Democrats attend COP31 summit shunned by Trump,"'Climate action is alive': Triumphant Democrats attend COP31 summit shunned by Trump A delegation of 18 Democratic lawmakers arrived at the COP31 climate summit in Turkey on Saturday to reaffirm the US commitment to tackling global warming following their sweeping midterm election victory. A delegation of 18 Democratic lawmakers arrived at the COP31 climate summit in Turkey on Saturday to reaffirm the US commitment to tackling global warming following their sweeping midterm election victory. Issued on:14/11/2026 - 11:25Modified:14/11/2026 - 15:32 Fresh from theirUS midterm election triumph, an emboldened group of Democratic lawmakers descended on the COP31 climate talks shunned by PresidentDonald Trumpon Saturday to signal their commitment to tackling global warming. The 18-strong delegation joined the annualUNconference inTurkeyafter their party regained control of both chambers of Congress in a landslide victory last week cheered by climate campaigners. Read moreWhy the Democrats routed the Republicans in the US midterm elections ""Many of our allies and partners across the world think the United States has not been predictable or dependable. So we have a lot of trust to earn back,""FloridaRepresentative Kathy Castor told AFP. ""We have so much work to do. And yes, I hope the United States gets back on track with urgent climate action,"" she said after the group took photos in front of a largeCOP31sign in a sprawling expo centre. The election has been a topic of discussion at COP31 in Antalya, with hopes that Democrats can restore some clean energy policies and that a pro-climate president can be elected in two years. ""What happened in the US is remarkable, and a much needed shift that we all needed, not only from a climate perspective, but overall,"" Harjeet Sing","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:25:22 GMT",https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261114-climate-action-is-alive-triumphant-democrats-take-on-cop31-shunned-by-trump,2026-11-15 03:26:17
France 24 (EN),Western Europe,en,SpaceX's Starship encounters problems during 15th test flight,SpaceX's Starship encounters problems during 15th test flight,"SpaceX's Starship encounters problems during 15th test flight Elon Musk’s SpaceX successfully launched its Starship, the world's largest spaceship, into orbit where it should release 15 satellites for its Starlink network. A few minutes after lift off however, the rocket's booster which was meant to return to the pad splashed down in the Gulf of Mexico. Details by Daniel Quinlan. To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Issued on:14/11/2026 - 11:21 Elon Musk’s SpaceX successfully launched its Starship, the world's largest spaceship, into orbit where it should release 15 satellites for its Starlink network. A few minutes after lift off however, the rocket's booster which was meant to return to the pad splashed down in the Gulf of Mexico. Details by Daniel Quinlan. Keywords for this article The content you requested does not exist or is not available anymore.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:21:09 GMT",https://www.france24.com/en/spacex-s-starship-encounters-problems-during-15th-test-flight,2026-11-15 03:26:17
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,"Saudi-led coalition intercepts two missiles, two drones in Riyadh","Saudi-led coalition intercepts two missiles, two drones in Riyadh","Saudi-led coalition intercepts two missiles, two drones in Riyadh Fighting escalates in Yemen&#039;s Marib and al-Jawf, as UN agency says more than 340,000 Yemenis displaced since August. Save Share Saudi-led coalition forces fighting Yemen’s Houthis have said they intercepted two missiles and two drones targeting Riyadh, allegedly launched by the Houthis, as fighting intensifies across various front lines in Yemen. “Air defences intercepted and destroyed two ballistic missiles launched by the Houthi terrorist militia toward Riyadh,” Turki al-Maliki, the Saudi-led coalition spokesperson, said in a post on X early on Sunday. Earlier on Saturday, al-Maliki said two suspected Houthi drones “were intercepted and destroyed” in the Riyadh and southern regions. At least 26 people have been killed in suspected Houthi drone and missile attacks in Saudi Arabia since September 23, according to the kingdom’s authorities. The Houthis haverepeatedly targetedRiyadh’s King Khalid International airport, as well as the East-West pipeline andoil infrastructurein eastern and southern Saudi Arabia. The interceptions come as the Saudi-led forces supporting Yemen’s internationally recognised government also said they intercepted several drones launched towards the Yemeni city of Marib. Yemeni army spokesman Colonel Majid al-Nuzaili said government forces had made gains against the Houthis during heavy fighting in the al-Hazm and Madghal districts of al-Jawf, as fighting intensified in Marib. Al-Nuzaili said 321 Houthi leaders had been killed or wounded in 723 targeted operations by Saudi-backed forces in the Taiz, Lahij, Marib and al-Jawf governorates, and that 117 military vehicles","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:59:06 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/15/saudi-led-coalition-intercepts-two-missiles-two-drones-in-riyadh?traffic_source=rss,2026-11-15 03:26:18
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Iraq PM sacks nine officials over oil smuggling in pro-Iran stronghold,Iraq PM sacks nine officials over oil smuggling in pro-Iran stronghold,"Iraq PM sacks nine officials over oil smuggling in pro-Iran stronghold Dismissals follow probe that uncovered illegal oil refineries and smuggling in a region run by Kataib Hezbollah. Save Share Iraq’s Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi has dismissed nine senior security officials over an alleged oil smuggling operation in the Jurf al-Nasr area, a stronghold of the Iran-backed Kataib Hezbollah group. Al-Zaidi chaired an emergency security meeting to review the findings of a committee investigating smuggling in Jurf al-Nasr, Babil province, military spokesperson Sabah al-Numan told the Iraqi News Agency (INA). The move follows an investigation that uncovered illegal oil refineries and evidence of manipulation linked to the smuggling activities. “In light of the investigation’s findings, [the prime minister] ordered that all individuals accused of involvement in oil smuggling operations be referred to the judiciary,” al-Numan said. The prime minister “also ordered the dismissal” of nine officials, including security and intelligence officers in Babil province, an Interior Ministry commander, and the director of the Oil Pipelines Company at the Ministry of Oil, he said. The police chief of Babil province was among those dismissed. Kataib Hezbollah, an Iran-aligned paramilitary group and one of Iraq’s most heavily armed factions, has recently issued several sharp statements against the prime minister, threatening his government and accusing him of corruption. Senior Iraqi politicians previously told the AFP news agency that al-Zaidi had repeatedly said he was ready to confront groups refusing to disarm. Al Jazeera’s Peter Smith, reporting from Baghdad, said previous ","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:54:55 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/15/iraq-pm-sacks-nine-officials-over-oil-smuggling-in-pro-iran-stronghold?traffic_source=rss,2026-11-15 03:26:18
