Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,SpaceX’s Starship nails a smooth return with historic catch,SpaceX’s Starship nails a smooth return with historic catch,"SpaceX’s Starship nails a smooth return with historic catch SpaceX Starship made a triumphant return to Earth, caught midair by giant mechanical ‘chopsticks’. SpaceX’s Starship nails a smooth return with historic catch SpaceX has caught the upper stage of its giant Starship rocket in midair for the first time, using mechanical arms nicknamed ‘chopsticks’. The spacecraft made a triumphant return to Earth, landing at the same launch pad it left 22 hours earlier in a milestone moment for the company. Save Share","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:22:01 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/11/15/aje-onl-nf_spacexs-starship-nails-a-smooth-return-141126?traffic_source=rss,2026-11-15 03:26:18
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Israeli air strike kills senior Hamas commander in Gaza,Israeli air strike kills senior Hamas commander in Gaza,"Israeli air strike kills senior Hamas commander in Gaza Hamas confirms the death of Rafah brigade commander Samir Abu Younis in an attack on Khan Younis on Saturday. Save Share Hamas has confirmed that Rafah brigade commander Samir Abu Younis was killed in an Israeli air strike on the al-Mawasi area of Khan Younis, southern Gaza. Israel’s military and Shin Bet security agency earlier said in a joint statement that they had targeted a senior Hamas military commander in a drone strike in Khan Younis on Saturday. The attack that hit a tent sheltering displaced people wounded two others. The casualties were taken to Nasser Medical Complex in Khan Younis, medical personnel told Al Jazeera on Saturday. Video footage verified by Al Jazeera and posted by Palestinian journalists from the vicinity of the hospital showed ambulances inside the grounds and stretchers that appear to be stained with blood. Al-Mawasi, a coastal strip on the Mediterranean, is crowded withdisplaced Palestiniansliving in tents. Israel has repeatedly attacked the area despite previously designating it a humanitarian zone. Gaza’s Ministry of Health said in its latest update on Saturday that Israeli attacks have killed 16 people and injured 68 others over the past 48 hours. Since the “ceasefire” in Gaza took effect on October 11, 2025, Israel has killed at least 1,643 Palestinians and injured 5,964. At least 850 bodies have been recovered from under the rubble. Since Israel began its genocidal war on Gaza in October 2023, at least 74,695 people have been killed and 176,093 injured, according to the Health Ministry. The ministry also reported that the number of deaths related t","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:00:42 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/15/israeli-air-strike-kills-senior-hamas-commander-in-gaza?traffic_source=rss,2026-11-15 03:26:18
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Hundreds of men march in Switzerland to protest violence against women,Hundreds of men march in Switzerland to protest violence against women,"Hundreds of men march in Switzerland to protest violence against women Organisers say men must speak out, as Swiss study finds half of men aged 18 to 24 hold restrictive view of masculinity. Save Share Hundreds of men have led a demonstration in Switzerland’s capital, Bern, to denounce misogyny and violence against women, saying men need to take a more effective role in fighting both. The “Men Against Violence Against Women” rally outside parliament on Saturday follows persistent concerns that misogyny is too prevalent online among teenage boys and young men and that other men need to build a stronger counter-narrative. The misogynistic views are pushed by the right-wing “manosphere” – a loose network of online forums and influencers that promote male supremacy and hostility to feminism. Such influencers were emboldened after Donald Trump won the US presidential election in 202 to justify and amplify misogynistic derision and threats online. “We men are part of the problem – the problem being violence against women and queer people,” said Christoph Gosteli, a 42-year-old social worker who co-organised the rally with a group called maenner. “That is why it is important for us to take a stand and say, ‘We no longer want to be part of the problem; we want to be part of the solution.’” An academic and advocacy group survey released in June by the University of Zurich and MenCare, an umbrella group of Swiss men’s and fathers’ organisations, found that half of male respondents aged 18 to 24 held a “restrictive and dominance-based view of masculinity”, expressing concerns that “real men are increasingly marginalised in society”. The study called for “a systematic and so","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:27:14 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/15/hundreds-of-men-march-in-switzerland-to-protest-violence-against-women?traffic_source=rss,2026-11-15 03:26:19
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,SpaceX’s Starship captured by launchpad arms in dramatic first,SpaceX’s Starship captured by launchpad arms in dramatic first,"SpaceX’s Starship captured by launchpad arms in dramatic first SpaceX officials say catch by mechanical arms shows Starship&#039;s full reusability, crucial for rapid, low-cost recycling. Save Share SpaceX’s Starship ‌spacecraft has returned to Earth, caught midair by giant mechanical arms where its journey began 22 hours earlier. The spaceship emerged from a cloudy sky on Saturday, descending slowly over Starbase before slipping smoothly between mechanical “chopstick arms” above Launch Pad 2 in Texas – the first-ever capture of a Starship flying back from space. Soon afterwards, SpaceX founder and CEO Elon Musk congratulated his “incredible team”. SpaceX officials said Saturday’s catch demonstrates Starship’s full reusability, crucial for rapid, low-cost recycling. However, with the first-stage booster exploding shortly after Friday’s liftoff from Texas, the company fell short of its desired double catch. Separating neatly from its booster before things went awry, the upper-stage spacecraft soared into orbit and released 26 advanced Starlink satellites. SpaceX’s Kate Tice said its engines stopped firing too soon on the way back down. The booster’s guidance system sensed it was not in the right position and automatically initiated the watery detour and self-destruction. Engineers are still investigating the cause. Although Friday’s booster recovery failed, the company had already made three previous booster catches, validating the technique. NASA, which is paying billions of dollars for Starship to land Artemis astronauts on the Moon later this decade, welcomed the achievement. “It was almost magic,” NASA Administrator Jared Isaacman said on X. Starship comple","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:14:22 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/15/spacexs-starship-captured-by-launchpad-arms-in-dramatic-first?traffic_source=rss,2026-11-15 03:26:19
