Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Netanyahu says only a unity government can guarantee Israel’s security,Netanyahu says only a unity government can guarantee Israel’s security,"Netanyahu says only a unity government can guarantee Israel’s security Eisenkot, in charge of forming a government, dismisses the appeal as ‘tricks’ as talks and a Knesset speaker vote loom. Save Share Israeli caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has renewed his call for a national unity government with his rival, Gadi Eisenkot, saying only such a government can guarantee Israel’s security. In a video statement on Saturday, Netanyahu said a meeting with Eisenkot on Thursday “only strengthened the conviction that it is essential to form a national unity government”. The prime minister said such a government could “eliminate the Iranian threat once and for all”, claiming Tehran would “not hesitate to use nuclear weapons against us”. “Let’s meet in one room, without preconditions,” he said. Within minutes, however, Eisenkot dismissed the appeal as a ploy. A former army chief, Eisenkot said Netanyahu “knows he lost the election”. “Netanyahu is calling for negotiations while they are already underway,” he said. “These tricks don’t work on me.” Neither side won a majority in the October 27 election. Netanyahu’s right-wing and religious bloc took 53 seats in the 120-seat Knesset, Eisenkot’s four-party bloc got 48 seats, and Arab-led parties won a record 19. President Isaac Herzog last week tasked Eisenkot with forming a government, after 67 lawmakers, including those from Arab-led parties, endorsed him, while 46 backed Netanyahu. Eisenkot has 28 days, with a possible 14-day extension. He has ruled out including Arab-led parties in his government. Under Eisenkot’s plan for a minority “national emergency government”, his bloc’s 48 lawmakers would vote in favour aga","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:01:30 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/14/netanyahu-says-only-a-unity-government-can-guarantee-israels-security?traffic_source=rss,2026-11-15 03:26:19
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Explosion near Syria’s capital kills father and child,Explosion near Syria’s capital kills father and child,"Explosion near Syria’s capital kills father and child Syria’s Internal Security Forces have launched an investigation into a suspected bomb attack in a suburb of Damascus. Save Share Deadly car bomb blast kills two near Syria's capital A blast from a suspected explosive device planted inside a car in a suburb of the Syrian capital, Damascus, has killed at least two people, including a child, and wounded one. The explosion in Jaramana, on the southeastern edge of Damascus, on Saturday killed a man and his daughter, while a third person, said to be the wife of the man, was seriously injured. Syria’s Internal Security Forces said they sealed off the area and opened an investigation into the circumstances surrounding the blast. Jaramana is home to a large community of the Druze religious minority and has seen tensions between some Druze members and the Sunni majority backing President Ahmed al-Sharaa’s government. Witnesses described the vehicle as a Kia Rio parked between two apartment buildings in Jaramana, which is largely considered a quiet residential area, said Al Jazeera’s Heidi Pett, reporting from the blast scene. Pett said the security situation in the capital remains complex, despite improvements since the regime of former President Bashar al-Assad fell two years ago. “In the last couple of months, there were two very high-profile incidents,” she said, includinga double-tap attackin July during French President Emmanuel Macron’s visit, which Syrian authorities attributed to a cell affiliated with ISIL (ISIS). “There was also a very deadly attack on a cafe frequented by lawyers near the Palace of Justice, which is where these very high-pr","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:43:12 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/14/explosion-near-syrias-capital-kills-father-and-child?traffic_source=rss,2026-11-15 03:26:19
