Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Ronaldo-less Portugal thrashed 4-1 by Denmark in the Nations League,Ronaldo-less Portugal thrashed 4-1 by Denmark in the Nations League,"Ronaldo-less Portugal thrashed 4-1 by Denmark in the Nations League Rasmus Hojlund stars with brace as Denmark close in on a spot in the Nations League quarterfinals. Save Share Portugal have beenhammered 1-4by Denmark, an embarrassing Nations League defeat in their first match without Cristiano Ronaldo, following the superstar forward’s retirement from international football. Rasmus Hojlund starred with a superb brace on Saturday as second place Denmark close in on a spot in the quarterfinals with a brilliant display in Braga. The Danes are on nine points from five fixtures, three behind Portugal, who were already sure of qualification for the last eight having won all four of their previous group fixtures. A draw against third-placed Norway on Tuesday, 3-1 winners over Wales earlier, will see Denmark through. Ahead of kickoff, Portugal paid tribute to Ronaldo, who announced hisexit from the international gamelast week, with the team and mascots walking out wearing Ronaldo’s number seven and his name on their jerseys. Fans held up a huge banner that read “Thank you, captain” as the teams entered the field, while applause rolled around the stadium once the match clock hit seven. Ronaldo made his debut for Portugal in 2003 and went on to establish world records for goals and appearances in international football, netting 146 times in 234 matches. The highlight of his international career was winning Euro 2016, but it ended badly when the 41-year-old fell out with Portugal coach Jorge Jesus over not being selected for a Nations League fixture in September. That row led to the five-time Ballon d’Or winner being handed a 30-day suspension by t","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:00:45 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/11/14/ronaldo-less-portugal-thrashed-4-1-by-denmark-in-the-nations-league?traffic