Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Expanding missile range is our new deterrence strategy,Expanding missile range is our new deterrence strategy,"Expanding missile range is our new deterrence strategy Esmail Kosari, a member of Parliament, discussed Iran’s missile-range expansion in an interview with Javan. Following growing threats, the Islamic Republic of Iran unveiled an increase in the range of its missiles as part of its broader strategy to strengthen deterrence capabilities. The move came after remarks by Iran’s Leader emphasizing an immediate response to threats without geographical limitations. Esmail Kosari, a member of Parliament, discussed Iran’s missile-range expansion in an interview with Javan. Following growing threats, the Islamic Republic of Iran unveiled an increase in the range of its missiles as part of its broader strategy to strengthen deterrence capabilities. The move came after remarks by Iran’s Leader emphasizing an immediate response to threats without geographical limitations. The announcement received extensive international media attention, with some analysts describing it as a sign of a shift in Tehran’s deterrence doctrine. Iranian officials have repeatedly stated that if another confrontation occurs, the country will reveal part of its advanced military equipment and capabilities on the battlefield, creating a new level of surprise for its enemies. The country aims to maintain the capabilities necessary to respond wherever required, whether at the regional or extra-regional level, within the framework of deterrence and countering hostile actions by its opponents. Etemad: A turbulent transition period In an article, Etemad examined the simultaneous formation of a new government in Israel and the transfer of congressional power in the US. The current transition period is what makes the situation particularly complicated. Recent political setbacks do not necessarily reduce the likelihood of war. Although Trump suffered an electoral defeat, he still retains significant authority as commander in chief. In a post-election environment, he could seek","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:57:37 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532151/Expanding-missile-range-is-our-new-deterrence-strategy,2026-11-15 03:27:06
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Baby in Gaza freezes to death as UN counts 245 child deaths in West Bank,Baby in Gaza freezes to death as UN counts 245 child deaths in West Bank,"Baby in Gaza freezes to death as UN counts 245 child deaths in West Bank TEHRAN — Kinan Ahmad Raqiq died in a tent in Khan Younis on November 12. He was nine months old. TEHRAN — Kinan Ahmad Raqiq died in a tent in Khan Younis on November 12. He was nine months old. Gaza’s Health Ministry called it the first cold-related death of the winter. The hospital that received his body, Nasser, had been hit by an Israeli airstrike the same day. Six people were killed, among them the surgeon Rizq Abu Shaeira. “I woke up only to see his skin had turned blue, so I rushed him to Nasser Hospital, but he had already died from hypothermia and frozen to death,” his father, Ahmed Raqiq, told AFP. The baby died after a storm that Gaza’s Government Media Office says flooded about 70,000 tents in 12 hours. Oxfam estimates the water displaced around 100,000 people. By November 8, the UN humanitarian office, OCHA, had received appeals from more than 26,000 households whose shelters or belongings were damaged. Shelter on the wrong side of the border About 1.4 million Palestinians, 65 percent of Gaza’s population, now live in tents or makeshift shelters, OCHA says. More than 150,000 tents are waiting outside the Strip. Inside, aid agencies have virtually nothing left to distribute. In early November, they calculated that Gaza needed 121,000 tents and 57,000 emergency shelter kits. None of the kits were in stock. In October, the UN migration agency, IOM, said the supply pipeline covered only 17 percent of winter shelter needs. Reuters reported that 8,600 emergency shelter kits were held up. The so-called ceasefire was supposed to ease this. A year on, Gaza’s Governmen","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:53:42 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532138/Baby-in-Gaza-freezes-to-death-as-UN-counts-245-child-deaths-in,2026-11-15 03:27:07
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Officials’ shifting explanations deepen doubts over US airspace shutdown,Officials’ shifting explanations deepen doubts over US airspace shutdown,"Officials’ shifting explanations deepen doubts over US airspace shutdown TEHRAN — The U.S. Federal Aviation Administration grounded every departing flight in the country on Friday, and the public’s first explanation fit in a single phrase: a “temporary telecommunications outage.” The order began at 3:54 p.m. Eastern Time and lasted until 8:15 p.m. It left thousands of flights canceled and a government that has spent months promising a modernized air traffic system, explaining why its old one failed everywhere at once. TEHRAN — The U.S. Federal Aviation Administration grounded every departing flight in the country on Friday, and the public’s first explanation fit in a single phrase: a “temporary telecommunications outage.” The order began at 3:54 p.m. Eastern Time and lasted until 8:15 p.m. It left thousands of flights canceled and a government that has spent months promising a modernized air traffic system, explaining why its old one failed everywhere at once. The FAA said trouble had hit the Air Route Traffic Control Centers, the facilities that steer planes between airports. By evening, Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy supplied detail. Switches and routers, he said, “got overloaded with data” and began returning inconsistent information. He corrected himself mid-sentence: “I shouldn’t say they went down.” Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin described new technology “overwhelming the older system,” while Duffy stressed that none of the new equipment failed. “We have old switches, old routers,” he said. “We use 1980s little copper lines.” Questions the briefing left open Those accounts do not line up neatly. Mullin said nothing points to a cyberattack and that the failure looked mechanical, then added that officials were “still looking.” Duffy said he did not want to rule out what he called “nefarious activity.” Neither explained why backups did not contain the problem, which matters because, as aviation law professor Ron Bartsch told Al Jazeera, the who","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:39:35 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532139/Officials-shifting-explanations-deepen-doubts-over-US-airspace,2026-11-15 03:27:08
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iranian painter unveils two paintings commemorating Hazrat Fatemeh Zahra (SA),Iranian painter unveils two paintings commemorating Hazrat Fatemeh Zahra (SA),"Iranian painter unveils two paintings commemorating Hazrat Fatemeh Zahra (SA) TEHRAN – Iranian painter Ali Bahreini unveiled two new paintings depicting the martyrdom of Hazrat Fatemeh Zahra (SA), the daughter of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH), on Friday, the anniversary of her martyrdom. TEHRAN – Iranian painter Ali Bahreini unveiled two new paintings depicting the martyrdom of Hazrat Fatemeh Zahra (SA), the daughter of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH), on Friday, the anniversary of her martyrdom. The two newly released works portray different moments associated with the martyrdom of Hazrat Fatemeh (SA), Mehr reported. The first painting depicts the moment of her martyrdom, while the second portrays Imam Ali (AS) mourning over her body during her funeral procession. Bahreini, an experienced painter and calligrapher known for his religious and historical subjects, has devoted much of his artistic career to depicting figures and events from Islamic history, particularly the lives of the Ahl al-Bayt (the family of Prophet Muhammad). Born in 1970, in Bushehr province, Bahreini began painting professionally in 1989. Over the course of his career, he has held 18 solo exhibitions in Bushehr province and approximately 11 others in different parts of Iran. He has also participated in 25 group exhibitions. His artistic approach is primarily realist, although he incorporates elements of traditional Persian miniature painting and Impressionism into his works. Religious themes have been a recurring feature of his artistic output, with paintings such as “The Loneliness of Hazrat Fatemeh,” “The Loneliness of Imam Ali,” “Birth of the Jasmine,” and “Manifestation of the Advent” among his notable works. Among his major projects is the “Mehr-o-Mah” (Sun and Moon) collection, comprising ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:38:57 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532129/Iranian-painter-unveils-two-paintings-commemorating-Hazrat-Fatemeh,2026-11-15 03:27:09
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Nolan’s ‘Odyssey’ to be shown, reviewed in Tehran","Nolan’s ‘Odyssey’ to be shown, reviewed in Tehran","Nolan’s ‘Odyssey’ to be shown, reviewed in Tehran TEHRAN – The 2026 epic action fantasy film “The Odyssey,” written and directed by Christopher Nolan, will be shown at the cineplex of the Tehran Book Garden on Wednesday. TEHRAN – The 2026 epic action fantasy film “The Odyssey,” written and directed by Christopher Nolan, will be shown at the cineplex of the Tehran Book Garden on Wednesday. The 172-minute movie screening is set for 16:30 and it will be followed by a review session in the presence of the veteran film critic Masoud Farassati, ILNA reported. An adaptation of Homer's ancient Greek epic poem, the “Odyssey,” it stars an ensemble cast including Matt Damon, Tom Holland, Anne Hathaway, Robert Pattinson, Lupita Nyong'o, Samantha Morton, Zendaya, and Charlize Theron. In the film, Odysseus (Damon), the Greek king of Ithaca, undergoes a long and perilous journey home after the Trojan War and encounters mythical beings as he attempts to reunite with his wife, Penelope (Hathaway). Throughout his voyage, he is forced to confront the whims of gods, mythological monsters, and trials that stretch both his cunning and his humanity to the breaking point. With an estimated budget of $250 million, it is among the most expensive films of Nolan's career, and the first feature film to be shot entirely on IMAX's 70 mm film cameras. The film received acclaim for its direction, performances, and set pieces, though some criticized Nolan's deviations from the source material. It has grossed $1.804 billion worldwide, becoming Nolan's highest-grossing film, the second-highest-grossing film of 2026, the highest-grossing R-rated film ever, the highest-grossing film distributed by Universal, and the eleventh-high","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:38:19 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532118/Nolan-s-Odyssey-to-be-shown-reviewed-in-Tehran,2026-11-15 03:27:10
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Women artists explore Hadith al-Kisa through calligraphy, visual arts in Tehran","Women artists explore Hadith al-Kisa through calligraphy, visual arts in Tehran","Women artists explore Hadith al-Kisa through calligraphy, visual arts in Tehran TEHRAN - An exhibition featuring more than 80 artworks inspired by Hadith al-Kisa, created by Iranian women artists, opened at the Khaneh Gallery of the Art Bureau in Tehran on Friday, marking the martyrdom anniversary of Hazrat Fatemeh Zahra (SA). TEHRAN - An exhibition featuring more than 80 artworks inspired by Hadith al-Kisa, created by Iranian women artists, opened at the Khaneh Gallery of the Art Bureau in Tehran on Friday, marking the martyrdom anniversary of Hazrat Fatemeh Zahra (SA). Hadith al-Kisa recounts an occasion when Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) gathered his close family members under a cloak. In Islamic tradition, the narration highlights the special status of the Prophet’s household, known as the Ahl al-Bayt. The visual arts exhibition brings together works by 50 women artists specializing in calligraphy, illumination, poetry and photography. The artworks offer different artistic interpretations of Hadith al-Kisa, Mehr reported. Hamideh Givi, a member of the Iranian Calligraphers Association, said the exhibition is being held for the second consecutive year and features more than 80 works produced by members of the Women of the Sun's Design artistic group. Explaining the exhibition's central theme, Givi said the text of Hadith al-Kisa has been rendered in Naskh calligraphy, while its Persian translation has been written in Nastaliq and Shekasteh Nastaliq scripts. The exhibition also includes paintings inspired by the narration, alongside poems written by women members of the group. These literary works have been transcribed by calligraphers, while illumination artists have prepared ornamental title pages intended for a forthcoming illustrated book. The exhibition's poster also incorporates a photograph take","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:37:44 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532130/Women-artists-explore-Hadith-al-Kisa-through-calligraphy-visual,2026-11-15 03:27:11
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Iran downs 17th US MQ-1 drone, reports two tankers hit by sea mines east of Hormuz Strait","Iran downs 17th US MQ-1 drone, reports two tankers hit by sea mines east of Hormuz Strait","Iran downs 17th US MQ-1 drone, reports two tankers hit by sea mines east of Hormuz Strait TEHRAN – Iran’s Islamic Revolution Guard Corps (IRGC) has shot down another US reconnaissance and combat drone over the Persian Gulf, while the Iranian Navy has reported that two oil tankers separately caught fire after striking sea mines in a restricted maritime zone east of the Strait of Hormuz. TEHRAN – Iran’s Islamic Revolution Guard Corps (IRGC) has shot down another US reconnaissance and combat drone over the Persian Gulf, while the Iranian Navy has reported that two oil tankers separately caught fire after striking sea mines in a restricted maritime zone east of the Strait of Hormuz. In a statement released on Saturday, the IRGC announced that its Aerospace units had destroyed a US MQ-1-series drone over Qeshm Island using an advanced air defense system. The downing marked the 17th US MQ-1 drone destroyed by the IRGC, according to the statement, which described the incident as another failure of US reconnaissance operations along Iran’s maritime borders. The IRGC also reported that its forces had so far destroyed 56 US MQ-9 drones, bringing the total number of MQ-1 and MQ-9 drones downed to 73. Meanwhile, the Iranian Navy announced that two oil tankers had separately struck sea mines and caught fire in a prohibited area east of the Strait of Hormuz. According to statements issued by the Navy’s public relations office on Saturday, the two incidents occurred after the vessels entered the restricted maritime zone despite prior warnings from Iranian authorities. The Navy said one of the tankers was sailing through the designated unsafe area early Saturday morning while its tracking and identification systems were switched off. The vessel subsequently struck a sea mine, caught fire and was disabled. In a separate announcement, the Navy reported that another tanker ha","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:34:53 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532150/Iran-downs-17th-US-MQ-1-drone-reports-two-tankers-hit-by-sea,2026-11-15 03:27:12
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Iran demonstrated remarkable strength in two wars, says ex-FM","Iran demonstrated remarkable strength in two wars, says ex-FM","Iran demonstrated remarkable strength in two wars, says ex-FM TEHRAN – Iran demonstrated extraordinary resilience and strength in the two imposed wars (the 12-day war and the Ramadan war), surprising the international community with its ability to withstand external pressure, former Iranian foreign minister Ali Akbar Salehi has said. TEHRAN – Iran demonstrated extraordinary resilience and strength in the two imposed wars (the 12-day war and the Ramadan war), surprising the international community with its ability to withstand external pressure, former Iranian foreign minister Ali Akbar Salehi has said. Speaking to Mehr News Agency, Salehi, who also previously headed the Atomic Energy Organization of Iran (AEOI), reflected on the two wars Iran has experienced over the past two years, saying the Islamic Republic had displayed remarkable capabilities in the face of widespread international expectations. “We do not claim to be a global military power, nor do we claim to be a global economic power. But we can say with confidence that we have been able to stand firm against the bullying and unjust pressure imposed on us by others,” he stated. Salehi pointed to the importance of national unity in the face of wars and economic pressure, saying people has backed the government and prevented the political system from collapsing under pressure. Drawing a comparison with the Arab Spring and the Islamic Awakening movements, he said popular uprisings in several countries had failed to achieve their intended outcomes because of the lack of necessary unity between the people and their governments. In Iran's case, he argued, the principle of Velayat-e Faqih (Guardianship of the Islamic Jurist) had played a pivotal role in preserving the cohesion and continuity of the Islamic Revolution.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:31:54 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532149/Iran-demonstrated-remarkable-strength-in-two-wars-says-ex-FM,2026-11-15 03:27:13
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Rosatom to increase workforce at Bushehr nuclear plant to 300,Rosatom to increase workforce at Bushehr nuclear plant to 300,"Rosatom to increase workforce at Bushehr nuclear plant to 300 TEHRAN – Russia’s state nuclear corporation Rosatom plans to increase its workforce at Iran’s Bushehr Nuclear Power Plant from the current 180 employees to 300 in the near future, as it moves to resume previously scheduled operations despite ongoing regional tensions. TEHRAN – Russia’s state nuclear corporation Rosatom plans to increase its workforce at Iran’s Bushehr Nuclear Power Plant from the current 180 employees to 300 in the near future, as it moves to resume previously scheduled operations despite ongoing regional tensions. Rosatom CEO Alexei Likhachev announced the plan on Friday, according to Russia’s TASS news agency, saying the company saw no significant risks that would impede the pace of its work at the facility. “The headcount is growing at present: 180 people are already on the site; we plan to increase it to 300 in the near future,” Likhachev said. He acknowledged that the regional situation remained tense but said Rosatom was seeking to restore its operations to the planned pace and reach its target workforce level over the coming year. On October 28, Likhachev said the corporation aimed to increase the number of Russian personnel in Iran to 700. Rosatom had previously evacuated hundreds of its employees from the country on security grounds following US-Israeli aggression against Iran. In November 2025, Likhachev told Russia’s Channel One that Rosatom planned to construct two additional nuclear power units, each with a capacity of 1,000 megawatts, alongside the existing unit at the Bushehr plant. He also said construction was progressing. Meanwhile, on September 24, 2025, Iran and Russia signed a memorandum of understanding on cooperation in the construction of small nuclear power plants in Iran. The agreement was conclud","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:30:16 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532148/Rosatom-to-increase-workforce-at-Bushehr-nuclear-plant-to-300,2026-11-15 03:27:14
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Strengthening strategic ties with China must be a priority for Iran,Strengthening strategic ties with China must be a priority for Iran,"Strengthening strategic ties with China must be a priority for Iran TEHRAN – A member of the Iranian Parliament’s Presiding Board has called for closer coordination among government bodies to strengthen strategic relations between Iran and China and translate existing agreements and opportunities into tangible results. TEHRAN – A member of the Iranian Parliament’s Presiding Board has called for closer coordination among government bodies to strengthen strategic relations between Iran and China and translate existing agreements and opportunities into tangible results. Speaking to Mehr News Agency, Farshad Ebrahimpour said China, given its extensive relations with Iran and Arab countries, was well positioned to establish a sustainable regional security framework. Referring to the 2023 agreement between Tehran and Riyadh, brokered by Beijing, Ebrahimpour said the initiative had demonstrated China's capacity to help ease regional tensions. However, he stressed that such cooperation should lead to lasting mechanisms for security dialogue and mutual respect for national sovereignty. Regional stability, he added, cannot be achieved without taking Iran's security and national interests into account. Ebrahimpour said relations with China should not be viewed merely as a means of easing international pressure. Rather, they should serve as an opportunity to strengthen national security and advance Iran's economic development. The parliament member pointed to the gap between economic agreements with China and their practical outcomes, saying that the 25-year Comprehensive Cooperation Program, along with the opportunities arising from Iran's membership in the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) and BRICS, provides significant potential for expanding economic ties. However, he cautioned that signing ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:27:42 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532147/Strengthening-strategic-ties-with-China-must-be-a-priority-for,2026-11-15 03:27:15
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Iran to press ahead with defense industry development, lawmaker says","Iran to press ahead with defense industry development, lawmaker says","Iran to press ahead with defense industry development, lawmaker says TEHRAN – Iran will continue to advance its defense industry with determination and full strength, a member of the Iranian Parliament’s National Security and Foreign Policy Commission said, emphasizing that the country’s military capabilities will undergo significant improvements. TEHRAN – Iran will continue to advance its defense industry with determination and full strength, a member of the Iranian Parliament’s National Security and Foreign Policy Commission said, emphasizing that the country’s military capabilities will undergo significant improvements. Speaking to Mehr News Agency, Alaeddin Boroujerdi said Iran’s air defense and offensive capabilities would see a major transformation, alongside substantial progress across other areas of the defense industry. He stressed the importance of strengthening the country’s defensive capabilities, saying that sustained investment in the missile and drone sectors had already yielded significant results, including the development of the Shahed drone, which has gained international recognition. Similar advances, he added, would be achieved in other areas of the country’s defense industry, further enhancing Iran’s military capabilities. He noted that despite the damage and losses sustained during the imposed wars, including the 12-day and 40-day conflicts, the developments had also produced significant gains in terms of military and political standing, national authority and social cohesion. Referring to the assassination of Leader of the Islamic Revolution Ayatollah Seyyed Ali Khamenei in a joint US-Israeli attack on February 28, 2026, the lawmaker stressed that Iran must take a firm response for the blood of the martyred Leader and other victims of the United States and the Israeli regime. “ We must remain vi","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:25:08 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532144/Iran-to-press-ahead-with-defense-industry-development-lawmaker,2026-11-15 03:27:16
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iran defeat Palestine at Basra tournament,Iran defeat Palestine at Basra tournament,"Iran defeat Palestine at Basra tournament TEHRAN - Iran football team defeated 10-man Palestine on Saturday at the Basra four-nation tournament. TEHRAN - Iran football team defeated 10-man Palestine on Saturday at the Basra four-nation tournament. Palestine went to 10-man in the 66th minute after Ameed Sawafta was shown his second yellow card. Sardar Azmoun opened the scoring for Team Melli in 77th minute and Saleh Hardani made it 2-0 with six minutes remaining at the Basra International Stadium. Iran will play Iraq on Tuesday, while Palestine meet Lebanon. The tournament is expected to provide an important opportunity for coaches to test player readiness and assess their levels ahead of official competitions, as the date for continental commitments approaches. Reporting by Masoud Hossein","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:02:34 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532145/Iran-defeat-Palestine-at-Basra-tournament,2026-11-15 03:27:17
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Senior MP: Iran’s steadfastness has left US in a strategic dead end,Senior MP: Iran’s steadfastness has left US in a strategic dead end,"Senior MP: Iran’s steadfastness has left US in a strategic dead end TEHRAN – Iran’s steadfast resistance on multiple fronts has pushed the United States into a strategic dead end, with any further miscalculation by its adversaries likely to provoke an even more consequential response from Tehran, the chairman of the Iranian Parliament’s National Security and Foreign Policy Commission said. TEHRAN – Iran’s steadfast resistance on multiple fronts has pushed the United States into a strategic dead end, with any further miscalculation by its adversaries likely to provoke an even more consequential response from Tehran, the chairman of the Iranian Parliament’s National Security and Foreign Policy Commission said. Ebrahim Azizi made the remarks on Friday, attributing the failure of US and Israeli calculations to the Iranian nation’s resilience in the face of sustained hostile actions by Washington and the Israeli regime. Recalling decades of US hostility toward Iran, Azizi said Washington had sought to undermine the country since the victory of the Islamic Revolution through various measures, including coup attempts such as the Nojeh coup, the Tabas incident, the imposition of war, economic and political sanctions, and efforts to create instability across different sectors. He said the US president’s contradictory and frequently changing statements on negotiations, agreements, war, military action, the Strait of Hormuz and threats to destroy Iran reflected Washington’s failure to anticipate the Islamic Republic’s response and its inability to bring developments under control. Addressing political developments in the United States and the occupied territories, Azizi said Iran did not regard changes in American political parties or administrations as significant, stressing that neither Republican nor Democratic governments altered Washington’s fundamental approach towa","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:49:31 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532143/Senior-Iranian-MP-Iran-s-steadfastness-has-left-US-in-a-strategic,2026-11-15 03:27:18
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iran rejects normal IAEA inspections under abnormal conditions,Iran rejects normal IAEA inspections under abnormal conditions,"Iran rejects normal IAEA inspections under abnormal conditions TEHRAN – Iran’s Mission to the United Nations Office in Vienna has condemned resolutions adopted by the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) Board of Governors on Iran as legally and technically flawed, stressing that normal implementation of safeguards cannot resume under the abnormal conditions created by attacks on the country’s safeguarded nuclear facilities. TEHRAN – Iran’s Mission to the United Nations Office in Vienna has condemned resolutions adopted by the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) Board of Governors on Iran as legally and technically flawed, stressing that normal implementation of safeguards cannot resume under the abnormal conditions created by attacks on the country’s safeguarded nuclear facilities. In a statement posted on its X account, the Iranian mission also criticized IAEA Director General Rafael Grossi’s reporting on Iran, arguing that the Board’s decisions were adopted through an abuse of process and that US-Israeli attacks had disrupted inspections and forced the Agency to withdraw its inspectors. The mission said the IAEA had based its reports on Board of Governors resolutions that were “technically and legally flawed,” adopted through an abuse of process, and contained findings that exceeded the Board’s legal authority. It further noted that Grossi himself had acknowledged that attacks on Iran’s safeguarded nuclear facilities had created unprecedented circumstances, disrupted inspections and compelled the Agency to withdraw its inspectors, while making it necessary to take Iran’s security concerns into account. “The US erased its aggression from biased resolutions, but not its consequences from reality. Facts don’t vanish because politics demands!” the mission stated. It emphasized that the normal implementation of safeguards could not resume under abnormal circumstances, calling on the Board of ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:46:40 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532142/Iran-rejects-normal-IAEA-inspections-under-abnormal-conditions,2026-11-15 03:27:19
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Bet on the losing horse: Abu Dhabi's gamble in Hormuz,Bet on the losing horse: Abu Dhabi's gamble in Hormuz,"Bet on the losing horse: Abu Dhabi's gamble in Hormuz TEHRAN - When Sultan Ahmed Al Jaber took the screen at CERAWeek in Houston on March 23, 2026, he chose his words carefully. The Managing Director and Group CEO of ADNOC, speaking by video link because war had closed the skies, called any disruption of the Strait of Hormuz “weaponizing” energy and “economic terrorism against every nation.” TEHRAN - When Sultan Ahmed Al Jaber took the screen at CERAWeek in Houston on March 23, 2026, he chose his words carefully. The Managing Director and Group CEO of ADNOC, speaking by video link because war had closed the skies, called any disruption of the Strait of Hormuz “weaponizing” energy and “economic terrorism against every nation.” He warned that “twenty-one miles wide, twenty million barrels a day” was now squeezed, that oil prices had already risen by 50 percent, and that “no country should be allowed to hold Hormuz hostage. Not now. Not ever.” He invited American capital into ADNOC, XRG and AI ventures, and promised ADIPEC in November as proof that the UAE could keep energy flowing. Eight months later, that Houston speech reads less as analysis and more as confession. The UAE was not describing a crisis. It was announcing its role in it. From the first bombs, the war moved to Hormuz From the first hours of the American-Israeli war against Iran on February 28, 2026, it was clear the fate of this war would be decided not in the air over Tehran or Isfahan, but in the waters of the Persian Gulf. Its focal point was inevitable: the Strait of Hormuz. Washington and Tel Aviv began with a massive air campaign against nuclear sites in Fordow, Natanz and Isfahan, military bases and commanders. Tehran answered where it is strongest. It did not chase American stealth fighters across the sky. It closed the strait. That single decision reversed the initiative. The aggressors had ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:43:48 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532141/Bet-on-the-losing-horse-Abu-Dhabi-s-gamble-in-Hormuz,2026-11-15 03:27:19
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Iran calls on US to end aggression, lift maritime blockade","Iran calls on US to end aggression, lift maritime blockade","Iran calls on US to end aggression, lift maritime blockade TEHRAN – Iran has called on the United States to immediately end its aggression against the country, lift its maritime blockade and provide credible guarantees against further attacks, warning that any renewed US-Israeli aggression would be met with an immediate and decisive response. TEHRAN – Iran has called on the United States to immediately end its aggression against the country, lift its maritime blockade and provide credible guarantees against further attacks, warning that any renewed US-Israeli aggression would be met with an immediate and decisive response. Addressing a UN Security Council meeting on the situation in the Middle East in New York on Friday, Gholamhossein Darzi, Iran’s Ambassador and Deputy Permanent Representative to the United Nations, said insecurity in the Persian Gulf and around the Strait of Hormuz was a direct consequence of US-Israeli military aggression and Washington’s unlawful measures against Iran. Darzi said the United States had launched wars of aggression against Iran on June 13, 2025, and again on February 28, 2026, in flagrant violation of the UN Charter and fundamental principles of international law. He said the two rounds of aggression had claimed more than 5,000 lives, including 254 children and 251 women, while extensive attacks had targeted civilians and civilian infrastructure, including hospitals, bridges, industrial facilities, airports, transport networks and energy installations. Referring to the February 28 attacks, Darzi said two waves of US Tomahawk missiles had struck a school in Minab, killing 168 children. He also cited a US strike on Lamerd Stadium that killed at least 21 civilians, including children, and wounded around 100 others. The Iranian envoy further condemned threats by US officials to destr","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:37:31 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532140/Iran-calls-on-US-to-end-aggression-lift-maritime-blockade,2026-11-15 03:27:20
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,From the battlefield to the ballot box: war comes home,From the battlefield to the ballot box: war comes home,"From the battlefield to the ballot box: war comes home TEHRAN – Western leaders assumed they could keep the Palestinian bloodshed, the flames of war in Iran, and the resulting costs far removed from their own societies. TEHRAN – Western leaders assumed they could keep the Palestinian bloodshed, the flames of war in Iran, and the resulting costs far removed from their own societies. They believed American and European citizens would continue watching the war unfold on their screens, without it affecting their lives or reshaping their political choices. But the massacres in Gaza shattered the moral barrier, while U.S.-Zionist aggression against Iran shook energy and shipping markets. Then came the ballot boxes and popular protests, declaring that wars ignited beyond national borders can return home as questions of legitimacy, bills to be paid, and votes of political punishment. These developments are not isolated events. They are different expressions of a single moment: the erosion of the hegemonic order’s ability to wage war, monopolize its narrative, and leave others to bear its costs. The collapse of moral immunity October 7, 2023, marked a major turning point in the history of the conflict, not simply because of what happened that day, but because of what the ensuing genocidal war exposed about the true nature of the Zionist project and the limits of the Western shield protecting it. What the West presented under the banner of “self-defense” turned into mass killing, starvation, the destruction of hospitals, schools and residential neighborhoods, and an attempt to make life itself impossible in the Gaza Strip. By October 2026, the number of Palestinians killed in Gaza had exceeded 74,000,","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:15:26 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532137/From-the-battlefield-to-the-ballot-box-war-comes-home,2026-11-15 03:27:21
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Efforts to encircle the resistance bloc within its borders,Efforts to encircle the resistance bloc within its borders,"Efforts to encircle the resistance bloc within its borders LONDON – In response to the transformations that could give Iran and its allies greater room to expand their influence, the United States and its allies are not standing idle. Another front in this confrontation involves attempts to weaken the resistance bloc from within and restrict the room for maneuver available to forces aligned with it in each country. LONDON – In response to the transformations that could give Iran and its allies greater room to expand their influence, the United States and its allies are not standing idle. Another front in this confrontation involves attempts to weaken the resistance bloc from within and restrict the room for maneuver available to forces aligned with it in each country. The objective is to prevent Iran from fully taking advantage of the outcomes of the confrontation with the Israeli regime and the United States. In this case, the aim is not necessarily to defeat Iran on the battlefield, but rather to obstruct its ability to translate its achievements into sustainable political and economic influence. For this reason, pressure is being directed towards Lebanon, Iraq, Iran's borders with neighboring countries, and relations between governments and local political forces. This opens up parallel internal fronts, alongside the military confrontation. In Lebanon, one aspect of this strategy is the intensification of pressure on Hezbollah, attempts to restrict its freedom of movement, and efforts to push the Lebanese state towards taking measures targeting its weapons and military role. These measures are viewed as part of an attempt to encircle the bloc from all directions. In addition, to reduce its ability to influence the Lebanese and regional balance of power. The performance of the Lebanese authorities, amid external understandings and pressures, is also regarded as an influential factor i","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:03:22 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532136/Efforts-to-encircle-the-resistance-bloc-within-its-borders,2026-11-15 03:27:22
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iran sends 70 athletes to Open SCO Cup,Iran sends 70 athletes to Open SCO Cup,"Iran sends 70 athletes to Open SCO Cup TEHRAN - A total of 70 Iranian athletes are representing the country at the Open Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) in Moscow. TEHRAN - A total of 70 Iranian athletes are representing the country at the Open Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) in Moscow. The international sporting event, running from Nov. 11 to 23 in Moscow and the Moscow Region, has brought together more than 2,000 athletes from Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) member states and invited teams. Around 100 sets of medals are up for grabs. The competition features 11 sports: table tennis, trampoline gymnastics, sambo, sport climbing, artistic gymnastics, weightlifting, fencing, rhythmic gymnastics, chess, judo and wushu. Iran has sent a 70-member delegation to compete in six disciplines: sport climbing, judo, weightlifting, artistic gymnastics, chess and table tennis.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:15:12 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532134/Iran-sends-70-athletes-to-Open-SCO-Cup,2026-11-15 03:27:23
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Isfahan’s pigeon towers emerge as potential World Heritage candidate,Isfahan’s pigeon towers emerge as potential World Heritage candidate,"Isfahan’s pigeon towers emerge as potential World Heritage candidate TEHRAN – Iran’s historic pigeon towers in Isfahan province could have the potential to be nominated for UNESCO World Heritage status, prompting renewed calls for comprehensive documentation, comparative research and stronger conservation measures to establish their significance on a global scale. TEHRAN – Iran’s historic pigeon towers in Isfahan province could have the potential to be nominated for UNESCO World Heritage status, prompting renewed calls for comprehensive documentation, comparative research and stronger conservation measures to establish their significance on a global scale. The towers, many dating from the Safavid era, are more than distinctive mud-brick structures built to shelter pigeons. They represent an ingenious combination of vernacular architecture, traditional agricultural technology and natural resource management that supported farming communities across Iran’s central plateau. Alireza Izadi, director-general of the office for registration, preservation and rehabilitation of cultural heritage at the Ministry of Cultural Heritage and Tourism, raised the prospect of their international recognition during a meeting of the supreme council for the registration and buffer zones of immovable heritage in Falavarjan, Isfahan province, Mehr new agency reported on Saturday. He described the pigeon towers as valuable heritage assets and called for a comprehensive nomination dossier to be prepared to facilitate their potential introduction to the international community. Izadi also stressed the importance of documenting the climatic, historical and cultural characteristics of heritage sites, completing registration files and securing cooperation among government agencies, municipal authorities and the private sector to provide resources for conservation. ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:51:08 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532133/Isfahan-s-pigeon-towers-emerge-as-potential-World-Heritage-candidate,2026-11-15 03:27:23
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Crash site of former Iranian President Ebrahim Raisi named national heritage site,Crash site of former Iranian President Ebrahim Raisi named national heritage site,"Crash site of former Iranian President Ebrahim Raisi named national heritage site TEHRAN – The site where former Iranian President Ebrahim Raisi and seven others were martyred in a helicopter crash in East Azarbaijan province has been officially registered on Iran’s National Heritage List, a provincial cultural heritage official announced on Saturday. TEHRAN – The site where former Iranian President Ebrahim Raisi and seven others were martyred in a helicopter crash in East Azarbaijan province has been officially registered on Iran’s National Heritage List, a provincial cultural heritage official announced on Saturday. Vahid Navdad, deputy director of East Azarbaijan’s Cultural Heritage Department, said the site, located near the village of Uzi in the Dizmar region of Varzaqan county, was registered under No. 34570 in recognition of its national and historical significance. The crash occurred on May 19, 2024, when a Bell 212 helicopter carrying Raisi and a number of other officials and crew went down in the Dizmar forest area while they were returning to Tabriz from a ceremony marking the inauguration of the Qiz-Qalasi Dam on the Iran-Azerbaijan border. Those martyred included Raisi, Foreign Minister Hossein Amir-Abdollahian, Mohammad Ali Ale-Hashem, the representative of the Leader of the Islamic Revolution in East Azarbaijan and Friday prayer leader of Tabriz, and Malek Rahmati, the province’s governor-general, along with members of the flight crew and other accompanying personnel. Speaking about the significance of the registration, Navadad described the May 19 incident as one of the most consequential events in Iran’s contemporary history. He said the historical value of a site was not necessarily determined by its age, architectural features or surviving physical remains, adding that places could also acquire national ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:42:58 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532132/Crash-site-of-former-Iranian-President-Ebrahim-Raisi-named-national,2026-11-15 03:27:24
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iran's bentonite industry: production and export potential,Iran's bentonite industry: production and export potential,"Iran's bentonite industry: production and export potential TEHRAN- This article examines Iran's bentonite industry, highlighting recent production data, major industrial applications, and export potential. It explores the role of bentonite in drilling fluids, foundry operations, construction, iron ore pelletizing, and absorbent products. TEHRAN- This article examines Iran's bentonite industry, highlighting recent production data, major industrial applications, and export potential. It explores the role of bentonite in drilling fluids, foundry operations, construction, iron ore pelletizing, and absorbent products. The article also explains key quality specifications, technical documentation, processing requirements, and supply chain considerations that international buyers should evaluate when sourcing bentonite from Iran. Iran is an established producer of industrial minerals, including bentonite, a clay material used in manufacturing, engineering, and processing. According to the U.S. Geological Survey (USGS), Iran's bentonite production was estimated at 1.3 million metric tons in 2024, compared with 1.31 million metric tons in 2023 and 1.34 million metric tons in 2022. USGS data also record production of 715,000 metric tons in 2020 and 1.15 million metric tons in 2021. These figures indicate the scale of domestic production, not export volumes. Domestic demand, processing capacity, product grade, and logistics determine what is available to international buyers. Why bentonite matters to industrial markets Bentonite is a naturally occurring clay primarily composed of minerals from the smectite group, particularly montmorillonite. Its ability to absorb water, swell, bind particles, and form suspensions makes it useful across several industrial processes. Sodium and calcium bentonite are two commercially impor","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:19:41 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532131/Iran-s-bentonite-industry-production-and-export-potential,2026-11-15 03:27:25
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Tehran, Moscow set to convene joint ICT working group in 2027","Tehran, Moscow set to convene joint ICT working group in 2027","Tehran, Moscow set to convene joint ICT working group in 2027 TEHRAN – Iranian and Russian officials have agreed to hold the sixth meeting of their joint working group on information and communication technology (ICT) during the first quarter of 2027, as part of efforts to strengthen bilateral cooperation in the sector. TEHRAN – Iranian and Russian officials have agreed to hold the sixth meeting of their joint working group on information and communication technology (ICT) during the first quarter of 2027, as part of efforts to strengthen bilateral cooperation in the sector. ICT Minister Sattar Hashemi and Russian Deputy Minister of Digital Development, Communication, and Mass Media, Grigory Borisenko, met on the sidelines of the International Telecommunication Union (ITU) Plenipotentiary Conference (PP-26), which is taking place in Doha, Qatar, from November 9 to 27 November, Mehr news agency reported. Holding a specialized forum with the participation of technology companies from the two countries, exploring the possibility of establishing a joint information technology park, and expanding cooperation in the field of cybersecurity were among the main issues proposed by Hashemi during the meeting. He stressed that the sixth joint working group will provide an opportunity to follow up on collaborative projects. The Russian official, for his part, welcomed these proposals, highlighting the importance of constant interactions, and the development of specialized collaborations in the fields of ICT between both parties. Lauding Iran’s position and support at international forums, Borisenko said that cooperation between the two sides within the framework of ITU, BRICS, and the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) serve as great opportunities to pursue shared interests, highlighting the importa","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:58:17 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532128/Tehran-Moscow-set-to-convene-joint-ICT-working-group-in-2027,2026-11-15 03:27:26
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iranian students shine in Open World Astronomy Olympiad,Iranian students shine in Open World Astronomy Olympiad,"Iranian students shine in Open World Astronomy Olympiad TEHRAN – An Iranian team of six students has achieved remarkable success at the fifth edition of the Open World Astronomy Olympiad (OWAO), winning six gold medals. The Olympiad took place from November 6 to 14 in Russia. TEHRAN – An Iranian team of six students has achieved remarkable success at the fifth edition of the Open World Astronomy Olympiad (OWAO), winning six gold medals. The Olympiad took place from November 6 to 14 in Russia. Sarina Alampour, Parsia Hassanzadeh, Elshan Rouhani, Mohammad-Reza Mohammadi, Bardia Qilavizadeh, and Mehdi Aryafar secured gold medals, showcasing their dedication and academic excellence in the competition, IRNA reported. OWAO is a modern and rapidly growing competition that brings together talented and passionate astronomy students from around the world. OWAO combines the best astronomical traditions with cutting-edge knowledge assessment methods, and its tasks are developed by leading experts from various countries. The competition was organized with the support of the Ministry of Education of the Russian Federation. The Olympiad is open to teams of 2 to 6 participants (aged 18 years or younger). Each team may have one team leader and up to two observers (adults). One country can be represented by only one team.The Olympiad consists of four rounds: theoretical, practical, observational, and test rounds. The working language of the Olympiad is English; however, participants may use a glossary provided by the Academic Committee that has been pre-translated into their national languages by team leaders. Iran’s national Astronomy and Astrophysics Olympiad team was crowned world champion for the third consecutive year after winning five gold medals at the 19th","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:55:54 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532126/Iranian-students-shine-in-Open-World-Astronomy-Olympiad,2026-11-15 03:27:27
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,COP31: DOE chief meets Turkish officials to expand environmental ties,COP31: DOE chief meets Turkish officials to expand environmental ties,"COP31: DOE chief meets Turkish officials to expand environmental ties TEHRAN – The head of the Department of Environment (DOE), Shina Ansari, has met with Turkish officials to discuss ways to strengthen environmental cooperation between the two countries. TEHRAN – The head of the Department of Environment (DOE), Shina Ansari, has met with Turkish officials to discuss ways to strengthen environmental cooperation between the two countries. The meeting took place on the sidelines of the 31st session of the Conference of the Parties (COP31) to the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC), which is being held in Antalya, Turkey, from November 9 to 20. The discussions focused on exploring opportunities to expand bilateral collaboration in the environmental sector. On Wednesday, Ansari held a meeting with Turkish Vice President Cevdet Yilmaz, elaborating on the destructive impacts of the US-Israeli war against Iran, particularly explosions at fuel storage facilities, and the amount of toxic substances and greenhouse gases, underscoring that the implementation of constructive environmental programs depends on regional stability and security, IRNA reported. For his part, the Turkish official highlighted the long-standing cultural commonalities between Iran and Turkey, voicing the country’s readiness for the expansion of collaborations in different sectors, including the environment. Referring to the development of the Iran-Turkey joint environmental committee following last year’s Zero Waste Forum, which was held in Istanbul in October 2025, he called for the continuation of environmental cooperation, focusing on the protection of biological resources and habitats. “At a time when regional evolutions have once aga","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:53:38 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532124/COP31-DOE-chief-meets-Turkish-officials-to-expand-environmental,2026-11-15 03:27:27
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Trust Issues, Washington?","Trust Issues, Washington?","Trust Issues, Washington? Iran’s Parliament Speaker Mohammad Baqer Qalibaf says Washington’s lack of credibility and failure to honor past commitments remain the biggest hurdles to reaching an agreement with Tehran. Iran’s Parliament Speaker Mohammad Baqer Qalibaf says Washington’s lack of credibility and failure to honor past commitments remain the biggest hurdles to reaching an agreement with Tehran.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:49:57 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532121/Trust-Issues-Washington,2026-11-15 03:27:28
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iran defeat Nigeria at FIP World Polo Championship Zone E Qualifiers,Iran defeat Nigeria at FIP World Polo Championship Zone E Qualifiers,"Iran defeat Nigeria at FIP World Polo Championship Zone E Qualifiers TEHRAN – Iran defeated Nigeria 11-3 at the FIP World Polo Championship Zone E Qualifiers on Saturday. TEHRAN – Iran defeated Nigeria 11-3 at the FIP World Polo Championship Zone E Qualifiers on Saturday. Iran defeated Nigeria, with familiar faces, the Reza brothers, making their mark on the encounter. In another match, Pakistan stunned India with a 7–4 victory, securing their place in the final. Nigeria hosts the Federation of International Polo Zone E qualifiers for the World Polo Championship, with teams from Nigeria, India, Iran and Pakistan competing at Guards Polo Club, Abuja, from Nov. 9 to 16.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:46:30 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532120/Iran-defeat-Nigeria-at-FIP-World-Polo-Championship-Zone-E-Qualifiers,2026-11-15 03:27:29
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iran thrash Sri Lanka at AFC U17 Asian Cup Uzbekistan 2027 qualifier,Iran thrash Sri Lanka at AFC U17 Asian Cup Uzbekistan 2027 qualifier,"Iran thrash Sri Lanka at AFC U17 Asian Cup Uzbekistan 2027 qualifier TEHRAN - Iran made it two wins from two after a storming 11-0 victory against Sri Lanka in their AFC U17 Asian Cup Uzbekistan 2027 Qualifiers Group D match on Saturday. TEHRAN - Iran made it two wins from two after a storming 11-0 victory against Sri Lanka in their AFC U17 Asian Cup Uzbekistan 2027 Qualifiers Group D match on Saturday. Radin Haddarzi got the ball rolling for Iran in the third minute, tapping home from close range after good work from Mohammad Parsa on the right. Amirmohammad Zarei made it 2-0 in the 13th minute, benefitting from a poor Sri Lanka clearance before Aliasghar Naderi slotted home a 16th minute penalty. A breakaway a minute later saw Naderi tucking in the rebound after Imadh Shareeq had parried Zarei’s initial shot with the latter then curling a spectacular free-kick into the top corner in the 28th minute. Further strikes from Haddarzi (36th), Zarei (45th+1) and Amirali Alimardani (45th+3) gave Iran a comfortable 8-0 lead at the break. There was to be no respite for Sri Lanka after the interval as Iran pressed on with Amirsam Jannatalipour steering home from close range in the 56th minute after Shareeq had misjudged the flight of the ball with Naderi closing in for an attempted header. Naderi scored his fourth of the game two minutes later, curling in a beautiful shot from the edge of the box with Jannatalipour’s header in the 68th minute completing a superb Iran performance, the-afc.com reported.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:35:02 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532119/Iran-trash-Sri-Lanka-at-AFC-U17-Asian-Cup-Uzbekistan-2027-qualifier,2026-11-15 03:27:30
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iran are undisputed kings of beach soccer: AFC,Iran are undisputed kings of beach soccer: AFC,"Iran are undisputed kings of beach soccer: AFC TEHRAN - As excitement peaks for the AFC Beach Soccer Asian Cup Thailand 2026, the-afc.com  turns its attention to Group B, which promises to be a thriller. TEHRAN - As excitement peaks for the AFC Beach Soccer Asian Cup Thailand 2026, the-afc.com turns its attention to Group B, which promises to be a thriller. Leading the cast are defending champions Iran andthe-AFC.comtakes a look at just what stands in their way. The undisputed kings of beach soccer in Asia after winning their fourth title in 2025 to move past Japan with the most continental success, Iran will be confident of retaining their title as head coach Ali Naderi continues at the helm with Ali Mirshekari, who was crowned Most Valuable Player and Top Goalscorer at the last edition, leading their charge. Iran are drawn in Group B along with Lebanon, Afghanistan and Vietnam. The 2026 AFC Beach Soccer Asian Cup will be held in Phang Nga, Thailand. The group stage will run from Nov. 18 to 23, followed by the quarterfinals on Nov. 25 and semifinals on Nov. 27. The third-place play-off and final are scheduled for Nov. 28.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:20:44 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/532117/Iran-are-undisputed-kings-of-beach-soccer-AFC,2026-11-15 03:27:30
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Meta крупно оштрафовали за скрытую слежку,Meta крупно оштрафовали за скрытую слежку,"Meta крупно оштрафовали за скрытую слежку Реклама ВластиИталииоштрафовали Meta(признана вРФэкстремистской и запрещена)на 805 миллионов евро за слежку за пользователями. Об этом сообщаетANSA. Речь идет о функции «Получать подсказки из галереи» в приложении Facebook (запрещенная в России соцсеть) для Android. Она предлагала пользователям фото и видео из галереи в качестве идей для публикаций. Отмечается, что компания не запрашивала отдельное согласие на доступ к галерее, а обходилась общим согласием на работу приложения. При этом настройка доступа к фото и видео на устройстве была включена автоматически, из-за чего пользователям приходилось отключать ее вручную. Теперь Meta должна будет просить у итальянских пользователей отдельное согласие на эту функцию, объяснять, как она работает, и держать ее отключенной по умолчанию. Ранее суд","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:19:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/meta-krupno-oshtrafovali-za-skrytuyu-slezhku/,2026-11-15 03:27:35
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Украину предупредили о неприемлемом для России факте,Украину предупредили о неприемлемом для России факте,"Украину предупредили о неприемлемом для России факте Реклама Условия, которые Москва выдвигает для окончания конфликта, в целом приемлемы для Киева. Такое мнение выразил экс-помощник Леонида Кучмы Олег Соскин в эфире своегоYouTube-канала. «Самое важное для России — это нейтральный статус Украины. Это и русский лингвистический инструмент, чтобы был восстановлен. (...) Но самое главное — невступление в НАТО. Про НАТО надо уже забыть. (...) К Украине требования понятны: денацификация там, демилитаризация. В общем, там не так все смертельно», — высказался он. Соскин добавил, что факт развертывания иностранных контингентов на территории Украины для России неприемлем, отметив, что Киеву придется с этим считаться. Ранее британский военный эксперт Александр Меркурисвыразилмнение, что Зеленский может сорвать переговоры о мире с Россией, поскольку ему","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:15:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/ukrainu-predupredili-o-nepriemlemom-dlya-rossii-fakte/,2026-11-15 03:27:37
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Экс-премьер Великобритании Сунак призвал готовиться к ударам по российской Арктике. В чем Лондон видит угрозу?,Экс-премьер Великобритании Сунак призвал готовиться к ударам по российской Арктике. В чем Лондон видит угрозу?,"Экс-премьер Великобритании Сунак призвал готовиться к ударам по российской Арктике. В чем Лондон видит угрозу? Реклама Великобританиив случае вооруженного конфликта следует нанести удары по военной инфраструктуре России. К этомупризвалбывший британский премьер-министрРиши Сунакв статье для The Times. Он считает, чтоЛондонуследует сосредоточить свое внимание на Арктике, в районе базирования Северного флота Военно-морского флота (ВМФ) России. Политик назвал этот регион одним из главных источников военной угрозы для Британии. По его словам, российский президентВладимир Путиндолжен увидеть «уязвимость своих объектов перед британскими силами». В качестве аргумента Сунак привел слова британского министра обороны Уэса Стритинга о якобы усилении активности российских военно-морских сил у берегов Британии на 41 процент за год. «Последняя часть головоломки — показать русским, что в случае войны мы могли бы п","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:13:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/long-sunak/,2026-11-15 03:27:39
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Россиянам рассказали об угрозах взломов умных чайников и утюгов,Россиянам рассказали об угрозах взломов умных чайников и утюгов,"Россиянам рассказали об угрозах взломов умных чайников и утюгов Реклама Хакеры могут взламывать умные чайники, утюги и другие приборы с нагревательными элементами. Об этом рассказалТАССдиректор Аналитического центра УЦСБДмитрий Зубарев. По его словам, подобный взлом позволяет дистанционно включать приборы на максимальную мощность, что создает риск пожара. «Риск атаки хакеров на интеллектуальные системы домов существует — может использоваться множество сценариев. Например, роботы-пылесосы, смарт-телевизоры и колонки, оснащенные камерами и микрофонами, могут быть скомпрометированы для слежки за своими владельцами», — сказал Зубарев. Кроме того, добавил собеседник агентства, злоумышленники могут использовать умные домофоны, чтобы блокировать доступ жильцов или собирать данные об их передвижениях. Ранее россиян предупредили, что существуют тревожные сигнал","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:03:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/rossiyanam-rasskazali-ob-ugrozah-vzlomov-umnyh-chaynikov-i-utyugov/,2026-11-15 03:27:42
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Раскрыта связь между стрессом и старением кожи,Раскрыта связь между стрессом и старением кожи,"Раскрыта связь между стрессом и старением кожи Реклама Стресс — это полноценная физиологическая реакция, в которой участвуют нервная, эндокринная и иммунная системы, и кожа в ней участвует напрямую, ведь у нее есть собственная регуляция, поэтому она одной из первых реагирует на напряжение, сообщила косметолог по лицу и телу, эксперт в области аппаратной косметологии и инъекционных методик Ольга Макоед. В беседе с «Лентой.ру» она предупредила о связи распространенного состояния с ранним старением. «Когда мы нервничаем недолго, организм мобилизуется — и это нормально. Проблема начинается, когда стресс затягивается. Тогда постоянно включаются гормональные и воспалительные механизмы, кожа хуже восстанавливается, ее защитный барьер слабеет. Внешне это может проявляться сухостью, чувствительностью, тусклостью, замедленным заживлением и более","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:00:02 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/raskryta-svyaz-mezhdu-stressom-i-stareniem-kozhi/,2026-11-15 03:27:44
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,ВС России сорвали массированную атаку беспилотников ВСУ,ВС России сорвали массированную атаку беспилотников ВСУ,"ВС России сорвали массированную атаку беспилотников ВСУ Реклама Группы воздушного прикрытия группировки войск «Восток» сорвали массированную атаку беспилотных летательных аппаратов (БПЛА)Вооруженных силУкраины(ВСУ) в Запорожской области. Об этом пишетРИА Новостисо ссылкой наМинистерство обороны России. Отмечается, что в ходе отражения атаки уничтожено свыше 50 беспилотников самолетного типа, в том числе ударные БПЛА «Дартс», «Дартс-2», «Батон», а также разведывательные аппараты «Флай Ай», «Шарк» и «Вектор». В оборонном ведомстве подчеркнули, что уничтожение дронов ВСУ позволило обеспечить защиту передовых подразделений группировки «Восток» в регионе. Ранее подполковник Народной милиции Луганской Народной Республики в отставкеАндрей Марочкорассказал, что подразделения ВСУ бежали на запад со своих позиций южнее Василькового Запорожской области. П","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:53:17 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/vs-rossii-sorvali-massirovannuyu-ataku-bespilotnikov-vsu/,2026-11-15 03:27:45
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Назван рычаг давления США на Зеленского,Назван рычаг давления США на Зеленского,"Назван рычаг давления США на Зеленского Реклама СШАиспользуют операцию Национального антикоррупционного бюроУкраины(НАБУ) «Карфаген» как рычаг давления наВладимира Зеленского. Такое мнение высказал бывший подполковникСлужбы безопасности Украины(СБУ)Василий Прозоровв беседе сРИА Новости. Он отметил, что фигурантами дела стали сотрудники СБУ, которая, по его словам, сейчас является единственным весомым козырем Зеленского для влияния на внутриполитическую ситуацию в стране, поскольку только она подчиняется ему напрямую. Кроме того, как указал Прозоров, назначенный глава службаАлександр Покладявляется доверенным лицом украинского политика. Исходя из этого, НАБУ, оказывая давление на руководство СБУ, наносит удар по Зеленскому, считает он. «Я думаю, Зеленский стал позволять себе очень много лишнего в общении с американской администра","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:34:47 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/nazvan-rychag-davleniya-ssha-na-zelenskogo/,2026-11-15 03:27:47
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Названо неприятное последствие употребления сахарозаменителей,Названо неприятное последствие употребления сахарозаменителей,"Названо неприятное последствие употребления сахарозаменителей Реклама Сахарозаменители могут вызывать боли в животе. Об этом неприятном последствии в разговоре с RTпредупредилаврач-гастроэнтеролог клиники «Атрибьют»Мария Шаманская. Специалист пояснила, что чаще всего симптомы вызывает не сам «заменитель сахара», а сахарные спирты: ксилит, сорбит, маннит, мальтит и эритрит, которые нередко можно найти в жвачке, конфетах и напитках с надписью «без сахара». «Сахарные спирты плохо всасываются в тонкой кишке и частично ферментируются бактериями в толстой кишке. Отсюда могут появиться вздутие, урчание, метеоризм, послабление стула, спазмы или дискомфорт в животе», — добавила Шаманская, отметив, что чем больше доза, тем выше возможность появления симптомов. Помимо этого, указала врач, у людей с синдромом раздраженного кишечника переносимость обычно ниже, и ","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:20:53 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/nazvano-nepriyatnoe-posledstvie-upotrebleniya-saharozameniteley/,2026-11-15 03:27:49
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,ВСУ столкнулись с проблемой на фоне российских ударов,ВСУ столкнулись с проблемой на фоне российских ударов,"ВСУ столкнулись с проблемой на фоне российских ударов Реклама Вооруженные силыУкраины(ВСУ) испытывают большие проблемы с логистикой, включая эвакуацию раненых на ряде направлений на фоне российских ударов. Об этомТАССзаявил военный экспертВиталий Киселев. Он указал, что главные направления, на которых у противника наблюдается нарушение логистики и эвакуации, — донецкое, луганское, а также часть харьковского. Военный эксперт отметил, что на данных направлениях Вооруженные силы (ВС)РФсконцентрировали большое число операторов беспилотных летательных аппаратов (БПЛА). Ранее подполковник Народной милиции Луганской Народной Республики в отставкеАндрей Марочкорассказал, что командование ВСУ от безысходности отправляет необученных солдат тыловых служб для участия в штурмах уСлавянскаиКраматорска. По его словам, военных направляют на самые сложные для","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:12:56 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/vsu-stolknulis-s-problemami-na-fone-rossiyskih-udarov/,2026-11-15 03:27:51
