Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,В Киеве произошел взрыв,В Киеве произошел взрыв,"В Киеве произошел взрыв Реклама Взрыв раздался в украинской столице на фоне воздушной тревоги. Об этом 15 ноября пишет издание «Общественное» вTelegram-канале. Согласно информации, представленной на онлайн-карте Министерства цифровой трансформации Украины, сирена воздушной тревогизвучитв Киеве с 2:18 воскресенья по московскому времени. Ранее Вооруженные силы (ВС) Россииперерезалитрассу Харьков — Киев. Уточняется, что на участке перед Яготином возник сильный пожар. Горят автомобили, движение по автомагистрали парализовано.","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:02:24 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/v-kieve-progremel-vzryv/,2026-11-15 03:28:17
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,В Кремле ответили на вопрос о контактах с переговорщиками от ЕС,В Кремле ответили на вопрос о контактах с переговорщиками от ЕС,"В Кремле ответили на вопрос о контактах с переговорщиками от ЕС Реклама Переговорщики от Европы пока не выходили на контакт с Россией. Об этомТАССсообщил официальный представитель КремляДмитрий Песков. Ранее стало известно, что страныЕвросоюза(ЕС)согласовалиделегацию для участия в переговорах с Россией по урегулированию конфликта наУкраине. В нее войдут представителиЕврокомиссии,Совета ЕС,Германии,Франции,ИталиииПольши, а такжеВеликобритании. При этом, какотмечаетPolitico, европейские лидеры хотели найти «супергероя-переговорщика», который мог бы вести диалог с Россией иСШАот лица всего объединения, но безуспешно.","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:52:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/v-kremle-otvetili-na-vopros-o-kontaktah-s-peregovorschikami-ot-es/,2026-11-15 03:28:19
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,В Москве средняя пенсия за пять лет выросла почти на 60 процентов,В Москве средняя пенсия за пять лет выросла почти на 60 процентов,"В Москве средняя пенсия за пять лет выросла почти на 60 процентов Реклама Средний размер пенсии вМосквеза пять лет выросла почти на 60 процентов. Об этом сообщаетРИА Новостисо ссылкой на данные статистики. По состоянию на 1 октября 2026 года средний размер выплат в столице составил 27 309 рублей. При этом отмечается, что в октябре 2021 года пенсионерам начисляли 17 075 рублей. Таким образом, за пять лет средняя пенсия москвичей увеличилась на 10 234 рубля. Ранее сообщалось, что в 2027 году россиянампроиндексируютвсе виды пенсий, а страховые — дважды, в феврале и апреле. Повысят минимум, на который могут рассчитывать все получатели этих выплат. Минимальный размер пенсии должен увеличиться примерно на 6,8 процента в 2027 году.","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:44:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/v-moskve-srednyaya-pensiya-za-pyat-let-vyrosla-pochti-na-60-protsentov/,2026-11-15 03:28:21
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Стивен Кинг сообщил о прибытии пришельцев на Землю,Стивен Кинг сообщил о прибытии пришельцев на Землю,"Стивен Кинг сообщил о прибытии пришельцев на Землю Реклама Американский писательСтивен Кингсвязал авиаколлапс вСШАс прибытием пришельцев на Землю. Он пошутил об этом на своей странице в соцсетиX. «Инопланетяне высадились. Это настоящая причина остановки рейсов», — написал Кинг. Писатель пояснил, что правительство скрывает эту информацию, поскольку не хочет спровоцировать всеобщую панику. Ранее Федеральное управление гражданской авиации США (FAA)объявилооб ограничениях на взлет и посадку во всех аэропортах страны. Отмечается, что меры были введены из-за «чрезвычайных обстоятельств» и «соображений безопасности». Позднее министр транспорта США Шон Даффисообщил, что причиной масштабного сбоя авиасообщения в США были неполадки в работе оборудования.","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:41:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/stiven-king-soobschil-o-pribytii-prisheltsev-na-zemlyu/,2026-11-15 03:28:24
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Два танкера подорвались на минах в Ормузском проливе,Два танкера подорвались на минах в Ормузском проливе,"Два танкера подорвались на минах в Ормузском проливе Реклама Два танкера подорвались на минах при попытке пройти через Ормузский пролив. Об этомсообщилКорпус стражей исламской революции (КСИР) в своем Telegram-канале. После этого на судах начались пожары. Информации о пострадавших не поступало. Иранское новостное агентство Mehr выяснило, что четыре танкеры пытались пройти по «несанкционированному маршруту». Для маскировки на них были отключены системы навигации и автоматической идентификации (АИС). Два оставшихся судна прислушались к предупреждениям центра управления движением ВМС КСИР в Ормузском проливе и развернулись обратно в сторону акватории Персидского залива. РанееИранвыдвинулультиматумСША. Секретарь Высшего совета национальной безопасности Ирана Мохсен Резаи заявил, что Ормузский пролив не будет открыт до выполнения выдвинутыхТегера","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:23:07 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/dva-tankera-podorvalis-na-minah-v-ormuzskom-prolive/,2026-11-15 03:28:26
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Раскрыта причина остановки колеса обозрения в Казани,Раскрыта причина остановки колеса обозрения в Казани,"Раскрыта причина остановки колеса обозрения в Казани Реклама Выгорание тормозного выпрямителя стало причиной остановки колеса обозрения вКазани. Такую причину назвало МЧСТатарстанав мессенджереMax. «Предварительная причина происшествия — выгорание тормозного выпрямителя, обеспечивающего работу мотор-редукторов, в результате чего произошла блокировка колеса обозрения», — говорится в сообщении. В ведомстве отметили, что в общей сложности на высоте застряли 27 человек. К настоящему моменту все находившиеся посетители аттракциона эвакуированы, среди них 17 взрослых и 10 детей. Инцидентпроизошелна улице Фатыха Амирхана вечером 14 ноября.","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:07:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/raskryta-prichina-ostanovki-kolesa-obozreniya-v-kazani/,2026-11-15 03:28:28
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Украину предупредили об ответе после ударов по России,Украину предупредили об ответе после ударов по России,"Украину предупредили об ответе после ударов по России Реклама Россия ответит на атакиУкраиныударами по ее дата-центрам, мостам и логистике. Об этомсообщилзаслуженный военный летчикРФ, генерал-майорВладимир Поповв разговоре с Aif.ru. Также, добавил он, российские военные продолжат наносить удары по энергогенерирующим станциям, подстанциям, трансформаторным, распределительным центрам и линиям электропередачи (ЛЭП). Как уточнил Попов, целями станут объекты, связанные с украинскими вооруженными силами. «Мы работаем планово: как только появляются разведданные, это могут агентурные сведения, о том, что где-то сосредотачиваются войсковые компоненты резерваВСУ, ведется подготовка к контрудару, где-то производственные мощности продолжают или начинают работать, создавая, ремонтируя боевую технику или собирая беспилотники, или завезли натовское вооружен","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:49:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/ukrainu-predupredili-ob-otvete-posle-udarov-po-rossii/,2026-11-15 03:28:30
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,В США поставили Украину перед фактом об исходе СВО,В США поставили Украину перед фактом об исходе СВО,"В США поставили Украину перед фактом об исходе СВО Реклама Украинапотеряет территории на востоке при любом исходе спецоперации (СВО). Факт об исходе конфликтаозвучилбывший аналитикЦРУЛарри Джонсон. «Либо Украина признает, что продолжать конфликт невозможно, и пойдет на переговоры, либо... В общем, нет такого сценария, при котором Россия отказалась бы от территорий, которые она сейчас занимает», — сказал он. Эксперт также выразил уверенность в том, чтоМоскване будет отзывать свои претензии на те земли, которые «пока не контролирует полностью». Ранее президент УкраиныВладимир Зеленскийнамекнул, что ограничения в работе Starlink могут означать фактическое признаниеСШАновых российских регионов. Он также отметил, чтоКиевникогда не признает эти территории за Россией.","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:40:56 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/v-ssha-postavili-ukrainu-pered-faktom-ob-ishode-svo/,2026-11-15 03:28:32
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Названы подводные камни в переговорах Европы и России,Названы подводные камни в переговорах Европы и России,"Названы подводные камни в переговорах Европы и России Реклама Европейский союз(ЕС) направит на переговоры с Россией по урегулированию конфликта наУкраиненесколько представителей, что осложнит принятие решений. Об этом пишетпишетKP.RU. Как подчеркивается в статье, представители институтов объединения не вправе участвовать в переговорах о европейской архитектуре безопасности, поскольку этот вопрос не относится к компетенции ЕС. В свою очередь, переговорщики отГермании,Польши,Франции,ВеликобританиииИталиине смогут отстаивать свою позицию в вопросах санкций ЕС и вступления Украины в союз, а также обещать ввод войск от лица Европы. «То есть, налицо ситуация, когда вместо единой и согласованной позиции Европы на переговорах будут сразу несколько представителей, у каждого из которых в голове имеются свои, сугубо индивидуальные ""тараканы""», — резюмир","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:31:27 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/nazvany-podvodnye-kamni-v-peregovorah-evropy-i-rossii/,2026-11-15 03:28:34
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Экс-премьер Британии призвал нанести удары по России и назвал цель,Экс-премьер Британии призвал нанести удары по России и назвал цель,"Экс-премьер Британии призвал нанести удары по России и назвал цель Реклама Великобританииследует нанести удары по военной инфраструктуре России. К этому призвал бывший британский премьер-министрРиши Сунакв статье дляThe Times. Он считает, чтоЛондонуследует сосредоточить свое внимание на Арктике, а именно на Кольском полуострове, где базируется Северный флот России. Политик назвал этот регион одним из главных источников военной угрозы для Британии. По его словам, российский президентВладимир Путиндолжен увидеть «уязвимость своих объектов перед британскими силами». В качестве аргумента Сунак привел слова британского министра обороны об усилении активности российских военно-морских сил у берегов Британии на 41 процент за год. Ранее начальник Штаба обороны Вооруженных сил Британии Ричард Найтонзаявило намерении Северной Европы подписать соглашение по антиросс","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:19:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/eks-premier-britanii-prizval-usilit-udary-po-rossii/,2026-11-15 03:28:36
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Россиянам дали советы по правильному питанию осенью,Россиянам дали советы по правильному питанию осенью,"Россиянам дали советы по правильному питанию осенью Реклама Гастроэнтеролог, врач-эксперт лаборатории «Гемотест»Екатерина Кашухрассказала об особенностях правильного питания осенью. Слова специалистаприводитRT. Кашух отметила, что в осенний период потребность в энергии может возрасти, поскольку организму необходимо согреваться. Следует поддерживать стабильный уровень белка — его можно получать из нежирного мяса, рыбы, яиц и бобовых. Тягу к жирной еде врач связала с нехваткой витамина D, однако злоупотреблять такой пищей не стоит, особенно при заболеваниях ЖКТ и ожирении. Салаты стоит заправлять маслами холодного отжима. В осенний рацион нужно включать сезонные овощи и фрукты, например, тыкву, капусту, морковь, яблоки, груши. Гастроэнтеролог напомнила, что клетчатка поддерживает микрофлору кишечника, состояние которой напрямую связано с общи","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:14:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/rossiyanam-dali-sovety-po-pravilnomu-pitaniyu-osenyu/,2026-11-15 03:28:38
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,"«Издевалась и поплатилась». Москвич зарезал бывшую подругу, выложил фото с места преступления и отправился в стрелковый клуб","«Издевалась и поплатилась». Москвич зарезал бывшую подругу, выложил фото с места преступления и отправился в стрелковый клуб","«Издевалась и поплатилась». Москвич зарезал бывшую подругу, выложил фото с места преступления и отправился в стрелковый клуб Реклама ВМосквеместный житель жестоко расправился со своей бывшей подругой на Сельскохозяйственной улице на северо-востоке столицы. Об этомсообщаетTelegram-канал Shot. 38-летний Дмитрий З. нанес 28-летней Анастасии Д. несколько ударов ножом в область шеи. Травмы оказались смертельными. Мотивом жестокого убийства девушки стала ревность. После того, как злоумышленник нанес жертве несколько ножевых ранений в шею, онопубликовалв ее соцсетях пост с фотографией с места преступления. В подписи к снимку он обвинил девушку в издевательствах и заявил, что она «поплатилась» за это. Выяснилось, что убийца и жертва работали в бьюти-сфере: Дмитрий был мастером лазерной эпиляции, а Анастасия — косметологом-эстетистом. В последнее время девушка перешла на работу фитнес-тренером и посвящала много времени с","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:57:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/long-revnost/,2026-11-15 03:28:40
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Российские военные атаковали трассу «Киев — Харьков»,Российские военные атаковали трассу «Киев — Харьков»,"Российские военные атаковали трассу «Киев — Харьков» Реклама Вооруженные силы (ВС) России перерезали трассуХарьков—Киев. Об этом сообщаетTelegram-канал «Операция Z: Военкоры Русской Весны» (RusVesna). Уточняется, что на участке перед Яготином возник сильный пожар. «Горят автомобили, движение по автомагистрали парализовано», — говорится в сообщении. Ранее российские войскаударилипо расположенному в Киеве заводу «Генератор» — предприятию ракетно-космической промышленности, где производятся беспилотники средней дальности Hornet. Кроме того, вгороде Яготиннанесен удар по предприятию «Стеллар Джет», задействованному в создании твердотопливных ускорителей для дронов. ТакжеВСРФатаковали электроподстанции вЖитомиреи направлявшийся вОдессусухогруз с имуществом дляВооруженных силУкраины(ВСУ).","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:50:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/rossiyskie-voennye-atakovali-trassu-kiev-harkov/,2026-11-15 03:28:42
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Военкор сообщил об атаке «Гераней» на Украину,Военкор сообщил об атаке «Гераней» на Украину,"Военкор сообщил об атаке «Гераней» на Украину Реклама Российские реактивные дроны-камикадзе семейства «Герань» атаковалиИвано-Франковскна западеУкраины. Об этомсообщаетвоенкорЮрий Котенокв своем Telegram-канале. По его информации, в городе прогремела серия взрывов. Какие объекты попали под удар, пока неизвестно. Ранее советник президента Украины по оборонным технологиям Сергей Бескрестноврассказало новой тактике «Гераней». По его словам, дроны появляются «из ниоткуда» и атакуют цели бесшумно. Как пояснил Бескрестнов, реактивный мотор обеспечивает достаточный разгон и инерцию для завершения атаки в тишине.","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:38:43 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/voenkor-soobschil-ob-atake-geraney-na-ukrainu/,2026-11-15 03:28:44
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,На Западе рассказали об «отрезвляющем моменте» для Зеленского,На Западе рассказали об «отрезвляющем моменте» для Зеленского,"На Западе рассказали об «отрезвляющем моменте» для Зеленского Реклама Владимир Зеленскийне заинтересован в урегулировании конфликта наУкраине, так как его мотивация к миру «абсолютно нулевая». Об этом в комментарии aif.ruрассказалирландский журналист Чей Боуз. Он утверждает, что политик оказался в ситуации, когда мир означал бы для него личную катастрофу. Он также высказался об ослабевании поддержки Украины в Европе. С каждым годом все больше европейских политиков высказывается против финансированияКиева, отметил Боуз. «Сейчас очень отрезвляющий момент для Зеленского. Это проверка реальностью, которая ему не понравилась. И конечно, он проводит больше времени за пределами страны, которая разваливается на части», — указал журналист. Ранее председатель комиссии ОПРФпо поддержке соотечественников и развитию общественной дипломатииВладимир Роговзаявил, чт","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:35:50 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/na-zapade-rasskazali-ob-otrezvlyayuschem-momente-dlya-zelenskogo/,2026-11-15 03:28:46
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Макрон пригрозил критикам помощи Украине «новой войной»,Макрон пригрозил критикам помощи Украине «новой войной»,"Макрон пригрозил критикам помощи Украине «новой войной» Реклама ПрезидентФранцииЭммануэль Макронрезко высказался о критиках помощиУкраине, пригрозив им «новой войной». Об этом он написал на своей странице в соцсетиХ. «Те, кто хотят ограничить ресурсы Украины, в сущности, стремятся сделать ее уязвимой, а вместе с тем и всю Европу. Это дух поражения. Это рецепт для новой войны. Франция не может разделять такую позицию», — сказал он. По его словам, у Европы сейчас есть два приоритета: помочь Украине «пережить зиму» и вместе сКиевомдостичь «справедливого и прочного мира». Он отметил, что мир, который может быть достигнут в случае прекращения помощи Украине, будет «несправедливым». Ранее МакронпризвалЕвропу определить свои приоритеты на период после завершения конфликта на Украине и донести их до России.","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:24:08 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/makron-prigrozil-kritikam-pomoschi-ukraine-novoy-voynoy/,2026-11-15 03:28:48
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Спецпосланник Трампа объяснил требование включить Европу в переговоры по Украине,Спецпосланник Трампа объяснил требование включить Европу в переговоры по Украине,"Спецпосланник Трампа объяснил требование включить Европу в переговоры по Украине Реклама Европа должна участвовать в переговорах по Украине, потому что НАТО является важной частью европейской безопасности. Об этомзаявилспецпосланник президента США Джаред Кушнер в соцсети Х. «НАТО останется важной опорой европейской безопасности... Именно поэтому мы работаем над тем, чтобы напрямую вовлечь наших европейских партнеров в эти обсуждения», — объяснил он. Кушнер подчеркнул, что любое окончательное соглашение должны одобрить заинтересованные стороны. 12 ноября президент России Владимир Путин встретился со спецпосланником США Стивом Уиткоффом и Кушнером. Стороны обсудили итоги недавних переговоров России, США и Украины в Абу-Даби, гуманитарные вопросы, а также перспективы урегулирования конфликта на Украине. По итогам встречи Уиткоффсообщило согласовании нового раунда перегово","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:11:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/spetsposlannik-trampa-ob-yasnil-trebovanie-vklyuchit-evropu-v-peregovory-po-ukraine/,2026-11-15 03:28:50
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Некрологи бойцов ВСУ начали появляться после операции «Медвежий угол»,Некрологи бойцов ВСУ начали появляться после операции «Медвежий угол»,"Некрологи бойцов ВСУ начали появляться после операции «Медвежий угол» Реклама Некрологи бойцовВооруженных силУкраины(ВСУ) стали появляться после операции «Медвежий угол». Об этомРИА Новостив рассказали в российских силовых структурах. «Начинают всплывать некрологи и посты о поиске пропавших без вести украинских военнослужащих, уничтоженных в районе проведения операции ""Медвежий угол""», сообщил собеседник агентства. По словам представителя силовых структур, масштабные потери понес первый пограничный отряд Государственной пограничной службы Украины. РанееМинистерство обороны РФсообщило, что в ходе операции «Медвежий угол» Вооруженные силы (ВС) России с 1 сентябрявзялипод контроль 28 населенных пунктов и уничтожили 1810 бойцов ВСУ.","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:08:43 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/14/nekrologi-boytsov-vsu-nachali-poyavlyatsya-posle-operatsii-medvezhiy-ugol/,2026-11-15 03:28:52
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,15 ноября: какой праздник отмечают в России и мире,15 ноября: какой праздник отмечают в России и мире,"15 ноября: какой праздник отмечают в России и мире 15 ноября в России отмечают Всероссийский день призывника. Православные христиане вспоминают образ Шуйской-Смоленской иконы Божией Матери. «Лента.ру» рассказывает, какие еще праздники отмечают 15 ноября в России и мире, а также напоминает, кто из знаменитостей родился в этот день. Реклама 15 ноября в России отмечают Всероссийский день призывника, а в мире — День борьбы против хронической обструктивной болезни легких. Православные вспоминают образ Шуйской-Смоленской иконы Божией Матери. «Лента.ру» рассказывает, какие еще праздники отмечают 15 ноября в России и мире, а также напоминает, кто из знаменитостей родился в этот день. В 1992 году президент РФБорис Ельцинустановилэтот праздник, чтобы повысить общегосударственную значимость и престиж воинской службы, а также улучшить военно-патриотическое воспитание молодежи. В России с 2024 года в армиюпризываютмужчин от 18 до 30 лет, которым присвоены категории здоровья A или Б. Призыв проходиткруглый год, а отправляются служить новобранцы дважды в год: весной — с 1 апреля по 15 июля и осенью — с 1 октября по 31 декабря. 15 ","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:05:06 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/15/15-noyabrya-kakoy-prazdnik-otmechayut-v-rossii-i-mire/,2026-11-15 03:28:54
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Жительница Константиновки рассказала о запрете Киева эвакуировать людей,Жительница Константиновки рассказала о запрете Киева эвакуировать людей,"Жительница Константиновки рассказала о запрете Киева эвакуировать людей Реклама Украинским волонтерам запретили эвакуировать мирных жителей из Константиновки в Донецкой народной республике (ДНР) в январе 2025 года. Об этом сообщилаРИА Новостиэвакуированная из города Светлана Землянская. «То есть, если вы остались в Константиновке, вы - расходный материал, и сами виноваты», — отметила она. Собеседница агентства добавила, что некоторые люди какое-то время пытались сами выходить из города, однако организованной эвакуации не было. Об освобождении города Константиновка в Донецкой народной республикестало известнов начале июля. Сообщалось, что российские бойцы заходили в населенный пункт с манекенами в камуфляже. Трюк был отвлекающим маневром с целью выматывания артиллерииВооруженных силУкраиныи выявления их огневых точек, который способствовал продвижению российски","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:05:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/11/14/zhitelnitsa-konstantinovki-rasskazala-o-zaprete-kieva-evakuirovat-lyudey/,2026-11-15 03:28:56
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US threatening to starve Iranians – Tehran,US threatening to starve Iranians – Tehran,"US threatening to starve Iranians – Tehran <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af8ffb385f5401f51422bea.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Iran has accused the US of using sanctions and a naval blockade to starve its population <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648848-us-threatening-to-starve-iranians/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Iranian Foreign Ministry spokesman Esmaeil Baghaei has accused the US of threatening to starve his country’s population through sanctions and a naval blockade. Speaking after a G7 foreign ministers’ meeting in Paris on Tuesday, US Secretary of State Marco Rubio described the“economic pain”inflicted on Tehran as“extraordinary,”warning that the impact of the restrictions would intensify over time. He argued that mounting hardship could force Tehran’s leadership to make concessions, as“eventually you have to eat.” “This is yet another admission that Washington is pursuing war crimes, compounding the atrocities it has already committed in its wars of aggression and economic terrorism against Iran,”Baghaei wrote on X on Saturday. “After decades of failed coercion, threats, sanctions, terrorism, and aggression, the United States continues to repeat the same mistakes, merely repackaging them under new names,”he added. The US began blockading Iran’s southern ports in April after Tehran closed the Strait of Hormuz, a vital oil and LNG shipping route, in response to the US-Israeli bombing campaign launched on February 28. In August, the US launched Operation Economic Outcast, with Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent threatening the“economic asphyxiation”of Iran through sweeping sanctions targeting Iranian businesses and their foreign partners. Iran has also accused the US of striking civilian water infrastructure, including desalination facilities and drinking-water reservoirs, disrupting","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:12:04 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648848-us-threatening-to-starve-iranians/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:01
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Israeli settlers accused of torching Palestinian village scrapyard (VIDEOS),Israeli settlers accused of torching Palestinian village scrapyard (VIDEOS),"Israeli settlers accused of torching Palestinian village scrapyard (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af8f83685f5405f2674bb72.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Israeli settlers allegedly set fire to a scrapyard in the occupied West Bank, destroying over 100 vehicles <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648847-israeli-settlers-accused-burned-scrapyard/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> No arrests have been reported after Israeli settlers allegedly set fire to a vehicle scrapyard in the Palestinian village of al-Lubban ash-Sharqiya in the occupied West Bank on Wednesday, destroying more than 100 vehicles. According to Palestinian officials, the blaze also destroyed 10 cars parked outside nearby homes, a repair workshop, storage facilities, and dozens of streetlight poles and olive trees. The damage was estimated at more than 1 million shekels ($315,000), WAFA reported. Al-Lubban ash-Sharqiya, a village south of Nablus, is surrounded by the Israeli settlements of Eli and Ma’ale Levona. The UN considers Israeli settlements illegal under international law and an obstacle to establishing an independent Palestinian state. The Israeli military said troops had been dispatched to the village following reports of arson and were searching for suspects. It added that police and forensic investigators would enter the village to collect evidence once the fire was extinguished. 🚨مشاهد من إحراق المستوطنين موقف للسيارات في اللبن الشرقية جنوب نابلس #فلسطين #اسرائیل https://t.co/Gvajjc6s6h Settler violence has surged since the Israel-Hamas war in Gaza broke out in October 2023. On Wednesday, Israeli police arrested four settlers, including two teenagers, over a September 29 riot in the West Bank village of Jalud. The suspects allegedly tried to prevent Israeli troops from allowing a displaced Palestinian family to return to their home. RT’s Charlotte Dubenskij reports","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:10:28 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648847-israeli-settlers-accused-burned-scrapyard/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:02
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,SpaceX catches Starship spacecraft with giant mechanical arms (VIDEO),SpaceX catches Starship spacecraft with giant mechanical arms (VIDEO),"SpaceX catches Starship spacecraft with giant mechanical arms (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af8e17e20302754f3244313.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> SpaceX has successfully caught its Starship spacecraft returning from orbit using giant mechanical arms <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648846-spacex-spacecraft-chopsticks-catch/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> SpaceX has successfully caught its Starship spacecraft returning from orbit, using giant mechanical arms to capture the vehicle in midair at its launch site in Texas. The historic maneuver took place on Saturday afternoon, after the spacecraft completed 14 orbits of Earth during a mission lasting more than 22 hours. It marked the first time SpaceX had recovered a Starship spacecraft from orbit. The 124-meter Starship, the world’s largest and most powerful rocket, launched from the company’s Starbase facility in southern Texas on Friday. Its upper stage successfully reached orbit and deployed 26 next-generation Starlink satellites. The mission suffered an early setback when the Super Heavy first-stage booster failed to return to the launch tower. SpaceX aborted the planned catch after the booster deviated from its intended trajectory, diverting it toward the Gulf of Mexico, where it exploded. After completing its journey, the spacecraft reentered Earth’s atmosphere and descended toward Starbase. It then flipped upright and was captured by two enormous mechanical arms, nicknamed“chopsticks,”mounted on the launch tower. They did it! SpaceX has just caught their Starship rocket for the first time ever, marking the first recovery of a conventional orbital rocket upper stage in history! This is one of the greatest engineering achievements in history. Congrats to the entire @SpaceX team! 🚀 https://t.co/9KAzAcd3e8 The recovery marks a major step toward SpaceX’s goal of making both st","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:33:00 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648846-spacex-spacecraft-chopsticks-catch/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:03
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Poland and Bulgaria put brakes on Ukraine weapons funding,Poland and Bulgaria put brakes on Ukraine weapons funding,"Poland and Bulgaria put brakes on Ukraine weapons funding <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af88ed92030272cf729ca24.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Poland has refused more funding for US weapons for Ukraine, and Bulgaria has rejected an additional €70 billion aid demand <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648838-poland-bulgaria-put-brakes-ukraine-weapons-funding/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Poland has refused to bankroll further purchases of US-made weapons for Ukraine, citing its own military spending and budget deficit. Fellow NATO member Bulgaria has also refused to take part in a €70 billion European aid package and says it will no longer supply weapons and ammunition from its stockpiles. Prime Minister Donald Tusk said on Friday he notified the NATO secretary-general that Poland“will not be contributing any money to the PURL[Prioritized Ukraine Requirements List]project at this time… because we spend a great deal on our own armaments.”He also cited Poland’s“high deficit.” Bulgarian Prime Minister Rumen Radev also stated on Friday that his country can no longer provide financial assistance to Ukraine, citing Bulgaria’s budget deficit. “We will not provide any more weapons and ammunition from the Bulgarian Army’s stocks,”he added. Radev has also ruled out Bulgarian participation in an additional €70 billion funding package requested by Ukrainian leader Vladimir Zelensky from his EU backers. He warned that continued spending on the conflict at the expense of EU citizens is fueling social tensions and political instability across the bloc. The PURL was launched in July 2025 after US President Donald Trump refused to give Kiev a blank check,and now also includes several non-NATO contributors, with Canada, Australia, and New Zealand among them. According to a US government oversight report released this week, 27 NATO allies and partners pledged aro","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:38:26 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648838-poland-bulgaria-put-brakes-ukraine-weapons-funding/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:04
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Moscow to host international human rights forum,Moscow to host international human rights forum,"Moscow to host international human rights forum <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af8680b85f54043d6435e25.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Moscow will host an ombudsmen forum on human rights, protection of citizens abroad, and digital safety <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648837-forum-moscow-human-rights/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Representatives from 70 countries will convene in Moscow for an international ombudsmen forum to discuss human rights protection, online child safety, citizens’ rights abroad, and cooperation between national institutions. The event will run from Monday to Wednesday, drawing officials and rights advocates from countries including Brazil, Mexico, Türkiye, Indonesia, South Africa, Switzerland, and several ex-Soviet nations. The conference is being held under the auspices of Russia’s human rights commissioner, Yana Lantratova. “The focus is on developing international cooperation, finding common approaches and effective mechanisms to help people in the most difficult circumstances,”she said.“It is important that a person can count on support regardless of which country they are in.” The first day will be dedicated to discussing harmful online content and protecting children in the digital sphere. The next day will revolve around protection of citizens overseas, freedom of conscience, cultural identity, sovereign development, and support for trafficking victims. Participants also plan to adopt the“Moscow Principles,”a declaration intended to reinforce the independence of human rights institutions and keep channels open even when governments clash. Apart from foreign officials, the forum’s expected speakers include RT editor-in-chief Margarita Simonyan, former UN weapons inspector Scott Ritter, and former British MP George Galloway. Lantratova recently came into the spotlight afte","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:44:36 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648837-forum-moscow-human-rights/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:05
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,OpenAI security chiefs discuss Ukraine military ties with Russian pranksters (VIDEO),OpenAI security chiefs discuss Ukraine military ties with Russian pranksters (VIDEO),"OpenAI security chiefs discuss Ukraine military ties with Russian pranksters (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af83dc12030271d2f649d73.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Russian pranksters posing as a Ukrainian official have tricked OpenAI’s Pentagon veterans into discussing AI plans for Kiev <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648832-russian-pranksters-openai-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Three senior OpenAI national security officials, including two former Pentagon insiders, have been duped by Russian pranksters into discussing sensitive details of the company’s AI cooperation with Ukraine, including potential military applications. The pranksters,Vovan and Lexus, whose real names are Vladimir Kuznetsov and Alexey Stolyarov, are known for impersonating officials to draw high-profile figures into private conversations. Their previoustargetsinclude Emmanuel Macron, Angela Merkel, Giorgia Meloni, and Henry Kissinger. The duo also host a podcast about their pranks. This time, they posed as Rustem Umerov, Ukraine’s foreign intelligence chief, securing a 17-minute video call with Sasha Baker, OpenAI’s head of global national security policy and former US deputy undersecretary of defense; Caroline Zier, a former adviser to Defense Secretary Lloyd Austin; and Ben Crampton, the company’s national security lead for Europe. Despite their security credentials, the officials apparently failed to detect the impersonation. Baker and Zier greeted the supposed Umerov like a familiar contact, even though his camera remained off. The discussion centered on OpenAI’s ties with Kiev. The company had publicly announced in September that it would provide Ukraine with its cybersecurity tools to protect civilian infrastructure. The prank call, however, revealed how readily its national security officials discussed expanding that cooperation to potential milit","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:20:42 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648832-russian-pranksters-openai-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:06
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,‘Let them play’: Fans push back against Russia’s hockey ban,‘Let them play’: Fans push back against Russia’s hockey ban,"‘Let them play’: Fans push back against Russia’s hockey ban <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af861a720302729a6646797.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Russia’s hockey return faces Canadian restrictions and European boycott threats, while fans question why politics should decide who plays <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648803-let-them-play-russia-hockey/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> When Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney decided to refuse visas to Russians to play in next month’s World Junior Ice Hockey Championships, he became the first elected leader to openly ignore a court ruling and international sports federation decision. In doing so, he unleashed dangerous and virulent anti-Russian forces in his own country, setting back sports diplomacy over 50 years. The week before, on October 30, the Court of Arbitration of Sport (CAS) voted to allow Russian and Belarusian teams back into international play. The International Ice Hockey Federation (IIHF) accepted the decision and a plethora of national federations in Europe reacted predictably. Eight countries, including Latvia and France, stated that they would boycott any games with Russia. Germany, the host of the 2027 IIHF World Championships, objected but accepted Russia’s return, with only Slovakia welcoming it. Sponsors of the event in Germany have either pulled out or threatened to do so. What seems to be missing in this entire ‘discussion’ is what hockey fans think. Not the ‘nafoids’ and bots online who rant and rage against all things Russian. Not the opinion of the handful of Canadian-Ukrainians who protested in Ottawa at the visit of Russian star Alexander Ovechkin’s Washington Capitals. And certainly not grandstanding by politicians and sports administrators beholden to them. The voices of actual hockey fans are being studiously ignored by the media – so too the inherent danger posed b","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:41:33 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648803-let-them-play-russia-hockey/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:07
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Ukraine aid hurts US military – Pentagon,Ukraine aid hurts US military – Pentagon,"Ukraine aid hurts US military – Pentagon <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af848bc2030272b280ec901.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Ukraine aid has forced US troops in Europe to divert funds originally intended for procuring essential military parts, a new report says <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648834-ukraine-aid-hurts-us-military/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Ukraine support is draining resources from US troops stationed in Europe and damaging their combat readiness, according to a new Pentagon inspector general report. In its report to Congress in November, the watchdog said the US Army Europe and Africa (USAREUR-AF) was forced to divert resources from US forces and longstanding operations toward supporting Kiev because of the lack of dedicated Ukraine funding in fiscal years 2025 and 2026. “These resource gaps have negatively impacted USAREUR-AF’s overall readiness, training effectiveness, and capacity to exercise operations plans,”the report states. In particular, Ukraine-related operations were consuming funds intended for routine deployments and essential spare parts for US military equipment. On top of that, some rotating US units returned to their home bases with unpaid spare-parts bills, according to the report. An earlier report for January-March said the command redirected a total of $364.6 million from other requirements to support Ukraine. The funding squeeze stemmed from failure to approve major emergency aid packages for Ukraine in 2025 and 2026 in Congress, where many Republican leaders vehemently opposed the“blank-check”policy for Ukraine. Since returning to office, US President Donald Trump has also opposed further large-scale US-funded aid packages for Ukraine, seeking instead to shift the financial burden onto Kiev’s European backers. The US has committed more than $198 billion in Ukraine aid since 2022, much of","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:43:51 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648834-ukraine-aid-hurts-us-military/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:08
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US behaving like ‘mafia boss’ in Middle East – NGO founder (VIDEO),US behaving like ‘mafia boss’ in Middle East – NGO founder (VIDEO),"US behaving like ‘mafia boss’ in Middle East – NGO founder (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af77e2b85f540407074263b.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Activist Miko Peled has accused the US of coercing Gulf states into cooperation, warning that defiance could leave their countries in ruins <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648822-us-mafia-boss-middle-east/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The US is behaving like a mafia boss in the Middle East, forcing countries to cooperate or risk being attacked, Miko Peled, founder and director of the Palestine House of Freedom, said on Friday. He was speaking in an RT panel discussion on recent remarks by US Secretary of State Marco Rubio, who blamed Iran for instability in the region. Peled said the Gulf states fear that defying Washington could leave their countries in ruins, pointing to US military interventions in recent decades. “The US operates like a mafia boss,” he said.“If you’re a leader in the region and you know that if you don’t comply, you’re going to end up like Iraq... and Libya and Syria and Yemen… your country is going to end up in ruins.” He argued that cooperating with the US offers Gulf countries a chance to maintain stability.“But that’s not a question of trust. It’s a question of survival, really.” Tehran University Professor Seyed Mohammed Marandi accused Israel of being the main source of instability in the region, citing the displacement of Palestinians and the“ongoing genocide”in Gaza. “The US has contributed to this misery for the sake of the Israeli regime. The invasion of Iraq has brought about the destruction of that country, thanks to the US,”he said. “They destroyed Afghanistan. They initiated a dirty war in Syria,”he added, citing a February 2012 email in which Jake Sullivan, then an adviser to Secretary of State Hillary Clinton, wrote that Al-Qaeda was“on our side”in Syria","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:14:35 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648822-us-mafia-boss-middle-east/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:09
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Russia’s cultural diversity takes center stage in massive dance show (VIDEO),Russia’s cultural diversity takes center stage in massive dance show (VIDEO),"Russia’s cultural diversity takes center stage in massive dance show (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af74b2820302772a6282761.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The ‘Khorovod: Energy of Unity’ show brought more than 600 performers to Moscow for a celebration of folk dance <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648791-russia-cultural-diversity-dance-show/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> More than 600 dancers have taken part in the ‘Khorovod. The Energy of Unity’ folk dance production at the National Centre ‘Russia’ in Moscow The large-scale dance production celebrated Russia’s vast cultural diversity, traditions and the shared identity of its many ethnic communities. At its core was the khorovod, a traditional Slavic circle dance that shares much in common with similar traditions around the world. “What matters is that our production goes beyond classic folk dances. We have been able to present traditional art in a contemporary way. The khorovod brings people together, and virtually every people in the world has a dance like it,”‘Russia’ National Center Deputy Director General Anastasia Zvyagina told RT. The circle dance is especially symbolic in Russia, where so many different ethnic communities live together, she added.“No one comes first or last. It is this energy of unity that allows us to build on what we have today and, of course, look ahead to the future,”she said. We have managed to preserve the culture and distinct identity of all our peoples, and we are proud of that. The show combined traditional folk dances with contemporary choreography, electronic music, beatboxing and throat singing. Performers came from Russia’s Donetsk People’s Republic, Karelia, Yakutia, Crimea, the North Caucasus and other regions. The production featured original musical pieces exploring family bonds, nature, and cultural heritage. The performances ran from Tuesd","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:10:37 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648791-russia-cultural-diversity-dance-show/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:11
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US could spy on Germany through Tesla cars – regional intelligence chief,US could spy on Germany through Tesla cars – regional intelligence chief,"US could spy on Germany through Tesla cars – regional intelligence chief <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af7967b20302711c932d622.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A regional German spy chief has warned that Tesla cars could pose an espionage risk, urging restrictions near military and government sites <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648826-tesla-us-spy-germany/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Tesla vehicles could pose an espionage risk, Stephan Kramer, the head of Germany’s domestic intelligence agency (BfV) in the state of Thuringia, has warned. His remarks come as German officials call for restrictions on parking internet-connected cars near sensitive government and military facilities. Tesla is an American company led by Elon Musk, an ally of US President Donald Trump. The electric carmaker operates a major factory near Berlin, making it one of the few foreign automakers with a significant manufacturing presence in Germany. Kramer was commenting on the German Army’s decision to restrict access by internet-connected vehicles to sensitive areas of military bases. The measures apply regardless of manufacturer, including Tesla. “We should not assume that friends do not spy on one another,”Kramer told Handelsblatt on Friday.“The same security standards should apply to Tesla and all other manufacturers.” According to the Federal Office for Information Security (BSI), Germany’s digital security watchdog, most new vehicles sold in the country have the technical capability to collect information, including location data, camera footage, and sensor readings, and transmit it to manufacturers’ back-end systems. There is no specific evidence so far that the data has been used for espionage, Handelsblatt reported. According to the BSI, customers are often unaware of what data their vehicles generate and transmit. “The cameras and location-tracking systems in","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:21:25 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648826-tesla-us-spy-germany/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:12
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"SpaceX launches world’s largest rocket, loses booster in fiery crash (VIDEOS)","SpaceX launches world’s largest rocket, loses booster in fiery crash (VIDEOS)","SpaceX launches world’s largest rocket, loses booster in fiery crash (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af7baa22030271d2f649d62.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> SpaceX launched the world’s largest rocket, deploying satellites into orbit before its Super Heavy booster crashed into the Gulf of Mexico <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648829-starship-rocket-booster-explodes/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Elon Musk’s SpaceX has launched the world’s largest and most powerful rocket, attempting to recover an entire orbital launch system for the first time in history. The 124-meter (407-foot) Starship blasted off from the company’s Starbase facility in southern Texas on Friday, carrying 26 next-generation Starlink satellites into orbit. The mission was designed to demonstrate that both stages of the giant rocket could return to the launch site and be caught by mechanical arms attached to the launch tower, allowing them to be refurbished and reused. Liftoff of Starship! https://t.co/lc7UtE6H7z However, the Super Heavy booster failed to return to the tower as planned, instead making a fiery landing in the Gulf of Mexico. SpaceX did not immediately explain the failure, although safety systems diverted the booster offshore. Starship Flight 15 Super Heavy Booster soft water landing. Landing looked so smooth. It hovered for a good amount of time. https://t.co/V9NW4O9Dv9 The Starship upper stage continued into orbit and successfully deployed its satellite payload. It is expected to circle Earth 15 times before attempting to return to Texas on Saturday, where the company plans to catch it using the tower’s giant mechanical arms. If successful, it would mark the first recovery of a Starship spacecraft from orbit. SpaceX has caught the Super Heavy booster three times, but recovering the upper stage presents a greater challenge because it must survive atmosp","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:36:33 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648829-starship-rocket-booster-explodes/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:13
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Putin, Trump, and Xi to hold rare three-way meeting in China","Putin, Trump, and Xi to hold rare three-way meeting in China","Putin, Trump, and Xi to hold rare three-way meeting in China <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af7b267203027727767838a.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The leaders of Russia, China, and the US plan to meet in Shenzhen next week, with nuclear arms control and global conflicts on the agenda <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648828-trump-putin-xi-meeting-/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The leaders of Russia, China, and the US plan to meet on Thursday on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) summit in Shenzhen, China, AP reported on Saturday, citing officials. The White House confirmed plans for the unprecedented three-way meeting on Friday, the outlet said. The talks are expected to focus on nuclear arms control and international security, including the conflicts in Ukraine and Iran. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov subsequently confirmed the meeting. Chinese President Xi Jinping will host his Russian and US counterparts, Vladimir Putin and Donald Trump, at the November 18–19 summit. Putin aide Yury Ushakov said earlier that the Russian president discussed the upcoming meeting with Trump envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner.“We hope that the first meeting in this format will have a positive impact on the overall international situation,”Ushakov said last month. The summit will follow US-mediated talks between Russian and Ukrainian delegations in Abu Dhabi on November 10-11, which marked the resumption of trilateral negotiations after a nine-month hiatus. Although the talks ended without a major breakthrough, Kushner said the sides will carry out“the largest prisoner exchange of the war.” Ukraine’s European backers are currently discussing appointing representatives to take part in talks with Russia after being sidelined in Abu Dhabi, where European delegates met separately with Ukrainian and American teams. Moscow has insisted","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:58:48 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648828-trump-putin-xi-meeting-/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:14
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Tanker rams US cruise ship, capsizing it (VIDEOS)","Tanker rams US cruise ship, capsizing it (VIDEOS)","Tanker rams US cruise ship, capsizing it (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af79b2620302772ee66c562.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A tanker rammed and capsized a docked cruise ship in New Orleans, sending it into the Mississippi River <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648827-tanker-rams-cruise-ship/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> An asphalt tanker rammed a docked cruise ship in New Orleans, Louisiana on Friday, causing it to capsize and sending passengers into the Mississippi River. Videos from the scene show the much larger Atlantic Asphalt tanker striking the American Heritage cruise ship directly in the side. The vessel, operated by American Cruise Lines, was carrying 180 passengers and crew members at the time of the collision. The cruise ship rolled onto its side and partially sank as tugboat operators, police, and other rescuers rushed to help. Watch the moment a tanker struck a cruise ship in New Orleans. Rescues are underway. 📷: Kern Studios https://t.co/ZPspGtM0Yr https://t.co/O1qGr8kImf New Orleans Mayor Helena Moreno confirmed that everyone aboard was rescued. She added that 32 people were hospitalized, none with critical injuries. “It is a literal miracle on the Mississippi,”Louisiana Governor Jeff Landry told reporters.“When you think about the population that was on that cruise ship, and the ability for us to get them off, get them out of the water.” WATCH: Dramatic video shows passengers swimming for help as cruise ship capsizes after being struck by a tanker; 12 people hospitalized, officials say. https://t.co/2UtubUdktf The cause of the collision remains under investigation. Initial reports suggest that the tanker may have lost steering before striking the docked vessel. The American Heritage is a 90-meter-long paddlewheeler built in 2015. It was completing an eight-day Mississippi Ri","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:20:59 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648827-tanker-rams-cruise-ship/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:16
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Gestapo 2.0? Germany grants spy agencies sweeping new powers,Gestapo 2.0? Germany grants spy agencies sweeping new powers,"Gestapo 2.0? Germany grants spy agencies sweeping new powers <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af786d285f54041ed2cf6cd.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Germany has passed sweeping intelligence reforms granting spy agencies powers to conduct sabotage, enter homes, and deploy AI surveillance <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648825-gemany-spy-agencies-new-powers/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The German parliament has passed sweeping legislation granting the country’s intelligence agencies unprecedented powers to conduct sabotage, secretly enter homes, and expand surveillance. The controversial law has prompted comparisons with the Gestapo and Stasi, the notorious secret police organizations of Nazi Germany and Communist East Germany. The legislation, championed by Chancellor Friedrich Merz’s governing coalition, was approved on Friday by 300 votes to 190, with 71 abstentions. Only the ruling CDU/CSU bloc and Social Democrats backed the reform. The right-wing Alternative for Germany (AfD) and The Left opposed it, while the Greens abstained. Interior Minister Alexander Dobrindt hailed the overhaul as a“reform of the century,”declaring a“new era”for German intelligence agencies that would put them on an“equal footing with our European partners.” He defended the measures by citing alleged threats from espionage, sabotage, cyberattacks, and other hostile activities aimed at destabilizing Germany. The legislation fundamentally changes the role of Germany’s two principal intelligence agencies: the foreign intelligence service (BND) and the domestic Federal Office for the Protection of the Constitution (BfV). Previously focused primarily on gathering and analyzing intelligence, both agencies will gain powers to actively intervene against perceived threats. The BND will be authorized to penetrate foreign computer networks, disable servers used by suspected h","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:38:52 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648825-gemany-spy-agencies-new-powers/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:17
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Hope in Abu Dhabi, fighting in Europe, ‘hell’ in the Persian Gulf: RT’s reporting of the week’s top news","Hope in Abu Dhabi, fighting in Europe, ‘hell’ in the Persian Gulf: RT’s reporting of the week’s top news","Hope in Abu Dhabi, fighting in Europe, ‘hell’ in the Persian Gulf: RT’s reporting of the week’s top news RT’s top stories this week included trilateral peace talks, Europe’s struggle to find a Moscow envoy, and the looming threat of war in Iran <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648809-rt-top-stories-us-russia-talks-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> To follow the headlines this week, one needed simply to follow the movements of Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner. The two American envoys arrived in Abu Dhabi on Tuesday for the fourth round of trilateral talks between Washington, Moscow, and Kiev,bringing with them a planto“create the conditions for a sovereign, secure, and prosperous Ukraine within a more stable European security environment,”according to Kushner at least. The mere mention of a broader European security architecture represents progress,Russian analyst Fyodor Lukyanov wrote for RT, pointing out that Moscow’s calls to rethink European security were previously dismissed by Washington. Although the idea is still in its infancy,the trilateral talks ended positively, with Russia and Ukraine agreeing to alarge-scale prisoner swap Conspicuous in their absence were the Europeansthemselves, who at this point had yet to decide whether they should even speak to Russian President Vladimir Putin in the first place. At ameeting with Putinin Moscow on Thursday, Witkoff and Kushner managed to secure the EU a seat at the table in the next round of discussions. However, as RT explained, ‘Europe’ is split into squabbling camps ofrealists, maximalists, and fantasists, all vying for control of the peace process. Witkoff and Kushner left Moscow for Dublin on Thursday, where Ukrainian leader Vladimir Zelensky and his European backers were meeting for the European Political Community (EPC) and EU leaders’ summits. Their arrival at B","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:42:46 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648809-rt-top-stories-us-russia-talks-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:18
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US grounds departing flights nationwide,US grounds departing flights nationwide,"US grounds departing flights nationwide <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af78a1185f540411d2a92a8.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The Federal Aviation Administration has ordered all departing flights across the US grounded until further notice <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648824-us-grounds-fligghts-nationwide/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) has ordered a rare nationwide ground stop for all departing flights across the US, citing unspecified safety concerns. The emergency directive took effect at 3:54 PM Eastern Time on Friday, with all departing aircraft instructed to remain on the ground until further notice. According to the advisory, international flights arriving in the US were handled on a case-by-case basis. The ground stop was lifted around four and a half hours later, although flight disruptions continued. Around 1,900 flights were canceled and 10,500 delayed as of 6:00 PM Eastern Time on Friday, ABC13 reported, citing flight-tracking service FlightAware. US Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said the nationwide ground stop was prompted by a“communication issue impacting all Air Route Traffic Control Centers.” “FAA technicians are investigating the issue. We will provide immediate updates as we have them,”he wrote on X. Preliminary reports suggest the disruption was not caused by a cyberattack, CNN reported, citing two law enforcement officials. Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin said the grounding was caused by a“telecommunications outage,”which the authorities do not believe was the result of foul play. Duffy later blamed the shutdown on the“incredibly old”air traffic control system. “Our switches, our routers, actually got overloaded with data... and started to give us inconsistency in the data from those routers,”he said at a news conference. The N","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:11:25 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648824-us-grounds-fligghts-nationwide/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:20
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Who wanted Nvidia’s Huang out? ‘Honeypot’ scandal raises questions over AI power struggle,Who wanted Nvidia’s Huang out? ‘Honeypot’ scandal raises questions over AI power struggle,"Who wanted Nvidia’s Huang out? ‘Honeypot’ scandal raises questions over AI power struggle <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af736d620302771573953b6.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Jensen Huang’s downfall in an alleged Chinese spy scandal fuels questions over who benefits from his exit and the US-China AI war <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648799-huang-nvidia-downfall-explainer/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The downfall of Nvidia founder Jensen Huang in a scandal involving a suspected Chinese spy has raised a politically explosive question: who benefits from the removal of one of Washington’s most influential critics of chip restrictions on China? Huang resigned on Thursday following revelations of extramarital affairs, including one with Chinese businesswoman Alice Huang, former head of Nvidia customer, Singapore-based Megaspeed International. Anonymous US intelligence officials reportedly suspect that she was recruited by Beijing to potentially influence the Nvidia CEO to push Washington to ease AI chip export restrictions. The scandal came at a pivotal moment in the US-China technology war, just days before a planned summit between Presidents Donald Trump and Xi Jinping. With congressional hawks already pushing for tougher restrictions, the timing of Huang’s downfall has fueled questions about the political interests served by his resignation. RT examines the intrigue surrounding Huang’s exit and the struggle for control of the global AI industry. Huang’s resignation removes one of Washington’s most prominent advocates of keeping China connected to American AI technology, potentially handing China hawks a major political advantage. The Nvidia founder repeatedly warned that cutting Beijing off from American technology would accelerate China’s push for independence. In a May interview with Fox Business, he pointed to Huawei’s growing influence","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:55:49 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648799-huang-nvidia-downfall-explainer/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:21
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Deadly floods swamp tens of thousands in Gaza (VIDEOS),Deadly floods swamp tens of thousands in Gaza (VIDEOS),"Deadly floods swamp tens of thousands in Gaza (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af72ef62030273899552eac.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Gaza floods killed at least four and swamped tens of thousands of tents, as the UN accuses Israel of blocking vital aid <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648812-deadly-floods-swamp-gaza/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> At least four people have been killed after heavy rain flooded camps sheltering tens of thousands in Gaza, according to UN agencies. Much of the enclave, including its sewage system, has been reduced to rubble by Israeli bombardment. Heavy rain and strong winds, which are unusually intense for early November, battered the coastal territory for several days, the UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA) said. Floodwaters swept through makeshift camps and tents, soaking mattresses, washing away belongings, and collapsing shelters. At Al Berka Reservoir, west of Deir al-Balah, a rain-soaked sandy embankment collapsed onto tents, reportedly killing five people, including three children and two women, with an infant feared drowned, according to local rescuers cited by OCHA. UNICEF, however, reported four deaths in the collapse. At least 5 people are dead and thousands more without shelter after heavy rains hit Gaza. While Israeli authorities are not responsible for the rain, they are responsible for the displacement of 1.9 million Palestinians and obstructing entry of humanitarian aid. https://t.co/sVTTpc5g7n According to Gaza’s Government Media Office, around 70,000 tents were flooded within 12 hours. The UN separately recorded more than 6,000 family shelters destroyed and 17,400 damaged. UNICEF reported that around 950,000 displaced Palestinians live in flood-exposed areas, including 400,000 at extremely high risk. The scale of the devastation is exacerbated ","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:11:51 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648812-deadly-floods-swamp-gaza/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:22
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,UK approves controversial migrant center near ‘breakaway’ village,UK approves controversial migrant center near ‘breakaway’ village,"UK approves controversial migrant center near ‘breakaway’ village <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af72c56203027371d721441.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> UK approves an asylum center for 1,256 men near Piddington, a village of just 350 residents, Sky News has reported <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648817-uk-migrant-accomodation-piddington-breakaway/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The UK government has approved controversial plans to house up to 1,256 male migrants near a tiny Oxfordshire village of around 350 residents, Sky News reported on Thursday. To protest the plans, Piddington symbolically seceded from the UK in September. Residents of the village, which had a population of just 358 in 2021, have fiercely opposed the proposed asylum center at a nearby former military site, raising concerns about its impact on their small community. Despite 285 residents voting in favor of secession in the symbolic referendum, the government has refused to cancel the plans. British Housing Secretary Angela Rayner personally approved the project on Thursday, according to Sky News. A letter from her department to the Home Office said the facility would“provide a flexible and operationally resilient”response to housing demand and reduce reliance on migrant hotels, the news outlet reported, citing the correspondence. Although the facility was intended for temporary use, Rayner assessed the project“as if it was for a permanent development,”according to Sky News. The Home Office used the Urgent Crown Development procedure, allowing ministers to decide the application instead of the local planning authority, which would normally have the power to reject such projects following objections from residents. Reform UK leader Nigel Farage blamed Prime Minister Andy Burnham’s government for the expansion of asylum accommodations, arguing that the policy endangered wom","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:45:35 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648817-uk-migrant-accomodation-piddington-breakaway/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:23
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,EU leaders prolonging Ukraine conflict to stay in power – Swiss journalist (VIDEO),EU leaders prolonging Ukraine conflict to stay in power – Swiss journalist (VIDEO),"EU leaders prolonging Ukraine conflict to stay in power – Swiss journalist (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af7154a85f540411d2a9269.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Swiss journalist Peter Hansler says European leaders are dependent on the Ukraine war and would block peace efforts if they joined talks <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648795-eu-prolonging-ukraine-retain-power/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> EU leaders want to prolong the Ukraine conflict because they stand to lose their jobs if peace is achieved, Swiss journalist and Forum Geopolitica founder Peter Hansler has told RT. During the two-day Russia-Ukraine-US talks in Abu Dhabi earlier this week, European officials held separate consultations with the US and Ukrainian delegations but were not included in the main negotiations. On Thursday, US President Donald Trump’s envoy Jared Kushner said Moscow agreed to expand the next round of negotiations to include“our European partners.” Russia has not, however, confirmed that it agreed to direct European participation. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov has accused European governments of sending mixed signals, with their calls for peace contrasting with plans to deploy troops to Ukraine in the event of a ceasefire. Moscow has consistently said it would oppose any such move. “All the leaders in Europe, they will lose their job if there is peace. So does [Ukraine’s Vladimir] Zelensky,”Hansler told RT, arguing that the involvement of European governments in negotiations would be“highly problematic.” “They will block any peace. This is my personal opinion,”the journalist added. Hansler claimed that European leaders are not interested in negotiating an end to the conflict.“They will prolong the war. That’s their interest. Because all the European leaders, they are dependent on this war,”he said. He also pointed to divisions within the EU over","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:54:10 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648795-eu-prolonging-ukraine-retain-power/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:24
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump outlines Cuba plan,Trump outlines Cuba plan,"Trump outlines Cuba plan <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af70a7985f540415017ab4c.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Trump says he would consider military action against Cuba, adding he wants to “get done” with the island before his term ends <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648804-trump-outlines-cuba-plan/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US President Donald Trump has said he wants to“get Cuba done”before leaving office in two years, adding that he is open to ordering a military operation against the island. Speaking to conservative radio host Hugh Hewitt on Thursday, Trump made clear that he“would certainly consider”a week-long campaign against Cuba, which the US has kept under a de facto blockade while openly advocating for regime change. “I want to get Cuba done before I leave. And we have a very good, talented guy for Cuba named Marco,”he said, referring to US Secretary of State Marco Rubio, whose parents emigrated from Cuba and who has been particularly critical of the government in Havana. Last month, Rubio urged Cuban dissidents seeking“positive change”to establish a“discrete partnership with the CIA.”He has also defended US sanctions, blaming Cuba’s leadership rather than the six-decade-old American embargo for the country’s worsening economic crisis. Cuban Deputy Foreign Minister Carlos Fernandez de Cossio mocked Rubio’s comments, saying“there must be a great deal of desperation or misery within the agency for it to be forced to sell its services like a tube of toothpaste.” The US escalated pressure on Cuba after the kidnapping of Venezuelan leader Nicolas Maduro in January. Washington essentially cut Cuba off from crucial Venezuelan oil, while also threatening tariffs against other countries supplying the island. The resulting fuel shortages have aggravated an already severe humanitarian crisis, brin","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:04:18 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648804-trump-outlines-cuba-plan/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:25
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Berlin’s military spending spree risks debt surge – experts,Berlin’s military spending spree risks debt surge – experts,"Berlin’s military spending spree risks debt surge – experts <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af7011a2030272af6554cc9.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> German economic advisers have warned that debt-financed military spending could push public debt to nearly 100% of GDP by 2040 <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648801-berlin-military-spending-debt-surge/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Germany’s continued military buildup, financed largely through government borrowing, could push public debt to nearly 100% of GDP by 2040, an independent government advisory body has warned, urging Berlin to promptly rein in spending. The country’s deeply ingrained cultural and political aversion to debt has been slipping under the weight of an eroding economy and rearmament program aimed at confronting the supposed threat from Russia. Germany launched a €100 billion ($122 billion) military buildup and restructuring program in the wake of the escalation of the Ukraine conflict in 2022 under then-Chancellor Olaf Scholz. His successor, Friedrich Merz, has doubled down on this policy, vowing to turn the German military into Europe’s strongest conventional force while maintaining military support for Kiev. “Public finances in Germany are coming under growing pressure. In the federal budget, projected revenue will not be sufficient to cover the planned spending in the longer term,”the German Council of Economic Experts (GCEE) warned in its annual report released on Wednesday. According to the German Taxpayers Federation, the nation’s debt burden is currently increasing by €7,052 per second, with every citizen being effectively €34,046 in debt on behalf of the state. Although a debt-to-GDP ratio of 100% is not in itself fatal – the US currently sits at just over 125%, while Japan has long been above 200% – it is a much more troubling proposition for a Eurozone country. Becaus","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:43:00 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648801-berlin-military-spending-debt-surge/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:26
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Merz echoing Goebbels with ‘guns or butter’ choice – former Spanish diplomat to RT (VIDEO),Merz echoing Goebbels with ‘guns or butter’ choice – former Spanish diplomat to RT (VIDEO),"Merz echoing Goebbels with ‘guns or butter’ choice – former Spanish diplomat to RT (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af6f452203027384271768e.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Germany’s Merz echoes Goebbels as European leaders favor military spending and Ukraine aid over domestic needs, Jose Antonio Zorrilla says <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648792-merz-goebbels-guns-butter-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> German Chancellor Friedrich Merz’s approach to military spending is comparable to the rhetoric used by Nazi propaganda chief Joseph Goebbels, former Spanish diplomat Jose Antonio Zorrilla has told RT. Earlier this week, Merz described long-term support for Ukraine as“a common European task”at a joint press conference with Hungarian Prime Minister Peter Magyar in Berlin, saying continued funding for Kiev should be reflected in the EU’s next budget. European governments have also been pushing to increase military spending, citing what they claim is a growing threat from Russia. Commenting on the remarks, Zorrilla told RT:“Well, they have a very old tradition of that in Germany. If you remember a certain Goebbels, he said something like cannons and butter […] We have to make a choice between the cannons and the butter, so I think Merz is doing more or less the same.” The reference was to a 1936 speech in which Goebbels argued that Germany could do without butter but not guns, prioritizing military rearmament over civilian needs. Zorrilla also mocked claims that Russia poses an imminent threat to Europe, asking:“Who can believe that Russia is about to invade us?”He argued that invoking the alleged threat was being used to justify militarization rather than address pressing domestic problems. The former diplomat also criticized European support for Ukraine, saying that Spain had allocated €13 billion ($14.3 billion) for Kiev last year","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:34:48 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648792-merz-goebbels-guns-butter-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:27
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Why Moscow’s Taliban outreach unnerves Pakistan,Why Moscow’s Taliban outreach unnerves Pakistan,"Why Moscow’s Taliban outreach unnerves Pakistan <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af6b29a85f5400b827c752c.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The latest Moscow Format of Afghanistan exposed widening perception gap between Moscow and Islamabad <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648782-moscow-taliban-outreach-pakistan/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> DrGleb Makarevich, Research Fellow, Centre of the Indo-Pacific Region at Primakov National Research Institute of World Economy and International Relations, Russian Academy of Sciences(IMEMO). DrGleb Makarevich, Research Fellow, Centre of the Indo-Pacific Region at Primakov National Research Institute of World Economy and International Relations, Russian Academy of Sciences(IMEMO). Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov, speaking at the Minsk International Conference on Eurasian Security last week, called the Moscow Format consultations on Afghanistan“the most representative platform for developing a region-wide consensus.” It is hard to argue with the central point of the foreign minister’s remark. The Moscow Format really is broad-based, bringing together not only Afghanistan and the Central Asian states, but also India, Iran, China, and Pakistan, as well as guest delegations such as Belarus and Egypt. Yet while few doubt the forum’s representative character, the question of whether it can actually produce a region-wide consensus is much more complicated. At its anniversary meeting last month (the format has been in place since 2016) the participants could not even agree on a joint final statement. Moscow still appears to believe that the platform remains effective. The consultations are held regularly, and there is an exchange of views. As for the communique, in the view of Russian officials, while adoption of a final document is desirable from a protocol standpoint, it is ","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:33:52 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648782-moscow-taliban-outreach-pakistan/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:28
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump envoy touts new approach to Ukraine peace talks,Trump envoy touts new approach to Ukraine peace talks,"Trump envoy touts new approach to Ukraine peace talks <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af6d3542030273842717682.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Jared Kushner reported Ukraine peace progress, adding that the sides will discuss ending the hostilities in parallel with European security <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648793-trump-envoy-new-approach-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> This week’s efforts to resolve the Ukraine conflict yielded“meaningful progress,”US President Donald Trump’s envoy and son-in-law Jared Kushner has said. He announced plans to address the Russia-Ukraine territorial dispute and wider European security order in parallel. In a statement on X on Friday, Kushner summarized three days of intensive diplomacy that began with trilateral Russia-Ukraine-US negotiations in Abu Dhabi. He and fellow Trump envoy Steve Witkoff subsequently met with Russian President Vladimir Putin in Moscow and Ukrainian leader Vladimir Zelensky in Dublin, before consulting with security advisers from Ukraine and European countries. “We have made meaningful progress in understanding both sides’ concerns, identifying possible solutions, and establishing a path forward,”Kushner wrote, while acknowledging that“significant differences remain.” He went on to say that both Russia and Ukraine“have now agreed to expand the next round of negotiations to include our European partners,”adding that the expanded format will allow discussions on“broader postwar European security arrangements alongside the territorial issues between Ukraine and Russia.” Kushner stressed that a settlement will require credible security guarantees, mechanisms to prevent renewed confrontation, and mutual commitments to de-escalation.“We will begin discussing these interconnected issues in parallel, with the understanding that, apart from humanitarian measures, nothing will be finali","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:10:20 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648793-trump-envoy-new-approach-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:30
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,The Ukraine peace process has a Western European problem,The Ukraine peace process has a Western European problem,"The Ukraine peace process has a Western European problem <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af6d21685f54031d4189dd1.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A lasting Ukraine settlement needs Western Europe. Bringing it into negotiations too soon, however, could derail fragile progress. <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648787-ukraine-peace-process-problem/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByGeorgy Asatryan, political scientist Two days of negotiations in Abu Dhabi have ended without a breakthrough. This was predictable because the Ukraine conflict is too complex, and too many interested parties still believe they can improve their positions at somebody else’s expense, but the absence of a dramatic announcement shouldn’t be mistaken for the absence of progress. The delegations were experienced, the discussions lengthy, and judging by the accounts, substantive, so this wasn’t another diplomatic performance designed merely to buy time or lull the opponent into complacency. For once, the parties appear to have discussed the issues that might eventually make peace possible. An agreement on a prisoner exchange is the most visible result. These exchanges aren’t unprecedented, but they demonstrate a willingness to keep channels open, while US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner have since traveled to Moscow to brief President Vladimir Putin, before continuing consultations with the Ukrainian leadership in Ireland. However, for now, decisive political commitments remain beyond the authority of the negotiators. The delegations can assess battlefield developments, the state of the opposing economies, and the costs of continuing the war, but they can’t resolve the most difficult questions without instructions from their leaders, which means Abu Dhabi was an important stage in the process, not the conclusion. Still, there is a sense of approaching a crossroads. Either ","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:06:47 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648787-ukraine-peace-process-problem/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:31
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Ex-Nvidia boss faces Congress grilling over ‘Chinese honeypot’ scandal,Ex-Nvidia boss faces Congress grilling over ‘Chinese honeypot’ scandal,"Ex-Nvidia boss faces Congress grilling over ‘Chinese honeypot’ scandal <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af6cf3f2030273899552e5e.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang faces congressional scrutiny over an alleged Chinese spy affair and chip exports to Beijing <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648786-ex-nvidia-boss-congress-testimony/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang has been called to testify before Congress alongside US Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick over national security concerns sparked by an alleged affair between Huang and a suspected Chinese spy. Senator Tim Scott sent letters to both men on Thursday, seeking their testimony before the Senate Banking Committee in early December. “Recent reports raise serious concerns about our national security and the protection of sensitive US technology,”Scott wrote on social media.“The American people deserve answers.” Huang’s appearance is voluntary, but the committee warned it is prepared to use“all tools”at its disposal, including subpoenas, if he refuses to testify. Recent reports raise serious concerns about our national security and the protection of sensitive U.S. technology.I am requesting that NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang and Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick testify before the Senate Banking Committee.The American people deserve…pic.twitter.com/Xu1kiNzkhW The scandal erupted earlier this month following reports linking the CEO to Alice Huang, also known as Huang Le, a businesswoman formerly associated with Singapore-based Nvidia chip buyer Megaspeed International. The New York Times and Financial Times claimed US intelligence officials suspected her of gathering information for Beijing and attempting to influence Huang to loosen restrictions on chip exports to China. The FBI opened an investigation, while Nvidia’s board launched its own probe. ","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:05:30 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648786-ex-nvidia-boss-congress-testimony/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:32
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Military helicopter crash kills four soldiers in Türkiye (VIDEO),Military helicopter crash kills four soldiers in Türkiye (VIDEO),"Military helicopter crash kills four soldiers in Türkiye (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af6c99285f5402ac37d58fa.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> An S-70-type helicopter crashed in the Turkish eastern province of Malatya, killing four soldiers, the National Defense Ministry said <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648785-turkiye-helicopter-crash-four-soldiers/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Four Turkish military personnel were killed when an S-70-type helicopter crashed in the country’s eastern province of Malatya, the National Defense Ministry said on Thursday. The ministry did not provide details about the aircraft’s mission or the number of personnel on board. There was no immediate official information on casualties or on the causes of the crash. “As a result of an accident involving our S-70 helicopter in Malatya, for a reason not yet determined, four of our heroic comrades-in-arms aboard the helicopter were martyred,”the ministry said in a statement, extending condolences to the families of the soldiers. The helicopter went down in the Samankoy neighborhood of Malatya’s Yesilyurt district around 6:45 PM local time, according to reports by local media. A fire reportedly broke out at the crash site and spread to a nearby house. Video footage circulating online shows the helicopter’s burning wreckage near a cluster of buildings in an otherwise open area. The S-70 belongs to the Black Hawk family of military utility helicopters manufactured by US defense manufacturer Sikorsky Aircraft Corporation. Variants of the aircraft are operated by armed forces in several countries. The Black Hawk is able to carry up to 11 soldiers plus its air crew. The Turkish Air Force operates a large base – the 7th Main Jet Base – to the north of Malatya. RT News App © Autonomous Nonprofit Organization “TV-Novosti”, 2005–2026. All rights reserved. This website u","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:45:13 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648785-turkiye-helicopter-crash-four-soldiers/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:34
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Iran claims strike on US radar,Iran claims strike on US radar,"Iran claims strike on US radar <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af68f3c2030272cdd5cee77.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps claims that it struck a US radar installation in Bahrain, amid threats of renewed war <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648771-iran-claims-strike-us-radar/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) claims that it struck a US early-warning radar installation in Bahrain. In a statement carried by Iranian media on Friday, the IRGC said the attack was in retaliation for an alleged enemy airstrike on a telecommunications tower in Sirik, in Iran’s southern Hormozgan Province. The IRGC claimed that it destroyed the radar, although neither the strike nor the reported damage has been independently verified. There was no immediate confirmation from the US military or Bahrain. The incident comes amid continued tensions between Washington and Tehran, with peace negotiations stalled and fears persisting over a possible resumption of major US military operations. US President Donald Trump said on Monday that further military action against Iran does not appear to be necessary. He expressed hope for a diplomatic breakthrough amid calls for restraint from Arab allies. However, he warned that US forces are“locked and loaded”and ready to resume strikes if the circumstances change. In a Truth Social post on Thursday, Trump declared that the US no longer needs a peace deal with Iran, claiming that Washington controls Iranian funds and the Strait of Hormuz. The US carried out limited airstrikes against Iranian air-defense positions on Qeshm Island on November 2 and 6. Trump described the latest operation as“minor.”Media reports have said Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu pressed Trump to launch a new offensive against Iran following th","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:18:35 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648771-iran-claims-strike-us-radar/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:34
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Mamdani moves to disband NYPD protest-control unit – Politico,Mamdani moves to disband NYPD protest-control unit – Politico,"Mamdani moves to disband NYPD protest-control unit – Politico <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af6839585f5402ebb21102e.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani is reportedly preparing to disband an NYPD unit responsible for policing protests and counterterrorism <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648770-mamdani-police-protest-unit-disbands/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani, a democratic socialist, is finalizing plans to disband a specialized police unit responsible for counterterrorism and crowd control, Politico reported on Thursday, citing people familiar with the matter. Mamdani pledged to dismantle the NYPD’s Strategic Response Group (SRG) during his 2025 mayoral campaign following accusations that its officers used excessive force against protesters. According to Politico, the mayor is considering replacing the SRG’s protest-response function with a civilian-led unit focused on de-escalation, which could assist police in making arrests when necessary. The new unit could operate under Mamdani’s Office of Community Safety, established earlier this year. The plan could be announced as early as this week and formalized through an executive order. “As the mayor has said, our administration will disband the Strategic Response Group and separate protest response from counterterrorism,”Mamdani’s spokeswoman, Dora Pekec, said, promising further details soon. Established in 2015, the SRG came under increased scrutiny over its handling of the nationwide unrest sparked by the killing of George Floyd by a Minneapolis police officer in 2020. In 2023, the NYPD agreed to restrict the unit’s deployment at peaceful demonstrations and prohibit the practice of surrounding and trapping protesters without grounds for arrest. New York City Public Advocate Jumaane Williams has called for the SRG to be removed from prot","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:30:03 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648770-mamdani-police-protest-unit-disbands/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:35
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Israel bars French presidential hopeful over Gaza flotilla pledge,Israel bars French presidential hopeful over Gaza flotilla pledge,"Israel bars French presidential hopeful over Gaza flotilla pledge <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af65d4085f5400b827c7522.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Israel has banned Jean-Luc Melenchon after the French left-wing leader pledged to send warships to escort Gaza flotillas. <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648769-israel-bars-melenchon-gaza/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Israel has banned French left-wing presidential candidate Jean-Luc Melenchon from entering the country after he vowed to deploy warships to escort activist flotillas seeking to break the blockade of Gaza. The Israeli Foreign Ministry also imposed an entry ban on Mathilde Panot, the parliamentary leader of Melenchon’s La France Insoumise (LFI) party. “Both have made statements spreading blood libels against Israel, while Jean-Luc Melenchon has also called for French naval vessels to escort illegal flotillas to Gaza,”the ministry said in a statement on Thursday. “The State of Israel will respond firmly to those who seek to harm it.” French Foreign Minister Jean-Noel Barrot called the move“a demagogic decision made by a government that has repeatedly violated international law.”He argued that the ban will only help LFI to“thrive on exploiting the Israeli-Palestinian conflict for political gain.” According to recent opinion polls, Melenchon ranks second behind Marine Le Pen of the right-wing National Rally (RN) in voting intentions for the 2027 presidential election. LFI is one of the largest opposition parties in the French parliament. A vocal critic of Israel, Melenchon has pledged to“take direct action”to support Palestinians in Gaza and the West Bank if elected president. “French naval vessels will, if necessary, escort flotillas of citizens mobilized to assert their rights,”he said on Saturday, referring to civilian boats attempting to reach Gaza. Israel has repeatedly inter","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:46:02 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648769-israel-bars-melenchon-gaza/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:36
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,German democracy satisfaction hits decades-low – study,German democracy satisfaction hits decades-low – study,"German democracy satisfaction hits decades-low – study <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af631952030276a2e09feef.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Two-thirds of Germans are dissatisfied with how democracy works, with satisfaction at its lowest level in 20 years, a Leipzig study finds <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648767-germans-dissatisfied-state-democracy/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Two in three Germans are dissatisfied with how democracy functions in their country, according to the latest Leipzig Authoritarianism Study conducted by researchers at Leipzig University in cooperation with the Heinrich Boll Foundation and the Otto Brenner Foundation. The findings, published on Wednesday, show that satisfaction with democracy as experienced in everyday life has fallen to just 33.3%, down from 42.3% in 2024. It is the lowest level recorded since researchers began measuring the indicator in 2006. Discontent is particularly pronounced in the former East Germany, where only 22.8% of respondents expressed satisfaction, compared with around 36% in the west. More than half of Germans expressed at least some sympathy for either“nostalgic idealization of the past”or“apocalyptic expectations of the future,”according to the study. The survey involved 2,507 respondents interviewed from March 16 to June 3. The findings follow an INSA poll showing that 82% of Germans are dissatisfied with Chancellor Friedrich Merz and his government. Around 60% said their personal circumstances have worsened since he took office. Merz became chancellor following snap elections in February 2025, after promising to revive the struggling economy. However, economic difficulties have persisted, while his government has increased military spending, maintained financial and military support for Ukraine, and advocated for reforms to Germany’s welfare system. The chancellor urged Germa","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:37:50 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648767-germans-dissatisfied-state-democracy/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:38
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Denmark ‘moving towards dictatorship’ – MP to RT (VIDEO),Denmark ‘moving towards dictatorship’ – MP to RT (VIDEO),"Denmark ‘moving towards dictatorship’ – MP to RT (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af600182030277bda21ca10.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Denmark is moving toward dictatorship by prioritizing Ukraine over its citizens, Danish MP Jacob Harris has told RT <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648755-harris-danish-mp-snubs-zelensky/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Denmark is“moving towards a dictatorship,”independent MP Jacob Harris has told RT in an exclusive interview. The Citizen’s Party lawmaker defended his refusal to stand and applaud Vladimir Zelensky during the Ukrainian leader’s controversial address to the Danish parliament. Harris sat with his arms crossed as other lawmakers gave Zelensky, who openly mocked US President Donald Trump during his speech, a standing ovation on Wednesday. He later posted photos of his protest on X. His protest was condemned by Danish politicians. Foreign Minister Lars Lokke Rasmussen called it a provocation, while opposition leader Inger Stojberg accused Harris of“doing [Russian President Vladimir] Putin’s bidding.” Et diktatur kommer ikke fra den ene dag til den anden. Det vokser frem gennem tavshed, når befolkningen holder op med at sige fra. Demokratiet kræver, at vi tør stille spørgsmål – også når det er ubelejligt for magthaverne. https://t.co/nl8pinTdEG Speaking to RT on Thursday, Harris accused the Danish government of undermining democratic rules by allowing a foreign leader to address parliament from its main podium. “According to our democratic laws, you have to be elected to the Danish parliament before you are allowed to speak there,”he said. Harris accused Prime Minister Mette Frederiksen of setting aside parliamentary rules for political reasons, calling the decision a move towards dictatorship. The Danish parliament has rejected his interpretation, explaining that Zelensky’s addres","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:29:08 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648755-harris-danish-mp-snubs-zelensky/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:39
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Fantasy vs. reality: The confusion of the willing and Ukraine peace talks,Fantasy vs. reality: The confusion of the willing and Ukraine peace talks,"Fantasy vs. reality: The confusion of the willing and Ukraine peace talks <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af60e5785f5402b854d2d3f.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The EU is under pressure to appoint an envoy to Russia, but its squabbling members can’t even agree on whether they should talk at all <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648763-europe-ukraine-russia-talks/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByRT newsroom, a team of multi-lingual journalists with over a decade of experience in Russian and international reporting, delivering original research and insights often missing from mainstream coverage ByRT newsroom, a team of multi-lingual journalists with over a decade of experience in Russian and international reporting, delivering original research and insights often missing from mainstream coverage In their most recent talks with Russian President Vladimir Putin, US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner apparently secured a place for ‘Europe’ at the negotiating table with Russia. European leaders will have to overcome deep factional divides and square away their most ideologically-driven fantasists to have any influence over the talks. “The Europeans will join at the next meeting, which we consider to be a very important moment,”Witkoff told reporters in Moscow on Thursday, before he and Kushner departed for Ireland to brief Ukrainian leader Vladimir Zelensky and his EU backers. The Kremlin has not set a date for the next round of talks, nor has Moscow confirmed the precise extent of European participation. However, as Kushner pointed out the previous day, Europe has a more immediate problem on its hands :“If Europe could identify one person to speak on their behalf,”he said,“that would be a bigger achievement than getting the Russians to include them in the negotiation.” The US president’s son-in-law is not the first American to express bewilderm","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:55:05 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648763-europe-ukraine-russia-talks/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:40
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Progress made in Ukraine peace talks – Russian deputy FM,Progress made in Ukraine peace talks – Russian deputy FM,"Progress made in Ukraine peace talks – Russian deputy FM <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af60f5985f5402fe037a7f7.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Progress made in the Abu Dhabi talks could be undermined by European involvement, Russian Deputy Foreign Minister Sergey Ryabkov has told RT <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648754-ukraine-talks-russia-us/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The two-day trilateral talks involving Russia, Ukraine, and the US in Abu Dhabi this week have brought progress toward settling the Ukraine conflict, Russian Deputy Foreign Minister Sergey Ryabkov has told RT in an exclusive interview. However, involving European governments in the process could undermine diplomatic efforts, he warned. Ryabkov was among the Russian delegates at the negotiations, which concluded on Wednesday with an agreement in principle on a major prisoner exchange. US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner subsequently traveled to Moscow, where they met Russian President Vladimir Putin on Thursday for talks lasting around two and a half hours. Ryabkov noted that the latest round in Abu Dhabi differed from previous meetings, with American representatives seeking to make discussions more concrete. Much of the attention focused on a future European security architecture that could support a lasting settlement and prevent“uncontrolled escalation,”he said. “We have made progress. That is an indisputable fact,”Ryabkov said, while cautioning that previous diplomatic advances had been followed by setbacks and attempts to derail the process. “Bringing the Europeans into the negotiating process could mean a reversal and the disruption of efforts,”the diplomat warned. He pointed to a fundamental divide between European governments and both Moscow and Washington, adding that they rejected Russia’s approach and appeared equally opposed to proposals advanced by the ","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:52:48 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648754-ukraine-talks-russia-us/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:41
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Dublin summit: European leaders double down on the Zelensky disaster,Dublin summit: European leaders double down on the Zelensky disaster,"Dublin summit: European leaders double down on the Zelensky disaster <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af623fc2030277bda21ca1d.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> With Moscow absent and peace efforts elsewhere advancing, the gathering was just a show of stubborn loyalty to a failing proxy war <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648764-eu-leaders-zelensky-disaster/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByTarik Cyril Amar, a historian from Germany working at Koç University, Istanbul, on Russia, Ukraine, and Eastern Europe, the history of World War II, the cultural Cold War, and the politics of memory ByTarik Cyril Amar, a historian from Germany working at Koç University, Istanbul, on Russia, Ukraine, and Eastern Europe, the history of World War II, the cultural Cold War, and the politics of memory Let’s start with the obvious, which, oddly enough, remains largely unnoticed: Ifthe summit of the European Political Community (EPC), a formally informal gathering that brings together the high and mighty of NATO-EU Europe plus friends, was serious about reflecting Europe, then Russia (and, by the way, Belarus, too) would have been invited. The fact that Moscow is not present is, once you think about it, a striking anomaly, even if Western mainstream media framing has been quite effective at making the obviously strange appear to be the new normal. Russia’s longstanding exclusion is, of course, also very telling. At the risk of re-stating the obvious, it reflects NATO-EU Europe’s fundamentally flawed, catastrophically costly (including for Ukraine), and very obstinate policy of waging a proxy war against Russia, while using up Ukraine and Ukrainians. It’s a shame: Europe could have been the ideal framework for preventing, or at least quickly ending, the Ukraine War by offering honest mediation, facilitating real compromise, and, last but not least, helping review and re","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:41:12 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648764-eu-leaders-zelensky-disaster/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:42
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US no longer needs Iran deal – Trump,US no longer needs Iran deal – Trump,"US no longer needs Iran deal – Trump <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af6003b203027775f12a8e6.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Trump says the US no longer needs an Iran deal and directs J.D. Vance to tackle corruption and crime after Republicans’ midterm defeat <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648761-trump-no-iran-deal-needed/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Washington no longer needs a deal with Iran, US President Donald Trump has declared. He has directed Vice President J.D. Vance to focus instead on alleged corruption and crime in Democrat-run states and cities. The announcement follows Vance’s criticism of the US-Israeli war on Iran, which he blamed for Republicans’ defeat in last week’s midterm elections. On Wednesday, the vice president questioned whether the conflict had been worth its cost. Vance had previously pursued diplomatic efforts to end the war and reportedly favored reaching an agreement with Tehran over continued military pressure. In aTruth Social poston Thursday, Trump ordered Vance to devote his“complete and total attention”to tackling the domestic issue, arguing that a sweeping corruption crackdown could help balance the federal budget. “We don’t need a deal with Iran. Those days have long since passed,”Trump wrote.“We’ve got their money, Hundreds of Billions of Dollars, and we’ve got their Strait!” Trump offered no explanation for his claim about Iranian money, which some media outlets have interpreted as a reference to frozen Iranian assets. Tehran estimates the funds at more than $100 billion, largely consisting of oil and gas revenues held in foreign banks under US sanctions. His assertion of control over the Strait of Hormuz appears to refer to the US naval blockade, which restricts shipping to and from Iranian ports while allowing vessels serving other Gulf countries to pass. On Monday, Trump said he w","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:21:42 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648761-trump-no-iran-deal-needed/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:43
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump floats Tim Cook as Nvidia chief after ‘Chinese honeypot’ scandal,Trump floats Tim Cook as Nvidia chief after ‘Chinese honeypot’ scandal,"Trump floats Tim Cook as Nvidia chief after ‘Chinese honeypot’ scandal <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af616612030275b40123a39.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Donald Trump has suggested former Apple CEO Tim Cook replace Nvidia’s Jensen Huang who resigned following espionage scandal <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648758-nvidia-ceo-huang-resigns/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US President Donald Trump has suggested that former Apple CEO Tim Cook take over Nvidia following the resignation of its longtime chief Jensen Huang, who stepped down after reports of two extramarital affairs, including one with a woman suspected of spying for China “A legend replaces a legend!”Trump wrote, floating Cook, who now chairs Apple’s board, as a potential successor to Huang. The American president had previously defended Huang as“an amazing guy,”saying he believed that the executive had been unaware of the alleged espionage. Trump and Cook have maintained ties for years, with the president previously claiming that the Apple executive had called him to“kiss my ass”while seeking help during his first term. In August 2025, Cook visited Trump in the Oval Office, presenting him with a plaque featuring a 24-karat gold base as Apple announced plans to increase its US investment commitment to $600 billion over four years. Trump later praised Cook as an“incredible guy,”describing their relationship as“long and very nice.” Nvidia announced on Thursday that Huang had stepped down as president, chief executive, and board member“effective immediately,”ending his 33-year tenure. Finance chief Colette Kress will serve as interim CEO while Nvidia seeks a permanent replacement. The crisis erupted over reports linking Huang to Alice Huang, also known as Huang Le, a businesswoman formerly associated with Singapore-based Nvidia chip buyer Megaspeed International. The New York Times","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:43:43 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648758-nvidia-ceo-huang-resigns/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:43
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,EU member jails woman over pro-Russia TikTok posts,EU member jails woman over pro-Russia TikTok posts,"EU member jails woman over pro-Russia TikTok posts <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.11/thumbnail/6af5d29820302760917cbd5f.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A Latvian court has sentenced a woman to three years in prison over pro-Russia TikTok posts deemed to glorify war crimes in Ukraine <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/648752-latvia-prison-tiktok-posts-russia/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> A court in Riga, Latvia has sentenced a woman to three years in prison over TikTok posts deemed to glorify alleged war crimes committed by Russian forces in Ukraine, LETA news agency reported on Wednesday. The case is the latest in a series of prosecutions in Latvia over statements deemed supportive of Moscow or critical of Kiev. Since the escalation of the Ukraine conflict in 2022, the Baltic state has tightened restrictions on Russian-language media, cultural activities, and public expressions of pro-Russian sentiment. According to LETA, the case involved around 20 videos and comments posted by Latvian citizen Tatyana Masenko from April to July 2024. The agency cited several examples of content that prosecutors considered criminal. One video reportedly showed a Ukrainian serviceman with a prosthetic limb standing in front of a cemetery lined with Ukrainian flags. Masenko captioned it:“Forward, to the gay-European future.” Another video included a similar message:“Soon, all of you from across gay Europe will be gathered together and sent to defend Ukraine with bags of sunflower seeds and packets.” Masenko’s defense argued that the three-year sentence is excessively harsh, noting that she had already spent four months in custody. Her lawyer said the verdict would be appealed. This comes after a series of similar cases in Latvia. In January, a court sentenced 72-year-old professor Aleksandr Gaponenko to ten years in prison over his participation in an academic roundtable, wher","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:00:32 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/648752-latvia-prison-tiktok-posts-russia/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-11-15 03:29:44
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,New mechanisms required to prevent conflicts in Europe — US envoy Kushner,New mechanisms required to prevent conflicts in Europe — US envoy Kushner,"New mechanisms required to prevent conflicts in Europe — US envoy Kushner According to the official, NATO ""will remain a critical pillar of European security,"" while these mechanisms are seen as a means of strengthening its capacities WASHINGTON, November 15. /TASS/. The participation of the US allies in Europe in negotiations to resolve the ongoing Ukrainian conflict is necessary in order to create new conflict-prevention mechanisms within the NATO framework, US Special Presidential Envoy Jared Kushner said. ""NATO will remain a critical pillar of European security, enhanced by stronger mechanisms for military, communication, deconfliction, and reciprocal de-escalation, with practical ways to address disputes before they become crises,"" he stated on his X social network account. ""This is why we are working to bring our European partners directly into these discussions,"" the US official noted. ""Any final agreement must be agreed to by the relevant parties, and President (of the US Donald - TASS) Trump will only support arrangements that strengthen Ukraine’s and Europe’s security and make future conflict less likely,"" he continued. Kushner added that ""both sides understand that practical compromises will be necessary to end this war."" Russian Presidential Spokesman Dmitry Peskov stated earlier that negotiations with Europe would be required when the discussion turns to ensuring the security of Russia and Ukraine and the future of the security system in Europe. Russia, the United States and Ukraine held talks in Abu Dhabi on November 10-11. Presidential Aide Vladimir Medinsky led the Russian delegation, while Foreign Intelligence Service chief Rustem Umerov headed the Ukrainian delegation. US envoys Steve Wit","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:01:32 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218243,2026-11-15 03:29:46
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,North Korea’s official delegation arrives in Moscow — KCNA,North Korea’s official delegation arrives in Moscow — KCNA,"North Korea’s official delegation arrives in Moscow — KCNA The delegation was greeted by Andrey Klimov, member of the Bureau of the Supreme Council of the United Russia Party, Sin Hong Chol, DPRK ambassador to Russia, and members of his embassy PYONGYANG, November 15. /TASS/. A delegation of North Korean officials has arrived in the Russian capital of Moscow for an official visit, theKorean Central News Agency(KCNA) reported. ""A delegation of the Party and government of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea led by Jo Yong Won, member of the Presidium of the Political Bureau and secretary of the Central Committee of the Workers' Party of Korea, arrived in Moscow by the private plane on November 14 to visit the Russian Federation,"" the agency reported. According to KCNA, ""Jo Yong Won, member of the Presidium of the Political Bureau and secretary of the C.C., WPK, and the delegation were warmly greeted by Andrey Klimov, member of the Bureau of the Supreme Council of the United Russia Party and first vice-chairman of the International Affairs Committee of the State Duma of Russia, officials concerned, Sin Hong Chol, DPRK ambassador to Russia, and members of his embassy.""","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:06:19 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218241,2026-11-15 03:29:48
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Europe’s negotiators have not yet contacted Russia — Kremlin,Europe’s negotiators have not yet contacted Russia — Kremlin,"Europe’s negotiators have not yet contacted Russia — Kremlin Agence France-Presse previously reported that the EU delegation will include representatives of the European Commission, the European Council, Germany, France, Italy, and Poland, as well as the UK MOSCOW, November 15. /TASS/. Negotiators assigned by Europe have not yet attempted to establish contact with Russia, Russian Presidential Spokesman Dmitry Peskov said. ""No. Not yet,"" Peskov told TASS in response to a corresponding question. Agence France-Presse (AFP) reported on Friday that the EU delegation will include representatives of the European Commission, the European Council, Germany, France, Italy, and Poland, as well as the United Kingdom, which is not a European Union member.","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:33:23 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2218239,2026-11-15 03:29:49
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Kiev troops bombard Donetsk People’s Republic 32 times over past day,Kiev troops bombard Donetsk People’s Republic 32 times over past day,"Kiev troops bombard Donetsk People’s Republic 32 times over past day A civilian was killed and four more sustained wounds DONETSK, November 15. /TASS/. The Ukrainian military shelled residential areas in the Donetsk People’s Republic (DPR) 32 times over the past 24 hours, a civilian was killed and four more sustained wounds, the department for documenting Ukraine’s war crimes at the DPR head’s office and government said in a statement on Sunday. ""Over the past 24-hour period, 32 shelling attacks by Ukraine’s armed formations were registered. According to reports, a civilian was killed and four more were wounded,"" the statement said. According to the statement, 32 munitions of various types were fired from Ukraine. Five residential buildings, two civilian infrastructure facilities, a passenger bus, several trucks and other motor vehicles were damaged.","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:27:40 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2218237,2026-11-15 03:29:50
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russia’s top racquet Andreeva through to final of 2026 WTA Finals in US,Russia’s top racquet Andreeva through to final of 2026 WTA Finals in US,"Russia’s top racquet Andreeva through to final of 2026 WTA Finals in US The player has defeated American Jessica Pegula WASHINGTON, November 15. /TASS/. Russian top female racquet Mirra Andreeva has defeated American Jessica Pegula in straight sets 6-3; 6-4 to reach the final of the 2026 WTA (Women Tennis Association) Finals tournament in Indian Wells, the United States. In a match that lasted 1 hour and 25 minutes, the 3rd-seeded Andreeva, who is playing under a neutral status at the tournament, blasted past her 5th-seeded US opponent with straight sets win 6-3; 6-4. ""It was very interesting for me to see how the match would actually go because I don't really know how she plays, and she's actually one of the players where when I watch her matches, I cannot really understand where exactly she will hit,"" the official WTA website quoted Andreeva as saying after the match. ""With her, today I was really trying to react at the spot because I couldn't really understand her pattern. Then, the longer the match went, the more I understood more or less what she does,"" Andreeva, who is the first Russian to reach the final of the WTA Finals tournament in 14 years, stated. The Russian is now set to play in the final against Elina Svitolina from Ukraine (6th-seed), who later in the day outplayed Linda Noskova of the Czech Republic (8th-seed) 6-2; 6-1 in 1 hour and five minutes. Reached for a comment about the upcoming match against Svitolina, the Russian player said: ""I actually don't know because it's also the first time that it happens to me."" ""I will try to rely a little bit more on [coach] Conchita [Mar","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:02:19 +0300",https://tass.com/sports/2218235,2026-11-15 03:29:51
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,US aims to facilitate direct contacts between Russia and Europe on Ukraine — Kushner,US aims to facilitate direct contacts between Russia and Europe on Ukraine — Kushner,"US aims to facilitate direct contacts between Russia and Europe on Ukraine — Kushner The envoy added that US President Donald Trump believes it is necessary to have ""actionable"" conflict prevention mechanisms WASHINGTON, November 14. /TASS/. The US administration aims to facilitate direct contacts between Russia and America’s European allies on resolving the conflict in Ukraine, Jared Kushner, son-in-law of the US leader, said. ""Our focus now is on facilitating direct engagement between Moscow and European partners and preparing the agenda for the next round of trilateral talks,"" he wrote on X. Kushner added that US President Donald Trump believes that ""a lasting peace requires credible security guarantees for Ukraine and detailed, actionable postwar security arrangements that reduce the risk of another war.""","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:01:53 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218233,2026-11-15 03:29:55
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Kushner says new ideas have emerged for resolving Ukrainian conflict,Kushner says new ideas have emerged for resolving Ukrainian conflict,"Kushner says new ideas have emerged for resolving Ukrainian conflict These ideas are ""now being explored,"" the US envoy added WASHINGTON, November 14. /TASS/. US envoy Jared Kushner said that new ideas for resolving the Ukrainian conflict have emerged during recent discussions with Russia, Ukraine, and Europe. ""Several new ideas emerged from these discussions and are now being explored. Some may lead to breakthroughs directly, while others may evolve into new proposals that help bridge the remaining gaps,"" Kushner wrote on X.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:54:56 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218231,2026-11-15 03:29:56
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Over 120 people detained during rallies in France — TV,Over 120 people detained during rallies in France — TV,"Over 120 people detained during rallies in France — TV According to the French Interior Ministry, 106,000 people took part in the rallies held across the country on Saturday PARIS, November 14. /TASS/. French police and gendarmes have detained 121 people during rallies held across the country on November 14 against rising prices and police violence, the BFMTV television channel reported, citing the French Interior Ministry. These figures cover the entire country as of 5:00 p.m. local time (4:00 p.m. GMT) and are subject to further updates by the end of the day. Earlier, the Paris Police Prefecture reported the detention of 22 people in the capital, including three teenagers. Most of the detentions were for carrying items classified as weapons, verbal abuse, or violating bans on entering specific areas or participating in rallies. According to the French Interior Ministry, 106,000 people took part in the rallies held across the country on Saturday. The largest rally took place in Paris, where, according to ministry estimates, 24,000 people took to the streets. University and high school student associations involved in organizing the protests claimed that 200,000 people participated nationwide, including 100,000 in Paris. As a TASS correspondent witnessed, the rally in the French capital remained largely peaceful. However, near the end of the route, clashes broke out between groups of troublemakers and police. All participants eventually reached the Place de la Nation, where police officers stationed around the perimeter urged them to disperse. Law enforcement officers pushed back the crowd several times using batons and tear gas, and by now almos","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:54:10 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218221,2026-11-15 03:29:57
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Police detain 22 protesters in Paris — TV,Police detain 22 protesters in Paris — TV,"Police detain 22 protesters in Paris — TV The arrests were made primarily for possession of Category D weapons PARIS, November 14. /TASS/. Police have detained 22 participants in protests against rising prices and police violence underway in Paris, theBFMTVtelevision channel reported, citing the city Police Prefecture. ""The arrests were made primarily for possession of Category D weapons, verbal abuse, and violating bans on entering certain areas or participating in demonstrations,"" the prefecture said. Three minors are among those detained, it specified. One of the largest rallies against rising prices and police violence is taking place in central Paris. As a TASS correspondent witnessed, marchers proceeded calmly along most of the route from the Place de la Republique to the Place de la Nation. However, toward the end of the route, clashes broke out between police officers stationed along the perimeter and a group of troublemakers who began throwing stones and bottles at law enforcement. In response, officers deployed stun grenades and tear gas canisters. Currently, some protesters have reached the Place de la Nation, where further clashes are underway between police and aggressive demonstrators.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:53:59 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218217,2026-11-15 03:29:58
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Over 100,000 people took part in protests across France on November 14 — Interior Ministry","Over 100,000 people took part in protests across France on November 14 — Interior Ministry","Over 100,000 people took part in protests across France on November 14 — Interior Ministry The largest rally took place in Paris, where, according to ministry estimates, 24,000 people took to the streets PARIS, November 14. /TASS/. Rallies against rising prices and police violence drew 106,000 participants across France, the CNEWS television channel reported, citing the country’s Interior Ministry. The largest rally took place in Paris, where, according to ministry estimates, 24,000 people took to the streets. While the atmosphere remained relatively calm for most of the event, clashes with police broke out toward the end of the march, prompting officers to use stun grenades and tear gas to disperse groups of aggressive hooligans. Unrest also occurred in several other major cities, where marches were called by the Yellow Vests movement, as well as by university and high school student associations. In Nantes, police deployed a water cannon to disperse the crowd, and reports of skirmishes with law enforcement also came in from Bordeaux and Lyon. Mass protests have been underway in France since late September, when school students began blockading educational institutions to express dissatisfaction with their poor condition, overloaded schedules, and a shortage of teachers for certain subjects. In October, trade unions also began staging protests, demanding wage hikes and calling on the authorities to scrap further austerity measures.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:52:51 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218215,2026-11-15 03:29:59
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Air defenses downed 39 Ukrainian UAVs over Russian regions during day — Defense Ministry,Air defenses downed 39 Ukrainian UAVs over Russian regions during day — Defense Ministry,"Air defenses downed 39 Ukrainian UAVs over Russian regions during day — Defense Ministry Air defense forces intercepted and destroyed unmanned aerial vehicles over the territories of the Belgorod, Bryansk, Voronezh, Kaluga, Kursk, Lipetsk, Oryol, and Ryazan regions, as well as the Moscow Region and the Republic of Crimea MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. Russian air defense systems intercepted and destroyed 39 Ukrainian unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) over Russian regions during the day, the Russian Defense Ministry reported. ""During the day, between 8:00 a.m. and 8:00 p.m. Moscow time, on-duty air defense forces intercepted and destroyed 39 Ukrainian unmanned aerial vehicles over the territories of the Belgorod, Bryansk, Voronezh, Kaluga, Kursk, Lipetsk, Oryol, and Ryazan regions, as well as the Moscow Region and the Republic of Crimea,"" the ministry said.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:44:51 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2218213,2026-11-15 03:30:00
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,NATO undermines immunity of Europe and entire world — Zakharova,NATO undermines immunity of Europe and entire world — Zakharova,"NATO undermines immunity of Europe and entire world — Zakharova According to the diplomat, there would be far greater security in Europe were it not for NATO MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. The North Atlantic Alliance undermines the immunity of Europe and the entire world, much like a bad tooth, Russian Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Maria Zakharova told TASS on the sidelines of the PR Weekend event organized by the New Media Workshop. ""NATO is precisely the kind of organization that -- much like a bad tooth -- has suppressed the immunity of Europe -- its western and central parts -- and indeed the entire world, by siphoning off and consuming a colossal amount of response resources,"" she said. Zakharova was commenting on a statement by German Chancellor Friedrich Merz, who argued that there was no need to discuss a security architecture with Russia in the context of a Ukrainian settlement, as such an architecture already existed in the form of NATO. According to the diplomat, there would be far greater security in Europe were it not for NATO. ""If NATO did not exist -- or, more precisely, if it did not play the role that it has played and continues to play -- there would likely be much more security in Europe,"" she added. Zakharova emphasized that NATO was not established to maintain stability, but exclusively for aggressive, expansionist goals and objectives. ""It was created to orchestrate coups in various countries, to carry out 'color revolutions,' to pursue economic expansion, and to facilitate all manner of schemes for the benefit of those who profit from such policies within NATO,"" she added. ""Among other things, I would like to r","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:59:27 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2218211,2026-11-15 03:30:01
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Putin, Xi Jinping, Trump trilateral summit to be held in Shenzhen on November 19 — Kremlin","Putin, Xi Jinping, Trump trilateral summit to be held in Shenzhen on November 19 — Kremlin","Putin, Xi Jinping, Trump trilateral summit to be held in Shenzhen on November 19 — Kremlin This meeting will take place on the sidelines of the APEC summit MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. A summit of the leaders of Russia, China, and the United States - Vladimir Putin, Xi Jinping, and Donald Trump - will take place in Shenzhen on November 19 following an agreement reached by the sides, Kremlin Spokesman Dmitry Peskov told TASS. ""An agreement has been reached to hold a trilateral meeting on the 19th [of November] between President Putin, President Xi, and President Trump. This meeting will take place in Shenzhen on the sidelines of the APEC summit,"" the Kremlin spokesman said.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:58:40 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2218203,2026-11-15 03:30:02
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Russian, UAE foreign ministers meet in Abu Dhabi — Russian MFA","Russian, UAE foreign ministers meet in Abu Dhabi — Russian MFA","Russian, UAE foreign ministers meet in Abu Dhabi — Russian MFA The two top diplomats discussed bilateral relations and tensions in the Persian Gulf region MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov held talks with UAE Foreign Minister Abdullah bin Zayed Al Nahyan as part of his visit to Abu Dhabi, the two top diplomats discussed bilateral relations and tensions in the Persian Gulf region, the Russian Foreign Ministry reported. ""The sides reviewed current areas for developing the traditionally friendly Russian-Emirati ties, which represent a strategic partnership,"" the ministry said. ""A thorough exchange of views was held on key issues of the global and regional agenda. In this context, priority attention was given to discussing the persistent tensions in the Persian Gulf region,"" the ministry noted. Furthermore, the ministers emphasized that there is no alternative to resolving existing disagreements through political and diplomatic means, while strictly adhering to international law and fully taking into account the legitimate interests of all states involved in the conflict. ""The need to ensure stable, unimpeded, and safe navigation in the Strait of Hormuz -- which is of great importance to the global economy -- was highlighted,"" the Russian ministry stressed. Lavrov once again drew attention to Russia’s updated Concept for Ensuring Collective Security in the Persian Gulf Region. ""He reaffirmed readiness for constructive engagement with all interested countries and organizations with the aim of shaping a comprehensive security architecture in this strategically important region,"" the Russian Foreign M","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:16:05 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2218209,2026-11-15 03:30:03
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Iran shoots down 17th US MQ-1 drone over Qeshm Island in country’s south — IRGC,Iran shoots down 17th US MQ-1 drone over Qeshm Island in country’s south — IRGC,"Iran shoots down 17th US MQ-1 drone over Qeshm Island in country’s south — IRGC It specifies that the interception took place at 2:30 p.m. local time TEHRAN, November 14. /TASS/. The 17th American MQ-1 drone was intercepted and destroyed on Saturday over the Iranian island of Qeshm, the press service of the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) reported. ""The 17th American MQ-1 drone was intercepted and destroyed by a new, advanced air defense system of the IRGC Aerospace Force in the skies over Qeshm Island,"" the statement reads. It specifies that the interception took place at 2:30 p.m. local time (11:00 a.m. GMT). According to the IRGC, the downed vehicle is an MQ-1 series reconnaissance and strike drone operated by the US military. The statement describes the destruction of the UAV as yet another failure of the enemy's intelligence missions.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:35:17 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218199,2026-11-15 03:30:04
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Ukrainian forces attack passenger bus in Gorlovka, DPR — mayor","Ukrainian forces attack passenger bus in Gorlovka, DPR — mayor","Ukrainian forces attack passenger bus in Gorlovka, DPR — mayor It was a drone attack, Ivan Prikhodko reported DONETSK, November 14. /TASS/. A passenger bus has been damaged in a Ukrainian drone attack in Gorlovka, in the Donetsk People’s Republic (DPR), Mayor Ivan Prikhodko reported. ""A passenger bus was damaged in Gorlovka's Kalininsky District as a result of a drone strike by Ukrainian terrorists,"" he wrote on his Max channel.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:10:34 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2218195,2026-11-15 03:30:05
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Thousands take to the streets of Paris to protest rising prices and police violence,Thousands take to the streets of Paris to protest rising prices and police violence,"Thousands take to the streets of Paris to protest rising prices and police violence A primary trigger for the protest is a bill currently under parliamentary debate that would establish a presumption of legality regarding the use of weapons by law enforcement officers PARIS, November 14. /TASS/. Thousands of people have taken to the streets in Paris to protest against rising prices and violence by law enforcement officers against participants in previous rallies, a TASS correspondent reports. ""All together against brutality,"" ""Our children's lives are worth more than their profits,"" and ""Tax the rich!"" - these and many other slogans have brought together a massive crowd, which is marching from the Place de la Republique to the Place de la Nation. A primary trigger for the protest is a bill currently under parliamentary debate that would establish a presumption of legality regarding the use of weapons by law enforcement officers. Issam el-Halfawi, a representative of the association SAVE, told reporters that this legislation would complicate the investigation of potential misconduct by police officers or gendarmes, making it harder to prove such wrongdoing - as it would be impossible to challenge findings if no proper investigation takes place. The march includes many young people representing student organizations, alongside a large number of activists carrying the flags of left-wing political parties and movements. In addition to concerns over rising prices and violence, representatives of student and school associations have condemned the elimination of certain benefits for international students, as well as the inadequacy of grants for those currently enrolled in universities. ""We advocate for equal access to education for all, as well ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:02:41 +0300",https://tass.com/society/2218197,2026-11-15 03:30:06
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Bulgaria to stop supplying weapons to Ukraine — PM,Bulgaria to stop supplying weapons to Ukraine — PM,"Bulgaria to stop supplying weapons to Ukraine — PM Bulgaria does not intend to block EU member states’ decision to provide aid to Kiev, but cannot afford additional financial commitments, Bulgarian Prime Minister Rumen Radev said SOFIA, November 14. /TASS/. Sofia no longer intends to supply Kiev with weapons from its own stockpiles, Bulgarian Prime Minister Rumen Radev said on Facebook (banned in Russia and owned by Meta, designated as extremist in the country). ""The Bulgarian government’s position is that weapons and ammunition from Bulgarian army stockpiles will no longer be supplied to Ukraine,"" Radev wrote. He stressed that Bulgaria does not intend to block EU member states’ decision to provide aid to Kiev, but cannot afford additional financial commitments. Radev added that Bulgaria would also stay out of military exercises organized by the Coalition of the Willing because such informal missions ""undermine the unity of the EU and NATO."" Radev previously said Bulgaria could not allocate funds for loans to Ukraine. ""Bulgaria has never stopped supporting Ukraine. We provide assistance to thousands of Ukrainian families free of charge, supply electricity and help repair the power system and railway infrastructure. We’re now running an excessive deficit and are being asked to stay within the 3% deficit limit, so we have no additional funds,"" the prime minister stated.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:55:21 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218193,2026-11-15 03:30:07
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Staying out of EANA, other ‘decaying’ European forums serves Russia — Russian MFA","Staying out of EANA, other ‘decaying’ European forums serves Russia — Russian MFA","Staying out of EANA, other ‘decaying’ European forums serves Russia — Russian MFA Moscow believes that staying out of the European Alliance of News Agencies (EANA) and other European forums serves the interests of Russian organizations, Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Maria Zakharova said MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. Moscow believes that staying out of the European Alliance of News Agencies (EANA) and other European forums serves the interests of Russian organizations, Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Maria Zakharova said in a statement. ""We believe that leaving this forum and other decaying venues is fully in the interests of Russian organizations across a range of sectors that seek constructive cooperation and want to develop their own work,"" she stated. Zakharova also commented on inviting Lithuania’s ELTA news agency to join EANA in TASS’s place. ""Inviting Lithuania’s ELTA news agency to take TASS’s place looks like a grotesque caricature. ELTA has barely more than two dozen employees while the Russian news agency has around 2,000,"" she pointed out.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:45:36 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2218191,2026-11-15 03:30:08
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russia unwilling to set conditions on Europe’s negotiating team — Kremlin,Russia unwilling to set conditions on Europe’s negotiating team — Kremlin,"Russia unwilling to set conditions on Europe’s negotiating team — Kremlin Speaking about Russia’s position on EU representatives joining the talks on Ukraine, Peskov stressed that ""it would be better to speak with the Europeans and see to what extent their position could help advance the peace process"" MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. Moscow will not set conditions on who serves on Europe’s negotiating team, Russian presidential spokesman Dmitry Peskov told the Telegram channel Yunashev Live. ""We can’t and don’t want to set conditions on their negotiating team. That’s entirely the wrong way to frame the question,"" the Kremlin spokesman said. Speaking about Russia’s position on EU representatives joining the talks on Ukraine, Peskov stressed that ""it would be better to speak with the Europeans and see to what extent their position could help advance the peace process"".","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:29:02 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2218187,2026-11-15 03:30:09
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,EANA joins militaristic psychosis by expelling TASS — Russian MFA,EANA joins militaristic psychosis by expelling TASS — Russian MFA,"EANA joins militaristic psychosis by expelling TASS — Russian MFA By expelling the agency, EANA showed that it is unable to uphold press freedom, Maria Zakharova said MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. The European Alliance of News Agencies (EANA) succumbed to militaristic psychosis when it decided to expel TASS, Russian Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Maria Zakharova said in astatement. ""This time, EANA’s leadership could not stay clear of the militaristic psychosis into which the European Union’s ruling class is dragging it. With this decision, the leadership ritually pledged allegiance to a policy of escalating tensions with Russia to please the gang of terrorists and murderers entrenched in Kiev,"" Zakharova stated. By expelling the agency, EANA showed that it is unable to uphold press freedom, she added. ""The alliance has shown that it is incapable of upholding the principles set out in its own statutes, namely supporting press freedom, fostering cooperation among European media organizations and defending their interests,"" Zakharova stressed.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:04:19 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2218185,2026-11-15 03:30:10
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Lavrov holds series of meetings at Abu Dhabi forum — Russian MFA,Lavrov holds series of meetings at Abu Dhabi forum — Russian MFA,"Lavrov holds series of meetings at Abu Dhabi forum — Russian MFA The Russian foreign minister took part in a conference on political affairs MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov held a series of meetings on the sidelines of the Sir Bani Yas International Forum on Peace and Security in Abu Dhabi, Russian Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Maria Zakharova said. ""Sergey Lavrov took part in a conference on political affairs in Abu Dhabi and held a series of meetings on the sidelines,"" Zakharova wrote on herTelegramchannel.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:42:54 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2218183,2026-11-15 03:30:10
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,F-16s supplied to Ukraine constantly undergoing repairs — Zelensky,F-16s supplied to Ukraine constantly undergoing repairs — Zelensky,"F-16s supplied to Ukraine constantly undergoing repairs — Zelensky The jets aren’t new, he said MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. Ukraine rarely uses the F-16 fighter jets it received from Western countries because they are constantly undergoing repairs, Vladimir Zelensky said. ""We need two and a half times as many aircraft in the air at once as we’re flying now. On paper, we have that many, but the jets are constantly undergoing repairs because the F-16s aren’t new,"" Ukraine’s public broadcaster quoted him as saying. The Wall Street Journal previously reported that Kiev could be left without a single operational F-16 by the end of the year because of maintenance problems.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:19:40 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218181,2026-11-15 03:30:11
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Ukrainian forces target rescuers in Starobelsk, LPR — regional head","Ukrainian forces target rescuers in Starobelsk, LPR — regional head","Ukrainian forces target rescuers in Starobelsk, LPR — regional head No one was injured, Leonid Pasechnik said LUGANSK, November 14. /TASS/. Ukrainian forces deliberately struck emergency responders dealing with the aftermath of an attack on a gas station in Starobelsk in the Lugansk People’s Republic (LPR), its head Leonid Pasechnik said, specifying that no one was injured. ""In Starobelsk, Ukrainian armed formations deliberately struck emergency responders who were dealing with the aftermath of an enemy strike on a gas station. Emergencies Ministry personnel managed to take cover, and no one was injured,"" Pasechnik wrote on hisMaxchannel.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:09:57 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2218179,2026-11-15 03:30:12
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Ukrainian forces hit ambulance station in LPR — regional head,Ukrainian forces hit ambulance station in LPR — regional head,"Ukrainian forces hit ambulance station in LPR — regional head No medical staff were injured, Leonid Pasechnik said LUGANSK, November 14. /TASS/. Ukrainian forces used drones to attack an ambulance station in the Lugansk People’s Republic (LPR), damaging the building and vehicles, the republic’s head Leonid Pasechnik said. ""Neo-Nazis are striking those who save lives. Drones attacked an ambulance station in Novaya Astrakhan in the Kremenskoy municipal district. No medical staff were injured. The building and vehicles were damaged. Despite that, medical workers continue to provide residents with the care they need,"" Pasechnik wrote on hisMaxchannel.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:08:22 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2218177,2026-11-15 03:30:13
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"One killed, three wounded in Ukrainian attacks in LPR","One killed, three wounded in Ukrainian attacks in LPR","One killed, three wounded in Ukrainian attacks in LPR The injured had received the medical care they needed LUGANSK, November 14. /TASS/. Ukrainian military drone attacks killed one civilian and wounded three in the Lugansk People’s Republic (LPR), its head Leonid Pasechnik said. ""An enemy drone struck near a store in Rubezhnoye, killing a 37-year-old man. I extend my deepest condolences to his family and loved ones. Trucks came under attack on roads in the republic’s Starobelsky, Stanichno-Lugansky and Perevalsky municipal districts. They were carrying civilian goods: grain, bread and building materials. Three drivers were wounded,"" he wrote on hisMaxchannel. Pasechnik added that the injured had received the medical care they needed.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:06:17 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2218175,2026-11-15 03:30:17
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Drone attack kills pensioner riding e-bike in Bryansk Region — governor,Drone attack kills pensioner riding e-bike in Bryansk Region — governor,"Drone attack kills pensioner riding e-bike in Bryansk Region — governor The family would receive the assistance it needs, Governor Yegor Kovalchuk said BRYANSK, November 14. /TASS/. A kamikaze drone killed a 76-year-old pensioner riding an electric bicycle in a border area of the Bryansk Region, Governor Yegor Kovalchuk said. ""A 76-year-old local resident was killed in the village of Churovichi in the Klimovsky District. He was riding an electric bicycle when a Ukrainian kamikaze drone attacked him. This is a terrible loss for his loved ones,"" Kovalchuk wrote onMax, adding that the family would receive the assistance it needs.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:33:48 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2218173,2026-11-15 03:30:21
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Ukraine not going to enshrine neutrality in constitution, Zelensky says","Ukraine not going to enshrine neutrality in constitution, Zelensky says","Ukraine not going to enshrine neutrality in constitution, Zelensky says Enshrining neutrality means changing the country’s constitution, and Ukraine won’t do that, he said MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. Ukraine will not enshrine neutral status in its constitution, Vladimir Zelensky told reporters. ""If being neutral means staying out of NATO, then we’re already in that position. But what would safeguard our security in the long term? <...> Enshrining neutrality means changing your country’s constitution, and Ukraine won’t do that,"" Insider quoted Zelensky as saying. On October 6, Verkhovna Rada lawmaker Anna Skorokhod submitted a bill to parliament to enshrine Ukraine’s neutral status in the constitution. The bill has yet to be registered because registration requires the votes of 150 lawmakers. Another lawmaker, Alexey Goncharenko, whom Russia has placed on its list of terrorists and extremists, had previously proposed discussing neutral status for Ukraine. He said that to reach a peace settlement, Ukraine needs to make concessions, particularly on dropping its bid to join NATO, the status of the Russian language and the position of the canonical Ukrainian Orthodox Church.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:17:19 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218171,2026-11-15 03:30:22
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russian forces liberate Tersyanka in Zaporozhye Region — top brass,Russian forces liberate Tersyanka in Zaporozhye Region — top brass,"Russian forces liberate Tersyanka in Zaporozhye Region — top brass Troops from the Battlegroup East cleared more than 300 buildings while liberating the settlement, the Defense Ministry noted MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. Russian troops from the Battlegroup East have liberated Tersyanka in the Zaporozhye Region, the Defense Ministry said. ""Units of the Battlegroup East advanced deep into enemy defenses and liberated the settlement of Tersyanka in the Zaporozhye Region through active combat operations,"" the ministry reported. Troops from the Battlegroup East cleared more than 300 buildings while liberating the settlement, the ministry noted. ""Assault units of the Battlegroup East’s 29th Combined Arms Army’s 36th Separate Motor Rifle Brigade liberated the settlement of Tersyanka in the Zaporozhye Region, taking control of a major fortified enemy defensive area covering more than 10 square kilometers and clearing more than 300 buildings,"" the ministry said. It added that enemy personnel losses in the fighting for the settlement exceeded the equivalent of two platoons. Seven armored combat vehicles, six automobiles, 22 ground robotic systems and more than 70 heavy Baba-Yaga-type hexacopters were destroyed. ""The liberation of Tersyanka enabled units of the Battlegroup East to expand the area under their control in the Zaporozhye Region and take up new positions, creating ground for the battlegroup to advance further,"" the ministry stated. According to the report, the Ukrainian armed forces lost about 1,085 troops in the special military operation zone over the past 24 hours as a result of operations by Russian battlegroups. The ministry said the Ukrainian army lost more","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:04:22 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2218169,2026-11-15 03:30:26
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Farewell ceremony for Russian ambassador to US underway in Moscow,Farewell ceremony for Russian ambassador to US underway in Moscow,"Farewell ceremony for Russian ambassador to US underway in Moscow Among those paying their respects are Russian presidential aide Yury Ushakov and Deputy Foreign Ministers Sergey Ryabkov and Alexander Pankin MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. A farewell ceremony for Alexander Darchiev, Russia’s ambassador to the United States, is underway in Moscow, a TASS correspondent reports. Many of Darchiev’s colleagues and loved ones have gathered in the hall. They are laying flowers and taking turns paying their last respects. Wreaths in the hall include tributes from Russia’s senior officials. Among those paying their respects are Russian presidential aide Yury Ushakov and Deputy Foreign Ministers Sergey Ryabkov and Alexander Pankin. The ceremony is taking place in the farewell hall at Central Clinical Hospital No. 1, which is run by the Presidential Administrative Directorate. Russian Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Maria Zakharova previously said Darchiev died in Moscow on November 11 from a chronic illness.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:03:32 +0300",https://tass.com/society/2218167,2026-11-15 03:30:27
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,EC chief admits own decisions lead to gas overpayments — Russian MFA,EC chief admits own decisions lead to gas overpayments — Russian MFA,"EC chief admits own decisions lead to gas overpayments — Russian MFA Dmitry Birichevsky, director of the Russian Foreign Ministry’s Department of Economic Cooperation, stressed that ""Russia is a major player in the global energy market and a reliable, responsible supplier of natural gas"" MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen has admitted that the EU’s own decisions led it to overpay by 100 billion euros for gas imports in 2026, Dmitry Birichevsky, director of the Russian Foreign Ministry’s Department of Economic Cooperation, told TASS in an interview. ""The EU itself continues to buy energy from Russia, albeit in smaller volumes, and has paid $320 billion for those supplies since 2022. At the same time, European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen acknowledged that the EU has paid an extra 100 billion euros for its gas imports since the start of 2026 compared with 2025,"" he said. Birichevsky stressed that ""Russia is a major player in the global energy market and a reliable, responsible supplier of natural gas."" ""Our country has the world’s largest natural gas reserves and is its second-largest producer. Can a producer of that size be isolated as gas consumption rises? I think the question answers itself,"" the diplomat concluded.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:59:11 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2218141,2026-11-15 03:30:27
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,OSCE may fail to agree on 2027 chairmanship — Russian envoy,OSCE may fail to agree on 2027 chairmanship — Russian envoy,"OSCE may fail to agree on 2027 chairmanship — Russian envoy Some countries are engaged in nonstop shuttle diplomacy in search of a solution, Dmitry Polyansky said VIENNA, November 14. /TASS/. Member states of the Organization for Security and Cooperation in Europe (OSCE) are actively holding diplomatic consultations on which country will chair the organization in 2027, but they may fail to reach consensus, Russia’s Permanent Representative to the OSCE Dmitry Polyansky told TASS. ""I expect we’ll find some way forward. But we can’t rule out that possibility entirely,"" he said when asked whether the talks could end without an agreement. In that event, OSCE Secretary General Feridun Sinirlioglu would most likely oversee the organization’s work for a time, though that would require further decisions. ""The OSCE is a fairly resilient organization, so I think it will find a way forward even in that scenario,"" the diplomat noted. ""Some countries are engaged in nonstop shuttle diplomacy in search of a solution. The Americans are particularly active,"" Polyansky added. The envoy doubted that the issue would be fully resolved before the OSCE Ministerial Council meeting in Lugano in early December. He suggested that participants could reach some understandings at the meeting and formalize them later. Polyansky previously said Cyprus and Georgia are seeking the 2027 OSCE chairmanship. According to him, Turkey is blocking Cyprus’s bid while Georgia’s prospects are highly uncertain.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:52:08 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2218139,2026-11-15 03:30:28
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Italy rejects full German role in next-generation fighter project — media,Italy rejects full German role in next-generation fighter project — media,"Italy rejects full German role in next-generation fighter project — media Italian Defense Minister Guido Crosetto insisted that Berlin be granted observer status LONDON, November 14. /TASS/. Italy has rejected a UK proposal to bring Germany into the Future Combat Air System (FCAS) project to develop next-generation fighter jets, theFinancial Timesreported, citing sources. Italian Defense Minister Guido Crosetto strongly opposed full German participation at an online meeting with his UK and Japanese counterparts on the future of the fighter jet project, the newspaper reported. He insisted that Berlin be granted observer status. The Japanese government was also wary of the unexpected prospect of adding a new partner to an already complex project, the publication’s sources said. It expressed concern that Germany’s involvement could delay the program. The FT said Berlin would most likely reject observer status. An unnamed German official told the newspaper that the government found Italy’s proposal ""unacceptable"" and that Berlin would continue to press for full membership. UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham proposed bringing Germany into the fighter jet project in October during talks with German Chancellor Friedrich Merz. Berlin needed to look for alternatives after the Franco-German project to develop a next-generation European fighter jet collapsed this summer following years of disagreements between the two sides. The UK, Italy and Japan agreed in December 2022 to develop a sixth-generation fighter jet. The aircraft is intended as an alternative to fighters being developed in the United States. The UK’s BAE Systems, Italy’s Leonardo and J","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:56:03 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218137,2026-11-15 03:30:29
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Armenian PM says plans three visits to Russia in December,Armenian PM says plans three visits to Russia in December,"Armenian PM says plans three visits to Russia in December Nikol Pashinyan hopes Yerevan can maintain a friendly atmosphere in the relations with Moscow YEREVAN, November 14. /TASS/. Armenian Prime Minister Nikol Pashinyan plans to visit Russia three times in December, he said at the Institute of International and European Affairs in Dublin. ""I’ll be in Russia three times in December. I’ll make three visits for talks. I’ll go to Russia for talks on December 3, 11 and 22. I hope we can maintain a friendly atmosphere in our relations with Russia,"" Pashinyan said. Over the past few months, there have been repeated reports that Pashinyan was preparing to visit Russia, but neither side had confirmed an exact date. In briefings and interviews, he has said that relations with Moscow are undergoing a transformation and will inevitably change. On September 3, Pashinyan said that he and Russian President Vladimir Putin had agreed to take stock of Armenian-Russian relations during their September 2 meeting in Bishkek.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:16:14 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2218135,2026-11-15 03:30:33
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Hungary plans to complete Paks II audit by year-end,Hungary plans to complete Paks II audit by year-end,"Hungary plans to complete Paks II audit by year-end Attila Sagodi, chairman of the board and CEO of Paks II, said Hungary’s new government is very interested in the project, but decision-makers do not yet have all the information they need ANTALYA /Turkey/, November 14. /TASS/. Hungary plans to complete its audit of the Paks II nuclear power plant construction project by the end of this year, Attila Sagodi, chairman of the board and CEO of Paks II, told TASS. ""I took over as head of the nuclear power plant construction project just four months ago, so I’m still gaining experience and learning about the project. We’re now conducting a formal, thorough audit of the entire project, covering everything from the design, the readiness of the design documentation and the work schedule to the financial, technological and legal aspects. We plan to complete the audit by the end of this year, then see whether we need to look into any issues in more depth or do any additional work,"" Sagodi stated. He said Hungary’s new government is very interested in the Paks II project, but decision-makers do not yet have all the information they need. ""They’re gathering that data now. This is an extremely complex project for them and effectively the largest in Hungary. Everyone recognizes that, and those in leadership positions need to get into the details and understand what’s happening. Only then can they make a considered decision and choose the right course,"" he said. Sagodi highlighted that financing is also a complex issue. ""The question goes beyond whether the government will provide funding. The EPC contract has a complex structure that imposes obligations on all parties, so the government can’t simply decide to do things in a w","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:58:55 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2218133,2026-11-15 03:30:36
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Latvian Foreign Ministry drafts ban on Russian, Belarusian grain transit","Latvian Foreign Ministry drafts ban on Russian, Belarusian grain transit","Latvian Foreign Ministry drafts ban on Russian, Belarusian grain transit The ministry proposes imposing the ban through national sanctions, the Delfi news website reported VILNIUS, November 14. /TASS/. Latvian Foreign Minister Baiba Braze said her ministry had drafted a government regulation that would ban the transit of grain from Russia and Belarus through Latvia. ""The Foreign Ministry has prepared and submitted a draft Cabinet regulation that would ban the transit of Russian and Belarusian grain through Latvia,"" Braze wrote on X. The ministry proposes imposing the ban through national sanctions, the Delfi news website reported, citing Latvia’s Foreign Ministry. It said this approach would allow Latvia to impose restrictions, monitor compliance and hold violators accountable. Latvia had previously explored an EU-wide ban on the transit of grain from Russia and Belarus, but the initiative did not garner enough support among EU member states. Baltic leaders say Russia is preventing Ukrainian grain from reaching global markets while trying to profit from shipping its own grain through the EU using the bloc’s infrastructure. On October 9, Latvia, Lithuania and Estonia sent a joint letter to Brussels calling for a ban on the transit of Russian grain exports through the EU.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:54:05 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2218129,2026-11-15 03:30:37
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Europe hit by self-imposed ban on Russian gas — Russian MFA,Europe hit by self-imposed ban on Russian gas — Russian MFA,"Europe hit by self-imposed ban on Russian gas — Russian MFA Dmitry Birichevsky, director of the Russian Foreign Ministry’s Department of Economic Cooperation, noted that the EU’s initiative is in line with the politicized sanctions policy of recent years aimed at isolating Russia economically MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. Europe has faced significant setbacks since imposing a self-ban on Russian gas, Dmitry Birichevsky, director of the Russian Foreign Ministry’s Department of Economic Cooperation, said in an interview with TASS. ""It is clear to us that these measures are entirely untenable. Such self-imposed bans and other restrictions directly hurt those who impose them,"" he said. ""European economies and end users, both industry and households, now face sharply higher costs, while businesses are shutting down or moving to other jurisdictions. As Russian President Vladimir Putin said at the 8th summit of the Gas Exporting Countries Forum in Moscow, ‘Whoever digs a pit will fall into it,’"" the diplomat stated. Birichevsky noted that the EU’s initiative to impose a complete ban on imports of Russian pipeline gas and liquefied natural gas (LNG) is in line with the politicized sanctions policy of recent years aimed at isolating Russia economically. ""It was the Europeans who began severing the longstanding, mutually beneficial energy ties with our country that dated back to Soviet times,"" he recalled.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:11:22 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2218127,2026-11-15 03:30:38
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,US company Medline reports seven deaths linked to its products,US company Medline reports seven deaths linked to its products,"US company Medline reports seven deaths linked to its products It makes orthopedic mattresses and beds among other products NEW YORK, November 14. /TASS/. Medline, a US company that makes orthopedic mattresses and beds among other products, said seven people had died due to causes linked to its goods. ""As of November 8, 2026, Medline has received reports related to seven deaths and 35 serious injuries associated with these issues,"" the company said in a press release. Medline added that it recalled the products and stopped making them in October because of potential fire and entrapment hazards that could result in injury or death.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:58:59 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2218121,2026-11-15 03:30:39
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Europeans mum on Abu Dhabi talks at latest OSCE meeting — Russian mission,Europeans mum on Abu Dhabi talks at latest OSCE meeting — Russian mission,"Europeans mum on Abu Dhabi talks at latest OSCE meeting — Russian mission Russia’s permanent representative to the organization Dmitry Polyansky stressed that the Europeans came with old talking points VIENNA, November 14. /TASS/. At the latest meeting of the OSCE Permanent Council, European delegations reiterated their previous positions on the Ukrainian conflict and did not mention the Abu Dhabi talks even once in their statements, Russia’s permanent representative to the organization Dmitry Polyansky told TASS. ""The Europeans seemed completely out of touch. They came with their old talking points. They didn’t even mention the word 'Abu Dhabi' once, as if it were happening on another planet,"" the diplomat emphasized. According to him, only the Ukrainian and US delegations mentioned the talks in Abu Dhabi. At the same time, the Ukrainian representatives spoke in their usual Russophobic tone, while the US representative emphasized the importance of the efforts all sides are making in connection with the negotiation process.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:00:53 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2218103,2026-11-15 03:30:39
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Ukraine loses over $7 billion due to nearly four months of port downtime,Ukraine loses over $7 billion due to nearly four months of port downtime,"Ukraine loses over $7 billion due to nearly four months of port downtime Commercial merchant ships continue to avoid the ports of Odessa, Chernomorsk, and Yuzhny MOSCOW, November 14. /TASS/. Ukraine has lost over $7 billion in foreign exchange revenue due to the nearly four-month-long shutdown of the Odessa Region ports, according to TASS calculations. Commercial merchant ships continue to avoid the ports of Odessa, Chernomorsk, and Yuzhny. Only vessels affiliated with the Ukrainian armed forces are calling at those ports. Meanwhile, maritime trade is being routed through the Danube ports of Izmail in Ukraine and Constanta in Romania, which together can handle no more than one-third of the exports that previously passed through the Odessa Region ports. Consequently, Ukraine exported only about half of its planned agricultural exports in October. Exports of metallurgical products ceased entirely at the end of September due to the shutdown of steel mills. These products together accounted for approximately 65% of Ukraine’s total exports and $26 billion in foreign exchange earnings per year. By utilizing the railway network and Danube ports for exports, Ukraine has partially reduced its losses, albeit only to a limited extent, from approximately $70 million per day in August to $50-60 million from September to November. The Odessa Region ports have been shut down since July 22.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:35:13 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2218101,2026-11-15 03:30:40
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"From Karakoram to Arabian Sea, Ep. 7: Woven Together","From Karakoram to Arabian Sea, Ep. 7: Woven Together","From Karakoram to Arabian Sea, Ep. 7: Woven Together From Karakoram to Arabian Sea, Ep. 7: Woven Together Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied From the towering Karakoram mountains in the north to the shores of the Arabian Sea in the south, join CGTN's Danial Khan on a 12-part journey across Pakistan, following the China-Pakistan Economic Corridor (CPEC). Along the way, the series explores the infrastructure, industries and communities at the heart of Pakistan's development and the growing cooperation between China and Pakistan. In this episode, Danial explores Faisalabad, where Chinese technology is helping shape the future of Pakistan's textile hub. He visits factories to see how Chinese machinery is transforming weaving, digital printing and garment production, and meets the owners and workers behind the process. Through their stories, he discovers how shared expertise, new skills and a spirit of cooperation are bringing fresh opportunities to local communities and helping the Pakistani industry move forward.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:22:11 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-14/From-Karakoram-to-Arabian-Sea-Ep-7-Woven-Together-1S4cQePUc5G/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:41
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Hamas says senior armed commander killed in Israeli strike,Hamas says senior armed commander killed in Israeli strike,"Hamas says senior armed commander killed in Israeli strike Hamas says senior armed commander killed in Israeli strike Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Hamas' armed wing said on Sunday that ​a senior commander who helped plan and oversee the ‌October 7, 2023, attack on Israel had been killed in an Israeli air strike. The Al-Qassam Brigades identified the commander as Samir Abu ​Younis, 53, the commander of its Rafah brigade, and ​said he was killed on Saturday. The Israeli military said on Sunday that it had struck a senior commander ​in Hamas' armed wing but did not identify him. Medics said ​Abu Younis was killed, and others were wounded in an air strike that targeted him in a street in the Mawasi area of ​Khan Younis in the southern Gaza Strip. Hamas said Abu ​Younis joined Hamas' armed wing in 1991 and had held several senior ‌operational roles in Rafah before becoming commander of the brigade. Hamas said his funeral would be held on Sunday afternoon in Khan Younis. An October 2025 ceasefire halted major fighting but has ​not stopped ​Israeli attacks or secured Hamas' disarmament. Gaza health authorities say at least 1,600 Palestinians have been killed since ​the ceasefire went into effect. Five Israeli ​soldiers have been killed during the same period. Palestinian authorities say more than 74,000 people have been killed in Israel's military campaign against Gaza, ​launched after Hamas-led fighters killed abou","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:58:03 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-15/Hamas-says-senior-armed-commander-killed-in-Israeli-strike-1S5gM102H28/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:41
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"China, US maintain close communication on tariff reduction arrangement","China, US maintain close communication on tariff reduction arrangement","China, US maintain close communication on tariff reduction arrangement China and the United States are maintaining close communication on implementing a reciprocal tariff-reduction framework that would cover $30 billion worth of products from each side, China's Ministry of Commerce said on Thursday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied China's Ministry of Commerce in Beijing. /VCG China and the United States are maintaining close communication on implementing a reciprocal tariff-reduction framework that would cover $30 billion worth of products from each side, China's Ministry of Commerce said on Thursday. He Yadong, the ministry's spokesperson, made the remarks at a regular press conference, saying the arrangement would help stabilize and expand bilateral trade and had raised high expectations among business communities in both countries. He expressed hope that the two sides would work together to advance the implementation of the arrangement at an early date and create more favorable conditions for bilateral agricultural trade. China and the United States are maintaining close communication on their respective concerns regarding trade and investment, He said, adding that progress will be announced in due course.","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:08:54 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/China-US-maintain-close-communication-on-tariff-reduction-arrangement-1S0KbRF7Adi/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:41
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Chinese tech helps Australian iron ore giant go green,Chinese tech helps Australian iron ore giant go green,"Chinese tech helps Australian iron ore giant go green Chinese tech helps Australian iron ore giant go green Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied As APEC economies advance green transition and seek sustainable supply chains for critical minerals, Chinese technology is helping western Australia's mining sector cut emissions and shift toward renewable power. CGTN Correspondent Greg Navarro reports.","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:46:59 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/Chinese-tech-helps-Australian-iron-ore-giant-go-green-1S0HsfVm8yA/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:41
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Breaking stereotypes: Are Chinese products really just cheap?,Breaking stereotypes: Are Chinese products really just cheap?,"Breaking stereotypes: Are Chinese products really just cheap? Breaking stereotypes: Are Chinese products really just cheap? Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied ""Affordable prices do not mean low quality."" Andrea Castillo, a Mexican university student, explains how her perception of Chinese products has changed. From the stereotypes she held as a child to her appreciation through firsthand experience, her story shows how real-life experiences can challenge cultural prejudices.","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:12:43 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/Breaking-stereotypes-Are-Chinese-products-really-just-cheap--1S0E6SNAGRi/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:42
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China's anti-poverty victory shines a light on other nations' paths,China's anti-poverty victory shines a light on other nations' paths,"China's anti-poverty victory shines a light on other nations' paths For other developing countries looking for their own strategies, China's experience is extremely valuable. Global progress against poverty has slowed in many regions, and solutions require flexibility. Perhaps China's most useful contribution isn't a beaten track for others to follow, but rather a light shining on what's possible through hard-won experience. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Guan Chao Copied In February 2021, Chinese President Xi Jinping declared the elimination of absolute poverty, after the final 98.99 million rural Chinese residents living under the then national poverty line had all been lifted out of poverty. It marked the end of a four-decade campaign. Data from the Chinese government and the World Bank shows that approximately 800 million people were raised above the extreme-poverty threshold over the period, accounting for more than 70% of global poverty reduction. That declaration was followed by a five-year transition period intended to consolidate gains and prevent people from backsliding into poverty. It concluded at the end of 2025 with the establishment of regularized anti-relapse mechanisms. International observers were taking note. Building risk-prevention mechanisms There's no guarantee that people who emerge from poverty will stay out of it. Illness, crop failure, job loss, or a single large expense can push a household back below the threshold. China's response has been to build a follow-up system that tracks those risks. It relies on various channels: self-reporting by rural households, routine assessments by local officials, and data screening for sudden changes in income, medical spending, housing and school attendance. When ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:02:53 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-14/-China-s-anti-poverty-victory-shines-a-light-on-other-nations-paths-1S4bmqXDbLW/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:42
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Chinese vice president meets Turkish president on sidelines of COP31,Chinese vice president meets Turkish president on sidelines of COP31,"Chinese vice president meets Turkish president on sidelines of COP31 Chinese Vice President Han Zheng, as President Xi Jinping's special representative, met with Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan on Wednesday on the sidelines of the Antalya Leaders' Summit of the 31st United Nations Climate Change Conference (COP31). Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese Vice President Han Zheng, as President Xi Jinping's special representative, met with Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan on Wednesday on the sidelines of the Antalya Leaders' Summit of the 31st United Nations Climate Change Conference (COP31). Conveying President Xi's cordial greetings and best wishes to Erdogan, Han said that China and Türkiye enjoy a long history of friendly exchanges. Under the strategic guidance of Xi and Erdogan, China-Türkiye relations have maintained sound and steady development, Han said, noting that China stands ready to work with Türkiye to advance high-quality Belt and Road cooperation, deepen practical cooperation across various fields, and promote the continuous development of the China-Türkiye strategic cooperative relationship. Noting that the two heads of state have reached an important political consensus on accommodating each other's core interests and major concerns, Han said the two sides should support each other in pursuing the paths chosen by their own people and safeguarding their respective national sovereignty, security and development interests. The two countries should elevate the level of practical cooperation, he said, stressing that China is ready to encourage more Chinese enterprises to invest and start bu","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:58:41 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/Chinese-vice-president-meets-Turkish-president-on-sidelines-of-COP31-1S0cgQ5GYs8/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:42
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China flags six problems with Belgium-Chile BBNJ secretariat bid,China flags six problems with Belgium-Chile BBNJ secretariat bid,"China flags six problems with Belgium-Chile BBNJ secretariat bid China flags six problems with Belgium-Chile BBNJ secretariat bid Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied China's Foreign Ministry spokesperson Mao Ning on Thursday criticized a joint bid by Belgium and Chile to host the secretariat of the Agreement on Marine Biodiversity of Areas Beyond National Jurisdiction (BBNJ), saying it has at least six ""non-conformities."" Belgium and Chile announced on November 6 that they would jointly bid, proposing to base the secretariat in Valparaiso, Chile, the information-exchange mechanism in Brussels, and subsidiary body meetings in Brussels – without consulting the broader membership. Mao said the move improperly handles matters that should be decided by the Conference of the Parties (COP). The six problems: it violates the agreement, under which the COP decides the secretariat's location and the mechanism's setup; it violates procedural justice by bundling two distinct issues to force a package deal; it violates international practice, since treaty secretariats and information-exchange mechanisms are normally co-located, and a trans-oceanic split would raise costs and hurt efficiency; it violates geographic balance, as most major international bodies are in Europe and none in Asia, and Brussels – home to NATO and the EU and a non-coastal city – would widen the digital divide; it violates fair competition by politicizing the bid; and ","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:58:39 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/China-flags-six-problems-with-Belgium-Chile-BBNJ-secretariat-bid-1S0Q5Ek3uCI/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:42
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Several schools in Italy evacuated after emailed bomb threats,Several schools in Italy evacuated after emailed bomb threats,"Several schools in Italy evacuated after emailed bomb threats New bomb threat emails have been sent to schools in several parts of Italy on Thursday, including the Veneto, Liguria, Umbria and Lazio regions, as well as Sicily, local media reported. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Officers search an elementary school in Rome after authorities evacuated schools across the country following a bomb threat, Rome, Italy, November 11, 2026. /VCG New bomb threat emails have been sent to schools in several parts of Italy on Thursday, including the Veneto, Liguria, Umbria and Lazio regions, as well as Sicily, local media reported. Some schools have been evacuated, while checks are underway at others, according to ANSA News Agency. A series of schools received bomb threat emails, with the provisional figure standing at 1,803 institutions, according to Italian newspaper Corriere della Sera. Media reported that the threatening emails were all signed ""Mikhail Andropov,"" the same name used in the emails sent on Wednesday.","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:43:59 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/news-1S0WU96uphK/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:42
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Raffarin: Asia-Pacific region is important for world's economy,Raffarin: Asia-Pacific region is important for world's economy,"Raffarin: Asia-Pacific region is important for world's economy Raffarin: Asia-Pacific region is important for world's economy Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Copied The 2026 APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting opens next week. CGTN’s You Yang sits down with former French Prime Minister Jean-Pierre Raffarin to hear his views on the key gathering.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:15:41 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-14/Raffarin-Asia-Pacific-region-is-important-for-world-s-economy-1S48aNef61y/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:43
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,World Diabetes Day: South Africa pushes early detection,World Diabetes Day: South Africa pushes early detection,"World Diabetes Day: South Africa pushes early detection The World Health Organization (WHO) says diabetes can be managed through a combination of healthy eating, regular physical activity and medication. Complications can also be prevented or delayed through regular screening and timely treatment. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied On World Diabetes Day, observed on Saturday, November 14, hundreds of Johannesburg residents received free health screenings as part of an awareness campaign aimed at strengthening South Africa’s fight against the disease. Health professionals used the initiative to raise awareness of diabetes among local residents, a potentially life-threatening condition affecting hundreds of millions of people worldwide. ""In South Africa, the number one killer (disease) used to be HIV. It has now changed, and the number one killer is diabetes. All the figures are showing that,"" said Health Minister Aaron Motsoaledi. According to the latest mortality statistics from Statistics South Africa, diabetes was among the leading underlying causes of death in the country in 2024, accounting for more than 28,700 deaths. The Johannesburg screening campaign also encouraged residents to take a proactive approach to their health by undergoing regular medical check-ups. ""Diabetes is a problem because you can't tell when you have it. You only start seeing it when your life is changing,"" said local resident Honey Mchunu. ""That’s why it's important to eat healthy and watch what we eat. Sometimes it runs in the family; others say they got it because of how they eat."" The World Health Organization (","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:51:43 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-15/World-Diabetes-Day-South-Africa-pushes-early-detection-1S4qWiRknUA/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:43
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China willing to further boost political mutual trust with Thailand,China willing to further boost political mutual trust with Thailand,"China willing to further boost political mutual trust with Thailand Chinese Premier Li Qiang said on Friday that China is willing to work with Thailand to further consolidate the foundation of political mutual trust, support each other's core interests and major concerns, tap cooperation potential in various fields and deliver more tangible results to better benefit the peoples of both countries. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese Premier Li Qiang (L) meets with Thai Prime Minister Anutin Charnvirakul in Bangkok, Thailand, November 13, 2026. /Xinhua Chinese Premier Li Qiang said on Friday that China is willing to work with Thailand to further consolidate the foundation of political mutual trust, support each other's core interests and major concerns, tap cooperation potential in various fields and deliver more tangible results to better benefit the peoples of both countries. Li made the remarks when meeting with Thai Prime Minister Anutin Charnvirakul. He said Chinese President Xi Jinping met with Anutin during the Thai prime minister's official visit to China in July, and the two leaders jointly charted the course for the development of China-Thailand relations. Li said that, with his visit to Thailand, he and Anutin have exchanged visits within four months, fully demonstrating the high level of bilateral relations. Noting that both China and Thailand are at an important stage of national development, Li said China firmly supports the Thai government in smoothly carrying out its work. China is willing to work with Thailand to make good use of mechanisms such as the ""2+2"" strategic dialogue between foreign and defense ministers and the joint committee on economic and trade cooperatio","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:57:10 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-14/China-willing-to-further-boost-political-mutual-trust-with-Thailand-1S3vVvzVNKg/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:43
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Premier Li says China ready to deepen economic exchanges with Thailand,Premier Li says China ready to deepen economic exchanges with Thailand,"Premier Li says China ready to deepen economic exchanges with Thailand Chinese Premier Li Qiang said on Saturday that China is ready to deepen trade and economic exchanges with Thailand and accelerate the construction of the China-Thailand railway. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese Premier Li Qiang said on Saturday that China is ready to deepen trade and economic exchanges with Thailand and accelerate the construction of the China-Thailand railway. Li made the remarks during talks with Sophon Zaram, president of Thailand's National Assembly and speaker of the House of Representatives, in Bangkok. China encourages enterprises from both countries to cooperate in emerging sectors such as new energy and electronic information, strengthen collaborative innovation and jointly promote industrial upgrading, Li said. He said that in recent years, China-Thailand relations had maintained steady and sound development, with fruitful cooperation across various fields. Last year, the two countries held grand celebrations marking the 50th anniversary of diplomatic relations and 50 golden years of China-Thailand friendship, Li said, noting that bilateral relations now stand at a new historic starting point and face new development opportunities. Looking ahead, Li said China is willing to work with Thailand to carry forward their traditional friendship, consolidate political mutual trust and make solid progress in building a China-Thailand community with a shared future, so as to bring greater benefits to the two peoples and better serve the modernizat","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:55:11 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-14/Premier-Li-urges-stronger-China-Thailand-cooperation-in-emerging-areas-1S3Y77VWMYo/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:43
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Chinese official discusses China's global influence at Paris forum,Chinese official discusses China's global influence at Paris forum,"Chinese official discusses China's global influence at Paris forum The ninth Paris Peace Forum was held in the French capital on November 10-11. During the forum, China's global impact emerged as a key theme. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Kong Quan, executive director of the Sixth China Economic and Social Council, former deputy director of the Office of the Central Commission for Foreign Affairs and former Chinese ambassador to France, speaks during a session titled ""Making Sense of China's Global Role and Impact,"" at the Paris Peace Forum in Paris, France, November 11, 2026. /VCG The ninth Paris Peace Forum was held in the French capital on November 10-11. During the forum, China's global impact emerged as a key theme. With a focus on reinforcing multilateral cooperation to confront global challenges across security, climate, technology and development, the forum featured discussions on how nations must strengthen cooperation while preserving sovereignty to effectively address worldwide crises. Kong Quan, the executive director of the Sixth China Economic and Social Council, former deputy director of the Office of the Central Commission for Foreign Affairs and former Chinese ambassador to France, attended the forum and spoke at a session titled ""Making Sense of China's Global Role and Impact."" In his remarks, Kong outlined ""responsibility,"" ""mutual respect,"" ""multilateralism"" and ""cooperation based on respect for sovereignty"" as four key terms that help better understand China's foreign policy. Ko","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:01:42 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/Chinese-official-discusses-China-s-global-influence-at-Paris-forum-1S0xlN8Katy/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:44
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Microsoft apologizes for global outage, rules out cyberattack","Microsoft apologizes for global outage, rules out cyberattack","Microsoft apologizes for global outage, rules out cyberattack Microsoft apologizes for global outage, rules out cyberattack Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied In this posed picture, a smartphone displays the Microsoft sign-in page in London, November 13, 2026. /VCG Microsoft has apologized for a global service outage that disrupted millions of users worldwide, saying the incident was triggered by an earlier network capacity upgrade and was unrelated to cyberattacks or AI agents, according to CCTV News. The company said it could not give a timeline for full service restoration. Earlier updates described recovery progress as ""encouraging,"" while engineers were working to clear residual impacts from the failure. The breakdown took down Teams, Outlook and its AI-powered Copilot across at least 70 countries. Microsoft also warned users they may continue to face intermittent access issues. Public services across multiple nations felt the ripple effects. Britain's NHS said the disruption inevitably caused disruption for staff, though appointments remained on track. Some schools switched to phone-only contact with parents. US federal government agencies and court systems also reported service problems.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:29:04 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-14/Microsoft-apologizes-for-global-outage-rules-out-cyberattack-1S3I9qOB6F2/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:44
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,FAA lifts nationwide ground stop after thousands of flights disrupted,FAA lifts nationwide ground stop after thousands of flights disrupted,"FAA lifts nationwide ground stop after thousands of flights disrupted FAA lifts nationwide ground stop after thousands of flights disrupted Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied United planes wait outside their gates at George Bush Intercontinental Airport in Houston after the Federal Aviation Administration grounded all flights nationwide on November 13, 2026. /VCG The US Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) lifted a nationwide ground stop on Friday evening after hours of disruption affected thousands of flights across the country. Flight cancellations and delays are expected to continue through the weekend. Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy blamed the country's aging air traffic control system for the nationwide ground stop, saying at a press conference that the system was ""incredibly old."" He said earlier on the social media platform X that the FAA had issued a nationwide ground stop following a ""communication issue"" impacting all air route traffic control centers. US media reported that the FAA had issued an advisory citing ""extraordinary circumstances"" and ""reasons of safety"" as grounds for the nationwide ground stop, describing it as a rare move. More than 10,000 flights were disrupted, according to a report by CNBC, which noted that more flight cancellations were expected to extend into Saturday. The nationwide ground stop was the first since January 2023, when a key FAA computer system malfunctioned, and the second since the aft","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:18:36 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-14/news-1S3CjcBaTg4/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:44
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,A robot showdown like no other,A robot showdown like no other,"A robot showdown like no other A robot showdown like no other Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied What kind of competition could leave the author of Young China, Zak Dychtwald, on the edge of his seat? Forget picking a character in a video game. Here, university students build their own robots and send them head-to-head in competition. After a year of preparation, university teams across China converge in Shenzhen for an electrifying showdown, where the city's appetite for innovation meets the next generation of engineering talent.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:12:58 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-14/A-robot-showdown-like-no-other-1S3LkRzgoyk/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:44
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Microsoft announces service 'restored,' global outage over","Microsoft announces service 'restored,' global outage over","Microsoft announces service 'restored,' global outage over Tech giant Microsoft said on Saturday it had ""restored service"" to customers, effectively bringing to a close a massive outage that caused chaos and disrupted public services and businesses around the world. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A Microsoft Outlook logo. /VCG Tech giant Microsoft said on Saturday it had ""restored service"" to customers, effectively bringing to a closea massive outagethat caused chaos and disrupted public services and businesses around the world. ""We have completed our efforts to address the underlying issue of the incident and restored service to the remaining impacted customers and regions,"" the US-based company said in an X post. Microsoft had already reported a ""broad recovery"" for Outlook email and other services the day before, stating that the major disruption was due to a technical issue and ""not related to cyber or AI/agents."" The outage swept the globe on Thursday, taking the company's products offline in at least 74 countries and territories across the Americas, Europe, Asia and Africa, according to the monitoring site Downdetector. Microsoft had attributed the disruption to ""elevated load"" on its infrastructure. It said the outage affected its Outlook email service, as well as its Teams communication platform and Copilot AI assistant. Microsoft warned on Saturday of an ""active phishing campaign"" exploiting the disruption, with fake emails imitating its service notifications. The emails, detected on Friday, told users that messages blocked during the outage would ","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:46:04 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-15/Microsoft-announces-service-restored-global-outage-over-1S5bb8KYL4c/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:45
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,US envoys Witkoff and Kushner arrive at Kremlin,US envoys Witkoff and Kushner arrive at Kremlin,"US envoys Witkoff and Kushner arrive at Kremlin US envoys Witkoff and Kushner arrive at Kremlin Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The United States' special envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner have arrived at the Kremlin for a meeting with Russian President Putin on Thursday, according to TASS.","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:07:51 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/news-1S0Uk2fR5pm/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:45
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"China, Thailand eye higher-level cooperation in digital, green sectors","China, Thailand eye higher-level cooperation in digital, green sectors","China, Thailand eye higher-level cooperation in digital, green sectors Chinese Premier Li Qiang on Saturday called on Chinese and Thai enterprises to seize new opportunities and elevate bilateral cooperation by expanding from ""dining tables and taste buds"" to ""digital intelligence and green development,"" strengthening industrial synergy and supply chain integration, and moving up the global value chain. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese Premier Li Qiang on Saturday called on Chinese and Thai enterprises to seize new opportunities and elevate bilateral cooperation by expanding from ""dining tables and taste buds"" to ""digital intelligence and green development."" The two sides could strengthen industrial synergy and supply chain integration, and move up the global value chain, he said. Li made the remarks while attending a symposium with Chinese and Thai entrepreneurs, along with Thai Prime Minister Anutin Charnvirakul, in Bangkok. After listening to remarks from representatives of both countries' business communities, Li said that as China and Thailand work together to usher in a new golden 50 years of bilateral relations, new opportunities are emerging for economic and trade cooperation. To begin with, China and Thailand enjoy the stability brought by high-level mutual trust and friendship, Li said. In today's world marked by turbulence and uncertainty, stability has become a scarce resource, he said, noting that China-Thailand relations and cooperation have demonstrated strong stability. Close and regular communication between the leaders of the two countries, along with strong people-to-people ties and cultural affinity, has provided businesses in both countries with a stable and predictab","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:05:56 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-14/China-Thailand-eye-higher-level-cooperation-in-digital-green-sectors-1S4nYHxKgtW/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:45
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,ROK's foreign minister to visit China,ROK's foreign minister to visit China,"ROK's foreign minister to visit China ROK's foreign minister to visit China Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A file photo of Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Korea Cho Hyun. /VCG As agreed between China and the Republic of Korea (ROK), Minister of Foreign Affairs of the ROK Cho Hyun will visit China from November 13 to 14, a Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson announced on Thursday.","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:48:19 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/ROK-s-foreign-minister-to-visit-China-1S0K2OiNtvO/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:45
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Xi Jinping's key quotes on building a greener, sustainable future","Xi Jinping's key quotes on building a greener, sustainable future","Xi Jinping's key quotes on building a greener, sustainable future Chinese President Xi Jinping has repeatedly emphasized China's commitment to environmental protection, ecological conservation and green development. Noting that Earth is a shared home, Xi has stressed that however the world may change, China will not slow down its climate actions. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The 31st United Nations Climate Change Conference is underway in Antalya, Türkiye. At the Leaders' Summit during the conference on Wednesday, Chinese Vice President Han Zheng, as President Xi Jinping's special representative, put forward a four-point proposal in light of the increasingly apparent adverse effects of global climate change. President Xi has repeatedly emphasized China's commitment to environmental protection, ecological conservation and green development. Noting that Earth is a shared home, Xi has stressed that however the world may change, China will not slow down its climate actions. Here are some of his key quotes in this regard.","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:47:05 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/Xi-Jinping-s-key-quotes-on-building-a-greener-sustainable-future-1S0KftQP9FC/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:45
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Chinese VP urges Global South solidarity to achieve green development,Chinese VP urges Global South solidarity to achieve green development,"Chinese VP urges Global South solidarity to achieve green development Chinese Vice President Han Zheng said on Wednesday that countries of the Global South are bound by a shared future, and only through solidarity and cooperation can they achieve green development. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Participants arrive for the COP31 United Nations climate summit in Antalya, Türkiye, November 11, 2026. /VCG Chinese Vice President Han Zheng said on Wednesday that countries of the Global South are bound by a shared future, and only through solidarity and cooperation can they achieve green development. Han made the remarks while attending the High-level Forum on South-South Cooperation on Climate Change in Antalya, Türkiye. In his speech, the Chinese vice president said that climate change concerns the common future of humanity and requires the joint efforts of all countries to address it. Chinese President Xi Jinping has said that as a member of the Global South, China will vigorously deepen South-South cooperation and continue to provide help for fellow developing countries to the best of its capability, Han stressed. Han put forward three proposals. First, the Global South should join hands to advance green development and work together to protect our planet. Firmly committed to a green development path that prioritizes ecological conservation, China has built the world's largest clean power generation system and the most complete new energy industrial chain, said Han, adding that China stands ready to deepen cooperation with countries of the Global South in ar","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:34:58 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/Chinese-VP-urges-Global-South-solidarity-to-achieve-green-development-1S0fKA6cc2k/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:45
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China concerned over certain EU countries' ban on Chinese equipment,China concerned over certain EU countries' ban on Chinese equipment,"China concerned over certain EU countries' ban on Chinese equipment China has expressed serious concern over the moves by some European Union countries to ban equipment from Chinese companies, China's Ministry of Commerce said on Thursday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied China's Ministry of Commerce in Beijing. /VCG China has expressed serious concern over the moves by some European Union countries to ban equipment from Chinese companies, China's Ministry of Commerce said on Thursday. China has consistently maintained that 5G is critical infrastructure for the development of the global digital economy, and that its construction and operation should respect market principles, technological neutrality, and international rules, He Yadong, a ministry spokesperson, said during a regular press conference. China firmly opposes the politicization of technological issues and the overstretching of the concept of national security, He said. China hopes that the relevant countries will promptly correct their erroneous practices and provide a fair, just and non-discriminatory business environment for Chinese companies, the spokesperson added.","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:23:41 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/China-concerned-over-certain-EU-countries-ban-on-Chinese-equipment-1S0Q3tbRbos/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:45
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Ambassador Xie Feng calls for steady development of China-US relations,Ambassador Xie Feng calls for steady development of China-US relations,"Ambassador Xie Feng calls for steady development of China-US relations Chinese Ambassador to the United States Xie Feng has urged joint efforts to faithfully implement the important consensus reached by Chinese and US leaders, translate the vision into concrete action at a faster pace, and promote the steady and sustained development of a constructive China-US relationship of strategic stability. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese Ambassador to the United States Xie Feng speaks at the Gala Dinner 2026 Celebrating 60 Years of the National Committee on US-China Relations in New York, US, November 10, 2026. /Chinese Embassy in the US Chinese Ambassador to the United States Xie Feng has urged joint efforts to faithfully implement the important consensus reached by Chinese and US leaders, translate the vision into concrete action at a faster pace, and promote the steady and sustained development of a constructive China-US relationship of strategic stability. Speaking at the Gala Dinner 2026 Celebrating 60 Years of the National Committee on US-China Relations on Tuesday, Xie said, ""Across the Pacific, a consensus is growing ever stronger: China and the United States stand to gain from cooperation and lose from confrontation, and it is vital for our two major countries to find a right way to get along."" He said that this year holds historic and landmark significance for China-US relations. ""President Xi Jinping and President Donald Trump exchanged state visits within half a year. The two sides have agreed on building a constructive China-US relationship of strategic stability on the basis of respect, fairness and reciprocity, sending a clear signal that China and the United States can compl","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:31:48 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/Ambassador-Xie-Feng-calls-for-steady-development-of-China-US-relations-1S0oWtP3kkw/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:46
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Xi's Shenzhen visits show China's commitment to reform and opening up,Xi's Shenzhen visits show China's commitment to reform and opening up,"Xi's Shenzhen visits show China's commitment to reform and opening up In November 1991, China officially joined APEC. Thirty-five years later, China is bringing APEC to Shenzhen, the very place where China's opening up to the world began, and as global leaders gather to explore ways to advance development, the world will see China's opening up to the world taking on new dimensions. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese President Xi Jinping is set to attend the 2026 APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting in Shenzhen, in south China's Guangdong Province, marking his fourth visit to the birthplace of the country's market-based reforms. Selected in the late 1970s as a testing ground for China's transition to a more open and market-driven economy, Shenzhen benefited from its proximity to Hong Kong and Macao and its access to maritime trade routes. It has since transformed from a small fishing village into a key driver of China's economic development. Over the years, Xi has made three visits to Shenzhen. Though each of his visits came at a different stage of the city's and the nation's development, they shared a common thread: China's commitment to pressing ahead with reform and opening up. Chinese President Xi Jinping places a floral tribute at the bronze statue of Deng Xiaoping in Lianhuashan Park, Shenzhen, Guangdong Province, China, on October 14, 2012. /Xinhua 2012: the first inspection tour Spearheaded by former Chinese leader Deng Xiaoping, reform and opening up marked a watershed moment that fundamentally reshaped China's economic and social fabric. Launched in December 1978, the policy steered the country away from a centrally planned economy toward a market-oriented system, u","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:21:39 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-15/Xi-s-Shenzhen-visits-show-China-s-commitment-to-reform-and-opening-up-1S4eOfT7K6Y/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:46
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Russia, Ukraine agree on prisoner swap, but no peace breakthrough","Russia, Ukraine agree on prisoner swap, but no peace breakthrough","Russia, Ukraine agree on prisoner swap, but no peace breakthrough Trilateral talks involving Russia, the United States and Ukraine ended on Wednesday in Abu Dhabi, the capital of the United Arab Emirates (UAE), with Russia and Ukraine reaching an agreement on a ""large-scale"" prisoner exchange. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A view of Abu Dhabi's skyline, United Arab Emirates, November 11, 2026. /VCG Trilateral talks involving Russia, the United States and Ukraine concluded on Wednesday in Abu Dhabi, the capital of the United Arab Emirates (UAE), with Russia and Ukraine reaching an agreement on a ""large-scale"" prisoner exchange. While the agreement marked a tangible outcome of the two-day discussions, no agreement was announced on a ceasefire, territorial disputes or long-term security guarantees. Officials' reactions to the progress Vladimir Medinsky, head of the Russian delegation, said the delegations had discussed humanitarian issues, with the future of European security being a central focus of the US-mediated talks. He added that the parties had reached understandings on some issues, without providing further details. Medinsky called for a fair security framework that takes into account the interests of all countries, arguing that the conflict in Ukraine had exposed shortcomings in Europe's security system. Jared Kushner, a member of the US negotiating team, told reporters that the discussions were thorough and covered all major issues, describing them as a good first step forward. He noted that the prisoner exchange deal was one of the positive outcomes of the negotiations, with","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:26:45 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/Russia-Ukraine-agree-on-prisoner-swap-but-no-peace-breakthrough-1S0oBdFA3pm/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:46
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,President Xi to attend APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting in Shenzhen,President Xi to attend APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting in Shenzhen,"President Xi to attend APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting in Shenzhen President Xi to attend APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting in Shenzhen Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese President Xi Jinping will chair the 33rd APEC Economic Leaders’ Meeting and deliver remarks, the Chinese Foreign Ministry announced on Friday. The meeting will be held in Shenzhen from November 18 to 19 under the theme ""Building an Asia-Pacific Community to Prosper Together."" The APEC CEO Summit will be held in Shenzhen from November 17 to 18 under the theme “To Prosper and Win the Future Together.” President Xi will attend the opening ceremony and deliver a keynote speech. Xi will also hold a welcome banquet for participating leaders and representatives, and hold bilateral meetings with foreign leaders.","Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:39:11 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-13/President-Xi-to-attend-APEC-Economic-Leaders-Meeting-in-Shenzhen-1S1VV8klmPS/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:46
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Evidence speaks for itself: Irrefutable crimes of Unit 731,Evidence speaks for itself: Irrefutable crimes of Unit 731,"Evidence speaks for itself: Irrefutable crimes of Unit 731 Evidence speaks for itself: Irrefutable crimes of Unit 731 Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Copied During WWII, Japan secretly established the notorious Unit 731 in Harbin, northeast China, which served as the command center for its biological warfare program. At least 3,000 people were subjected to human experimentation by Unit 731, while hundreds of thousands of people in China were killed or injured by Japanese biological and chemical weapons. Despite this history, some Japanese political forces have long sought to deny the country's wartime atrocities, even attempting to portray Unit 731 as a ""public health research unit."" However, mounting evidence continues to expose the truth about its horrific crimes.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:57:19 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-14/Evidence-speaks-for-itself-Irrefutable-crimes-of-Unit-731-1S45IQbWLM4/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:46
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,President Xi Jinping's key quotes on advancing APEC cooperation,President Xi Jinping's key quotes on advancing APEC cooperation,"President Xi Jinping's key quotes on advancing APEC cooperation Chinese President Xi Jinping has repeatedly called for greater openness and cooperation to promote shared prosperity in the Asia-Pacific. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The 33rd Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) Economic Leaders' Meeting will be held in Shenzhen, south China's Guangdong Province, on November 18 and 19 under the theme ""Building an Asia-Pacific Community to Prosper Together,"" with openness, innovation and cooperation as the three priorities. Chinese President Xi Jinping has repeatedly called for greater openness and cooperation to promote shared prosperity in the Asia-Pacific. Here are some of his key quotes on the subject.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:33:34 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-14/President-Xi-Jinping-s-key-quotes-on-advancing-APEC-cooperation-1S3KpqcrJTi/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:46
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Indian PM Modi to attend ASEAN summit in Manila November 16-17,Indian PM Modi to attend ASEAN summit in Manila November 16-17,"Indian PM Modi to attend ASEAN summit in Manila November 16-17 Indian PM Modi to attend ASEAN summit in Manila November 16-17 Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Indian Prime ​Minister Narendra Modi ‌will visit the Philippines from ​November 16 ​to 17 to ⁠attend the ​summit of the ​Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) in ​Manila, India's ​foreign ministry said on ‌Thursday.","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:37:57 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/news-1S0Wtq2OCIM/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:47
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"How China Engages: Blue Helmets, No Borders","How China Engages: Blue Helmets, No Borders","How China Engages: Blue Helmets, No Borders Beneath blue helmets stand Chinese peacekeepers. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Thousands of miles from home, gunfire echoes. Beneath blue helmets stand Chinese peacekeepers. Since China first sent military observers overseas in 1990, its peacekeeping presence has expanded to missions around the world. To date, China has deployed more than 50,000 peacekeeping personnel cumulatively. As the largest troop-contributing country and the second-largest financial contributor to UN peacekeeping operations among the five permanent members of the UN Security Council, its blue helmets have helped uphold peace and security around the world, standing firm wherever they are needed most. This is more than a military deployment to distant lands. It is China’ssolemn commitment to safeguarding world peace.","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:08:01 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/How-China-Engages-Blue-Helmets-No-Borders-1RVM3nFgEzS/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:47
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"U.S. gears up for Singles’ Day, the world’s largest shopping event","U.S. gears up for Singles’ Day, the world’s largest shopping event","U.S. gears up for Singles’ Day, the world’s largest shopping event U.S. gears up for Singles’ Day, the world’s largest shopping event Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Copied As Singles’ Day, the world’s biggest shopping day of the year kicks into full swing, retailers are busy promoting products as millions of customers scour for deals. But in the U.S. and the West, are shoppers joining the frenzy? CGTN’s Mark Niu reports. For more, check out our exclusive content onCGTN Nowand subscribe to our weekly newsletter,The China Report.","Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:45:22 GMT",https://newsus.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/U-S-gears-up-for-Singles-Day-the-world-s-largest-shopping-event-1S03SziCDEA/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:48
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Premier Li: China, Thailand as close as one family a unique advantage","Premier Li: China, Thailand as close as one family a unique advantage","Premier Li: China, Thailand as close as one family a unique advantage Chinese Premier Li Qiang said on Saturday that ""China and Thailand are as close as one family"" is a unique advantage of bilateral relations, as reflected in the practical achievements across various fields. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese Premier Li Qiang meets with Thai King Maha Vajiralongkorn in Bangkok, Thailand, on November 14, 2026. /Xinhua Chinese Premier Li Qiang said on Saturday that ""China and Thailand are as close as one family"" is a unique advantage of bilateral relations, as reflected in the practical achievements across various fields. Li made the remarks during his meeting with Thai King Maha Vajiralongkorn in Bangkok. Conveying cordial greetings from Chinese President Xi Jinping to the king, Li said that during the king's state visit to China last year, Xi held talks with him, and the two sides reached important consensus on advancing the building of a China-Thailand community with a shared future. China appreciates that the Thai royal family has long attached great importance to and remained committed to promoting China-Thailand friendship, Li said. The Chinese premier noted that the continued growth of China-Thailand economic and trade cooperation despite headwinds was particularly commendable amid the current turbulent international situation. Li said that China stands ready to work with Thailand, under the strategic guidance of the two heads of state, to maintain close exchanges, expand cooperation in investment, technological innovation, new energy vehicles and other are","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:53:50 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-15/Premier-Li-China-Thailand-as-close-as-one-family-a-unique-advantage-1S59QILg0r6/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:48
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Jensen Huang resigns as NVIDIA CEO, Colette Kress takes over","Jensen Huang resigns as NVIDIA CEO, Colette Kress takes over","Jensen Huang resigns as NVIDIA CEO, Colette Kress takes over Jensen Huang resigns as NVIDIA CEO, Colette Kress takes over Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Jensen Huang has resigned as president and CEO of NVIDIA. /VCG Jensen Huang has resigned as President, Chief Executive Officer, and a member of the Board, effective immediately, NVIDIA's Board of Directors announced on Thursday. CFO Colette Kress has been appointed interim CEO as the board begins searching for a permanent successor. Kress will continue to serve as executive vice president and CFO while serving as interim CEO. The board said it would consider both internal and external candidates in its search for a permanent chief executive. Kress joined NVIDIA in September 2013 and has served as executive vice president and CFO since then, leading the company's finance organization and playing a key role in its growth and development. Before joining NVIDIA, she spent nearly 25 years in finance positions at major technology companies, including Cisco and Microsoft. Harvey Jones, chair of NVIDIA's board, said Kress had helped lead the company through a period of extraordinary growth and had a deep understanding of its business, customers, operations and financial position. The board expressed confidence in Kress and the company's leadership team, saying operations, customer commitments and the product roadmap were expected to continue without interruption. Kress sai","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:49:27 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/news-1S1a9P9X8iI/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:48
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Building a sustainable future in the face of climate crises,Building a sustainable future in the face of climate crises,"Building a sustainable future in the face of climate crises Building a sustainable future in the face of climate crises Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Did you know that the El Niño phenomenon is scorching Andean forests and ravaging South American coasts? At the APEC Youth Talks, Víctor Ticllacuri, a biomedical engineer from Peru, outlined the stark reality of climate change in South America and called on APEC economies to stand united in jointly addressing the phenomenon.","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:11:56 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/Building-a-sustainable-future-in-the-face-of-climate-crises-1S0v3rDrVQc/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:48
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China Film Showcase brings Chinese cinema to Dublin,China Film Showcase brings Chinese cinema to Dublin,"China Film Showcase brings Chinese cinema to Dublin The China Film Showcase was held on Tuesday at the Stella Cinema in Dublin, Ireland, bringing together more than 200 guests and moviegoers. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The China Film Showcase is launched in Dublin, Ireland, November 10, 2026. /CMG The China Film Showcase was held on Tuesday at the Stella Cinema in Dublin, Ireland, bringing together more than 200 guests and moviegoers. Attendees included Jiang Haiqing, a member of China Media Group's (CMG) editorial board and chairman of China International Television Corporation (CITVC); Zhao Yingguang, chargé d'affaires ad interim of the Chinese Embassy in Ireland; former Irish Prime Minister Enda Kenny; former Irish Ambassador to China Declan Kelleher; former European Parliament President Pat Cox; John Kennedy, principal officer at Ireland's Department of Culture, Communications and Sport; Liang Hong, director of CMG's Film, Drama and Documentary Center; Dublin City Councillor Danny Byrne; and Anthony Leo, CEO of animation studio Cartoon Saloon. Jiang Haiqing, a member of CMG's editorial board and chairman of CITVC, addresses the launch event in Dublin, Ireland, November 10, 2026. /CMG Jiang noted that CMG has long been committed to promoting innovation in the film industry and international exchange. She expressed hope that the screenings would give Irish audiences a better understanding of contemporary Chinese cinema and help strengthen cultural ties between the two countries","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:24:33 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/China-Film-Showcase-brings-Chinese-cinema-to-Dublin-1S0myvcz5Zu/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:48
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Global leaders call for urgent climate action, finance reform at COP31","Global leaders call for urgent climate action, finance reform at COP31","Global leaders call for urgent climate action, finance reform at COP31 The Antalya Leaders' Summit of the 31st United Nations Climate Change Conference (COP31) opened on Wednesday, with a focus on turning climate commitments into concrete action. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The Antalya Leaders' Summit of the 31st United Nations Climate Change Conference (COP31) opened on Wednesday, with a focus on turning climate commitments into concrete action. Opening the high-level meeting, UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres urged international cooperation on shared challenges. ""We do not need countries to agree on everything, but we do need them to cooperate on the things no country can solve alone,"" he said. UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres delivers a speech during the Leaders' Summit of the COP31 in Antalya, Turkiye, November 11, 2026. /VCG Guterres noted that global emissions reached a record high in 2025 and that the past four years were the hottest in history. Pointing out that fossil fuels must be phased out, he stated that major oil companies should contribute to recovery efforts through taxes on their windfall profits. Highlighting the transition in the energy sector, Guterres added that solar power alone met nearly three quarters of the growth in global electricity demand last year, proving that clean energy has become the cheapest source of new electricity across most of the world. This year's summit aims to bridge the gap between ambition and delivery by focusing on implementation, finance delivery and climate resilience. Turki","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:47:46 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/Global-leaders-call-for-urgent-climate-action-finance-reform-at-COP31-1S0sfls2GeA/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:48
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Setback for Google as EU Court adviser backs $1.7 bln antitrust fine,Setback for Google as EU Court adviser backs $1.7 bln antitrust fine,"Setback for Google as EU Court adviser backs $1.7 bln antitrust fine Setback for Google as EU Court adviser backs $1.7 bln antitrust fine Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Google suffered a setback on Thursday as an advisr to Europe's top court faulted a lower tribunal's decision to scrap a 1.49 billion euro (about $1.7 billion) fine levied against the US tech giant seven years ago for anti-competitive practices related to online advertising.","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:58:47 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-12/news-1S0Po26ISsw/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:49
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Yemen's warring sides report heavy casualties in fresh attacks,Yemen's warring sides report heavy casualties in fresh attacks,"Yemen's warring sides report heavy casualties in fresh attacks Yemen's warring sides report heavy casualties in fresh attacks Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Yemen's government forces and the Houthi group reported fresh attacks across several fronts on Saturday, with both sides claiming heavy casualties. Majid al-Nuzaili, spokesperson for the government forces, said on social media platform X that government forces had carried out 723 attacks on Houthi positions in recent hours, including 37 air strikes, 56 drone attacks and hundreds of rocket and artillery strikes. He said the attacks targeted Houthi troop gatherings, fortifications and military equipment, claiming that about 321 fighters and commanders had been killed or wounded and 117 military vehicles and pieces of equipment destroyed or disabled. Meanwhile, Houthi military spokesperson Yahya Sarea said on X that the group had fired several ballistic missiles at Saudi troop gatherings in the Kharaz area of southern Yemen, claiming the strikes killed or wounded dozens of soldiers and destroyed numerous military vehicles. Sarea also accused Saudi warplanes of carrying out 72 air strikes against civilian sites across four Yemeni provinces over the past 24 hours. The claims from both sides could not be independently verified. Also on Saturday, coalition spokesman Turki Al-Maliki said on X that coalition forces had intercepted and destroyed two drones launched by the Ho","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:47:58 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-11-15/Yemen-s-warring-sides-report-heavy-casualties-in-fresh-attacks-1S5fso83Q5i/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-11-15 03:30:49
The Hindu,South Asia,en,Nations grapple with loss of 1.5C target at UN climate summit,Nations grapple with loss of 1.5C target at UN climate summit,"Nations grapple with loss of 1.5C target at UN climate summit The world has already warmed about 1.4C above pre-industrial times and the UN declared in September that crossing 1.5C — the most ambitious target threshold of the Paris accord — was imminent and unavoidable You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Published- November 15, 2026 08:54 am IST - Antalya People wait in line at the COP31 U.N. Climate Summit, in Antalya. | Photo Credit: AP For a decade, the 1.5C goal has served as the northstar of climate action, a line nations pledged to hold to avoid the worst ravages of a warming planet. But atthis year’s global climate conference— the first since the United Nations said the 1.5C threshold would be missed — nations appear unsure how to take the news. The world has already warmed about 1.4C above pre-industrial times and theUN declared in September that crossing 1.5C— the most ambitious target threshold of the Paris accord — was imminent and unavoidable. Yet in Turkiye, where the COP31 negotiations are at the midway point, some nations are clinging to the goal, particularly those on the frontlines of the climate crisis. Palau President Surangel Whipps Jr, whose Pacific island nation is threatened by rising seas, said 1.5C was not “an abstract target”. “It is an existential threat to our food, our economies and sovereignty,” he told world leaders in Antalya. Some countries want a final deal at ","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:54:58 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/energy-and-environment/nations-grapple-with-loss-of-15c-target-at-un-climate-summit/article71704051.ece,2026-11-15 03:30:50
The Hindu,South Asia,en,"Coalition to move away from fossil fuels presses ahead without Colombia, its original champion","Coalition to move away from fossil fuels presses ahead without Colombia, its original champion","Coalition to move away from fossil fuels presses ahead without Colombia, its original champion The coalition, launched in the Colombian coastal city of Santa Marta in April, is expected to release a progress report this week outlining steps taken by participating countries, including additional national plans to reduce dependence on coal, oil and gas You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Published- November 15, 2026 08:38 am IST - Mexico City People wait in line at the COP31 U.N Climate Summit on November 12, 2026 | Photo Credit: AP A coalition of countries seeking to accelerate the global transition away from fossil fuels is preparing to unveil new national plans at the ongoing United Nations climate talks, known as COP31, in Antalya, Turkey, pressing ahead despite the withdrawal of Colombia, one of its founding members. The coalition, launched in the Colombian coastal city of Santa Marta in April, is expected to release a progress report this week outlining steps taken by participating countries, including additional national plans to reduce dependence on coal, oil and gas. The announcement comes as Ireland and the Pacific island nation of Tuvalu prepare to take over leadership of the initiative from Colombia and the Netherlands, with a second international conference planned for July 2027. A statement from Ireland's Department of Climate, Energy and the Environment confirmed Colombia's withdrawal and said preparations were well advanced for a program of events in both countr","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:38:59 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/coalition-to-move-away-from-fossil-fuels-presses-ahead-without-colombia-its-original-champion/article71704040.ece,2026-11-15 03:30:50
