The Hindu,South Asia,en,"All passengers, crew on New Orleans cruise ship survive crash with tanker on Mississippi River","All passengers, crew on New Orleans cruise ship survive crash with tanker on Mississippi River","All passengers, crew on New Orleans cruise ship survive crash with tanker on Mississippi River Tanker owned by subsidiary of Chinese shipbuilder; too early to tell what might have caused the crash, but videos indicate some kind of catastrophic system failure on the vessel, a maritime law expert said You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Updated- November 14, 2026 07:42 am IST Emergency responders and crews are on the scene after a tanker crashed into a river cruise in New Orleans, on November 13, 2026. | Photo Credit: The Advocate via AP A tanker in New Orleans that apparently lost its steering slammed into a docked river cruise boat with about 180 people aboard on Friday (November 13, 2026), the mayor said. All aboard survived after the crash prompted a massive rescue operation for passengers and crew who plunged into the Mississippi River as the ship took on water and began to topple over. Video from the scene showed the much larger Atlantic Asphalt tanker hit the cruise boat while it was docked as metal and glass crashed and crunched. Tugboat operators, nearby workers, police and other rescuers rushed to help. “We have zero people unaccounted for, which truly is a miracle on the Mississippi,” New Orleans Mayor Helena Moreno said at a news conference as rescuers and others cheered. The Mayor said 32 people were taken to the hospital, but none of them had critical injuries. “It was docked right at the Port of New Orleans when","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:42:12 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/new-orleans-usa-tanker-ship-river-cruise-crash-updates/article71699607.ece,2026-11-15 03:31:00
