Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Robot dogs mounted with rifles deployed in anti-gang stadium operation in Haiti,Robot dogs mounted with rifles deployed in anti-gang stadium operation in Haiti,"Robot dogs mounted with rifles deployed in anti-gang stadium operation in Haiti El Salvador President Nayib Bukele shared video of armed robot dogs storming Sylvio Cator Stadium as forces joined Haitian police in a gang crackdown on the violent island nation. The video shared by El Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele suggested the robots assisted in an operation to take back a stadium from gang control in Haiti. (Credit: Presidency of El Salvador via AP) El Salvador President Nayib Bukele released a video this week showing military forces usingrobotic dogsmounted with rifles in an operation to take back a stadium in Haiti from gang control. ""Under the bilateral agreement between the Haitian government and the government ofEl Salvador, a joint operation involving the Haitian National Police, the Haitian Armed Forces (FAd’H), the Task Force, and the Salvadoran Special Forces successfully took control of Sylvio Cator Stadium and secured it,"" Bukele wrote on X in a translation from Haitian Creole. The video showed the robots moving down a hallway and up a set of stairs with the rifle on top. EL SALVADOR-BACKED AIR ASSAULT DESTROYS HAITI GANG HEADQUARTERS AMID SEARCH FOR MISSING TROOPS El Salvador’s President Nayib Bukele released footage Thursday showing military forces using robotic dogs mounted with rifles in an operation to take back a stadium in Haiti from gang control.(Nayib Bukele/X) It’s unclear exactly how the robots assisted in thePort-au-Princeoperation. Bukele said ""several human skulls"" were found inside the stadium during the operation. 'THEY FED HIM HIS OWN EARS': TOP REPUBLICAN SHARES HORRIFYING STORIES OF GANG RULE IN HAITI The video showed the robot climbing up a set of stairs.(Nayib Bukele/X) ""We will now establish an ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:51:47 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/robot-dogs-mounted-rifles-deployed-anti-gang-stadium-operation-haiti,2026-11-15 03:31:17
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Two Americans drown after Caribbean current pulls them out to sea,Two Americans drown after Caribbean current pulls them out to sea,"Two Americans drown after Caribbean current pulls them out to sea Two American tourists drowned off Birimi island after swimming beyond a warning sign area and being swept out by a strong current, Bahamas police said. Two American tourists drowned in the Bahamas after strong currents swept them out to sea near Bimini Island. Police said the victims were swimming beyond warning signs. Two American tourists drowned in theBahamasafter a strong current pulled a group of swimmers out to sea Friday, the Royal Bahamas Police Force said in a press release. The pair — a 38-year-old man and a 40-year-old woman — were swimming with a larger group in waters off the island of Bimini when the strong current swept them away. Police said the victims were swimming in an area beyond a sign warning ofstrong currents. MOM OF 2 WHO DIED RESCUING SONS DURING BAHAMAS SNORKELING TRIP IS IDENTIFIED A nearby ferry boat rescued some of the swimmers, but the American duo were already unresponsive by the time the boat got to them, police said. One of Bimini's beaches is found on the west side of North Bimini, the most popular of which is a long stretch of three contiguous beaches in Alice Town.(iStock) Though CPR was administered to the pair, they remained unresponsive. WOMAN FOUND FLOATING IN SEA AFTER GOING OVERBOARD FROM ROYAL CARIBBEAN SHIP ""Both victims were transported to the local clinic, where medical personnel continued life-saving efforts. Unfortunately, despite their efforts, both individuals were pronounced deceased by the attending physician shortly before 4:00 p.m.,"" the police statement read. Bimini Island, The Bahamas(iStock) Police do not suspect foul play but are investigating the circumstances. ROBB","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:42:12 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/two-americans-drowned-strong-current-ripped-them-bahaman-sea-police-say,2026-11-15 03:31:17
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Inside Arab nation's battle against radicalism as top official warns of threat brewing on Europe's streets,Inside Arab nation's battle against radicalism as top official warns of threat brewing on Europe's streets,"Inside Arab nation's battle against radicalism as top official warns of threat brewing on Europe's streets A senior United Arab Emirates official warns that European protests have crossed into national security threats, urging coexistence education first. Reporting from Abu Dhabi, Fox News Digital speaks exclusively with officials about the UAE’s approach to preventing radicalization. ABU DHABI, United Arab Emirates — A senior Emirati official is warning that demonstrations in Europe have crossed a line from political expression into a national security threat, arguing that extremism must be confronted before it turns violent. ""You can go demonstrate, talk, give a speech, but what [we] saw in the street in 11 cities in Europe is not freedom of speech. It is a threat to national security,"" Dr. Ali Rashid Al Nuaimi, chairman of the Defense, Interior and Foreign Affairs Committee of the UAE's Federal National Council, told Fox News Digital in an exclusive interview. The remarks come against a wider European debate over radicalization. On Nov. 3,Europol reportedthat authorities from 16 countries had referred more than 9,000 links to extremist and terrorist material appearing across 47 social media and gaming platforms. The operation targeted online role-playing content promoting jihadist, far-right, far-left and anarchist violence, including material that could draw minors toward extremist networks. AN IRANIAN REFUGEE'S WARNING TO AMERICAN UNIVERSITIES EMBRACING FOREIGN FUNDING AND RADICALISM A car burns during a nationwide day of strikes and protests over wages, the cost of living and public services by French labor unions and high school and university students calling for better education conditions, in Lyon, France, Nov. 5, 20","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:00:53 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/inside-arab-nations-battle-against-radicalism-top-official-warns-threat-brewing-europes-streets,2026-11-15 03:31:17
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Iran's shadow operations stretch across Europe as chilling spy convictions expose Tehran's reach,Iran's shadow operations stretch across Europe as chilling spy convictions expose Tehran's reach,"Iran's shadow operations stretch across Europe as chilling spy convictions expose Tehran's reach Two Iranian men convicted of spying in Britain as France accuses the IRGC of cyberattacks and UAE officials warn of Iranian sleeper cells abroad. Lisa Daftari says years of hacking, surveillance and threats have changed how she lives, warning that Iran’s intimidation tactics are designed to silence critics abroad. Two Iranian men were convicted in Britain on Thursday of spying on journalists and critics of Tehran, the latest case raising alarm over Iranian operations beyond the Middle East, as France accuses the IRGC of unprecedented cyberattacks and a senior UAE official warns of Iranian sleeper cells abroad. The developments come as the Trump administration continues its campaign of economic pressure against Tehran while leaving the door open to diplomatic negotiations, raising questions about how Iran's overseas intelligence networks and alleged covert activities might factor into any future agreement. A jury at Woolwich Crown Court in London found Mostafa Sepahvand, 41, and Farhad Javadi Manesh, 46, guilty of engaging in conduct likely to assist a foreign intelligence service after prosecutors said they carried out surveillance of journalists and other individuals critical of the Iranian government, according toReuters. IRAN TURNS CITIZENS INTO INFORMANTS AS CHILLING CRACKDOWN SPREADS BEYOND ITS BORDERS EU designates Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps as a terrorist organization as Ursula von der Leyen pledges rapid implementation following a violent crackdown.(Morteza Nikoubazl/NurPhoto via Getty Images) The targets included journalists working for Iran International, a London-based Persian-language news out","Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:10:49 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/irans-shadow-operations-stretch-across-europe-chilling-spy-convictions-expose-tehrans-reach,2026-11-15 03:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,El Salvador-backed air assault destroys Haiti gang headquarters amid search for missing troops,El Salvador-backed air assault destroys Haiti gang headquarters amid search for missing troops,"El Salvador-backed air assault destroys Haiti gang headquarters amid search for missing troops Helicopters struck Haiti gang compound, dozens fled and President Bukele touted the assault amid a search for four missing Salvadoran personnel. El Salvador’s president said the operation destroyed a major Haiti gang’s headquarters believed to be used for kidnappings, weapons trafficking and extortion. (@nayibbukele/X) El Salvador's president on Tuesday said the country'smilitaryhelped deliver a devastating air assault against the headquarters of one of Haiti's most powerful criminal gangs, which has been linked to mass kidnappings, weapons trafficking and extortion. Airstrikes targeted strongholds belonging to 400 Mawozo and the home of its leader, Lanmò San Jou, Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele said. The attack took place Sunday near Port-au-Prince and was carried out by a Haitian police task force backed by Salvadoran troops, The Miami Heraldreported. BUKELE WARNS HAITIAN GANG LEADERS THAT HIS FORCES WILL 'FINISH' THEM AS HE DID IN EL SALVADOR El Salvador’s president said the operation destroyed a major Haiti gang’s headquarters used for kidnappings, weapons trafficking and extortion.(@nayibbukele/X) The operation appears to be part of an ongoing military effort in response to the disappearance of four Salvadoran members of a U.N.-backed security missionabducted in a gang ambush near Port-au-Prince Oct. 18. ""We kept our promise,"" Bukele said in a post on X. Videos showed several helicopters launching airstrikes against multiple compounds inside sprawling complexes. Dozens of people were also seen fleeing the properties on foot and motorbikes after the strikes. ""Most of them ran away without even trying to fight. W","Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:04:45 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/el-salvador-air-assault-destroys-haiti-gang-headquarters-search-missing-troops,2026-11-15 03:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Iran escalates in Hormuz, claims strike on Omani island it says 'enemy' uses for US military ops","Iran escalates in Hormuz, claims strike on Omani island it says 'enemy' uses for US military ops","Iran escalates in Hormuz, claims strike on Omani island it says 'enemy' uses for US military ops Iran claims its Revolutionary Guard struck navigation equipment on Oman&apos;s Didamar Island in the Strait of Hormuz, but Omani officials dispute damage. The IRGC reported a strike against ‘enemy navigation aid systems,’ radar and communications equipment located on Didamar Island in Hormuz (Credit: Reuters). Iran claims it struck a small Omani island in theStrait of Hormuz, targeting oil tanker navigation infrastructure as CENTCOM maintains its blockade of Iranian ports and protects commercial shipping from Iranian attacks along the southern route. Three sources also confirmed toReutersWednesday that navigation systems and communications equipment on Didamar Island, also known as Little Quoin Island, had been attacked, raising concerns about the vulnerability of maritime infrastructure used to maintain oil shipments through the Gulf. Iran's semiofficialFars News Agencyreported that the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) navy targeted the island, alleging the systems were being used to help vessels transit the strait without Tehran's authorization. WHITE HOUSE SILENT ON IRAN-OMAN HORMUZ PLAN TEHRAN SAYS WOULD BAN US WARSHIPS A satellite image shows Didamar Island, Oman(Google/Airbus/Handout via Reuters) Iranian state television also claimed that personnel and equipment on the island ""were helping the flow of oil smuggling by the enemy,"" with the IRGC maintaining it had carried out the strikes, Reuters reported. Video published by Reuters showed smoke rising near the rocky outcrop. TheInstitute for the Study of War(ISW) said it identified the attack as occurring Nov. 8, before Iranian state media claimed responsibility on","Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:48:03 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/iran-escalates-hormuz-claims-strike-omani-island-enemy-uses-us-military-ops,2026-11-15 03:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Fiery chaos erupts across Spain as protesters clash with police during massive nationwide strike,Fiery chaos erupts across Spain as protesters clash with police during massive nationwide strike,"Fiery chaos erupts across Spain as protesters clash with police during massive nationwide strike Spain&apos;s first general strike in 14 years turned violent in Barcelona as protesters set fires and launched fireworks at riot police on Paseo de Gracia. Clashes broke out during a general strike in Madrid, with riot police detaining demonstrators in the Spanish capital. (Credit: Reuters) Unruly protesters set fires, smashed storefronts and launched fireworks at riot police across parts ofSpainon Wednesday as a massive nationwide strike over soaring housing costs disrupted transportation and businesses. Violent scenes unfolded in Barcelona, where some demonstrators vandalized stores along the city's popular Paseo de Gracia shopping boulevard, set small bonfires and launched fireworks at officers arriving in riot gear and armored vehicles, according toThe Associated Press. The violence erupted after a largely peaceful march as Spain experienced its first general strike in 14 years,with workers demandingrelief from skyrocketing rents and the rising cost of living. TRAVELERS MAY FACE MAJOR DISRUPTIONS AS STRIKES THREATEN AIRPORTS AND POPULAR ATTRACTIONS A protestor holds up a poster as objects burn in the background during a demonstration over the housing crisis Wednesday in Barcelona, Spain.(David Ramos/Getty Images) Housing activists claimed 400,000 people marched through Barcelona, while city officials estimated attendance at 55,000. Government officials reported another 120,000 demonstrators gathered in Madrid despite heavy rain, the AP reported. The nationwide walkout disrupted public transportation,forced some businessesto close and blocked major roads. Police made arrests across the country, while officers used pepper spra","Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:46:50 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/fiery-chaos-erupts-spain-protesters-clash-police-massive-nationwide-strike,2026-11-15 03:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"DNA links 4 grizzly bears to deadly attack on mother and daughter in Canada, officials say","DNA links 4 grizzly bears to deadly attack on mother and daughter in Canada, officials say","DNA links 4 grizzly bears to deadly attack on mother and daughter in Canada, officials say DNA evidence linked four grizzly bears to the deaths of Jennifer Balcarras and Selah Reed near Bella Coola, British Columbia, officials said. Canadian wildlife officials say DNA testing linked an adult female grizzly and her three offspring to the deaths of a mother and daughter near Bella Coola, British Columbia. Investigators say the attack likely involved predatory behavior. Four grizzly bears have been linked through DNA evidence to a deadly attack on a mother and daughter inBritish Columbia, prompting Canadian wildlife officers to kill all four animals, officials announced Tuesday. The British Columbia Conservation Officer Service said forensic testing conclusively linked an adult female grizzly and her three offspring to the deaths of Jennifer Balcarras, 48, and her daughter, Selah Reed, 20, near Bella Coola. The bears were captured over the weekend and killed in accordance with provincial human-wildlife conflict response guidelines to protect public safety, according to a Nov. 10 statement from the agency. BODY OF MISSING HIKER DISCOVERED OFF TRAIL AS INVESTIGATORS PROBE RARE DEADLY BEAR ENCOUNTER An image showing a photo of Jennifer Balcarras, 48, and her 20-year-old daughter Selah Reed, who were killed in a grizzly bear attack.(Facebook/Josh Kara Balcarras) Investigators determined that the encounter likely involved predatory behavior, although officials did not elaborate on how the attack unfolded. ""This was a heartbreaking event for the families, the Nuxalk Nation and the Bella Coola community. We hope the efforts of everyone who responded, along with these findings, bring some measure of closure,"" said ","Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:59:30 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/dna-links-4-grizzly-bears-deadly-attack-mother-daughter-canada-officials-say,2026-11-15 03:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Russian Ambassador to US Alexander Darchiev dies suddenly at 66,Russian Ambassador to US Alexander Darchiev dies suddenly at 66,"Russian Ambassador to US Alexander Darchiev dies suddenly at 66 Russia&apos;s ambassador to the United States Alexander Darchiev, 66, had been appointed by Putin to lead a rapprochement with the Trump administration. Fox News' Gillian Turner reports on the arrest of a senior U.S. Army officer in Britain on suspicion of spying for Russia following a joint U.S.-U.K. investigation. Russia's Ambassador to the United States Alexander Darchiev, 66, died suddenly Wednesday, the Russian Foreign Ministry announced. ""The leadership and staff of the Russian Foreign Ministry report with deep sorrow that on Nov. 11, at the age of 66, the Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Russian Federation to the United States of America, Alexander Nikitich Darchiev, passed away suddenly,""Russia's statement, as translated to English, said. ""A distinguished diplomat, experienced leader, kind colleague, and mentor has departed this life. A consummate professional and brilliant Americanist, A.N. Darchiev served on one of the most critical and demanding fronts of Russian foreign policy."" ""We express our deepest and most sincere condolences to the family and loved ones of Alexander Nikitich Darchiev,"" the statement added. ""The cherished memory of our untimely departed colleague will forever remain in our hearts."" Fox News confirmed the death came in Russia and not the U.S. MELANIA TRUMP HAILS OLESHKY CEASEFIRE AS POTENTIAL ‘SPARK’ FOR PROGRESS AMID UKRAINE-RUSSIA WAR Alexander Darchiyev, head of the Russian Foreign Ministry's North America Department and a candidate for the position of ambassador to the United States, poses for a picture before a session of the Federation Council's committee on foreign af","Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:02:20 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/russian-ambassador-us-alexander-darchiev-dies-suddenly-66,2026-11-15 03:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Israel's political shake-up enters new phase as former PM plays kingmaker — and deadline looms,Israel's political shake-up enters new phase as former PM plays kingmaker — and deadline looms,"Israel's political shake-up enters new phase as former PM plays kingmaker — and deadline looms Benjamin Netanyahu called for unity, but Gadi Eisenkot canceled Likud talks after calling the outgoing prime minister&apos;s speech &quot;delusional.&quot; With final election results leaving both major blocs short of a majority, Fox News Digital reporter Efrat Lachter reports from Israel on the negotiations that could determine the country's next government. Israel's newly elected parliament was sworn in Tuesday, marking the beginning of a political transition that could end Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's long tenure in power. Despite the opposition's parliamentary gains, the country remains without a new government, and negotiations to form one face significant obstacles. At the center of those negotiations is former Israeli military chief Gadi Eisenkot, who wastasked by President Isaac Herzog onSunday with assembling Israel's next governing coalition after 67 lawmakers recommended him for the position, compared with 46 who supported Netanyahu. Although Eisenkot's Yashar party won 21 seats in theOct. 27 election, he is working closely with former Prime Minister Naftali Bennett, whose B'Yachad party, formed with former Prime Minister Yair Lapid, secured another 12 seats. NETANYAHU FACES COALITION SHOWDOWN AS RIVALS MANEUVER TO FORM ISRAEL'S NEXT GOVERNMENT Former military chief Gadi Eisenkot, Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, Israeli President Isaac Herzog and other Israeli officials pose for a photo on the day of the inauguration of Israel's 26th parliament, at the Knesset in Jerusalem, Nov. 10, 2026.(Ronen Zvulun/Reuters) The two parties have not merged, but their cooperation effectively gives Eisenkot the negot","Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:36:36 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/israels-political-shake-up-enters-new-phase-former-pm-plays-kingmaker-deadline-looms,2026-11-15 03:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Inside Holocaust memorial in heart of Arab world as founder reveals what changed everything,Inside Holocaust memorial in heart of Arab world as founder reveals what changed everything,"Inside Holocaust memorial in heart of Arab world as founder reveals what changed everything Inside Dubai&apos;s Crossroads of Civilizations Museum, founder Ahmed Obaid Al Mansoori reveals how a temporary Holocaust tribute became a permanent gallery. Reporting from Dubai, Fox News Digital visits one of the Arab world's first permanent Holocaust exhibitions and speaks with its founder. DUBAI, United Arab Emirates— In a historic house near Dubai Creek, a small gallery commemorating the six million Jews murdered in the Holocaust stands alongside collections exploring Islamic civilization, Emirati heritage and the history of Palestine and the Holy Land. The Holocaust exhibition at the privately owned Crossroads of Civilizations Museum is among the first permanent displays of its kind in the Arab world. Opened in May 2021, less than a year after the UAE normalized relations withIsraelthrough the Abraham Accords, it has become a symbol of the Emirates' approach to religious coexistence. During a recent visit to the museum, Fox News Digital saw displays documenting Nazi persecution, including a life-size image of the boy from the famous Warsaw Ghetto photograph, his hands raised in surrender. The gallery also tells the stories of Muslims who rescued Jews during the Holocaust, including Egyptian physician Mohammed Helmy, who sheltered Jews from Nazi persecution in Berlin. US-BACKED ISRAEL-MOROCCO DEAL DEEPENS ABRAHAM ACCORDS AMID GROWING REGIONAL THREATS An image of a young Jewish boy with his hands raised as armed German soldiers round up civilians in the Warsaw Ghetto in 1943, displayed at the Holocaust gallery of the Crossroads of Civilizations Museum in Dubai, United Arab Emirates. The photograph has become one of the most re","Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:24:26 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/inside-holocaust-memorial-heart-arab-world-founder-reveals-changed-everything,2026-11-15 03:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,US evacuates 13 military aircraft from second UK base as new Iran threat raises alarm,US evacuates 13 military aircraft from second UK base as new Iran threat raises alarm,"US evacuates 13 military aircraft from second UK base as new Iran threat raises alarm More than a dozen U.S. Air Force aircraft left RAF Mildenhall after a reported Iran-linked threat triggered the second-highest military alert level. Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Tuesday after the G7 Foreign Ministers' meeting in Paris, that ""bad things are happening to the Iranian economy and it's unfortunate."" TheU.S. Air Forceabruptly relocated more than a dozen aircraft from RAF Mildenhall in eastern England amid an emerging security threat, U.S. officials confirmed Tuesday. TheWall Street Journalfirst reported the move, citing sources who said the threat originated in Iran. As U.S. officials assessed the threat's nature and urgency, commanders raised the base's security level to Force Protection Condition Charlie, the military's second-highest alert level, indicating a likely terrorist threat against personnel or facilities. IRAN HAS 'SUBSTANTIALLY INCREASED' EFFORTS TO TARGET AMERICANS ABROAD, US INTELLIGENCE MEMO WARNS U.S. Air Force KC-135, used for in-flight refueling, takes off from RAF Mildenhall Airbase.(AP Photo/Max Nash, File) Flight-tracking data and open-source analysts with the Military Air Tracking Alliance identified 13 U.S. aircraft leaving the base late Monday, theAssociated Presssaid. Nine Boeing KC-135 Stratotankers were moved to airfields in Scotland, Germany and Spain. Three CV-22B Ospreys were relocated to nearby RAF Lakenheath, which has hardened aircraft shelters. A U.S. official told The Associated Press the moves were precautionary, noting that some aircraft were on rotational deployments while others were permanently stationed in theUnited Kingdom. IRAN UNDER SCRUTINY AFTER PLOT FOILED","Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:53:31 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/us-evacuates-13-military-aircraft-second-uk-base-new-iran-threat-raises-alarm,2026-11-15 03:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"American girl, 7, killed during Mexican cartel operation; mother blames police helicopter: report","American girl, 7, killed during Mexican cartel operation; mother blames police helicopter: report","American girl, 7, killed during Mexican cartel operation; mother blames police helicopter: report Aranza Aidelany Pardo&apos;s mother says a Tamaulipas state police helicopter fired the shot that killed her 7-year-old during a Gulf Cartel operation. A 7-year-old dual U.S.-Mexican citizen was shot and killed during a security operation in Matamoros, Mexico. Her mother says police aboard a helicopter opened fire on the family's vehicle. A 7-year-old girl with dual U.S. and Mexican citizenship was shot and killed during a Mexican security operation targeting an alleged cartel member, and her mother accused police officers aboard a helicopter of firing the deadly shot. Aranza Aidelany Pardo died Oct. 29 in Matamoros, a Mexican border city across from Brownsville, Texas. She was among six people killed during the operation and subsequent roadblocks erected by the Gulf Cartel, according to The Associated Press. Her mother, Claudia Pardo García, told the AP that gunfire from a Tamaulipas state police helicopter struck her daughter in the head. Pardo was also wounded in the leg. Mexican authorities are investigating three officers aboard the helicopter who remain on active duty, according to Tamaulipas Public Security Secretary Carlos Arturo Pancardo. EXCLUSIVE: INSIDE TRUMP'S CARTEL CRACKDOWN AS WHITE HOUSE OFFICIAL DETAILS PRESIDENT'S PRIVATE BRIEFINGS The Rio Grande is seen from an international bridge in Matamoros, Mexico, Jan. 15, 2026. A 7-year-old American girl was killed in the border city during a Mexican security operation.(Gabriel V. Cardenas/AFP via Getty Images) The operation resulted in the arrest of Axel Alfredo Cárdenas Rodríguez, also known as El Titán, the son of an allegedGulf Cartel leaderand nephew of the gr","Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:59:56 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/american-girl-7-killed-mexican-cartel-operation-mother-blames-police-helicopter-report,2026-11-15 03:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Senior US Army soldier arrested in UK on suspicion of spying for Russia,Senior US Army soldier arrested in UK on suspicion of spying for Russia,"Senior US Army soldier arrested in UK on suspicion of spying for Russia U.K. police arrested a senior U.S. Army soldier in a Russia-linked espionage probe, drawing a sharp warning from FBI Director Kash Patel. A senior US Army soldier was arrested in England on suspicion of Russia-linked espionage in an investigation involving UK police and the FBI. A senior U.S. Army soldier was arrested in England Tuesday on suspicion of espionage offenses related to Russia, according to U.K. police. The 41-year-old man, whose identity was not released, was detained as part of an investigation into suspected national security threats led byCounter Terrorism Policing, according to the Metropolitan Police. Officials said the arrest was carried out in coordination with the U.S. military and the FBI. ""This important arrest involves allegations of espionage, which is of the utmost concern to the United States and our allies,""FBI Director Kash Patelsaid in a statement. FBI OFFERS $200K REWARD FOR FORMER AIR FORCE INTELLIGENCE AGENT ACCUSED OF SPYING FOR IRAN FILE — The 41-year-old senior U.S. Army soldier remains in custody in London on suspicion of espionage offenses related to Russia.(U.S. Army) The soldier was arrested near Gloucester, and police are currently searching two locations in the wider Gloucestershire area as part of the ongoing joint U.K.-U.S. investigation. Police said the man was detained under the National Security Act 2023 and remains in custody at a London police station. The investigation is ongoing and is being led by officers from the Counter Terrorism Policing team in London. RUSSIAN SPIES ORCHESTRATED $40K MURDER PLOT IN NATION’S CAPITAL, US ALLEGES Deputy Assistant Commissione","Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:51:09 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/senior-us-army-soldier-arrested-uk-suspicion-spying-russia,2026-11-15 03:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Mojtaba Khamenei aide's chilling '40 years' warning surfaces amid US push for Iran deal,Mojtaba Khamenei aide's chilling '40 years' warning surfaces amid US push for Iran deal,"Mojtaba Khamenei aide's chilling '40 years' warning surfaces amid US push for Iran deal Mohsen Rezaei once warned that ceasefire talks could last decades, as JD Vance reportedly reached out to him about resuming U.S.-Iran peace talks. Fox News senior strategic analyst Ret. Gen. Jack Keane discusses reports that Vice President JD Vance contacted an Iranian hard-liner at President Donald Trump’s direction. Keane argues that Iran is not serious about reaching a deal and would not comply with one. Iran's top security official, who reportedly received a letter from Vice President JD Vance about resuming peace talks, warned in a resurfaced interview thatwartime negotiationswith Tehran could drag on for decades, and during which both sides should ""be prepared to fight."" Mohsen Rezaei, a former commander of Iran'sIslamic Revolutionary Guard Corps(IRGC), now serves as secretary of the Supreme National Security Council and acts as a key aide to Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei. He also helped shape Tehran's military strategy during the 1980-88Iran-Iraq War. That eight-year conflict ended after Iran's then-supreme leader, Ayatollah Ruhollah Khomeini, accepted a U.N.-brokered cease-fire that he famously likened to drinking from a ""poisoned chalice."" JD VANCE RETURNS TO WASHINGTON AFTER 16 HOURS OF IRAN PEACE TALKS COLLAPSE IN PAKISTAN Senior Iranian general Mohsen Rezaei issues a direct threat against President Donald Trump as the U.S. repositions aircraft carrier amid rising tensions with Tehran, according to reports.(Ayoub Ghaderi/YJC/WANA (West Asia News Agency) via REUTERS) ""Ceasefire means an unfinished war,"" Rezaei had said of the war in a 2006 interview with the Iranian publication Baztab. An English translation","Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:33:04 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/mojtaba-khamenei-aide-chilling-40-years-warning-surfaces-us-push-iran-deal,2026-11-15 03:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"TV anchor found dead with gunshot wound to head, officials arrest husband","TV anchor found dead with gunshot wound to head, officials arrest husband","TV anchor found dead with gunshot wound to head, officials arrest husband The broadcaster’s husband claimed he was playing with a firearm when it discharged inside their home, according to a provincial official Rabiya Ahsan, 41, was found dead inside her Pakistan home. Her husband claimed a gun accidentally discharged while he was playing with it, according to officials. The husband of a TV anchor was arrestedin PakistanSunday after his wife was found dead with a gunshot wound to the head, according to officials. Rabiya Ahsan, 41, was allegedly killed inside her home in Rawalpindi, according to Punjab Information Minister Azma Zahid Bokhari. Ahsan worked as a program host for 92 News, where she established herself as a dedicated journalist alongside senior colleagues. She also frequently posted videos about national affairs on social media. Officials identified her husband as Ahsan Tahir Khan, who claimed he was playing with a firearm in the home when it accidentally discharged, Bokhari said. POPULAR TV HOST, MEDIA STAR FACES HANGING AFTER CONVICTION IN MAJOR SYNTHETIC DRUG TRAFFICKING CASE News anchor Rabiya Ahsan speaks in a video recorded before she was found fatally shot Sunday.(@rabiyaahsanofficial/Instagram) Khan reportedly works as a civil service officer at the Overseas Pakistanis Foundation, a government agency that supports citizens living abroad,according tolocal outlet The Express Tribune, citing police sources. Police are preparing to pursue a murder case againstthe suspect, according to the report. Rawalpindi police also confirmed in a post on X that a woman was killed in a Sunday shooting but did not immediately identify her. Authorities said officers seized the suspe","Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:59:04 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/tv-anchor-found-dead-gunshot-wound-head-officials-arrest-husband,2026-11-15 03:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Riot-torn France struggles with chaos at home as Macron eyes military mission thousands of miles away,Riot-torn France struggles with chaos at home as Macron eyes military mission thousands of miles away,"Riot-torn France struggles with chaos at home as Macron eyes military mission thousands of miles away French President Emmanuel Macron&apos;s Lebanon military force plan hits resistance from Italy as Marco Rubio floats a civilian alternative to UNIFIL. As Israeli and Lebanese military officials meet in Washington for rare Pentagon-mediated talks, Ahmed Sharawi of the Foundation for Defense of Democracies warns Hezbollah’s grip on Lebanon continues to undermine hopes for a broader agreement. French President Emmanuel Macron is pushing ahead with plans for a new European military presence inLebanonwhile struggling with mounting political and economic turmoil at home, even as the initiative encounters resistance from a key European partner and Washington considers an alternative that may not require troops. Secretary of State Marco Rubio confirmed that he had discussed the future of theUnited NationsInterim Force in Lebanon (UNIFIL) with Macron, suggesting that a replacement monitoring mechanism could be civilian rather than military. ""It doesn't have to be a military mission. It could be a civilian mission,"" Rubio said inremarks published Tuesday. Rubio explained that the administration is seeking a credible mechanism to verify arrangements under which Israeli forces withdraw from designated areas, the Lebanese Armed Forces (LAF) assume control and the Iran-backed terrorist group Hezbollah is prevented from returning. RUBIO ANNOUNCES FRAMEWORK DEAL BETWEEN ISRAEL AND LEBANON AS EXPERTS WARN IRAN WILL FIGHT TO SABOTAGE IT Soldiers from the United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon UNIFIL attend a ceremony marking the International Day of UN Peacekeepers in Naqoura, Lebanon, May 29, 2025.(Ali Hashisho/Xinhua via Getty Images) He ","Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:22:36 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/riot-torn-france-struggles-chaos-home-macron-eyes-military-mission-thousands-miles-away,2026-11-15 03:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Trump meets key Iran war mediator as UAE reveals major oil export surge despite conflict,Trump meets key Iran war mediator as UAE reveals major oil export surge despite conflict,"Trump meets key Iran war mediator as UAE reveals major oil export surge despite conflict Trump met Qatar&apos;s prime minister at the White House as Marco Rubio warns Iran negotiations are far from a breakthrough amid Strait of Hormuz chaos. Reporting from Abu Dhabi, Fox News Digital examines how the UAE is navigating disruptions to global energy supplies. ABU DHABI, United Arab Emirates— President Donald Trump met Qatar's prime minister, Sheikh Mohammed bin Abdulrahman Al-Thani, on Monday at the White House as diplomatic efforts to end thewar with Irancontinue, even as Secretary of State Marco Rubio warns that negotiations remain far from a breakthrough and Tehran signals a willingness to negotiate without yielding to pressure. The competing messages come as the Strait of Hormuz remains a major source of global economic disruption and regional governments push for a diplomatic solution to a conflict that has subjected Gulf countries to thousands ofIranian missile and drone attacks. Speaking to reporters Sunday before departing for a G7 foreign ministers meeting in Paris, Rubio said there had been little progress in negotiations and rejected the terms put forward by Tehran. ""I wouldn't say we're on the verge of a breakthrough,"" Rubio said. RUBIO DEFENDS TRUMP'S IRAN WAR AS NOT 'NECESSARILY POPULAR, BUT NECESSARY' Cargo is loaded at the Port of Fujairah, as the U.S.-Israel conflict with Iran limits marine traffic in the Strait of Hormuz, in Fujairah, United Arab Emirates, May 6, 2026.(Amr Alfiky/Reuters) He emphasized that Trump prefers a diplomatic settlement but described Iran's demands as unrealistic. Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian said Monday that Tehran was prepared to negotiate an end to what he describ","Mon, 09 Nov 2026 13:27:23 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/trump-meets-key-iran-war-mediator-uae-reveals-major-oil-export-surge-despite-conflict,2026-11-15 03:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Gunman who killed 6 in Poland's Krakow square dies in hospital after police shootout,Gunman who killed 6 in Poland's Krakow square dies in hospital after police shootout,"Gunman who killed 6 in Poland's Krakow square dies in hospital after police shootout The Krakow shooter, 24, died Monday after police shot him during Saturday&apos;s mass shooting that killed six and wounded 15 in the historic square. The death toll rises following the mass shooting in Krakow’s Main Market Square after three people were found dead inside the gunman’s home. Polish authorities also say two police officers were injured during the shooting. The gunman who killed six people and wounded 15 others in a shooting at a crowded square inPolanddied Monday after being shot by police during the attack, authorities said. The 24-year-old suspect had been hospitalized in critical condition since Saturday's shooting in Krakow and underwent several operations before his death. Polish prosecutors have opened an investigation into the killings and attempted killings, including attacks on police officers, as a possible terrorist offense. Emergency responders gather after a deadly shooting on November 7, 2026 in the Main Market Square of Krakow, Poland. At least five were killed and more were injured in the incident.(Omar Marques/Getty Images) Authorities saidthe gunman held far-right views, though investigators have not publicly established a motive for the attack. TEEN WEARING HELMET CAMERA KILLS WORKER AT POLISH SCHOOL AMID FEARS OF COPYCAT ATTACKS Police also discovered the bodies ofthe suspect's mother, father and sisterat the family's home in Ostrowiec Świętokrzyski, roughly 93 miles northeast of Krakow, per reporting from The Associated Press. The three are believed to have died from gunshot wounds, though authorities have not confirmed the circumstances of their deaths. Emergency responders gather after ","Mon, 09 Nov 2026 04:05:26 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/poland-krakow-square-shooting-gunman-dies,2026-11-15 03:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Trump’s proposed Russia deal raises NATO alarm as ex-commander warns Putin seeks influence over Europe,Trump’s proposed Russia deal raises NATO alarm as ex-commander warns Putin seeks influence over Europe,"Trump’s proposed Russia deal raises NATO alarm as ex-commander warns Putin seeks influence over Europe President Donald Trump says a Russia deal could involve &quot;all of Europe&quot; as retired Gen. Philip Breedlove warns Putin wants spheres of influence. Retired Gen. Philip Breedlove warns any deal meeting Russia's demands could face European resistance. PresidentDonald Trump'spush for a deal with Russia to end the war in Ukraine and potentially reshape European security has raised alarm among NATO allies, with a former top alliance commander warning Fox News Digital that President Vladimir Putin has long sought to divide the world into competing spheres of influence. The warning came as PresidentVolodymyr Zelenskyyalso appeared to reject what he called a potential ""Yalta 2.0,"" and NATO allies debated direct outreach to Putin ahead of delegations preparing for talks inAbu Dhabion Nov. 10-11. Retired Gen.Philip Breedlove, the former Supreme Allied Commander Europe, warned that Putin's ambitions extend far beyond Ukraine and reflect a broader vision for how global powers should divide influence. ""Putin has a plan for the world, and he has pushed that plan on leaders several times,"" Breedlove warned before adding: ""He talks about it and he writes about it."" ZELENSKYY TO SEEK OFFRAMP FOR YEARS-LONG RUSSIA WAR IN UN SPEECH AFTER TRUMP REVEALS PEACE DEAL IS CLOSE Finnish President Alexander Stubb, Polish Prime Minister Donald Tusk, French President Emmanuel Macron, German Chancellor Friedrich Merz, Ukraine’s President Volodymyr Zelenskyy, Steve Witkoff, Jared Kushner, Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni, front row from left, and Jonas Gahr Støre, NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte, Danish Prime Minister Mette Frederiksen, Ursula v","Sun, 08 Nov 2026 18:48:13 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/trumps-proposed-russia-deal-raises-nato-alarm-ex-commander-warns-putin-seeks-influence-over-europe,2026-11-15 03:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Iran vows ‘astonishing’ strikes and lifts missile-range limit as US targets land routes,Iran vows ‘astonishing’ strikes and lifts missile-range limit as US targets land routes,"Iran vows ‘astonishing’ strikes and lifts missile-range limit as US targets land routes Iran&apos;s IRGC lifted its 2,000-kilometer ballistic missile-range limit and threatened new weapons hours after U.S. Central Command launched a new task force. Iran proxy attacks target a key Saudi Arabian oil pipeline as host Kayleigh McEnany reports on the expanding conflict. Former Navy SEAL Jack Carr joins the program to discuss ballistic missile production and Chinese satellite intelligence linked to a strike killing three American troops. Carr warns that Houthis threaten global shipping chokepoints near the Red Sea. Iran lifted its self-imposed ballistic missile-range limit and threatened to unleash new, homegrown weapons that would ""astonish the entire world,"" within hours of the U.S. military launching a new task force aimed at choking off Tehran's weapons shipments and illicit trade Nov. 7. Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) spokesperson Brig. Gen. Hossein Mohebbi confirmed that Iran was now abandoning its previous 2,000-kilometer, or roughly 1,240-mile, ballistic missile-range restriction, according toThe Associated Press. ""That restriction has been lifted for us,"" Mohebbi clarified in the wake of the task force announcement. RUSSIA SECRETLY BOLSTERED IRAN'S MISSILE ARSENAL BEFORE WAR WITH US, RECORDS UNCOVER FILE PHOTO: Iranian missiles are displayed at the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) Aerospace Force Museum in Tehran, Iran, November 15, 2024. Majid Asgaripour/WANA (West Asia press Agency) via REUTERS U.S. Central Commandestablished ""Task Force Iron Gate"", an initiative targeting the movement of advanced Iranian weapons systems, dual-use materials and illicit revenue across Iran's land borders and the Ca","Sun, 08 Nov 2026 18:08:57 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/iran-vows-astonishing-strikes-lifts-missile-range-limit-us-targets-land-routes,2026-11-15 03:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Israeli president taps Netanyahu rival to form government as coalition battle looms,Israeli president taps Netanyahu rival to form government as coalition battle looms,"Israeli president taps Netanyahu rival to form government as coalition battle looms Gadi Eisenkot secured 67 Knesset endorsements over Benjamin Netanyahu, but deep coalition divisions over Arab parties and conscription cloud his path. Chief correspondent Jonathan Hunt reports from Tel Aviv, Israel, on deadlocked coalition negotiations as political factions meet with President Isaac Herzog. Following the elections, Benjamin Netanyahu and political rival Gadi Eisenkot make bids to secure the recommendations needed to form a government. Israeli President Isaac Herzog announced Saturday that he has chosen opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot to form the country's next government, handing Prime MinisterBenjamin Netanyahu'schief rival the first opportunity to build a coalition following an inconclusive national election. Herzog announced his decision on Nov. 7, but the formal presentation of the mandate is scheduled for Sunday, Nov. 8, at 5 p.m. Israeli time. Eisenkot will then have 28 days to assemble a government, with a possible 14-day extension. The decision could mark a significant step toward ending Netanyahu’s tenure, but it would also launch a difficult round of coalition negotiations, with deep disagreements among parties seeking to replace him. NETANYAHU DEFIES EXIT POLLS AS VOTE SHIFTS IN HIS FAVOR, BUT MAJORITY REMAINS ELUSIVE Gadi Eisenkot, leader of the Yashar (""Straight"") party, waves an Israeli flag onstage following the release of the first exit poll results, in Tel Aviv, Oct. 28, 2026.(Ariel Schalit/AP Photo) Following two days of consultations with Israel’s newly elected parliament, Herzogannounced Thursdaythat factions representing 67 of the Knesset’s 120 members had recommended Eisenkot, chairman","Sat, 07 Nov 2026 17:17:37 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-rival-form-government-coalition-battle-looms,2026-11-15 03:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Paris agitators defy police orders, renew nationwide protests centered in Paris","Paris agitators defy police orders, renew nationwide protests centered in Paris","Paris agitators defy police orders, renew nationwide protests centered in Paris Videos and photos show tear gas and fires throughout Paris as 70,000 security forces deploy against France protests despite police bans on gatherings. Thousands of French citizens protested across the country with protests centered in Paris as cost of living and student protests entered their fourth straight week. French authorities dispatched 70,000 officers across the country. Credit: Reuters. Protesters inFranceare continuing to demonstrate in Paris and across the nation despite police prohibitions on gatherings in the capital. The Paris Police Prefecture denied numerous formal requests for permits allowing protests in various areas of the city, citing October riots that led to thousands of arrests and violent clashes between protesters and law enforcement. ""These events demonstrated the intention of certain individuals to target the institutions of the Republic, specifically through actions directed against public buildings and State services in order to undermine the foundations of the Republic,"" the police wrote, according to a Fox News Digital translation of apolice order. ""That these elements characterize a particular and serious risk to public institutions, agent safety, and the normal functioning of public services during such demonstrations,"" the statement continued. FRANCE'S MACRON BLAMES PROTESTS ON 'ULTRA-LEFT GROUPS WHOSE AIM IS TO BRING DOWN THE REPUBLIC' Protesters face policemen during a demonstration for higher wages and in support of the high school protest movement in Paris, Saturday, Nov. 7, 2026.(AP Photo/Emma Da Silva) FRANCE DEPLOYS 70,000 POLICE OFFICERS TO PREPARE FOR NEW WAVE OF PROTESTS ON HALLO","Sat, 07 Nov 2026 14:32:27 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/paris-agitators-defy-police-orders-renew-nationwide-protests-centered-paris,2026-11-15 03:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Gunman opens fire from moving car in European tourist hot spot, leaving 6 dead and at least 15 wounded","Gunman opens fire from moving car in European tourist hot spot, leaving 6 dead and at least 15 wounded","Gunman opens fire from moving car in European tourist hot spot, leaving 6 dead and at least 15 wounded A gunman, reportedly wearing military-style fatigues, allegedly opened fire from a moving vehicle on Kraków, Poland&apos;s Main Square, killing five and injuring at least 15. Fox News correspondent Stephanie Bennett joins ‘Fox Report’ with the latest on the deadly Krakow shooting. Poland’s prime minister says three people were found dead in the gunman’s home. Małopolska Police and MPK S.A. confirmed a Polish gunman opened fire at a popular tourist destination in Kraków Saturday, killing six people and wounding at least 15 more. Of the six dead, four are women and two are men, according to Małopolska Police. Shooting from a moving vehicle, the gunman allegedly targeted people at random, injuring civilians as well as police during the attack on Kraków's bustling Main Square. TEEN WEARING HELMET CAMERA KILLS WORKER AT POLISH SCHOOL AMID FEARS OF COPYCAT ATTACKS ""Six people were killed and fifteen were injured in the incident in the Main Market Square, the Małopolska Provincial Office reported. The perpetrator of the attack was shot and detained by police officers. Rescue services are still working at the scene,"" MPK S.A., the city's municipal public transport company, wrote in a statement shared to X. Video posted on social media showed people running while gunshots rang out. Police shot and wounded the suspect during a gunfight, and the area is now secured, according to authorities. A woman reacts at the site of a shooting near the main market square of Kraków, Poland, Nov. 7, 2026.(Reuters/Jakub Porzycki ) The suspect, who has only been identified by police as a ""citizen of the Republic of Poland,"" was wearing military-style fatigues and used a mil","Sat, 07 Nov 2026 12:37:33 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/gunman-opens-fire-moving-car-european-tourist-hotspot-leaving-5-dead-12-wounded,2026-11-15 03:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Top Gulf official offers glimmer of hope on Trump-Iran nuclear talks as threat of war hangs over region,Top Gulf official offers glimmer of hope on Trump-Iran nuclear talks as threat of war hangs over region,"Top Gulf official offers glimmer of hope on Trump-Iran nuclear talks as threat of war hangs over region A senior United Arab Emirates official says he is cautiously optimistic about U.S.-Iran nuclear talks through Qatari mediation but won&apos;t rule out war. Reporting from Dubai, Fox News Digital examines how the UAE is balancing hopes for a diplomatic breakthrough with preparations for escalation, as Emirati officials and experts warn of Iran's threats to regional security and the global economy. DUBAI, United Arab Emirates — A senior United Arab Emirates official says he is cautiously optimistic about negotiations between the United States and Iran, citing progress through Qatari mediation over the past days, even as fears of renewed military confrontation continue to grip theMiddle East. ""We see some progress. … We hope that both sides will be able to reach a point where they will start building trust and engaging in a way to avoid the war, to find a political solution. … I am a little bit optimistic, but I don't exclude the other option,"" Dr. Ali Rashid Al Nuaimi, chairman of the Defense, Interior and Foreign Affairs Committee of the UAE's Federal National Council, told Fox News Digital in an exclusive interview. His remarks came as Reuters reportedNov. 5that Iran had submitted a new nuclear proposal to Washington through Qatar. Tehran, however, continued to insist that the U.S. meet seven conditions before negotiations could proceed, including sanctions relief and an end to the American naval blockade. IS THIS TRUMP’S LAST ‘LAST CHANCE?' CEASELESS STRING OF BROKEN CEASEFIRES FUELS DOUBT OVER IRAN DEAL Dr. Ali Rashid Al Nuaimi, chairman of the UAE Federal National Council's Defense, Interior and Foreign Affairs Committee, spe","Sat, 07 Nov 2026 04:00:39 -0500",https://www.foxnews.com/world/gulf-official-glimmer-hope-trump-iran-nuclear-talks-threat-war-hangs-region,2026-11-15 03:31:19
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Trump Says US and Canada Have Reached Last-Minute Deal to Delay 50% US Tariffs on Canadian Imports,Trump Says US and Canada Have Reached Last-Minute Deal to Delay 50% US Tariffs on Canadian Imports,"Trump Says US and Canada Have Reached Last-Minute Deal to Delay 50% US Tariffs on Canadian Imports The announcement, which Trump made on his social media platform, buys time for more negotiations and avoids, for now, another strain in already tense relations between the historic allies. Washington:President Donald Trump said Tuesday he was delaying 50% U.S. tariffs on $20 billion worth of Canadian imports after the two countries reached a last-minute deal hours before the sanctions were to go into effect. The announcement, which Trump made on his social media platform, buys time for more negotiations and avoids, for now, another strain in already tense relations between the historic allies. “I have paused the 50% Tariffs against Canada, that were scheduled to kick in tomorrow morning for three days, based on the fact that Canada and the U.S.A., subject to the finalisation of documents, have a DEAL!” Trump posted on Truth Social less than two hours before the 12:01 a.m. Wednesday deadline. If they had gone into effect as scheduled at 12:01 a.m. Wednesday, Trump’s import taxes would have hit Canadian products ranging from hockey sticks to tongue depressors. But the political impact would likely have been bigger than the economic one. Canada had threatened to retaliate against any new tariffs with levies of its own, aggravating a trade fight between countries that sold each other $880 billion worth of goods and services last year. Canadian officials did not immediately respond to requests for comment Tuesday night. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney and Trump had spoken twice by phone in the past two days about the ongoing negotiations, including a call Tuesday afternoon, Carney’s office said, underscoring the last-minute push for a deal. Both countries had re","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 08:51:34 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/trump-says-us-and-canada-have-reached-last-minute-deal-to-delay-50-us-tariffs-on-canadian-imports-2026-08-19-135042,2026-11-15 03:31:21
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,'Allegations Lack Seriousness': Turkiye Denies Israel's Claims Over Syria Airstrikes,'Allegations Lack Seriousness': Turkiye Denies Israel's Claims Over Syria Airstrikes,"'Allegations Lack Seriousness': Turkiye Denies Israel's Claims Over Syria Airstrikes &quot;These air strikes should stop, and we stand against them,&quot; Dujarric said at a UN press briefing on Tuesday. As per Al Jazeera, Egypt's Foreign Ministry also condemned the Israeli strikes, calling them a &quot;dangerous escalation that threatens security and stability in the region&quot;. Ankara:Turkiye on Wednesday rejected Israel's claim that its airstrikes on Syria's Abu al-Duhur military airport were linked to a planned Turkish troop deployment, saying the allegations ""lack seriousness"" and seek to legitimise strikes on Syria's sovereignty and territorial integrity. In a post on X, the Turkish Presidential Communications Directorate said, “The allegations put forward by the Israeli Prime Ministry, which lack seriousness, aim to legitimize Israel's unlawful airstrikes targeting the sovereignty and territorial integrity of Syria.” It added, ""The accusations raised stem from Netanyahu's intent to continue his expansionist and destabilizing policies in the region ahead of elections in Israel."" Turkiye said it supports the establishment of lasting peace in the region, adding that ""the sole path to this lies in Netanyahu abandoning his aggressive and coercive policies and demonstrating respect for international law"". ""Turkey will steadfastly continue its cooperation with the Syrian Government on legitimate grounds to establish peace, stability, and prosperity in Syria, and will never allow Syria to be destabilized,"" it said. The remarks came after Israel carried out airstrikes on the Abu al-Duhur military airport in Syria's eastern Idlib province. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's office said that Syria was allowing Turkish troops to deploy at an airbase near Aleppo. Meanwhile, on Tuesday (local time), UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres' spokesperso","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:27:49 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/allegations-lack-seriousness-turkiye-denies-israel-s-claims-over-syria-airstrikes-2026-08-19-135061,2026-11-15 03:31:21
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,'Substantial Progress Made': Canadian PM Carney as American Tariffs Postponed for 3 Days,'Substantial Progress Made': Canadian PM Carney as American Tariffs Postponed for 3 Days,"'Substantial Progress Made': Canadian PM Carney as American Tariffs Postponed for 3 Days Sharing the remarks in a letter posted on X, Prime Minister Carney reassured that while rigorous engagements remain in place with Washington, Canada remains focused on building a stronger, more independent, and more competitive economy at home. Ottawa:With Ottawa and Washington continually engaged in discussions over the 50 per cent tariff on a select range of Canadian goods, Prime Minister Mark Carney said that the implementation of the tariffs has been postponed until August 21. Sharing the remarks in a letter posted on X, Prime Minister Carney reassured that while rigorous engagements remain in place with Washington, Canada remains focused on building a stronger, more independent, and more competitive economy at home. ""Over the last number of weeks, Canada has engaged in intensive discussions with the United States to address outstanding trade issues and deliver greater certainty and real benefits for Canadian businesses, workers, farmers and families,"" he said. The Canadian Prime Minister observed that while significant headway has been made, key work remains to be done. Substantial progress has been made, although there is important work still to be done. As this work is ongoing, the United States has agreed to postpone the implementation of its 50% tariff on a range of Canadian goods under Section 338 of the U.S. Tariff Act of 1930 until the end of day, August 21,"" he said. The announcement comes in the nick of time as the Trump administration's latest round of tariffs was originally scheduled to take effect at 12:01 a.m. Eastern Time on Wednesday. According to Canadian public broadcaster CBC, the levies would have applied to hundreds of products worth more than USD 28 billion, from plywood and cement to wine ","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:09:03 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/substantial-progress-made-says-canadian-pm-carney-as-american-tariffs-postponed-for-3-days-2026-08-19-135058,2026-11-15 03:31:22
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Former Pakistan PM Imran Khan's Sister Noreen Meets Him at Adiala Jail After 9 Months,Former Pakistan PM Imran Khan's Sister Noreen Meets Him at Adiala Jail After 9 Months,"Former Pakistan PM Imran Khan's Sister Noreen Meets Him at Adiala Jail After 9 Months The development came after a three-member Pakistani Supreme Court bench, headed by Justice Shahid Waheed, directed the government earlier in the day to facilitate weekly meetings between Imran and his family amid concerns over his health. Rawalpindi:Pakistan Tehreek-e-Insaf (PTI) founder Imran Khan's sister, Noreen Niazi, met him at Adiala Jail on Tuesday after a gap of around nine months, following the Pakistani Supreme Court's order allowing weekly meetings between the former Prime Minister and his family, The Express Tribune reported. According to The Express Tribune, this meeting lasted approximately 15 minutes. Noreen briefed Imran about the Supreme Court's order regarding his transfer to Islamabad's Shifa Hospital, enquired about his health, and discussed some ongoing legal matters with him.After the meeting, Noreen confirmed that she had met Imran but did not speak to the media, in line with an assurance given before the court, the report said. She later left Adiala Jail along with her sisters Aleema Khan and Uzma Khan. The Express Tribune reported that Imran also met his wife, Bushra Bibi, with their meeting lasting around 30-35 minutes. Earlier, Bushra Bibi met her daughter, Mubashra Sheikh, and sister-in-law Mehrunnnisa. Speaking to the media after the meeting, Aleema expressed happiness over the Supreme Court order. ""Words cannot describe how happy I am about the meeting. I cannot even imagine where I would have got sweets from. I have appeared before the ATC Rawalpindi from the Supreme Court,"" she added. Asked whether she had received any indication that circumstances were changing, Aleema said, ""Where are we supposed to get any indication from? Do you mean this meeting? Yes, something has happened","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 08:34:57 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/former-pakistan-pm-imran-khan-s-sister-noreen-meets-him-at-adiala-jail-after-9-months-2026-08-19-135039,2026-11-15 03:31:23
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Trump Claims Over 24,000 Noncitizens Voted Illegally in 2020","Trump Claims Over 24,000 Noncitizens Voted Illegally in 2020","Trump Claims Over 24,000 Noncitizens Voted Illegally in 2020 The White House and the Trump administration have drawn direct comparisons between election administration in both countries, asserting that the US relies heavily on self-attestation for citizenship relative to international peers. Washington, DC:US President Donald Trump on Tuesday (local time) claimed that more than 24,000 noncitizens voted illegally in the 2020 election, citing an ongoing review by the US Census Bureau. In a post on Truth Social, Trump said, ""The Census Bureau has begun checking the Voter Records from 2020 against their Citizenship Records. On the first 128,000,000 Voters, the Census Bureau proves that over 24,000 Noncitizens voted illegally!"" ""The Census Bureau is going to analyse the next 32,000,000 Voters, and this number will explode,"" he added. Trump also reiterated his claim about the 2020 election, saying, “I won the election!” He further called for the passage of the SAVE America Act, saying, ""We must pass THE SAVE America Act. Thank you for your attention to this matter!"" His remarks came after he endorsed the proposed Safeguard American Voter Eligibility (SAVE) America Act, introduced in Congress on January 29, which aims to overhaul federal voting standards in the United States. It mandates that state election authorities require physical proof of US citizenship (such as a passport or birth certificate) upon voter registration, alongside valid photo identification at the ballot box; limits mail voting strictly to specific exceptions, including illness, physical disability, active military service, or travel; and directs US states to purge non-citizens from federal voter registries using federal databases. Earlier, in a post on Truth Social on Monday (local time), Trump rec","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 08:38:56 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/trump-claims-over-24000-noncitizens-voted-illegally-in-2020-2026-08-19-135040,2026-11-15 03:31:23
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,MEA Cites Security Concerns for Continued Kartarpur Corridor Closure as SGPC Seeks More Pilgrim Visas,MEA Cites Security Concerns for Continued Kartarpur Corridor Closure as SGPC Seeks More Pilgrim Visas,"MEA Cites Security Concerns for Continued Kartarpur Corridor Closure as SGPC Seeks More Pilgrim Visas MEA Spokesperson Randhir Jaiswal made the remarks while responding to questions on demands for an increase in the number of pilgrim visas and the reopening of the Kartarpur Sahib Corridor. New Delhi:The Ministry of External Affairs (MEA) on Tuesday reiterated that pilgrimage travel between India and Pakistan is governed by bilateral arrangements, while services along the Sri Kartarpur Sahib Corridor continue to remain suspended due to the prevailing security situation. MEA Spokesperson Randhir Jaiswal made the remarks while responding to questions on demands for an increase in the number of pilgrim visas and the reopening of the Kartarpur Sahib Corridor. Jaiswal was also asked about a high-level delegation from the Shiromani Gurdwara Parbandhak Committee (SGPC) meeting Pakistan's Charge d'Affaires in New Delhi to seek an increase in the visa quota for Sikh pilgrims travelling to Pakistan. ""We also have seen some reports about the meeting that you just talked about,"" Jaiswal said. “Every year, as you know, there is a bilateral arrangement between the two countries under which our jathas, Sikh jathas, visit pilgrimage sites in Pakistan.” On the demand from the SGPC and other Sikh organisations for the resumption of services along the Sri Kartarpur Sahib Corridor, the MEA spokesperson said the corridor remains closed in view of the existing security environment. ""On the Kartarpur corridor issue, we had recently addressed a question in the Parliament as well,"" Jaiswal explained. ""As you are aware, the Kartarpur corridor services of Sri Kartarpur Sahib corridor were suspended with effect from 7th May of 2025 given the extant security situation, which continues to be","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 08:13:52 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/mea-cites-security-concerns-for-continued-kartarpur-corridor-closure-as-sgpc-seeks-more-pilgrim-visas-2026-08-19-135033,2026-11-15 03:31:23
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,'We Will Correct Delusions of This Deluded Man': Iran Hits Back at Trump's Assertion Over Hormuz as 'New U.S. Territory','We Will Correct Delusions of This Deluded Man': Iran Hits Back at Trump's Assertion Over Hormuz as 'New U.S. Territory',"'We Will Correct Delusions of This Deluded Man': Iran Hits Back at Trump's Assertion Over Hormuz as 'New U.S. Territory' Iranian Deputy Foreign Minister Kazem Gharibabadi, who described the US President as a &quot;deluded man&quot;, said on Tuesday that while Trump had correctly referred to the &quot;eternal Persian Gulf&quot;, his claims over the Strait of Hormuz would soon be corrected, either by circumstances or by Iran itself. Tehran:As Donald Trump continued his assertions over control of the Strait of Hormuz through an AI-generated image depicting the strategic waterway as ""NEW U.S. Territory"", Iran hit back at the US President, warning that his claims would be ""corrected"", while labelling his claims as delusions. Sharing the image in a post on X, Iranian Deputy Foreign Minister Kazem Gharibabadi, who described the US President as a ""deluded man"", said on Tuesday that while Trump had correctly referred to the ""eternal Persian Gulf"", his claims over the Strait of Hormuz would soon be corrected, either by circumstances or by Iran itself. ""Just as Trump correctly wrote the name of the eternal Persian Gulf, soon his delusion regarding the Strait of Hormuz will either be corrected or we will correct the delusions of this deluded man,"" Gharibabadi said in a post on X. Iran's newly appointed head of the Supreme National Security Council (SNSC), Mohsen Rezaei, also criticised Trump's remarks, saying there was a wide gap between Washington's claims and its ability to influence the strategic waterway. ""The gap between America's inability to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and its claim to own it is greater than the 7,000-mile distance between Washington and the Strait itself. Welcome to the post-American order in the Persian Gulf,"" Rezaei said in a post on X. This comes after Trump, earlier on Tuesday, shared an AI-generated image of the Strait of Hormuz on his Truth Social platform, depicting the strategic wa","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:46:33 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/we-will-correct-delusions-of-this-deluded-man-iran-hits-back-at-trump-s-assertion-over-hormuz-as-new-us-territory-2026-08-19-135034,2026-11-15 03:31:24
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Israel and Syria Agreed to Maintain 'Status Quo' on Security Matters: Netanyahu,Israel and Syria Agreed to Maintain 'Status Quo' on Security Matters: Netanyahu,"Israel and Syria Agreed to Maintain 'Status Quo' on Security Matters: Netanyahu The statement came after reports of Israeli airstrikes on the Abu al-Duhur Airbase in Syria, with the US Special Presidential Envoy for Syria and Iraq, Tom Barrack, expressing concern over what he called an &quot;unnecessary escalation.&quot; Tel Aviv:Israel and Syria had agreed to maintain a status quo on security matters, but Syria was on the verge of breaching the understanding by allowing Turkish troops to deploy at an airbase near Aleppo, the Prime Minister's Office of Israel said on Tuesday. In a post shared on X, the office of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Israel had repeatedly warned Syria that such a deployment would pose a threat to its security. ""The Prime Minister's Office: Israel and Syria agreed to a status quo in security matters, which Syria was on the verge of breaching by permitting Turkish troops to deploy at an airbase near Aleppo. Israel repeatedly warned Syria that such a deployment would pose a threat to Israel's security. Syria chose to ignore these warnings,"" the post read. ""Israel will not tolerate threats to its security, and would welcome a return to the status quo,"" it added. The statement came after reports of Israeli airstrikes on the Abu al-Duhur Airbase in Syria, with the US Special Presidential Envoy for Syria and Iraq, Tom Barrack, expressing concern over what he called an ""unnecessary escalation."" Barrack said the confirmed Israeli airstrikes did not contribute to regional stability and highlighted Syria's recent efforts towards de-escalation with Israel. ""We are deeply concerned that the confirmed Israeli airstrikes on Abu al-Duhur Airbase constitute an unnecessary escalation that does not advance regional stability,"" Barrack said in a post on X. He added that ","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:37:11 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/israel-and-syria-agreed-to-maintain-status-quo-on-security-matters-netanyahu-2026-08-19-135032,2026-11-15 03:31:25
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,At Least 30 Dead After Artisanal Gold Mine Collapses in Central African Republic,At Least 30 Dead After Artisanal Gold Mine Collapses in Central African Republic,"At Least 30 Dead After Artisanal Gold Mine Collapses in Central African Republic Residents, emergency workers, and fellow miners immediately scrambled to initiate desperate rescue efforts, retrieving at least 30 bodies from the debris while administering emergency care to surviving workers pulled from the wreckage. Bangui:At least 30 miners have been killed, and numerous others remain missing following the collapse of an artisanal gold mine in the western region of the Central African Republic (CAR) on Tuesday, August 18. The disaster occurred during morning operations in the Abba region of the Nana-Mambéré prefecture. Residents, emergency workers, and fellow miners immediately scrambled to initiate desperate rescue efforts, retrieving at least 30 bodies from the debris while administering emergency care to surviving workers pulled from the wreckage. Video footage emerging from the site highlighted chaotic scene conditions as rescue personnel and locals worked frantically through heavy mud to locate trapped survivors. Lacking modern machinery, workers were seen using rudimentary tools and their bare hands to clear earth from the collapsed pit. Speaking on the disaster, Deputy Mayor Souleymane Bi issued an urgent plea for international and regional aid to support the ongoing operations. ""It is horrible, and we are calling for help from organisations and all people of goodwill to help pull from the hole those who are unable to do so,"" Bi stated, emphasising that local resources are severely stretched as search efforts continue. Government spokesman Evariste Ngamana expressed deep condolences on behalf of the administration to the affected families and workers, adding that authorities are mobilising relief resources to support the site. The incident highlights the severe risks associated w","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:33:38 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/at-least-30-dead-after-artisanal-gold-mine-collapses-in-central-african-republic-2026-08-19-135029,2026-11-15 03:31:25
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Iran Rejects UAE Claim of Missile Launch, Calls Accusations 'Baseless'","Iran Rejects UAE Claim of Missile Launch, Calls Accusations 'Baseless'","Iran Rejects UAE Claim of Missile Launch, Calls Accusations 'Baseless' Baghaei &quot;completely rejected&quot; the UAE's claim and expressed regret over the accusations against the Islamic Republic of Iran, according to a statement issued by the Iranian Foreign Ministry on its official Telegram channel. Tehran:Iran on Tuesday (local time) rejected the United Arab Emirates' claim that Tehran launched a missile towards the country, with Iranian Foreign Ministry spokesperson Esmail Baghaei calling the allegations contrary to the principle of good neighbourliness and harmful to regional efforts to build trust. Baghaei ""completely rejected"" the UAE's claim and expressed regret over the accusations against the Islamic Republic of Iran, according to a statement issued by the Iranian Foreign Ministry on its official Telegram channel. ""This behaviour is contrary to the principle of good neighbourliness and disrupts ongoing efforts to strengthen trust between regional countries and prevent the escalation of insecurity in the region,"" Baghaei said. The Iranian Foreign Ministry spokesperson called on regional countries to refrain from making ""baseless accusations"" against Tehran. Baghaei said the current situation in the region was already complicated due to what Iran described as actions by the United States and Israel against regional peace and security. ""The Foreign Ministry spokesman called on all regional parties to refrain from making baseless accusations against the Islamic Republic of Iran, considering the existing complexities due to the ongoing evils of the US and the Zionist regime against regional peace and security, especially the history of numerous false flag operations,"" he said. The statement came after the United Arab Emirates Ministry of Defence on Tuesday said its ai","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:27:18 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/iran-rejects-uae-claim-of-missile-launch-calls-accusations-baseless-2026-08-19-135030,2026-11-15 03:31:26
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"UAE Condemns 'Confirmed Israeli Airstrikes' on Syrian Airbase, Rejects 'Infringement of Sovereignty'","UAE Condemns 'Confirmed Israeli Airstrikes' on Syrian Airbase, Rejects 'Infringement of Sovereignty'","UAE Condemns 'Confirmed Israeli Airstrikes' on Syrian Airbase, Rejects 'Infringement of Sovereignty' &quot;The Ministry reaffirmed the UAE's unwavering position in support of Syria's stability and territorial integrity, underscoring solidarity with the Syrian people and support for all efforts aimed at fulfilling their aspirations for security, peace, dignity, peaceful coexistence, and development,&quot; it said. Abu Dhabi:The United Arab Emirates on Tuesday (local time) condemned ""confirmed Israeli airstrikes"" on the Abu al-Duhur Military Airbase in Syria's Idlib Governorate, calling them a violation of Syria's sovereignty and international law. In a statement, the UAE Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MoFA) said it ""condemns in the strongest terms"" the Israeli raids and reaffirmed its rejection of any actions that threaten Syria's security and stability. ""The UAE categorically rejects any infringement on the sovereignty of Syria or threats to its security and stability,"" the Ministry said. The UAE Ministry said Israel's continued attacks on Syrian territory constitute a ""flagrant violation of international law"" and the 1974 Disengagement Agreement between Syria and Israel. ""The Ministry reaffirmed the UAE's unwavering position in support of Syria's stability and territorial integrity, underscoring solidarity with the Syrian people and support for all efforts aimed at fulfilling their aspirations for security, peace, dignity, peaceful coexistence, and development,"" it said. The UAE also called on the international community to take immediate steps to stop repeated attacks on Syrian territory and prevent further escalation that could threaten regional and international peace and security. ""The UAE called on the international community to take immediate action to halt the repeated attacks on Syrian territory and to stop the escalation and any actions that could heighten regional tensions an","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:19:51 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/uae-condemns-confirmed-israeli-airstrikes-on-syrian-airbase-rejects-infringement-of-sovereignty-2026-08-19-135028,2026-11-15 03:31:26
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"US Sanctions ICC President, Senior Trial Lawyer Amid Trump Administration's Campaign Against Court","US Sanctions ICC President, Senior Trial Lawyer Amid Trump Administration's Campaign Against Court","US Sanctions ICC President, Senior Trial Lawyer Amid Trump Administration's Campaign Against Court In a press statement issued by Marco Rubio, Secretary of State, on Tuesday, the US administration said the action was taken as part of its campaign against what it described as the &quot;politicised&quot; and &quot;unaccountable&quot; nature of the ICC. Washington, DC:The Donald Trump administration has designated two officials of the International Criminal Court (ICC), including its President Tomoko Akane and ICC Senior Trial Lawyer Aboudoulaye Seye, under sanctions, accusing the global tribunal of abusing its authority and threatening national sovereignty. In a press statement issued by Marco Rubio, Secretary of State, on Tuesday, the US administration said the action was taken as part of its campaign against what it described as the ""politicised"" and ""unaccountable"" nature of the ICC. ""The Trump Administration has been clear: the International Criminal Court (ICC) is a corrupt and fatally politicised supranational court that has maliciously abused its authority and exceeded its mandate. We will not tolerate its assault on state sovereignty,"" the statement said. The administration said the sanctions were imposed under Executive Order 14203, titled “Imposing Sanctions on the International Criminal Court.” ""These individuals have directly engaged in efforts by the ICC to investigate, arrest, detain, or prosecute officials whose government has not consented to ICC jurisdiction,"" it said. The US further alleged that the ICC has repeatedly attempted to exercise authority over nationals of the United States and other countries that have neither accepted its jurisdiction nor ratified the Rome Statute. ""This sets a dangerous precedent for all nations,"" the statement added. The Trump administration said it plans to continue its dip","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:09:42 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/us-sanctions-icc-president-senior-trial-lawyer-amid-trump-administration-s-campaign-against-court-2026-08-19-135026,2026-11-15 03:31:27
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Trump Shares AI-Generated Image Declaring Strait Of Hormuz 'NEW US Territory' Amid Tensions With Iran,Trump Shares AI-Generated Image Declaring Strait Of Hormuz 'NEW US Territory' Amid Tensions With Iran,"Trump Shares AI-Generated Image Declaring Strait Of Hormuz 'NEW US Territory' Amid Tensions With Iran Trump shares an AI-generated image labelling the Strait of Hormuz as ‘New U.S. Territory’ as Tehran rejects US claims of control and vows to keep the key oil route closed until its conditions are met. Washington:Continuing his assertions of claiming control over the world's most critical oil transit bottleneck, the Strait of Hormuz, US President Donald Trump on Tuesday (local time) shared an AI-generated image of the waterway being labelled as ""New US Territory."" The image shared by Trump on his Truth Social Platform, depicts a blue map of the waterway between Iran and the Arabian Peninsula, with the Strait of Hormuz circled inside a frame reading ""NEW U.S. Territory"" in bold lettering. The post further escalates his administration's claims of control over the strategic energy choke point amid ongoing tensions with Iran. Trump made similar remarks on Monday (local time), asserting that Washington DC has ""total control"" in the region. Speaking to reporters, Trump emphasised the effectiveness of the US naval blockade on Iran and stressed that oil prices are coming down and the Strait of Hormuz is open. He added that Iran is in big trouble, noting, ""they have 300 per cent inflation, the country's a mess, and their military is totally defeated."" ""I think it's a great idea. I mean, we control it with the blockade. I like the idea of declaring it a territory. We have total control over the Strait. Now, they can be a nuisance; they can put a mine in the water, and people don't like having mines hit their billion-dollar ships. But the blockade has been very effective. Now, maybe that will stop, or maybe it'll open up even further, but we're taking out millions of barrels of oil a ","Tue, 18 Aug 2026 17:58:01 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/trump-shares-ai-generated-image-declaring-strait-of-hormuz-new-us-territory-amid-tensions-with-iran-2026-08-18-135001,2026-11-15 03:31:28
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Pakistan's Supreme Court Orders Former PM Imran Khan to Be Moved to Hospital from Jail Amid Health Concerns,Pakistan's Supreme Court Orders Former PM Imran Khan to Be Moved to Hospital from Jail Amid Health Concerns,"Pakistan's Supreme Court Orders Former PM Imran Khan to Be Moved to Hospital from Jail Amid Health Concerns The Supreme Court of Pakistan ordered former Prime Minister Imran Khan to be moved to a hospital from jail due to health concerns. He has been imprisoned since August 2023 and faces multiple cases following his ousting in 2022. Islamabad:The Supreme Court of Pakistan ordered on Tuesday that former Prime Minister Imran Khan ​be moved to a hospital from jail, his Pakistan Tehreek-e-Insaf party ‌said, meeting a longstanding demand of his party and family, who had raised concerns about his health. Cricketer-turned-politician Khan, 73, has been in jail since August ​2023, convicted in a string of cases that he ​says were politically driven following his ouster in 2022. A three-member Supreme Court bench, headed by Justice Shahid Wahid and comprising Justice Naeem Akhtar Afghan and Justice Ishtiaq Ibrahim, issued the ruling on Imran's petition for his hospitalisation. His sons ⁠repeatedly expressed concern regarding his deteriorating health last year, with his ​lawyers saying he had lost significant vision in his right eye ​while in prison. ""It's a very welcome order, and we wish it had happened sooner so his eye and general health would not have deteriorated this much,"" ​PTI spokesperson Zulfikar Bukhari said. ""He should remain in hospital until all ​doctors are satisfied,"" he said. The court has directed Khan be moved to Shifa ‌International ⁠Hospital within 48 hours and remain there until September 16, Khan's spokesperson Naeem Haider Panjutha said on X. Since he lost power in a no-confidence vote, Khan has faced multiple cases, including over state ​gifts and an ​unlawful marriage. Some ⁠convictions have been suspended or overturned, with appeals pending. He denies wrongdoing. Underscoring the severit","Tue, 18 Aug 2026 14:14:28 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/pakistan-s-top-court-orders-former-pm-imran-khan-be-moved-to-hospital-from-jail-his-party-says-2026-08-18-134984,2026-11-15 03:31:28
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,4 Air Strikes Hit Military Airport in Syria's Idlib in First Attack Since Al-Assad's Fall,4 Air Strikes Hit Military Airport in Syria's Idlib in First Attack Since Al-Assad's Fall,"4 Air Strikes Hit Military Airport in Syria's Idlib in First Attack Since Al-Assad's Fall According to Al Jazeera, four strikes targeted the military airport. There has been no official statement on the strikes so far, while the aircraft that carried them out have not been identified. Idlib: Four air strikes hit the Abu al-Zuhour military airport in the eastern countryside of Idlib province in northern Syria, in the first such attack on the facility since the fall of Bashar al-Assad's regime in December 2024, Al Jazeera reported. According to Al Jazeera, four strikes targeted the military airport. There has been no official statement on the strikes so far, while the aircraft that carried them out have not been identified. Several other airports in Syria have previously been targeted, including Aleppo International Airport, Nayrab military airport, al-Shairat airport in Homs, and the airports at Tiyas and al-Dab'a in central Syria. However, Abu al-Zuhour had not been targeted since the fall of the al-Assad regime in December 2024. According to Al Jazeera, before the regime's fall, Abu al-Zuhour airport was repeatedly caught in firing between Syrian revolutionary factions and forces loyal to the former regime and its militias, with control of the facility changing hands. The development also comes as former Syrian President Bashar al-Assad was sentenced to death in absentia by a criminal court in Damascus on Tuesday, after being convicted of premeditated murder, while Atef Najib, former head of political security in southern Syria's Deraa province, was also sentenced to death after being found guilty of premeditated murder and torture, Al Jazeera reported. Earlier on Monday, Colombia recognised Israeli sovereignty over the occupied Syrian Golan Heights, join","Tue, 18 Aug 2026 11:31:52 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/4-air-strikes-hit-military-airport-in-syria-s-idlib-in-first-attack-since-al-assad-s-fall-2026-08-18-134969,2026-11-15 03:31:29
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"'Took Full Advantage of Ceasefire': Iran Prepares for Bigger Fight with US and Israel, Eyes Kuwait Ground Raid","'Took Full Advantage of Ceasefire': Iran Prepares for Bigger Fight with US and Israel, Eyes Kuwait Ground Raid","'Took Full Advantage of Ceasefire': Iran Prepares for Bigger Fight with US and Israel, Eyes Kuwait Ground Raid Following the signing of the memorandum of understanding by US President Donald Trump with Iran in mid-June, Washington had anticipated that the arrangement would facilitate the reopening of the Strait of Hormuz and initiate a wind-down of the conflict. Washington, DC:Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) has utilised the period of relative calm following a June memorandum of understanding with the United States to prepare for a wider confrontation, including formulating plans for pre-emptive strikes and potential operations on enemy territory, according to a Wall Street Journal report citing Iranian and Arab officials. The military preparations encompass accelerated missile production, enhanced missile accuracy, expanded counterintelligence operations, and an enlarged role for the powerful Revolutionary Guard within Iran's military apparatus. ""We took full advantage of the ceasefire period,"" Revolutionary Guard spokesman Brig Gen Hossein Mohebbi said in July, according to the WSJ report. ""We enhanced our capabilities, accelerated our missile production rate and improved missile accuracy."" Following the signing of the memorandum of understanding by US President Donald Trump with Iran in mid-June, Washington had anticipated that the arrangement would facilitate the reopening of the Strait of Hormuz and initiate a wind-down of the conflict. However, Iran's hard-line leadership interpreted the agreement differently, according to Iranian and Arab officials cited by the WSJ. They assessed that the agreement might represent an attempt by the US and Israel to alleviate economic pressure globally while gaining time to prepare a larger attack. Consequently, Iran used the intervening window to prepare for what its leadership","Tue, 18 Aug 2026 11:20:33 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/took-full-advantage-of-ceasefire-iran-prepares-for-bigger-fight-with-us-and-israel-eyes-kuwait-ground-raid-2026-08-18-134968,2026-11-15 03:31:29
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,The 60-Day Deadline for an Iran Peace Deal Is Expiring: Here's Where Things Stand,The 60-Day Deadline for an Iran Peace Deal Is Expiring: Here's Where Things Stand,"The 60-Day Deadline for an Iran Peace Deal Is Expiring: Here's Where Things Stand It called for the Strait of Hormuz to be reopened but gave Iran a vaguely defined role in facilitating traffic, leaving open the possibility it could charge fees after the 60-day deadline. Iran has seized on that clause to claim control over the waterway. The deal that U.S. President Donald Trump signed at Versailles in June set an ambitious 60-day deadline for ending the war with Iran and reaching an accord on its nuclear program. The deadline was Monday, and the two sides are further apart than they were then. Talks, such as they are, have focused on reopening the Strait of Hormuz and lifting a U.S. blockade on Iran, both of which were supposed to have happened under the interim deal. There has been no sign of any compromise on the strait, or that detailed nuclear talks have even begun. The U.S., meanwhile, has no good options for getting out of the war it started alongside Israel. Acceding to Iran's latest demands would mean giving it control over a critical international waterway that carried a fifth of the world's traded oil and gas before the war — and would be tantamount to admitting defeat. Escalating the deeply unpopular war would further draw down U.S. supplies of advanced missile interceptors, jolt the world economy, and drive up gas prices ahead of U.S. congressional elections. So both sides have dug in, hoping the other will blink first. So far, neither has. The June deal, known as the Memorandum of Understanding, called for a halt to all military operations and set a 60-day deadline for an agreement to permanently end the war and resolve the longstanding dispute over Iran's nuclear activities. It called for the Strait of Hormuz to be reopened but gave Iran a vaguely defined role in facilitating traffic, leaving o","Tue, 18 Aug 2026 08:51:28 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/the-60-day-deadline-for-an-iran-peace-deal-is-expiring-here-s-where-things-stand-2026-08-18-134954,2026-11-15 03:31:30
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Mayor Says Shooting Incident at a School in Southern Philippines, Reports Two Casualties","Mayor Says Shooting Incident at a School in Southern Philippines, Reports Two Casualties","Mayor Says Shooting Incident at a School in Southern Philippines, Reports Two Casualties The mayor ​of the ‌southern Philippine city ​of ​Zamboanga said there had ⁠been ​a shooting ​incident at a high school ​on ​Tuesday. There were two ‌casualties, ⁠both students, one of whom ​was ​the ⁠gunman, Mayor ​Khymer Adan ​Olaso ⁠told DZMM radio. Manila:Two people were killed in a shooting at a high school in the ​southern Philippines on Tuesday and the situation was now ‌under control, officials said, in the second such incident in the country in nearly two months. The shooting took place at a ​school attached to the Ateneo de Zamboanga University ​in the southern city of Zamboanga. The city's mayor ⁠Khymer Adan Olaso told DZMM radio both casualties were ​students and one was the shooter, who used a ""high-powered ​firearm"". The university's president Ernald Andal confirmed there was no longer an active shooting and there were no additional fatalities or reported injuries. ""As of ​now, we confirm that there are two fatalities,"" Andal ​said. ""There are no more active shooters."" Andal said the university was coordinating ‌with ⁠authorities and would provide more details as information became available. ""We do not want any of these things to happen. We wish to prioritise the safety of all our students,"" ​he said. It followed ​an attack at ⁠a public high school in June in Tacloban City in which at least three ​students were killed and about 20 others injured ​after ⁠two of their schoolmates opened fire on campus. The shooting came less than 10 days after a high-profile incident in Thailand, ⁠where ​a student went on a shooting rampage ​at a school on the outskirts of the capital Bangkok.","Tue, 18 Aug 2026 08:03:11 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/mayor-says-shooting-incident-at-a-school-in-southern-philippines-reports-two-casualties-2026-08-18-134951,2026-11-15 03:31:31
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Trump Invokes Indian Electoral System in Bid to Pass Save America Act,Trump Invokes Indian Electoral System in Bid to Pass Save America Act,"Trump Invokes Indian Electoral System in Bid to Pass Save America Act US President Donald Trump urged Congress to pass the SAVE America Act, referencing India's election system and voter ID requirements. He highlighted that in India's last election, all voters had valid photo IDs. The Act aims to ensure only US citizens vote, require ID for registration, and restrict mail-in ballots. Washington:US President Donald Trump on Monday (local time) renewed his call for the passage of the Safeguard American Voter Eligibility (SAVE) America Act, citing India's election system and voter identification requirements. In a post on Truth Social, Trump recalled remarks attributed to India's Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar earlier this month regarding voter identification requirements in the US. ""Earlier this month, India's Chief Election Commissioner, Gyanesh Kumar, asked our Administration -- How can you have Elections in the US without a valid Photo ID?"" Trump said. Referring to India's last general election, Trump said, ""India's last Election had 646,000,000 Voters! Less than 1 per cent voted by mail, and every single Voter had to have a VALID Photo Identity Document."" Trump reiterated his call for Congress to pass the SAVE America Act, saying, ""We need to pass THE SAVE AMERICA ACT, now!"" According to the White House, the legislation is aimed at ensuring that only US citizens participate in deciding federal elections. ""American citizens -- and only American citizens -- should decide American elections,"" the White House said, describing the SAVE America Act as a ""common sense, bipartisan bill."" The White House said the proposed legislation would require voters to provide valid identification before registering to vote in a federal election, along with proof of citizenship. It also proposes restrictions on mail-in ballots, allowing them only in cases involvi","Tue, 18 Aug 2026 07:31:19 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/trump-invokes-indian-electoral-system-in-bid-to-pass-save-america-act-2026-08-18-134947,2026-11-15 03:31:31
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Trump's Son-in-law Urged Netanyahu to 'Not Create Obstacles' to Gaza Peace Plan; Israeli PM Says No Withdrawal Until Hamas Disarms: Report,Trump's Son-in-law Urged Netanyahu to 'Not Create Obstacles' to Gaza Peace Plan; Israeli PM Says No Withdrawal Until Hamas Disarms: Report,"Trump's Son-in-law Urged Netanyahu to 'Not Create Obstacles' to Gaza Peace Plan; Israeli PM Says No Withdrawal Until Hamas Disarms: Report US Special Envoy and son-in-law of US President Donald Trump, Jared Kushner, on Monday pressed Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu during a more than four-hour meeting to advance the Trump-backed Gaza ceasefire proposal and &quot;not create obstacles&quot; to the stalled peace plan, as per reports. Tel Aviv, Israel:US Special Envoy and son-in-law of US President Donald Trump, Jared Kushner, on Monday pressed Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu during a more than four-hour meeting to advance the Trump-backed Gaza ceasefire proposal and ""not create obstacles"" to the stalled peace plan, CNN reported, citing an Israeli source familiar with the discussions. According to CNN, Netanyahu, however, maintained his stance that Israel would not withdraw its forces from Gaza until Hamas was completely disarmed. The meeting came after Netanyahu rejected the Trump administration's 15-point Gaza ceasefire plan announced earlier this month. According to CNN, citing the Israeli source, Netanyahu told Kushner that moving ahead with the proposal was ""problematic"" because of Israel's upcoming elections at the end of October. The source said Netanyahu, who is seeking support from right-wing voters and has been trailing in several polls, has been reluctant to make concessions on Gaza ahead of the elections. The source further said Netanyahu told the US side that Israel would not alter its policy regarding the ongoing targeted killings of Hamas commanders. Instead, Netanyahu told Kushner and Nickolay Mladenov, director of the Board of Peace, that Hamas would need to take the first steps, according to CNN, citing the source. Kushner and Mladenov had met representatives of Hamas in Egypt on Sunday. The central disagreement remains over the sequencing of Hamas' disarmament and an Israeli mi","Mon, 17 Aug 2026 23:01:53 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/trump-s-son-in-law-urged-netanyahu-to-not-create-obstacles-to-gaza-peace-plan-israeli-pm-says-no-withdrawal-until-hamas-disarms-report-2026-08-17-134939,2026-11-15 03:31:32
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Bhojpuri’s Global Flame-Keeper: Dr Sarita Boodhoo’s Path to Winning India’s Highest Diaspora Honour,Bhojpuri’s Global Flame-Keeper: Dr Sarita Boodhoo’s Path to Winning India’s Highest Diaspora Honour,"Bhojpuri’s Global Flame-Keeper: Dr Sarita Boodhoo’s Path to Winning India’s Highest Diaspora Honour Dr Boodhoo's scholarly works, including Bhojpuri Traditions in Mauritius, Kanya Dan, &amp; Geet Gawai – Bhojpuri Folk Songs in Mauritius, remain indispensable bibles for researchers of global diaspora and linguistics. The Pravasi Bharatiya Samman stands tall as the ultimate validation of her life's work On Pravasi Bharatiya Divas in 2025, as President Droupadi Murmu handed over the Pravasi Bharatiya Samman -- India’s highest honor for the diaspora -- the applause wasn't just for a woman. It was an ovation for a language, a history, and a legacy that refused to be forgotten. For Dr. Sarita Boodhoo, that moment on 10 January 2025 was the culmination of a lifetime's quiet, fierce devotion. A fourth-generation daughter of the Bhojpuri belt, born as Sarita Makhan in Port Louis, Mauritius, she represents a lineage forged in the crucible of the 19th-century indenture system. Her ancestors were Girmitiyas, souls who boarded ships starting in 1834 carrying little more than grief, resilience, and the songs of the Gangetic plains. In the sugarcane fields of Mauritius, Bhojpuri became their lifeline – the language of the hearth, the soil, and a quiet resistance against erasure. Yet, as generations turned, the tongue of the ancestors faced a modern quietus, threatened by the pressures of Creole, French, English, and urban drift. Enter a scholar with the heart of a poet and the tenacity of a movement-builder. From the Gangetic Plains to the Mauritian Classroom Dr. Boodhoo’s journey to becoming the global flame-keeper of Bhojpuri began with the power of education. Armed with an Indian government cultural scholarship, she crossed oceans to study Geography at Lady Brabourne College in Calcutta, before diving deeper into her roots to earn a Master’s and a PhD in Hindi from the prestigious Ban","Mon, 17 Aug 2026 20:57:52 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/bhojpuris-global-flame-keeper-dr-sarita-boodhoos-path-to-winning-indias-highest-diaspora-honour-2026-08-17-134935,2026-11-15 03:31:33
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,'We'll Bomb Them': Trump Warns Oman Over Deal With Iran to Control Strait of Hormuz,'We'll Bomb Them': Trump Warns Oman Over Deal With Iran to Control Strait of Hormuz,"'We'll Bomb Them': Trump Warns Oman Over Deal With Iran to Control Strait of Hormuz US President Donald Trump warns Oman against interfering in Iran talks over the Strait of Hormuz, threatening military action as Tehran-Muscat negotiations continue. Washington:US President Donald Trump on Monday warned Oman against getting involved in a deal with Iran over control of the Strait of Hormuz, saying the United States would ""bomb the s*** out of them"" if Muscat interferes with Washington's position on the strategic waterway. During a phone call with Fox News correspondent Trey Yingst, Trump discussed the situation with Iran as the 60-day memorandum of understanding, signed in June, in order to open negotiations to end the war in West Asia, expires. Trump told Fox News that ""Iran should raise the white flag of surrender"" in that context while adding that he has ""no time schedule"". ""I'm not in a hurry,"" the US President said. Asked about parallel talks between Iran and Oman over control of the Strait of Hormuz, Trump said, ""If Oman gets in the way, we'll bomb the sh** out of them."" The US President further indicated that the US naval blockade was continuing to put new economic pressure on the Iranian regime despite counterstatements made publicly by Tehran. He said the Iranians were ""good poker players"" but were ""dying"" and added that the US midterm elections, scheduled to take place in November, had nothing to do with his thinking. Trump also spoke about the depletion of US weapons stockpiles currently in West Asia, saying, ""What we've used so far is peanuts."" He said the United States has a large number of mid-level weapons, while many of the more advanced systems had been given to Ukraine by former President Joe Biden, inclu","Mon, 17 Aug 2026 19:49:15 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/we-ll-bomb-the-sh-out-of-them-trump-warns-oman-over-deal-with-iran-to-control-hormuz-2026-08-17-134922,2026-11-15 03:31:33
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"PoJK Electoral Process Under Scrutiny, Human Rights Council Demands Independent Audit","PoJK Electoral Process Under Scrutiny, Human Rights Council Demands Independent Audit","PoJK Electoral Process Under Scrutiny, Human Rights Council Demands Independent Audit The Human Rights Council of Pakistan-occupied Jammu and Kashmir demanded that polling station-wise results, the number of votes cast, rejected ballots, vote counts and other electoral records be made publicly accessible so that the process can be independently verified. Muzaffarnagar, PoJK:The Human Rights Council of Pakistan-occupied Jammu and Kashmir has raised serious concerns over the recent electoral process, saying that the completion of polling in most constituencies and the emergence of a party in a position to form the government cannot by themselves settle questions surrounding transparency, participation and public trust. ""The electoral process cannot be reduced to the number of seats won,"" the Council said in a post on X, stressing that a genuine public mandate requires transparency, free participation, fundamental freedoms and confidence in the electoral system. The Council pointed to the postponement of elections in Poonch and Sudhanoti, reports of violence, communication blackouts and electoral boycotts as issues that require immediate attention. It also highlighted what it described as a significant discrepancy between reports of low turnout and electoral boycotts in certain areas carried by international media and subsequent official turnout figures. ""A reliable explanation is essential for this stark discrepancy between ground observations, official turnout and electoral results,"" the Council said. It demanded that polling station-wise results, the number of votes cast, rejected ballots, vote counts and other electoral records be made publicly accessible so that the process can be independently verified. The Council further called for an ""independent, impartial and credible audit"" of the entire electoral process and urged a","Mon, 17 Aug 2026 16:59:55 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/pojk-electoral-process-under-scrutiny-human-rights-council-demands-independent-audit-2026-08-17-134912,2026-11-15 03:31:33
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"'Trump Planning to Use Nuclear Weapons on Iran,' Claims Ex-US Congresswoman","'Trump Planning to Use Nuclear Weapons on Iran,' Claims Ex-US Congresswoman","'Trump Planning to Use Nuclear Weapons on Iran,' Claims Ex-US Congresswoman Former US Congresswoman Marjorie Taylor Greene claims that senior White House officials are discussing strategies for using nuclear weapons against Iran. She accuses the Trump administration of lowering the threshold for such actions, although she provides no evidence or specific names. Washington:Former US Congresswoman Marjorie Taylor Greene has alleged that senior officials at the White House are holding strategy meetings regarding the potential deployment of nuclear weapons against Iran. Taking to social media platform X on Sunday, Greene asserted that the high-level discussions were ""real"" and accused the Trump administration of lowering the threshold for nuclear action. However, she did not provide evidence or documents, nor did she identify specific officials involved in the alleged discussions. Greene further claimed that the administration is disregarding internal US intelligence assessments which, according to her, indicate Iran is not on the verge of developing a nuclear weapon. She argued that Washington is instead being influenced by warnings originating from Israel. Warning of dire global consequences, Greene stated that any US decision to deploy nuclear weapons against Iran could trigger a much wider conflict, resulting in massive casualties and severe economic strain. ""Trump promised no more foreign wars,"" she wrote, arguing that an escalation could instead result in a major global conflict.The White House has not immediately offered a comment regarding Greene's claims. Furthermore, there has been no public confirmation from the US government or defence officials that Washington has altered its nuclear posture or is actively preparing nuclear strikes against Iran. Greene's statements come amid heightened military friction between Washington a","Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:23:35 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/trump-planning-to-use-nuclear-weapons-on-iran-claims-ex-us-congresswoman-2026-08-17-134886,2026-11-15 03:31:34
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Iranian Army Chief Offers $30,000 Bounty for Killing or Capturing US Soldiers, Doubles Reward for Women","Iranian Army Chief Offers $30,000 Bounty for Killing or Capturing US Soldiers, Doubles Reward for Women","Iranian Army Chief Offers $30,000 Bounty for Killing or Capturing US Soldiers, Doubles Reward for Women Iranian Army Chief Amir Hatami announced a USD 30,000 reward for anyone who kills or captures a US soldier, increasing to double that amount for women. This decision follows numerous requests from individuals wanting to participate. Tehran:Iranian Army Chief Amir Hatami has announced a USD 30,000 bounty for anyone who kills or captures a US soldier, with the reward reportedly doubled when the act is carried out by a woman, amid ongoing friction between Tehran and Washington. The decision comes after a ""large number of requests"" from individuals seeking to participate, state-run IRNA cited the military chief as saying. However, he did not specify the location or timeframe for any such potential attack or capture. ""Anyone who kills or captures and hands over an invading American military personnel will receive a reward equivalent to USD 30,000 or 5 billion tomans from the Islamic Republic of Iran's Army,"" Hatami said, using an informal monetary unit equivalent to 10,000 Iranian rials. ""Courageous Iranian women who carry out such an action will receive double the reward,"" he added. Reiterating Tehran's standing demand for the withdrawal of US forces from the region, Hatami remarked that ""they no longer have permission to enter the Persian Gulf, the Gulf of Oman or the Strait of Hormuz"". The announcement comes despite there being no known deployment of US ground troops inside Iran during the conflict, apart from a major rescue operation in April involving approximately 200 US personnel and over 170 aircraft to recover the weapons systems officer of a downed F-15. The hostilities commenced on February 28 following US and Israeli strikes targeting Iran. Fighting was subsequently halted by an April ceasefire, f","Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:13:22 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/iranian-army-chief-offers-30000-bounty-for-killing-or-capturing-us-soldiers-doubles-reward-for-women-2026-08-17-134887,2026-11-15 03:31:34
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Ukraine Launches One of Its Largest Aerial Attacks of the War, Killing at Least 6 People in Russia","Ukraine Launches One of Its Largest Aerial Attacks of the War, Killing at Least 6 People in Russia","Ukraine Launches One of Its Largest Aerial Attacks of the War, Killing at Least 6 People in Russia Russia’s Ministry of Defense said that it had destroyed 822 Ukrainian drones overnight. Some 600 drones were detected headed toward the Russian capital, Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin said, with a third of those destroyed over the Moscow region itself. Ukraine launched hundreds of drones across Russia Sunday, killing at least six people in one of Kyiv’s largest aerial attacks of the war. Kyiv has stepped up its attacks on Russia this year, with long-range missiles and swarms of drones increasingly targeting military industries and energy facilities. It has also increasingly pummeled giant Wildberries depots, burning billions of dollars’ worth of merchandise belonging to the Russian online retail giant and bringing the war home to the Russian public nearly 4½ years into Moscow’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine. Russia’s Ministry of Defense said that it had destroyed 822 Ukrainian drones overnight. Some 600 drones were detected headed toward the Russian capital, Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin said, with a third of those destroyed over the Moscow region itself. An 83-year-old man was killed after a Ukrainian drone hit a private home in the Moscow region, local Gov. Andrey Vorobyov said. He also confirmed that a Ukrainian attack had sparked a blaze at a Wildberries warehouse in the town of Podolsk. A drone attack targeted three towns in Russia’s southwestern Rostov region, killing five people, local Gov. Yury Slyusar said. The attack, with more than 150 drones, damaged several homes and a railway station and sparked a forest fire. A Russian missile attack on Ukraine’s Kryvyi Rih killed two people and wounded 14 others, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy wrote on social media Sunday. He also said that one more person had been ","Sun, 16 Aug 2026 16:39:04 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/ukraine-launches-one-of-its-largest-aerial-attacks-of-the-war-killing-at-least-6-people-in-russia-2026-08-16-134858,2026-11-15 03:31:35
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Human Rights Council PoJK Alleges Security Forces Open Fire on Protesters in PoJK, Demands Probe","Human Rights Council PoJK Alleges Security Forces Open Fire on Protesters in PoJK, Demands Probe","Human Rights Council PoJK Alleges Security Forces Open Fire on Protesters in PoJK, Demands Probe According to the council, the incident took place last night amid the ongoing situation in Pakistan-occupied Jammu &amp; Kashmir. The Human Rights Council claimed that Saiyam Liaqat lost his life after security forces allegedly opened &quot;severe fire&quot; on protesters. Rawalakot:The Human Rights Council PoJK has alleged that security forces opened fire on peaceful protesters at Umer Farooq Chowk in Rawalakot, PoJK, resulting in the death of a youth identified as Saiyam Liaqat and injuries to several others. In a statement issued following the incident, the council said it had received information about the alleged firing along with a video that had come into the public domain. According to the council, the incident took place last night amid the ongoing situation in Pakistan-occupied Jammu & Kashmir. The Human Rights Council claimed that Saiyam Liaqat lost his life after security forces allegedly opened ""severe fire"" on protesters. It further said that reports indicated that several other individuals were injured in the incident. The council also referred to what it described as unverified cumulative reports concerning the broader situation in PoJK, claiming that nearly 100 people have lost their lives since June 5. ""These are not mere numbers but shattered homes, grieving families, and irreplaceable human lives,"" the council said, while questioning how long the people of PoJK would continue to pay with their lives for what it described as their basic rights. The Human Rights Council asserted that peaceful assembly and freedom of expression are fundamental rights of citizens. It termed the alleged use of lethal force and direct firing against protesters ""unacceptable under any circumstances"". The council called for an immediate halt to firi","Sun, 16 Aug 2026 15:00:42 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/human-rights-council-pojk-alleges-security-forces-open-fire-on-protesters-in-pojk-demands-probe-2026-08-16-134853,2026-11-15 03:31:36
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"US Navy Faces Fresh Sanitation Row As Sailors Report Poor Toilets, Shortages Aboard Warships","US Navy Faces Fresh Sanitation Row As Sailors Report Poor Toilets, Shortages Aboard Warships","US Navy Faces Fresh Sanitation Row As Sailors Report Poor Toilets, Shortages Aboard Warships The US Navy is under scrutiny for sanitation issues aboard the USS Abraham Lincoln and USS Boxer. A sailor criticized the poor toilet facilities on the Lincoln, while female crew members on the Boxer face shortages of feminine hygiene products. New Delhi:The US Navy is facing fresh scrutiny over conditions aboard its warships, with footage appearing to show poor sanitation facilities aboard the aircraft carrier USS Abraham Lincoln and reports of shortages of basic feminine hygiene products aboard the USS Boxer. A US Navy sailor has shared footage purportedly showing the condition of toilets aboard the USS Abraham Lincoln, criticising the facilities and questioning how sailors were expected to use them. ""Wait till y’all see toilets, man,"" the sailor says in the footage while showing the bathroom facilities inside the aircraft carrier. The sailor also mocks the familiar Navy recruitment pitch, saying, “They say join the Navy, right?” The footage has drawn attention to reported infrastructure and sanitation problems aboard the carrier. The claims come amid reports of wider sanitation-related concerns on the USS Abraham Lincoln that have reportedly caused frustration among members of the crew. Meanwhile, concerns have also emerged aboard the USS Boxer, where female service members are reportedly running short of basic feminine hygiene supplies, including sanitary pads and tampons. According to a family member of a service member aboard the Wasp-class amphibious assault ship, women on the vessel have been “begging” for additional supplies as existing stocks run low. The family member reportedly said that sailors have been rationing what they have and asking relatives back home to send additional supplies, but some care p","Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:31:10 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/us-navy-faces-fresh-sanitation-row-as-sailors-report-poor-toilets-shortages-aboard-warships-2026-08-16-134835,2026-11-15 03:31:36
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Twelve Killed and at Least 10 Injured in Polish Bus Crash in Hungary,Twelve Killed and at Least 10 Injured in Polish Bus Crash in Hungary,"Twelve Killed and at Least 10 Injured in Polish Bus Crash in Hungary A Polish bus overturned on a motorway in eastern Hungary, killing 12 people and injuring at least 10 others. The accident occurred near Mezokeresztes as the bus, carrying 57 passengers and two drivers, veered into a ditch, likely due to the driver falling asleep. Budapest:A dozen people were killed and at least 10 injured ​after a Polish bus overturned at night on a motorway ‌in eastern Hungary, Hungarian Prime Minister Peter Magyar said on Sunday morning in a Facebook post. The bus ran into a ditch and tipped over early on Sunday ​near the town of Mezokeresztes in eastern Hungary, police said, ​adding that the bus was heading towards the city of ⁠Nyiregyhaza on the motorway when the accident happened. State news agency MTI ​said there were 57 passengers and two drivers on the bus. Pictures ​from the scene showed a badly damaged red bus lying on one side in a ditch by the motorway with windows smashed and belongings and suitcases scattered ​around. ""A Polish-registered bus travelling on the M3 motorway towards Nyiregyhaza ... veered ​off the straight stretch of road into a ditch and overturned. Preliminary information suggests ‌the ⁠driver likely fell asleep,"" police said on their website. Polish President Karol Nawrocki said on X: ""It is with deep sorrow that I received the tragic news of the Polish bus accident in Hungary, in which so ​many of our ​compatriots died."" Twelve ⁠people lost their lives and several others were injured in the accident, police said, adding that they were ​taking the bus driver into custody. The injured have been ​taken to ⁠hospital. Polish Foreign Minister Radoslaw Sikorski said on X that a ""tragic accident"" involving a bus carrying Polish tourists happened in Hungary. ""The consular service is operational.","Sun, 16 Aug 2026 13:07:42 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/twelve-killed-and-at-least-10-injured-in-polish-bus-crash-in-hungary-2026-08-16-134844,2026-11-15 03:31:37
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Vietnam Airlines Boeing 787 Overruns Munich Runway During Takeoff, Returns Safely","Vietnam Airlines Boeing 787 Overruns Munich Runway During Takeoff, Returns Safely","Vietnam Airlines Boeing 787 Overruns Munich Runway During Takeoff, Returns Safely A Vietnam Airlines Boeing 787-9 Dreamliner on a Munich-Hanoi flight returned to Munich after a serious incident during takeoff. The aircraft overran the runway, suffered a tailstrike, and experienced tyre damage. Passengers evacuated safely. A Vietnam Airlines Boeing 787-9 Dreamliner operating a Munich-Hanoi flight returned to Munich Airport on Saturday after reportedly suffering a serious incident during takeoff, according to flight-tracking website Flightradar24 and the airline. Flight VN-34, operated by Boeing 787-9 aircraft VN-A867, reportedly rotated extremely late during takeoff and overran the runway before becoming airborne. Preliminary reports said the aircraft travelled around 120 metres beyond the runway end, entering the grass and coming close to the first row of approach lights. The aircraft also reportedly suffered a tailstrike and tyre damage. After takeoff, the aircraft climbed to around 10,000 feet before the crew received a tyre-pressure indication and decided to dump fuel before returning to Munich. Flightradar24 said the aircraft circled for more than two hours to burn fuel. Around 90 minutes after departure, the Boeing 787 made two low approaches to Munich's Runway 26R before landing safely. Smoke was reportedly seen coming from the left main landing gear, after which the aircraft became disabled on the runway. Passengers were evacuated using emergency slides, with the fire brigade present at the scene, according to Flightradar24. Vietnam Airlines said the Hanoi-bound flight returned to its departure airport due to a ""technical issue"", without providing further details. ""The flight crew followed all required procedures and landed safely at Munich Airport. The passengers and cabin crew members","Sun, 16 Aug 2026 09:16:16 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/vietnam-airlines-boeing-787-overruns-munich-runway-during-takeoff-returns-safely-2026-08-16-134832,2026-11-15 03:31:38
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,19-Year-Old Arrested in Connection With Virginia State University Shooting,19-Year-Old Arrested in Connection With Virginia State University Shooting,"19-Year-Old Arrested in Connection With Virginia State University Shooting Police arrested 19-year-old Camron Harris, who was found in a dormitory closet at Virginia State University, in connection with a shooting on campus that left five people injured, including one critically. Authorities reported that Harris is not a student and that four of the injured individuals, aged 17 to 23, were also not students. Police arrested a 19-year-old found hiding in a dormitory closet at Virginia State University on Saturday in connection with an overnight shooting on campus that left five people wounded, including one with critical injuries. Camron Harris of Henrico, Virginia, is not a student on campus nor were four of the people injured, Chesterfield County Police said in a statement. They ranged in age from 17 to 23. One of the injured, a 20 year old, is a student and has now been released from the hospital, authorities said. The victims’ names have not been released. Authorities have given no information about a possible motive. Police obtained eight felony warrants for Harris, including for malicious wounding and the use of a firearm in the commission of a felony. It wasn’t immediately clear if he had an attorney who could speak on his behalf. Efforts to reach Harris’ family by phone were unsuccessful. The university said in an earlier statement that authorities were searching for multiple suspects, but police provided no additional information Saturday evening about the search. University officials said earlier in the day that law enforcement did not believe there was an immediate threat to the campus community, and a campus lockdown had been lifted. The shooting, just after 1:30 a.m. Saturday, prompted a campus lockdown and came as students were getting ready for the new school year. It happened near the university’s Quad Annexes, where campus police and Chesterfield County officers d","Sun, 16 Aug 2026 07:46:53 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/19-year-old-arrested-in-connection-with-virginia-state-university-shooting-2026-08-16-134828,2026-11-15 03:31:38
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Magnitude 7.7 Earthquake Strikes Off Indonesia’s Coast, Killing at Least 47 and Toppling Buildings","Magnitude 7.7 Earthquake Strikes Off Indonesia’s Coast, Killing at Least 47 and Toppling Buildings","Magnitude 7.7 Earthquake Strikes Off Indonesia’s Coast, Killing at Least 47 and Toppling Buildings A magnitude 7.7 earthquake struck eastern Indonesia, resulting in at least 47 fatalities, according to the National Disaster Mitigation Agency (BNPB). Rescue efforts face challenges as landslides block access to Nagekeo, near the epicenter. Tsunami waves under 1 meter were reported, prompting a temporary warning. Jakarta:At least 47 people were killed after a magnitude 7.7 earthquake and dozens of aftershocks struck off ​eastern Indonesia on Saturday, the National Disaster Mitigation Agency (BNPB) said in its latest statement. Rescue teams have yet to reach Nagekeo, the region ‌closest to the epicentre, after landslides blocked roads and disrupted communications, officials said. ""The quake was massive, the shock was so strong,"" said Nona, a 51-year-old resident of Talibura, a village in East Nusa Tenggara. ""There were 13 of us inside the house and we all ran to save ourselves."" Tsunami waves of less than 1 metre (3 feet) were recorded in several areas of the ​Southeast Asian nation after the early-morning quake. Authorities lifted a tsunami warning about three hours later. Earlier, rescuers in the port town of Maumere found ​20 dead, six injured and two people trapped under rubble, said Fathur Rahman, head of the city's rescue agency. Maumere ⁠is the main town in Sikka Regency on Flores Island in eastern Indonesia. Suharyanto, head of the BNPB, earlier said residents remained trapped in several buildings across the ​affected area, while there were reports of landslides blocking a number of roads. Teams have yet to reach Nagekeo and mobile communications in the region were affected, Fathur ​told Reuters earlier. Attempts to reach the area by road were thwarted by landslides, while another team was trying to reach it by ferry, he said. About 2,000 residents in Nagekeo evacuated, and dam","Sun, 16 Aug 2026 07:28:25 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/magnitude-77-earthquake-strikes-off-indonesias-coast-killing-at-least-47-and-toppling-buildings-2026-08-16-134827,2026-11-15 03:31:39
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Qatar Denies Detaining Three Iranian Pilots, Dubs Reports As 'Misleading'","Qatar Denies Detaining Three Iranian Pilots, Dubs Reports As 'Misleading'","Qatar Denies Detaining Three Iranian Pilots, Dubs Reports As 'Misleading' Qatar denied claims of detained Iranian pilots, calling them misleading amid sensitive diplomatic efforts. Qatari Foreign Ministry spokesperson Al-Ansari explained that contact was made with pilots who allegedly breached airspace, and necessary defensive measures were taken. Doha:Qatar on Saturday (local time) categorically denied reports claiming that Iranian pilots were detained, stating that the allegations were misleading and came at a sensitive time amid ongoing diplomatic efforts to de-escalate regional tensions. Qatar's Foreign Ministry spokesperson, Majed Mohammed Al-Ansari, made the remarks in an X post, stating that contact had been established with the pilots after they allegedly breached Qatari airspace and that their targeting trajectory was confirmed. ""We categorically deny the claims that have been circulated regarding the detention of Iranian pilots, and we are surprised by these misleading statements at this specific timing,"" the spokesperson said. The spokesperson noted that Qatari authorities attempted to communicate with the pilots and, after receiving no response, followed the rules of engagement before taking ""the necessary measures"" to defend Qatari territory in accordance with international law. He added that Qatar had clarified the matter through official channels at the time. Regarding search and rescue operations, Qatar said its teams searched for the pilots' remains and later coordinated with Iran to hand over the remains of one pilot who was found. ""Qatari search and rescue teams, which possess global efficiency and expertise, fulfilled their duty to the fullest in searching for the pilots' remains,"" the spokesperson said. Qatar also stated that it had invited an Iranian team to visit and review the details of the sea","Sun, 16 Aug 2026 07:16:55 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/qatar-denies-detaining-three-iranian-pilots-dubs-reports-as-misleading-2026-08-16-134826,2026-11-15 03:31:39
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,CENTCOM Chief Concludes 10-Day West Asia Tour As USS Abraham Lincoln Prepares to Return,CENTCOM Chief Concludes 10-Day West Asia Tour As USS Abraham Lincoln Prepares to Return,"CENTCOM Chief Concludes 10-Day West Asia Tour As USS Abraham Lincoln Prepares to Return Admiral Brad Cooper, Commander of US Central Command, completed a 10-day visit to West Asia, meeting leaders in Bahrain, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Saudi Arabia, and the UAE. His trip coincided with tensions between the US and Iran regarding the Strait of Hormuz. Washington:As the United States continues its naval blockade on Iran, Commander of US Central Command (CENTCOM) Adm Brad Cooper completed a 10-day trip to West Asia on Saturday (local time), which included visits to six countries and a US Navy aircraft carrier operating in the Arabian Sea, according to a CENTCOM statement. Adm Cooper concluded the trip on August 15 after meeting senior civilian and military leaders in Bahrain, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Saudi Arabia, and the United Arab Emirates, in addition to meeting US service members deployed across the region. More than 50,000 US service members are currently operating across West Asia in support of various missions, CENTCOM said. The visit came in the backdrop of tensions between the US and Iran, with both nations staking claims over control of the Strait of Hormuz. According to CENTCOM, during his visits ashore, Cooper recognised exceptional performers, reenlisted troops, and presided over the leadership transition of the Combined Joint Task Force-Operation Inherent Resolve (CJTF-OIR). Major General Kevin Lambert handed over command of CJTF-OIR to Rear Adm Liam Hulin on August 11 during a ceremony at the task force's headquarters in Jordan. During the maritime leg of his visit, Cooper met sailors and Marines aboard the USS Abraham Lincoln (CVN 72) for the second time this year. He had earlier visited the aircraft carrier in February alongside US Special Envoy for Peace Missions Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner. Addressing th","Sun, 16 Aug 2026 07:09:40 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/centcom-chief-concludes-10-day-west-asia-tour-as-uss-abraham-lincoln-prepares-to-return-2026-08-16-134825,2026-11-15 03:31:40
Times of India,India (Mainstream),en,UK PM Burnham's speechwriter caught using ChatGPT to draft speech,UK PM Burnham's speechwriter caught using ChatGPT to draft speech,"UK PM Burnham's speechwriter caught using ChatGPT to draft speech <img align=""left"" border=""0"" hspace=""10"" src=""https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135845919.cms"" style=""margin-top: 3px; margin-right: 5px;"" />An anonymous speechwriter for Prime Minister Andy Burnham was seen using ChatGPT to draft a keynote address. The speech focused on criticizing former Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher's legacy and addressing the cost-of-living crisis. Burnham emphasized the importance of these issues during his talk with Welsh Labour members. Opposition members have criticized both the aide's actions and Burnham’s government's plans to address economic challenges. Join conversation Share your thoughts in the comments Be respectful ·TOI community guidelines",2026-11-15T08:19:50+05:30,https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-pm-burnhams-speechwriter-caught-using-chatgpt-to-draft-speech/articleshow/135845919.cms,2026-11-15 03:31:40
