Times of India,India (Mainstream),en,"Jimothy Card Auction: Rare card sells for $20,100; proceeds may fund Abby’s college","Jimothy Card Auction: Rare card sells for $20,100; proceeds may fund Abby’s college","Jimothy Card Auction: Rare card sells for $20,100; proceeds may fund Abby’s college <img align=""left"" border=""0"" hspace=""10"" src=""https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135788946.cms"" style=""margin-top: 3px; margin-right: 5px;"" />A young baseball enthusiast from Seattle secured an esteemed baseball card during a Mariners game. This unique card showcased Jimothy, a raccoon who captured the internet's attention due to his extraordinary look. Initially a complimentary giveaway, the card has now emerged as a remarkable collectible valued at an astonishing $20,100. With multiple offers pouring in, her family decided to auction it on eBay, generating significant buzz. Join conversation Share your thoughts in the comments Be respectful ·TOI community guidelines",2026-11-15T05:58:00+05:30,https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-13-year-old-seattle-baseball-fan-picked-up-a-free-trading-card-at-a-mariners-game-without-knowing-she-had-the-only-gold-version-in-existence-weeks-later-collectors-paid-20100-for-the-raccoon-themed-card/articleshow/135788946.cms,2026-11-15 03:31:41
Times of India,India (Mainstream),en,A bronze leg found in 1820 considered Roman loot now believed to belong to a statue of Antoninus Pius,A bronze leg found in 1820 considered Roman loot now believed to belong to a statue of Antoninus Pius,"A bronze leg found in 1820 considered Roman loot now believed to belong to a statue of Antoninus Pius <img align=""left"" border=""0"" hspace=""10"" src=""https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135837858.cms"" style=""margin-top: 3px; margin-right: 5px;"" />Emperor Antoninus Pius, celebrated for his peace-driven rule and military expeditions, may have a newly discovered connection to history. A bronze leg unearthed in Scotland suggests a statue that honored him was disassembled by Roman forces prior to their withdrawal in AD 161, challenging prior beliefs of theft. This discovery sheds light on how Rome strategically managed its monuments, and further archaeological investigations could reveal more insights. Join conversation Share your thoughts in the comments Be respectful ·TOI community guidelines",2026-11-15T05:50:00+05:30,https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/giant-statue-of-roman-emperor-antoninus-pius-discovered-in-scottish-bog-the-mystery-of-the-bronze-leg-unveiled/articleshow/135837858.cms,2026-11-15 03:31:41
