Times of India,India (Mainstream),en,"Texas appeals court upholds sale of marital home despite wife's challenge to $685,000 offer","Texas appeals court upholds sale of marital home despite wife's challenge to $685,000 offer","Texas appeals court upholds sale of marital home despite wife's challenge to $685,000 offer <img align=""left"" border=""0"" hspace=""10"" src=""https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135800314.cms"" style=""margin-top: 3px; margin-right: 5px;"" />In a Texas court, a woman expressed her discontent with the ruling permitting a receiver to sell her marital home. The appellate court upheld the initial decision, dismissing her objections to the receiver's role in accepting a $685,000 offer for the house. The ruling clarified that her financial stake did not afford her control over the sale, highlighting the need for precise wording in divorce agreements related to property transactions. Join conversation Share your thoughts in the comments Be respectful ·TOI community guidelines",2026-11-15T03:57:00+05:30,https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-woman-fought-the-court-ordered-sale-of-her-marital-home-after-a-receiver-received-a-685000-offer-despite-a-divorce-decree-awarding-her-60-of-net-proceeds-an-appeals-court-upheld-the-sale-and-related-orders/articleshow/135800314.cms,2026-11-15 03:31:43
