Times of India,India (Mainstream),en,"2 Infants buried in Peru about 1,600 years ago; one had a rare fatal birth defect called cyclopia","2 Infants buried in Peru about 1,600 years ago; one had a rare fatal birth defect called cyclopia","2 Infants buried in Peru about 1,600 years ago; one had a rare fatal birth defect called cyclopia <img align=""left"" border=""0"" hspace=""10"" src=""https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135831152.cms"" style=""margin-top: 3px; margin-right: 5px;"" />In southern Peru, archaeologists uncovered the remains of two infants buried together, one exhibiting cyclopia. Genetic analysis confirmed that the infant with cyclopia had trisomy 13, a chromosomal condition. Their burial in a single ceramic vessel reveals insights into ancient funerary practices. Researchers highlighted that the infant's condition did not result in unusual treatment in life or death. This discovery emphasizes the historical presence of congenital differences in human populations. Join conversation Share your thoughts in the comments Be respectful ·TOI community guidelines",2026-11-15T03:50:00+05:30,https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/ancient-dna-reveals-genetic-condition-behind-1600-year-old-infants-cyclopia-found-in-peru/articleshow/135831152.cms,2026-11-15 03:31:43
