Zee News,India (Right Wing),en,"Obama mocks Trump's White House decor, slams administration's stance on Iran war | Video","Obama mocks Trump's White House decor, slams administration's stance on Iran war | Video","Obama mocks Trump's White House decor, slams administration's stance on Iran war | Video US midterm elections: Barack Obama compared President Donald Trump's gold White House renovations to a Cheesecake Factory and criticised his Iran policy at an Ohio rally ahead of the November 3, midterm elections. Subhrajit is a journalist with over three years of newsroom experience, covering national and international geopolitics with a sharp focus on India–China–Pakistan affairs. He has spent more than two years with India’s largest television news agency, ANI, and over a year with DD News. He holds a Master’s degree in Mass Communication. He can be reached atsubhrajit.roy@india.com Former US president Barack Obama turned President Donald Trump's White House makeover into a campaign punchline on Saturday, comparing its gold-heavy decor to a restaurant run by Iraq's former dictator Saddam Hussein. Speaking at a rally in Cleveland, Ohio, Obama said Trump appeared more focused on renovating the White House than on addressing rising household costs ahead of the November 3 midterm elections. ""I don't know if you've noticed, but he seems very focused on home renovations. He should be on HGTV,"" Obama told supporters at the Cleveland Public Auditorium, drawing laughter from the crowd. QUOTE OF THE YEAR. Obama: “Trump seems very focused on home renovations. He should be on HGTV. What’s up with the gold? He’s got the White House looking like Saddam Hussein opened up a Cheesecake Factory.” https://t.co/WPGlB4ziFz Referring to the ballroom project, the paved Rose Garden and changes to the South Lawn, Obama said, ""He's got the White House looking like Saddam Hussein opened a Cheesecake Factory. Just gold everywhere."" The changes referred to by Obama are part of a wider renovation programme at th","Sunday, October 25, 2026, 16:13  +0530",https://zeenews.india.com/world/barack-obama-mocks-donald-trump-white-house-gold-cheesecake-factory-ohio-2026-3076984.html,2026-11-15 03:31:49
Zee News,India (Right Wing),en,Trump says France 'burning down' because of its immigration policies; claims protests not related to education,Trump says France 'burning down' because of its immigration policies; claims protests not related to education,"Trump says France 'burning down' because of its immigration policies; claims protests not related to education US President Donald Trump blamed France’s immigration policies for the ongoing unrest, drawing parallels with his administration’s immigration crackdown as protests over the cost of living and education funding spread across France. The bureau represents a collective of experienced journalists, editors, and correspondents who work across television, digital, and social platforms to deliver timely, accurate, and wide-ranging news coverage. Zee Media Bureau's coverage spans politics, business, economy, technology, health, entertainment, and global affairs. The bureau follows a collaborative newsroom model, where stories are researched, verified, and published by a team. This ensures speed, editorial consistency, and adherence to journalistic standards, particularly for breaking news and developing stories. US President Donald Trump on Saturday said that France was “burning down” because it had opened its borders to people who “hate it”, rejecting claims that the unrest was linked to education. ""They have police in France, but they're not allowed to do their job. So France is right now burning down because it opens its borders to people who hate it. These are people who hate it. They hate France. They hate the people of France,"" Trump said while addressing a campaign rally for Republican candidates in Perry, Georgia. Citing the situation in France, Trump drew comparisons with US immigration policies as he said, ""And you know what you do with those people? Never let them come into your country. That's what we do. But now, Ossoff (Georgia senator) wants to import millions and millions of anti-American third-world migrants who see our civilization as nothing but a target to loot, plunder, and pillage. And we'r","Sunday, October 25, 2026, 10:57  +0530",https://zeenews.india.com/world/trump-says-france-burning-down-because-of-its-immigration-policies-claims-protests-not-related-to-education-3076973.html,2026-11-15 03:31:49
Zee News,India (Right Wing),en,Trump says US could attack Iran 'tomorrow' despite earlier pledge,Trump says US could attack Iran 'tomorrow' despite earlier pledge,"Trump says US could attack Iran 'tomorrow' despite earlier pledge Donald Trump said US forces could strike Iran as soon as Sunday but also raised the possibility of a deal, while Tehran issued conflicting accounts of talks over the Strait of Hormuz. Subhrajit is a journalist with over three years of newsroom experience, covering national and international geopolitics with a sharp focus on India–China–Pakistan affairs. He has spent more than two years with India’s largest television news agency, ANI, and over a year with DD News. He holds a Master’s degree in Mass Communication. He can be reached atsubhrajit.roy@india.com US President Donald Trump has suggested US forces could strike Iran as early as Sunday, despite previously saying no attack would take place before the US midterm elections. Speaking after voting in Florida on Saturday, Trump also left open the possibility of a negotiated deal, as conflicting accounts emerged from Tehran about talks over the Strait of Hormuz. Asked whether Washington was preparing another attack, Trump refused to reveal his plans. ""Do you really think I'd tell you that? Maybe tomorrow,"" he told reporters at a polling station in West Palm Beach. He said there was also a chance of a ""nice, big, beautiful agreement"" with Iran. The president said Iranian officials wanted an agreement but questioned whether they would honour its terms. ""They want to make a deal, but the problem is, will they hold the deal?"" he asked. His remarks marked a change in tone from October 8, when he said the United States would not attack Iran before the midterm elections on November 3. His latest comments suggested he was no longer ruling out military action during that period. Trump also defended the US military's","Sunday, October 25, 2026, 10:16  +0530",https://zeenews.india.com/world/trump-iran-attack-maybe-tomorrow-strait-of-hormuz-deal-3076970.html,2026-11-15 03:31:49
Zee News,India (Right Wing),en,Trump hints at fresh military strike; Iran threatens to cut undersea cables in Gulf,Trump hints at fresh military strike; Iran threatens to cut undersea cables in Gulf,"Trump hints at fresh military strike; Iran threatens to cut undersea cables in Gulf Donald Trump has suggested fresh military action against Iran, prompting renewed concern over the Middle East conflict. Iranian security officials say Tehran has prepared plans to target undersea internet cables in the Gulf if attacked again. Subhrajit is a journalist with over three years of newsroom experience, covering national and international geopolitics with a sharp focus on India–China–Pakistan affairs. He has spent more than two years with India’s largest television news agency, ANI, and over a year with DD News. He holds a Master’s degree in Mass Communication. He can be reached atsubhrajit.roy@india.com US President Donald Trump has suggested another military strike on Iran, while Iranian officials have warned that they could retaliate by damaging internet cables beneath the Gulf. The warnings came on Friday as efforts to end the eight-month conflict struggled to advance. Any attack on these cables could disrupt banking, online services and communications across parts of the Middle East. At a rally in Fort Myers, Florida, on Friday, Trump said, ""We may do another little Epic Fury."" The reference was to Operation Epic Fury, the US military campaign launched against Iran on February 28. He did not say when any new attacks might happen or what they would target. Earlier in the day, Trump argued that Washington had the ability to end the conflict quickly, but suggested it could instead allow the fighting to wind down. His comments came despite a statement earlier this month that the United States would not attack Iran before the November 3, midterm elections. Rising fuel prices have placed new pressure on his administration as voters prepare to choose the next Congress. As per media reports, two senior Iran","Saturday, October 24, 2026, 11:21  +0530",https://zeenews.india.com/world/trump-iran-strikes-undersea-internet-cables-hormuz-threat-3076961.html,2026-11-15 03:31:50
Zee News,India (Right Wing),en,"Tibet hit by 7.0-magnitude earthquake: How deep was it, are there any casualties?","Tibet hit by 7.0-magnitude earthquake: How deep was it, are there any casualties?","Tibet hit by 7.0-magnitude earthquake: How deep was it, are there any casualties? The earthquake originated 173 km below the surface, weeks after an avalanche and floods devastated areas near the Nepal-Tibet border. The bureau represents a collective of experienced journalists, editors, and correspondents who work across television, digital, and social platforms to deliver timely, accurate, and wide-ranging news coverage. Zee Media Bureau's coverage spans politics, business, economy, technology, health, entertainment, and global affairs. The bureau follows a collaborative newsroom model, where stories are researched, verified, and published by a team. This ensures speed, editorial consistency, and adherence to journalistic standards, particularly for breaking news and developing stories. New Delhi:A 7.0-magnitude earthquake struck Tibet on Thursday evening (October 22). Tremors were felt across several areas. The National Centre for Seismology (NCS) said the earthquake originated 173 km below the earth's surface. People in several areas came out of their homes and buildings after feeling the tremors. No official reports of casualties or major damage to property have emerged so far. Authorities are expected to assess the situation as more information becomes available. The earthquake comes weeks after an August 26 avalanche and floods along the Nepal-Tibet border that left thousands dead or missing and damaged homes, roads, bridges and hydropower projects. Rescue and rehabilitation work is still under way in the affected areas. The earthquake's magnitude and depth put it among the stronger seismic events recorded in the region in recent months. Its depth of 173 km means it originated well","Thursday, October 22, 2026, 23:48  +0530",https://zeenews.india.com/world/tibet-hit-by-7-0-magnitude-earthquake-how-deep-was-it-are-there-any-casualties-3076911.html,2026-11-15 03:31:50
Zee News,India (Right Wing),en,"Indian embassy in France asks nationals to stay vigilant amid violent protests, curfews","Indian embassy in France asks nationals to stay vigilant amid violent protests, curfews","Indian embassy in France asks nationals to stay vigilant amid violent protests, curfews Indians have been asked to avoid large gatherings and crowded places where protests are taking place, and to follow instructions from French authorities. Simran Akhouri is a journalist currently serving as a Sub Editor with Zee News English. She holds a postgraduate degree from the University of Delhi and has three years of experience in the media industry. Prior to her current role, she was associated with organisations such as The Indian Express and Jagran New Media. She primarily writes on news, viral content, and education. She can be contacted atsimran.akhouri@india.com The Indian Embassy in France on Wednesday asked Indian nationals living in or travelling to the country to remain vigilant, after cost-of-living protests turned violent and several cities imposed curfews. In a post on X, the embassy said that in view of the recent developments and localised curfews, people should remain vigilant and exercise due caution. Advisory for Indian Nationals in France and Those Travelling to France In view of the recent developments and localised curfews imposed in France, please remain vigilant and exercise due caution. Please avoid large gatherings and crowded places where protests are taking place, and follow the instructions and advisories issued by the local French authorities. Please also stay informed through local news, follow official updates (https://t.co/mmCApj3WkV) and check for public transport disruptions (https://t.co/iyq6LLm83T). In case of any emergency, Indian nationals can contact: Embassy of India, Paris: +33 6 48 34 00 63 | cons.paris@mea.gov.in Consulate General of India, Marseille: +33 7 43 16 25 59| cgo.mar","Thursday, October 22, 2026, 10:40  +0530",https://zeenews.india.com/india/indian-embassy-in-france-asks-nationals-to-stay-vigilant-amid-violent-protests-curfews-3076854.html,2026-11-15 03:31:50
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Cape Verde votes for president, with incumbent Jose Maria Neves favoured to win","Cape Verde votes for president, with incumbent Jose Maria Neves favoured to win","Cape Verde votes for president, with incumbent Jose Maria Neves favoured to win The polls will remain open for 10 hours, with provisional results expected overnight. Cape Verde holds a presidential election on Sunday, with incumbent Jose Maria Neves favoured to win a second term as head of state of the west African archipelago renowned for its democratic stability. He goes up against the country's first-ever woman candidate, Joana Rosa Amado, among other contenders, when voting starts at 8:00 am (0900 GMT). Polls will remain open for 10 hours, with provisional results expected overnight. The island nation made world headlines this year when its national football team reached the knockout stages in its first-ever World Cup, and when a cruise ship containing people with hantavirus docked off its shores. Located in the middle of the Atlantic approximately 600 kilometres (375 miles) off the coast ofSenegal, the Portuguese-speaking country comprising 10 volcanic islands is attracting more tourists every year. Unlike several of its west African neighbours, where presidential elections have been tense in recent years, Cape Verde is known for its political stability and good governance. It is considered a model of democracy in Africa, with strong economic growth. The country is known for its ""morabeza"" (""hospitality"", in local creole), openness, and carnivals. It also has its own style of music. According to the Mo Ibrahim Foundation 2026 index on global governance, Cape Verde ranks third out of 54 countries on the continent. The archipelago has a semi-presidential system in which the executive is dominated by the prime minister. The president do","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:37:00 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/cape-verde-votes-for-president-with-incumbent-jose-maria-neves-favoured-to-win-101794708613305.html,2026-11-15 03:31:51
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"‘Gadi, lets set aside differences’: Netanyahu pushes for unity govt; Eisenkot rejects ‘spin move’","‘Gadi, lets set aside differences’: Netanyahu pushes for unity govt; Eisenkot rejects ‘spin move’","‘Gadi, lets set aside differences’: Netanyahu pushes for unity govt; Eisenkot rejects ‘spin move’ Netanyahu urged Eisenkot to put aside all disputes and join a unity government for Israel's security interests, particularly against the Iranian threat. Israeli caretaker prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Saturday urged Gadi Eisenkot's Yashar Party to enter a unity government, saying a government that relies on support from Arab parties will not be able to confront the Iranian threat. However, Eisenkot rejected the appeal as “yet another spin move”. In a video statement posted on X, Netanyahu said he had an important conversation with Eisenkot, adding that they have known each other for a long time, even before the latter's tenure as the IDF's chief of staff. ""This meeting only strengthened my understanding of how essential it is at this time to establish a national unity government, a government that will include all the parties that support the existence of the State of Israel as the state of the Jewish people, and that will be able to meet the immense and complex security challenges ahead of us,"" he said. Netanyahu alleged that the Iranian regime was working to revive its nuclear programme to be used against Israel and stressed the importance of removing ""this existential threat once and for all."" He said a minority government or a coalition that relies on ""supporters of terrorism"", referring to Arab parties, will not be able to achieve this goal, but a unity government can safeguard Israel's security for many years. Also Read |Israeli spy chief visits US as Netanyahu seeks to build pressure on Trump to resume Iran war ""Gadi, instead of trying to establish a shaky and dangerous government that will be unable to meet, ev","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:26:41 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/gadi-lets-set-aside-differences-netanyahu-pushes-for-unity-govt-eisenkot-rejects-spin-move-101794706325431.html,2026-11-15 03:31:51
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"US Labor Department official warns H-1B visas cannot be used as business model, signals wider crackdown","US Labor Department official warns H-1B visas cannot be used as business model, signals wider crackdown","US Labor Department official warns H-1B visas cannot be used as business model, signals wider crackdown The Labor Department’s inspector general warned companies not to treat temporary work visas as a business model. US Labour Department Inspector General Anthony D’Esposito has warned companies against treating temporary work visas as abusinessmodel, signalling further suspensions and intensified investigations into alleged immigration fraud as theTrumpadministration steps up scrutiny of foreign worker hiring. “Thevisasystem and these visas that are in place are all temporary. They are not a method of doing business. You're only supposed to use, for example, an H1B visa if you cannot find a willing and able American to do the same job.” D’Esposito said in an interview to Fox News. “Nobody can tell me that we don't have the best and brightest here in theUnited Statesof America,” he added, defending the administration’s emphasis on hiring American workers. The warning comes amid an expanding investigation into alleged abuses of the H-1B visa and employment-basedgreen cardprogrammes. Also Read:Trump administration warns of more H-1B, PERM suspensions for universities, companies In October, the Trump administration suspendedMicrosoft, Adobe and six major technology outsourcing companies from the Permanent Labor Certification (PERM) programme, which employers use to sponsor foreign workers for employment-based green cards. The affected companies include Cognizant,Infosys, Tata Consultancy Services, Wipro, HCL Technologies and Capgemini. The suspensions halted the acceptance and processing ofPERMapplications involving the companies, disrupting an important pathway to permanent residency for for","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:07:20 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/us-labor-department-official-warns-h-1b-visas-cannot-be-used-as-business-model-signals-wider-crackdown-101794705744672.html,2026-11-15 03:31:51
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Dr. Gary Dorshimer, team doctor for Flyers, dies at 71 after over 40 years of service","Dr. Gary Dorshimer, team doctor for Flyers, dies at 71 after over 40 years of service","Dr. Gary Dorshimer, team doctor for Flyers, dies at 71 after over 40 years of service Gary Dorshimer was the medical director for the Flyers, and also the assistant primary care sports medicine physician with the Sixers. Dr. Gary Dorshimer,known for havingworked at Penn Medicine and multiple Philadelphia sports teams, died aged 71 on Saturday, November 14, per CBS News.Dorshimer was the medical director for the Flyers, the assistant primary care sports medicine physician with theSixers, as well as the team sports medicine physician with the Union. He served as thePhiladelphia Eagles'head internist for nearly two decades.Theteam saidin an X post that it ""extends its condolences to his friends and family."" ""Dr. Dorshimer took exceptional care of our players and their families, coaches and entire staff over the span of several decades and was always on call whenever the team needed him,"" Dan Hilferty, the CEO of Comcast Spectacor and Flyers governor, said in a statement in part, per CBS News. ""His combination of wit and humor always brought a smile to the countless number of athletes in the city that he treated and helped perform at their best."" Also Read |Who was Hayden O'Dell? Former South Alabama pitcher dies at 22 after Wisconsin car accident ""Dr. Dorshimer not only treated but took the extra time to get to know and comfort every patient he saw during a career which spanned over 40 years,"" Hilferty wrote. ""He will be truly missed by all that knew him. We extend our heartfelt condolences to his wife, Deborah, and son Geoff, during this incredibly difficult time."" TheSixers saidin an X post, “The 76ers mourn the loss of Dr. Gary Dorshimer, a beloved member of our athlete care team and the Penn","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:24:52 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/dr-gary-dorshimer-team-doctor-for-flyers-dies-at-71-after-over-40-years-of-service-101794703640695.html,2026-11-15 03:31:51
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Indigenous Guatemalans say goodbye to Nobel writer who defended them,Indigenous Guatemalans say goodbye to Nobel writer who defended them,"Indigenous Guatemalans say goodbye to Nobel writer who defended them Indigenous Guatemalans say goodbye to Nobel writer who defended them Indigenous Guatemalans burned incense and made offerings at an ancestral site to say goodbye Saturday to Nobel laureate Miguel Angel Asturias, whose ashes were returned to his homeland from France half a century after his death. The lawyer, writer and diplomat known for denouncing dictators and defending the Indigenous received the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1967. He lived in Paris before he died in Spain aged 74 in 1974, during the last years of the Franco dictatorship. A dark green urn with the novelist's remains shaped like a kernel of corn arrived Thursday by his son, Miguel Angel Asturias Amado. The shape is a nod to his 1949 work entitled ""Men of Maize."" Saturday's ceremony was held in Kaminaljuyu, a Mayan archeological site west of Guatemala City. Surrounded by white flowers, the urn was placed on a small wooden table before a sacred round, stone altar. Indigenous people left offerings at the altar and burned incense to honor Asturias. ""Today we are celebrating something extraordinary,"" the 1992 Nobel peace laureate Rigoberta Menchu said of Asturias. ""Not just his eternal presence in Guatemala but his eternal presence in the world because he was a universal man,"" she said. Government officials and Asturias' son attended the ceremony. ""I am choked up with the emotion of this very important moment for my family,"" Asturias Amado, 85, said. Asturias' ashes will be interred on Sunday in a cultural center that bears his name. Asturias Amado told AFP Thursday the family had","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:13:24 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/indigenous-guatemalans-say-goodbye-to-nobel-writer-who-defended-them-101794703404885.html,2026-11-15 03:31:51
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,‘I do not stand for this’: Singer Sierra Ferrell condemns ICE for using her song ‘American Dreaming’ in controversial promotional video,‘I do not stand for this’: Singer Sierra Ferrell condemns ICE for using her song ‘American Dreaming’ in controversial promotional video,"‘I do not stand for this’: Singer Sierra Ferrell condemns ICE for using her song ‘American Dreaming’ in controversial promotional video Sierra Ferrell criticised ICE's video as ""racist"", adding that she is “weighing further legal action against our government for infringing on my rights.” Singer-songwriter Sierra Ferrell released a scathing statement slamming slammed U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) after the agency used her song ‘American Dreaming’ without permission in a promotional video. ICE posted the clip to their X account, touting1950s America for ""the way it was"" and ""the way it can be again,"" before encouraging viewers to ""join ICE."" “On Thursday, ICE used my song “American Dreaming” without permission in a video I found genuinely racist that was pushing a warped view of who belongs in this country,” Ferrell said in a social media post. “I do not stand for this. I rebuke that my art and expression are being used to victimize our citizens and neighbors and am frankly sickened.” “We have taken necessary steps to have these ads of propaganda taken down and are weighing further legal action against our government for infringing on my rights. But let me be clear, we are called to love and support our immigrant neighbors and I will continue to do just that,” she added. The clipopens with old-timey video of cars from the 1930s,before pivoting toscenes of American life in the 1950s. It featuresa mother pushing a baby stroller, big cars cruising the highways, views of Mt. Rushmore and a Coca Cola sign. White Americans are seen enjoying their lives. Ferrell’s song plays in the background. Also Read |Northern California nurse and professor's ICE detention sparks outrage, family calls out ‘evil’ move The messagingsays, ""The way it was. The way it c","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:08:55 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/i-do-not-stand-for-this-singer-sierra-ferrell-condemns-ice-for-using-her-song-american-dreaming-in-controversial-promotional-video-101794702373697.html,2026-11-15 03:31:51
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"US flights to return to normal by Sunday after nationwide ground stop, FAA says","US flights to return to normal by Sunday after nationwide ground stop, FAA says","US flights to return to normal by Sunday after nationwide ground stop, FAA says Air travel is expected to return to normal by the end of Sunday after a nationwide FAA ground stop led to thousands of flight cancellations and delays. Airlines canceled thousands of flightsacross theU.S.on Saturday as they worked to recover from a nationwideground stopa day earlier that left passengers scrambling for seats and disrupted travel around the world. The U.S. air travel schedule should be back to normal by the end of Sunday, two days after what was thenation's longest ground stop in 25 years, Federal Aviation Administration Administrator Bryan Bedford told reporters in Washington on Saturday. He said airlines “will still have delays and cancellations” Saturday but promised that the “worst is behind us.” Transportation SecretarySean Duffysaid the problem began when contractor L3Harris Technologies Inc. was replacing a section of the air traffic control system’s old copper wire with new fiber wire, somehow causing the system to overload. The work led to “intermittent” communications and radar gaps, prompting the government to shut down air traffic for more than four hours. Duffy said officials were investigating whether contractor “incompetence” or a faulty router was the cause. “Our contractor didn't meet the moment or the equipment didn’t meet the moment,” he added. Also read:Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy explains what caused FAA nationwide ground stop: ‘Contractor error or faulty equipment’ L3Harris said it was supporting the FAA in its investigation to “understand the conditions” that led to the ground stop. “L3Harris takes the nationwide ground stop and its impact on travelers, airlines and air traffic o","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:22:22 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-flights-to-return-to-normal-by-sunday-after-nationwide-ground-stop-faa-says-101794699412425.html,2026-11-15 03:31:51
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Global powers converge on Manila as ASEAN summit kicks off,Global powers converge on Manila as ASEAN summit kicks off,"Global powers converge on Manila as ASEAN summit kicks off Global powers converge on Manila as ASEAN summit kicks off A key regional summit opens on Sunday in Manila, with Southeast Asian heads of state facing questions on trade, security and an ongoing energy crisis while playing host to a who's who of global leaders. US President Donald Trump is scheduled to arrive on Tuesday near the summit's conclusion, a visit expected to include a sideline meeting with fellow Quad countries India, Japan and Australia the first of his second term. The meeting of the Quad a grouping broadly aimed at counterbalancing China's regional influence would come days before a historic sit-down with Chinese leader Xi Jinping and Russia's Vladimir Putin in Shenzhen. Brazil's recently re-elected Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, meanwhile, is set to attend a plenary session of the 11-member Association of Southeast Asian Nations on Sunday, while Australian Prime Minister Anthony Albanese will sign a new defence pact with host country the Philippines. Nearly 20,000 police officers have been deployed around Metro Manila for the summit, with progressive groups predicting a turnout of thousands on Tuesday for an anti-Trump march on the summit site. Much of the uproar targets the US Pax Silica programme a supply-chain initiative designed to counter China's dominance in semiconductors and rare earths whose flagship Philippine project, a 1,620-hectare AI manufacturing hub north of Manila, threatens to displace Indigenous families. US Ambassador to the Philippines Lee Lipton said last week that a widely rumoured November target da","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:21:29 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/global-powers-converge-on-manila-as-asean-summit-kicks-off-101794700290341.html,2026-11-15 03:31:51
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Israel warned US of possible attack on Donald Trump using drones carrying explosives: Report,Israel warned US of possible attack on Donald Trump using drones carrying explosives: Report,"Israel warned US of possible attack on Donald Trump using drones carrying explosives: Report Israeli officials say Mossad has warned that Iran may target Trump and top US officials, a threat that has reportedly changed how Trump deals with Iran talks. US intelligence agencies have received a warning from Israel about possibleIranianplans to target President Donald Trump and senior members of his administration, according to Israeli newspaperIsrael Hayom. The report about the warning comes as chances of a US-Iran deal have fallen and Trump has reportedly changed his approach to negotiations with Tehran. Senior Israeli and American officials reportedly told Israel Hayom Mossad has shared intelligence with the CIA about possible Iranian plans to target PresidentDonald Trumpand senior members of his administration. They said these threats were among the main reasons for Trump's recent change in approach to talks with Tehran. The officials said Israel confirmed the intelligence after US agencies asked the Mossad to check the information. Mossad Director Roman Gofman is currently visiting the US and has met CIA Director John Ratcliffe, Israel Hayom reported. The intelligence points to recent threats, including possible attacks using drones carrying explosives, which are difficult to stop with regular security measures. Officials believed to be at risk have reduced their public appearances, and some have been moved from their homes to secure locations. According to Fox News, Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent was moved from his home inWashington'sGeorgetown neighbourhood to a secure military base. Secretary of State Marco Rubio was also moved to secure military housing. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth is staying at a secure military","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:15:57 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/israel-warned-us-of-possible-attack-on-donald-trump-using-drones-carrying-explosives-report-101794696837872.html,2026-11-15 03:31:52
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Samir Abu Younis, Hamas commander who led group's Rafah brigade, killed in Israeli strike: Report","Samir Abu Younis, Hamas commander who led group's Rafah brigade, killed in Israeli strike: Report","Samir Abu Younis, Hamas commander who led group's Rafah brigade, killed in Israeli strike: Report An Israeli strike in Khan Younis killed Samir Abu Younis, Hamas' Rafah brigade commander, according to sources cited by Reuters. The Israeli military said on Sunday that it had carried out a strike targeting a senior commander in Hamas' military wing in the southernGazaStrip. Hamas sources told Reuters that the attack killed Samir Abu Younis, who led the group's Rafah brigade. Hamas subsequently acknowledged the commander's death and said a funeral service would be held in Khan Younis on Sunday afternoon. Abu Younis, 53, had joined the Al-Qassam Brigades in 1991 and went on to serve in several senior operational positions in Rafah, Reuters reported. According to the sources, Abu Younis was among the senior figures in Hamas' armed wing. The strike took place in the Mawasi area of Khan Younis, where medics confirmed that Abu Younis had been killed and several other people wounded. The Israeli military did not identify the commander in its initial statement but said it had targeted a seniorHamasmilitary figure. The identity of the person killed was reported by Hamas sources speaking to Reuters. Also Read:Israeli drone strike kills 2 Palestinians in Gaza, and other Mideast news The strike comes despite a ceasefire that took effect in October 2025 and brought an end to major fighting between Israel and Hamas. However, the agreement has not stopped Israeli military attacks in Gaza or resulted in Hamas disarming. Gaza health authorities say at least 1,600Palestinianshave been killed since the ceasefire came into effect. Five Israeli soldiers have also died during the same period. The latest strike comes as US","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:13:22 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/samir-abu-younis-hamas-commander-who-led-groups-rafah-brigade-killed-in-israeli-strike-report-101794698146481.html,2026-11-15 03:31:52
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Three tankers caught fire in Strait of Hormuz after hitting naval mines: Iran's navy,Three tankers caught fire in Strait of Hormuz after hitting naval mines: Iran's navy,"Three tankers caught fire in Strait of Hormuz after hitting naval mines: Iran's navy Iran’s navy said three oil tankers caught fire after hitting naval mines in the Strait of Hormuz on Saturday, claiming two were violating restricted routes. Iran's navy said three oil tankers caught fire on Saturday after hitting naval mines in theStrait of Hormuz, Iranian state media reported. One tanker hit a naval mine in the eastern Strait of Hormuz on Saturday morning, while two others struck mines later in the day. ""Two violating tankers ... were attempting to slip through a prohibited route in the Strait of Hormuz when they hit naval mines, exploded, and burst into flames,"" Iran's IRNA news agency quoted the Revolutionary Guards Navy as saying about the evening incident. Also read:Iran's IRGC claims it shot down US MQ-1 Predator drone over Qeshm Island in Strait of Hormuz Reuters could not immediately verify the reports. Iran has imposed restrictions on vessels seeking to pass through the Strait of Hormuz and has attacked ships it says violated those restrictions, as it seeks to assert control over the strategic waterway and exert pressure on the US.","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:47:21 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/three-tankers-caught-fire-in-strait-of-hormuz-after-hitting-naval-mines-irans-navy-101794697806467.html,2026-11-15 03:31:52
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Jared Kushner says US preparing next round of Russia-Ukraine peace talks with European partners directly involved,Jared Kushner says US preparing next round of Russia-Ukraine peace talks with European partners directly involved,"Jared Kushner says US preparing next round of Russia-Ukraine peace talks with European partners directly involved Jared Kushner says the US is preparing another round of Ukraine peace talks as new proposals and European security arrangements are discussed. US PresidentDonald Trump’sspecial envoy Jared Kushner has said Washington is preparing for the next round of trilateral talks involving Russia andUkraine, with discussions also underway to bring European partners directly into the peace process. Kushner said several new ideas had emerged from recent consultations and were being examined as possible ways to narrow differences between the sides. In aposton X, Kushner said he and US Special Envoy Steve Witkoff had remained in contact with Russian, Ukrainian and European representatives following their meetings with Russian PresidentVladimir Putinand Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy. He said the immediate focus was on arranging direct engagement between Moscow and European partners and setting the agenda for the next round of negotiations. Kushner indicated that the proposals under discussion could have different outcomes, with some potentially leading to breakthroughs and others developing into fresh proposals. He did not disclose details of the ideas or say whether Russia and Ukraine had agreed to any of them. Kushner said a lasting settlement would require credible security guarantees for Ukraine and detailed arrangements to reduce the risk of another conflict. He also described NATO as an important part of European security, while calling for stronger military communication, deconfliction and mechanisms to prevent disputes from escalating. Also Read:Fact check: Posts falsely claim Trump, top White House officials moved","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:32:14 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/jared-kushner-says-us-preparing-next-round-of-russia-ukraine-peace-talks-with-european-partners-directly-involved-101794696615177.html,2026-11-15 03:31:52
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Alex Jones claims Trump is slated to make ‘emergency’ announcement: Here's what we know so far,Alex Jones claims Trump is slated to make ‘emergency’ announcement: Here's what we know so far,"Alex Jones claims Trump is slated to make ‘emergency’ announcement: Here's what we know so far Alex Jones claimed Trump would make an emergency announcement Saturday evening, but the White House schedule shows no such event. Far-right commentator and former Trump ally, Alex Jones, claimed on Saturday afternoon thatDonald Trumpis slated to make an ""emergency announcement"" this evening. However, according to the White House press pool, Trump's schedule does not include any open press event. Alex Jones has been making a number of unsubstantiated claims about the FAA outage that brought all flight departures in the US to a halt for over 12 hours. Earlier, he had claimed that Trump had gone missing since the FAA first ordered the ground stop. The claim Saturday that Trump is slated to make an emergency announcement is part of a string of unsubstantiated claims the Jones has made following the recent outages with the FAA and Microsoft. ""MASSIVE NEWS: PRESIDENT TRUMP WILL MAKE AN EMERGENCY ANNOUNCEMENT TO THE NATION TODAY AT 6:00 PM ET! Are you ready for DOOMSDAY?""Jones wrotein a X post on Saturday afternoon. Also read:Elon Musk’s SpaceX carries out first-ever recovery of a spaceship with successful Starship catch Trump's schedule on theWhite Housepress pool document only one event on Saturday: The press pool roll call at 8:00 am ET when the president's executive time begins. There are no other public events scheduled for Saturday. Additionally, a press lid on the president's travel has been issued, meaning he will make no public appearances on Saturday anywhere. Also read:Fact check: Posts falsely claim Trump, top White House officials moved to bunker amid FAA outage On Saturday, CNN's senior White Hou","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:08:15 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/alex-jones-claims-trump-is-slated-to-make-emergency-announcement-heres-what-we-know-so-far-101794677308361.html,2026-11-15 03:31:52
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,A Mayan ceremony in Guatemala honors Nobel winner Miguel Ángel Asturias as his ashes return home,A Mayan ceremony in Guatemala honors Nobel winner Miguel Ángel Asturias as his ashes return home,"A Mayan ceremony in Guatemala honors Nobel winner Miguel Ángel Asturias as his ashes return home A Mayan ceremony in Guatemala honors Nobel winner Miguel Ángel Asturias as his ashes return home GUATEMALA CITY, Guatemala — A Mayan ceremony held Saturday at an archaeological site inGuatemala’scapital paid tribute to Nobel Prize-winning author Miguel Ángel Asturias, whose ashes returned to his Central American country this week after decades abroad. The ritual at the Kaminal Juyú site brought together the writer’s family and special guests, including Nobel Peace Prize laureateRigoberta Menchú Tum. The altar was adorned for the ceremony with white, purple, red and yellow flowers, representing the four cardinal directions. There were also candles, incense and cinnamon. Menchú approached the 32-kilogram green jade urn that holds Asturias’ ashes before the ritual, placing her hands upon it. She then offered a prayer, spoke to the urn and kissed it. “Today, we are here, honored by the eternal presence of Don Miguel Ángel Asturias, not only in Guatemala, but throughout the world,” she said. She later encouraged the Guatemalan people to keep the writer’s memory alive by reading his works. The remains of Asturias arrived in Guatemala on Thursday from France, where the writer had been buried following his death in exile in 1974. Asturias died of cancer in Madrid seven years after receiving theNobel Prize in Literature. His work is considered a precursor to Magical Realism and a key factor in the boom of Latin American literature during the 1960s and 1970s. He went into exile after a 1954 coup led by Gen. Carlos Castillo Armas, who revoked his passport and stripped him of his Gu","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:07:50 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/a-mayan-ceremony-in-guatemala-honors-nobel-winner-miguel-ngel-asturias-as-his-ashes-return-home-101794695870864.html,2026-11-15 03:31:52
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Amid Benjamin Netanyahu's calls for unity government, Gadi Eisenkot says ‘these tricks don't work’","Amid Benjamin Netanyahu's calls for unity government, Gadi Eisenkot says ‘these tricks don't work’","Amid Benjamin Netanyahu's calls for unity government, Gadi Eisenkot says ‘these tricks don't work’ Benjamin Netanyahu has renewed his call for a national unity government with Gadi Eisenkot, but the rival politician accused him of playing political tricks. Israel'scaretaker prime ministerBenjamin Netanyahuon Saturday reiterated his calls for a national unity government with his opponent Gadi Eisenkot, who in turn dismissed the appeal as a ruse. The latest exchange comes as Eisenkot is in the midst of negotiations to form a government, after he was tapped for the post of premier on Sunday. A meeting withEisenkoton Thursday ""only strengthened the conviction that it is essential to form a national unity government"" to guarantee Israel's security, Netanyahu said in a video statement, adding that such a government could ""eliminate the Iranian threat once and for all"". He said this government would be made up of parties that recognise Israel ""as a state for the Jewish people"". It would address security challenges, he added, most notably Iran which he claimed would ""not hesitate to use nuclear weapons against us"". Also read:Even after the elections, Israel waits for change The outgoing prime minister warned against Eisenkot's plan to form a minority government, presented as a ""national emergency government"". Such a plan would see the 48 lawmakers in Eisenkot's bloc vote in favour of his government, against the 46 Netanyahu backers. The 26 other members of parliament, from Arab and ultra-Orthodox parties, could abstain, allowing the government to be approved without an absolute majority in the Knesset, which has 120 seats. ""Instead of trying to form a weak and dangerous government... let's meet in one room, without preconditions, put a","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:48:20 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/amid-benjamin-netanyahus-calls-for-unity-government-gadi-eisenkot-says-these-tricks-dont-work-101794693031041.html,2026-11-15 03:31:52
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Elon Musk’s SpaceX carries out first-ever recovery of a spaceship with successful Starship catch,Elon Musk’s SpaceX carries out first-ever recovery of a spaceship with successful Starship catch,"Elon Musk’s SpaceX carries out first-ever recovery of a spaceship with successful Starship catch The initial attempt failed and was called off, with the booster redirected toward the ocean, where it erupted into flames just above the water's surface. Despite a booster explosion on Friday,SpaceXachieved a major milestone on Saturday by successfully catching Starship's upper stage, or spacecraft, as it returned intact from orbit. The spacecraft was captured using a pair of mechanical arms, nicknamed ""chopsticks,"" mounted on the launch tower at SpaceX's Starbase facility in Texas, CNBC reported. Loud cheers erupted as Starship's upper-stage spacecraft, known as the ""Ship,"" was successfully secured by the launchpad's mechanical arms. The successful recovery marked a significant moment for the company's ambitious Starship programme. During Test Flight 15, its most ambitious trial yet, SpaceX attempted for the first time to catch both the rocket's booster and upper stage using the tower's mechanical arms. During the initial phase of Friday’s test flight, SpaceX was unable to catch the booster for recovery and instead redirected it toward an offshore landing in the Gulf of Mexico. The booster burst into flames before reaching the water. Also read |Elon Musk says some of Nvidia’s 'critical' deals could be lost without Jensen Huang Meanwhile, the rocket’s upper stage continued its journey into orbit, completing 14 trips around Earth before successfully returning to land on SpaceX’s launch tower, known as Mechazilla. During Friday's Test Flight 15, SpaceX deployed an additional 26 of its latest Starlink v3 satellites into orbit, further expanding its satellite internet constellation. The company's network already consisted of more ","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:42:58 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/elon-musk-s-spacex-carries-out-first-ever-recovery-of-a-spaceship-with-successful-starship-catch-101794693499743.html,2026-11-15 03:31:53
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,SpaceX falls short of double catch after Starship booster explosion,SpaceX falls short of double catch after Starship booster explosion,"SpaceX falls short of double catch after Starship booster explosion SpaceX's Super Heavy booster failed to reach its planned catch point during Starship's 15th test flight, but the spacecraft remained healthy.&nbsp; SpaceXsaid its Starship spacecraft was ""healthy"" as it orbited the Earth and on track to return Saturday to itsTexaslaunch site, whereElon Musk'scompany was planning to ""catch"" the vehicle for the first time. It was the 15th test flight of the world's biggest and most powerful rocket system, originally meant to feature a groundbreaking twin capture of both the Super Heavy booster and the Starship. Successful recoveries of both stages would have marked a milestone in the space industry's decades-long pursuit of fully reusable rocket systems that can drastically reduce mission costs and make frequent launches possible. But that achievement slipped out of reach minutes after the 124-meter (407-foot) rocket blasted off Friday from its launch pad at Starbase. After the mid-air separation of the two stages, the Super Heavy booster was descending when its guidance, navigation and control system aborted the capture attempt. ""The booster was not in the place that it was supposed to be to proceed with the catch,"" SpaceX spokesman Dan Huot said, adding that engineers were still investigating the root cause. Also read:SpaceX's Starship booster explodes, prevents spacecraft's double catch Super Heavy, which SpaceX had caught three times previously, diverted to the Gulf of Mexico just off the launch site. It automatically self-destructed -- a fireball erupting from the booster -- before hitting the water. The Starship spacecraft that gives the rocket system its name was, meanwhile, orbitin","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:50:59 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/elon-musk-s-spacex-misses-starship-booster-catch-says-spacecraft-remains-healthy-before-texas-return-101794682521466.html,2026-11-15 03:31:53
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Elon Musk says some of Nvidia’s 'critical' deals could be lost without Jensen Huang,Elon Musk says some of Nvidia’s 'critical' deals could be lost without Jensen Huang,"Elon Musk says some of Nvidia’s 'critical' deals could be lost without Jensen Huang Elon Musk warned Nvidia could lose important supply chain deals after Jensen Huang’s departure, saying several agreements depended on personal relationships. Elon Muskhas warned that Nvidia could lose some of its important supply chain agreements following Jensen Huang’s departure as CEO, arguing that several of the chipmaker’s business arrangements depended heavily on personal relationships. TheTeslaand SpaceX chief said Huang had built partnerships based on trust and direct understanding, raising questions about whether those agreements will remain in place under new leadership. Musksharedhis comments on X on Saturday, November 14, pointing to Huang’s role in managing Nvidia’s suppliers and securing business arrangements. He suggested that some partners had agreed to work with Nvidia because of their relationship with Huang rather than through conventional written contracts. “Jensen drove supply chain brilliantly at Nvidia, but many of those deals were a handshake with Jensen, not a written contract,” Musk wrote. He added, “Without Jensen, at least some of those critical deals will be lost.” His remarks have brought attention to a possible challenge for Nvidia as it prepares for a leadership transition. The company is one of the world's biggest suppliers of processors used in artificial intelligence systems, making its relationships with manufacturers, suppliers and other business partners important to its operations. Musk’s latest comments follow his public support for an effort to bring Huang back to the top position at Nvidia. On Friday, the billionaire said he would sign a petition seeking the co-founder’s reinstatement. “A ","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:49:50 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/elon-musk-says-some-of-nvidia-s-critical-deals-could-be-lost-without-jensen-huang-101794687977813.html,2026-11-15 03:31:53
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Police lift evacuation after bomb found near ethanol plant in central Illinois,Police lift evacuation after bomb found near ethanol plant in central Illinois,"Police lift evacuation after bomb found near ethanol plant in central Illinois Police lift evacuation after bomb found near ethanol plant in central Illinois An evacuation order that forced hundreds of people from their homes near an industrial site in central Illinois was lifted Saturday after law enforcement agencies completed a search of the area, authorities said. A bomb was discovered Friday afternoon at the BioUrja Renewables facility in Peoria. Police said the device had been “rendered safe,” but authorities ordered residents within a 1-mile radius to evacuate while the surrounding area was searched. State, federal and local law enforcement conducted an extensive search at the facility and “they have found no other items of concern,” the Peoria Police Department said on its Facebook account on Saturday. “Residents are now free to return to their homes in the area that was affected,” the police said, adding that all roads will be opened and the investigation will continue. FBI Special Agent Ryan Presley said his agency was investigating, but declined to provide further details. “We will work tirelessly to identify the individual responsible and bring them to justice,” he said. No arrests have been made at this time, and no injuries have been reported. Peoria Mayor Rita Ali toldWMBD-TVon Friday that BioUrja is “a plant that has ethanol and highly combustible types of chemicals, and so that’s what alarms us.” It is not unusual for law enforcement to receive bomb threats and suspicious package calls, but they often don't result in a credible threat, even though such calls are taken seriously by officials who must assess and inv","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:08:57 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/police-lift-evacuation-after-bomb-found-near-ethanol-plant-in-central-illinois-101794688737536.html,2026-11-15 03:31:53
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Law enforcement searches Illinois plant after 'credible threat' of explosive device,Law enforcement searches Illinois plant after 'credible threat' of explosive device,"Law enforcement searches Illinois plant after 'credible threat' of explosive device USA-ILLINOIS/BOMBTHREAT:Law enforcement searches Illinois plant after 'credible threat' of explosive device Nov 14 - State and federal officers on Saturday searched a biofuels plant in Peoria, Illinois, for explosives after a device deemed a ""credible threat"" was found nearby, officials said, prompting a notice for residents to evacuate an area with a 1-mile radius. The evacuation order was lifted on Saturday, almost a full day after the device was discovered on Friday close to the BioUrja ethanol plant in Peoria, a city of about 110,000 people, some 150 miles southwest of Chicago, officials said. Bomb technicians rendered it safe, Peoria police said. Law enforcement personnel on Saturday afternoon finished their search of the sprawling facility, which is the size of 44-1/2 football fields, Peoria Police Chief Brad Dixon said. A standard American football field occupies roughly 1.3 acres . The Peoria Police Department said in a statement on Facebook that nothing ""of concern"" was found and the evacuation notice was lifted. The owner of the plant, the BioUrja Group of Houston, Texas, did not immediately respond to a request for comment. The incident began on Friday after the plant informed the police that it had received a bomb threat. Dixon on Saturday said he would not call the device a bomb because the process for determining its composition was ongoing. ""I can just tell you it was deemed a credible threat,"" Dixon told reporters at a briefing. ""There's an extensive criminal investigation going on."" Officials determined a potential blast radius of 1 mile based not solely on the dev","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:06:54 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/law-enforcement-searches-illinois-plant-after-credible-threat-of-explosive-device-101794688615104.html,2026-11-15 03:31:53
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Virginia lowers flags to half-staff today to honor late Congressman George Whitehurst,Virginia lowers flags to half-staff today to honor late Congressman George Whitehurst,"Virginia lowers flags to half-staff today to honor late Congressman George Whitehurst Virginia Governor Abigail Spanberger has ordered flags to be lowered on Saturday for former Congressman Dr George William Whitehurst, who died at 101. Virginia GovernorAbigail Spanbergerhas ordered US and state flags acrossVirginiato be flown at half-staff on Saturday, November 14, in memory of late Congressman Dr George William “Bill” Whitehurst. The formerRepublicancongressman, who represented Virginia’s 2nd congressional district for nine terms, died on November 7 at the age of 101. He is being laid to rest on Saturday. Spanberger issued the order on November 13, directing that flags on all state and local buildings and grounds across Virginia be lowered at sunrise on Saturday, November 14 and remain at half-staff until sunset. The order said the flags would be lowered “in memory and respect of former U.S. Congressman Dr. George William Whitehurst.” Also read:L3Harris, contractor that revamped Trump’s Qatar-gifted jet, questioned by Sean Duffy amid FAA outage According toWDBJ7, Whitehurst represented Virginia’s second congressional district from 1969 to 1987. In her statement, Spanberger said, “The entire Commonwealth of Virginia joins the people of Hampton Roads in mourning the passing of the Honorable George William ‘Bill’ Whitehurst — a distinguished public servant, devoted educator, and proud veteran whose extraordinary life exemplified a steadfast commitment to service, leadership, and country.” The governor said Whitehurst served in theUnited StatesNavy during World War II, before his time in Congress. She said that during his nine terms in Congress, he was “a tireless advocate for our service members, veterans, an","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:54:46 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/virginia-lowers-flags-to-half-staff-today-to-honor-late-congressman-george-whitehurst-101794686136749.html,2026-11-15 03:31:53
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Jamil Temple shooting: Gunshot triggers police response at Columbia gun show; details on suspect,Jamil Temple shooting: Gunshot triggers police response at Columbia gun show; details on suspect,"Jamil Temple shooting: Gunshot triggers police response at Columbia gun show; details on suspect A deputy was shot in the leg during a massive police response at a gun and knife show at Jamil Temple in Columbia, South Carolina. A massive police response was triggered at Jamil Temple in Columbia,South Carolina, on Saturday afternoon in the midst of a gun and knife show. According toCody Alcornof local media 11Alive, a deputy with the Lexington County Sheriff's Department was shot in the leg. The suspect is reportedly down. According to WIS10, a local broadcaster, the incident is being investigated by the Lexington County Sheriff's Department along with the Columbia Police Department. Law enforcement has not released details of the incident. This story is being updated. Shamik is a journalist covering the United States for Hindustan Times. He has more than four years of experience reporting on US politics, sports, and major breaking stories across fast-moving cycles. He previously worked at Times Now and Sportskeeda, building strong newsroom instincts and digital storytelling skills. At HT.com, he focuses on day-to-day coverage of US political developments while also handling high-impact stories that demand speed, accuracy, clarity, and context under pressure. Shamik has extensive experience covering NFL game days over the past two years, coordinating live updates, analysis, and explainers. He is particularly drawn to large news moments such as US elections and the Super Bowl, where he thrives at the news desk working alongside the team. He holds degrees in Media Studies from Jamia Millia Islamia and English Literature from Jadavpur University. Before entering journalism, he briefly worked in digital ","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:28:32 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/jamil-temple-shooting-gunshot-triggers-police-response-at-columbia-sc-gun-show-details-on-suspect-101794685978976.html,2026-11-15 03:31:53
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Fact check: Posts falsely claim Trump was moved to a secure bunker amid FAA outage,Fact check: Posts falsely claim Trump was moved to a secure bunker amid FAA outage,"Fact check: Posts falsely claim Trump was moved to a secure bunker amid FAA outage A viral hoax claimed Trump and aides were moved to a bunker during the FAA outage, amplified by Alex Jones. Officials ruled have out cyberattacks or foul play. As theFederal Aviation Administration(FAA) dealt with an unprecedented nationwide ground stop on Friday, a hoax about Trump and his top aides has gone viral. Multiple posts on social media claimed thatDonald Trumpand top officials in his administration have been moved to a bunker due to a potential threat. One of the voices that amplified the claim was far-right commentator and former Trump ally, Alex Jones. Jones claimed that a cyberattack purportedly caused the outage, and that Trump was moved to a secure bunker. FAA administrator Bryan Bedford said at a press conference on Saturday afternoon that a cyberattack or AI malfunction was not behind the outage. Sean Duffy, the US transportation secretary, attributed it to a possible error by a contractor or an equipment failure. Both have ruled out foul play as a possible cause as probe continues. Also read:Israeli spy chief visits US as Netanyahu seeks to build pressure on Trump to resume Iran war The claim about Trump being moved to a bunker seemed to have originated in social media accounts prompting far-right theories. Alex Jones claimed that Trump was ""holed up in the White House"" amid the outage. ""President Trump is holed up in the White House while historic mass cyber attacks are taking down major systems across the United States and the DHS is putting out the ridiculous cover story that a loose wire has caused all of this,""Jones wrote. What further amplified the claim was a newsstoryon the website AlertNet. The story fore","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:12:35 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/fact-check-posts-falsely-claim-trump-top-white-house-officials-moved-to-bunker-amid-faa-outage-101794679770886.html,2026-11-15 03:31:53
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Israeli drone strike kills 2 Palestinians in Gaza, and other Mideast news","Israeli drone strike kills 2 Palestinians in Gaza, and other Mideast news","Israeli drone strike kills 2 Palestinians in Gaza, and other Mideast news Israeli drone strike kills 2 Palestinians in Gaza, and other Mideast news An Israeli drone strike killed two Palestinians in theGaza Stripon Saturday, hospital officials said. Meanwhile, Iranian state TV reported that three oil tankers struck Iranian naval mines and caught fire around theStrait of Hormuzin the latest attack on shipping moving through the Persian Gulf. Here are the latest developments from the Middle East on Saturday. Read ourfull coverage here. The drone struck two Palestinians walking down a street in Jabaliya, on the northern edge of Gaza City, said Mohamed Abu Selmiya, director of Shifa Hospital in Gaza City, where the casualties were taken. The American field hospital said several other people were wounded but did not provide a number. Asked about the attack, the Israeli military said it had struck two Hamas militants in the area. Near-daily Israeli fire and airstrikes have continued in Gaza more than a year after Israel and Hamas reached a ceasefire deal. At least 1,600 Palestinians have been killed since the ceasefire, according to Gaza’s Health Ministry. The ministry, part of the Hamas-run government, maintains detailed records and is seen as generally reliable by U.N. agencies and independent experts. It does not distinguish between civilians and militants in its toll but says women and children make up around half the dead. Dozens of mourners gathered in Jabaliya in northern Gaza on Saturday evening to honor 70 people killed during the war whose remains were recovered in recent weeks from the rubble of buildings destroyed ","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:17:32 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/israeli-drone-strike-kills-2-palestinians-in-gaza-and-other-mideast-news-101794682052769.html,2026-11-15 03:31:53
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Portuguese housing protesters keep up the pressure with more marches,Portuguese housing protesters keep up the pressure with more marches,"Portuguese housing protesters keep up the pressure with more marches Portuguese housing protesters keep up the pressure with more marches Thousands marched through Lisbon and dozens of other cities and towns in Portugal on Saturday to protest at the rising cost of housing, in bid to keep up pressure on the government. The demonstrations began last month as anger over years of rising costs and stagnating incomes bubbled over. Housing prices have risen far quicker than incomes over the past decade, at the fastest rate in the EU, according to official data. Activists are calling for limits on rent increases, stronger protection from evictions, more public housing and measures to curb speculation in the property market. On Saturday, protesters in Lisbon marched through the city yelling: ""Lower rents, higher salaries."" Matile Cunha, a 20-year-old arts student, told AFP: ""We just want a place where we can study, but you can't find decent accommodation. ""Prices are at a level that no-one can afford."" ""With the little we earn and the prices of rent, we are the most unequal country in Europe,"" said Maite Chaves, a 40-year-old Uruguayan who has lived in Lisbon for 17 years. The protest movement sprang up after parliament adopted a bill that would speed up the procedure for property-owners to evict tenants. The government has taken a stern line against tent camps that have sprung up in Lisbon and Porto to protest at the situation, sending in police to forcibly clear them. Housing prices relative to incomes across Portugal rose 60.8 percent between 2015 and 2025, according to EU data, well ahead of the Netherlands in secon","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:15:34 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/portuguese-housing-protesters-keep-up-the-pressure-with-more-marches-101794681935233.html,2026-11-15 03:31:53
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Marco Rubio's memo presented CIA report on Jensen Huang in stronger terms leading to ex-Nvidia CEO's exit: Report,Marco Rubio's memo presented CIA report on Jensen Huang in stronger terms leading to ex-Nvidia CEO's exit: Report,"Marco Rubio's memo presented CIA report on Jensen Huang in stronger terms leading to ex-Nvidia CEO's exit: Report Rubio's intervention and Huang's resignation could strengthen congressional efforts to restrict China's access to Nvidia's advanced AI chips. Jensen Huang's resignation as Nvidia CEO could give US officials pushing for tougher restrictions on China's access to advanced artificial intelligence (AI) chips a major opportunity. A report byThe Washington Posthas revealed how Secretary of State and national security adviser Marco Rubio played a key role in bringing concerns about Huang's relationship with a woman suspected of working for Chinese intelligence to President Donald Trump. According to the report, Rubio sentTrumpa memo warning him about Huang's relationship. The memo was based on a CIA report, but Rubio presented its findings in stronger terms, according to a person familiar with the matter. The information later appeared in news reports, triggering a series of events that eventually led to Huang's resignation. The episode also exposed disagreements within the Trump administration over how much access China should have to AmericanAItechnology. While Huang had a close relationship with Trump and supported selling chips to China, several national security officials viewed those sales as a threat to US interests. Also Read:Rubio oversaw classified memo to warn top US officials about Nvidia CEO's affair with suspected Chinese spy: Report Rubio's intervention became a turning point in the controversy surrounding Huang. Nvidia's board launched an investigation into whether his relationship with the woman had created security concerns. Huang admitted to having an affair with an executive at an Nvidia customer and ap","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:12:21 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/marco-rubios-memo-presented-cia-report-on-jensen-huang-in-stronger-terms-leading-to-ex-nvidia-ceos-exit-report-101794679247074.html,2026-11-15 03:31:54
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"L3Harris, contractor that revamped Trump’s Qatar-gifted jet, questioned by Sean Duffy amid FAA outage","L3Harris, contractor that revamped Trump’s Qatar-gifted jet, questioned by Sean Duffy amid FAA outage","L3Harris, contractor that revamped Trump’s Qatar-gifted jet, questioned by Sean Duffy amid FAA outage US Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy has blamed contractor L3Harris, the same firm working on Trump’s Qatar jet, for Friday’s FAA ground stop. L3Harris Technologies is facing scrutiny after US Transportation SecretarySean Duffyquestioned whether the contractor's mistake or faulty equipment caused Friday's nationwideFAA outage. The company had also worked with the US government on modifying a Qatar-gifted jet that could become PresidentDonald Trump'snew Air Force One. L3Harris has responded to the scrutiny. “L3Harris takes the nationwide ground stop and its impact on travelers, airlines and air traffic operations seriously,” a company spokesperson said, as per Reuters. The spokesperson added that “L3Harris is supporting US FAA in its investigation of Friday’s aviation shutdown.” US Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said on Saturday thatinvestigatorsare checking whether contractor “incompetence” or a faulty router caused Friday’s air traffic control outage. The outage led to a rare nationwide ground stop that lasted about four hours. Duffy said the failure happened during a network upgrade from copper to fiber wiring. A router that was being replaced began flooding other routers in the system, as per ANI. “So what we’re working to determine was whether we had incompetence, meaning was it user error, installer error from L3Harris, or did they install a faulty router? We haven’t determined what the fault was,” Duffy told reporters. “Was it the router or were they not doing great work for us at L3Harris? Either through contractor error or a faulty piece of equipment, that router that was being replaced as we switch fro","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:02:53 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/l3harris-contractor-that-revamped-trump-s-qatar-gifted-jet-questioned-by-sean-duffy-amid-faa-outage-101794678343455.html,2026-11-15 03:31:54
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Sean Duffy appears unconvinced as Markwayne Mullin explains FAA failure: Awkward moment goes viral,Sean Duffy appears unconvinced as Markwayne Mullin explains FAA failure: Awkward moment goes viral,"Sean Duffy appears unconvinced as Markwayne Mullin explains FAA failure: Awkward moment goes viral As officials addressed the FAA system failure behind a nationwide flight halt, Markwayne Mullin said investigators were still examining a possible cyberattack. A tense exchange betweenTrumpadministration officials Sean Duffy and Markwayne Mullin drew attention during a White House press briefing addressing a major aviation disruption that brought flights across the United States to a standstill for several hours. The joint press conference, held Friday night by the Department of Transportation (DOT) and the Department of Homeland Security (DHS), was called to explain a Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) system failure that triggered an unprecedented five-hour nationwide ground stop. The disruption stemmed from communication problems at regional air traffic control centers, according to the FAA. The agency described the circumstances behind the decision to halt flights as “extraordinary circumstances for safety reasons.” The ground stop caused widespread disruption to air travel, with thousands of flights canceled and hundreds more experiencing delays across the country. As officials attempted to clarify what had gone wrong, reporters raised concerns about whether a possible cyberattack could have been responsible for the breakdown. Responding to questions about the possibility of a cyberattack, DHS Secretary MarkwayneMullinsaid officials were “still looking” into the cybersecurity aspect of the incident. However, he suggested that the initial findings pointed toward a technical compatibility problem involving newly introduced equipment and an older system. Attempting to describe the issue, Mullin said, “That new equipment, new te","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:58:34 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/sean-duffy-appears-unconvinced-as-markwayne-mullin-explains-faa-failure-awkward-moment-goes-viral-101794678758932.html,2026-11-15 03:31:54
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,New York Governor demands Sean Duffy’s resignation after nationwide US flight ground stop: ‘Trump must remove him’,New York Governor demands Sean Duffy’s resignation after nationwide US flight ground stop: ‘Trump must remove him’,"New York Governor demands Sean Duffy’s resignation after nationwide US flight ground stop: ‘Trump must remove him’ New York Governor Kathy Hochul called for Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy to resign or be removed, citing persistent aviation-system problems. New York GovernorKathy Hochulhas called for US Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy to resign or be removed from office by President Donald Trump following a nationwide aviation disruption that forced a ground stop on Friday. In a statement issued on Saturday, Hochul criticised Duffy's handling of problems within the country's aviation system, pointing to persistent air traffic controller shortages and repeated communication failures. She accused the Transportation Secretary of focusing more on his public image than addressing serious challenges facing the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA). “From chronic air traffic controller shortages to repeated communications breakdowns, serious lapses in our aviation system have become a pattern on Sean Duffy’s watch,” Hochul said. She added that Duffy had been “more focused on starring in his own reality show than addressing the crisis at his agency”. Hochul urged PresidentTrumpto remove Duffy “immediately” if he did not step down voluntarily. Also Read:FAA outage update: Sean Duffy assures passengers ‘it is safe to fly’ as US flight operations slowly returning to normal The New York governor also called on Congress to investigate the circumstances surrounding Friday's nationwide ground stop, stressing the importance of public confidence in aviation safety ahead of the busy holiday travel period. ""With millions of Americans preparing to travel for the holidays, families deserve answers and confidence in the safety of our skies,"" she ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:59:47 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/new-york-governor-kathy-hochul-demands-sean-duffy-s-resignation-after-nationwide-us-flight-ground-stop-101794675857549.html,2026-11-15 03:31:54
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Shehbaz Sharif says Pakistan can become world's 6th-largest economy by 2050, revises Goldman Sachs forecast","Shehbaz Sharif says Pakistan can become world's 6th-largest economy by 2050, revises Goldman Sachs forecast","Shehbaz Sharif says Pakistan can become world's 6th-largest economy by 2050, revises Goldman Sachs forecast The prime minister also called for closer cooperation between the federal and provincial governments to provide investors with the necessary support. Pakistan Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif has said he expects the country to become the world’s sixth-largest economy before 2050, revising the timeline projected in an earlier Goldman Sachs assessment. Addressing the Pakistan Minerals Investment Forum 2026 in Islamabad on Friday, Sharif recalled that Goldman Sachs had forecast Pakistan could become the world’s sixth-largest economy by 2075. He said he wanted to bring that target forward, Dawn reported. “I would like to make a small amendment here — instead of 2075, it will be earlier than 2050,” he was quoted as saying by Dawn. The prime minister also urged international investors to look beyond extracting and exporting raw minerals, calling for greater investment in processing, refining and manufacturing within Pakistan. Sharif said Pakistan was working to make its mining sector more attractive to investors by simplifying procedures, reducing bureaucratic delays and ensuring transparency in the allocation of licences and contracts. He said digitised records and the National Minerals Data Centre would allow investors to assess the country’s mineral resources before committing funds to projects. The prime minister also called for closer cooperation between the federal and provincial governments to provide investors with the necessary support. He said ensuring the safety of workers, assets and supply routes remained the government’s responsibility. “Your safety is our safety and your protection is our protection.” Sharif invited ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:58:59 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/shehbaz-sharif-says-pakistan-can-become-worlds-6th-largest-economy-by-2050-revises-goldman-sachs-forecast-101794675527714.html,2026-11-15 03:31:54
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"‘He always came through’: Elon Musk praises Jensen Huang, warns Nvidia could lose ‘critical’ deals without him","‘He always came through’: Elon Musk praises Jensen Huang, warns Nvidia could lose ‘critical’ deals without him","‘He always came through’: Elon Musk praises Jensen Huang, warns Nvidia could lose ‘critical’ deals without him Elon Musk also voiced support for an effort to reinstate Huang, saying he would sign a petition seeking the former CEO's return. Elon Musk has backed calls to reinstate Jensen Huang as Nvidia's chief executive, saying the chipmaker could lose ""critical"" business deals without its former CEO, who stepped down amid controversy over reports of his extramarital affairs. In a post on X on Saturday, Musk said Huang had managed Nvidia's supply chain ""brilliantly"" and that several business arrangements depended on personal assurances from the former chief rather than formal contracts. ""Many of these deals were a handshake with Jensen, not a written contract,"" Musk said. “If Jensen gave me his word about compute delivery or I asked for components to be accelerated, he always came through,” he added. “Sure, we’d put together a purchase order at some point later, but I never for a second thought it wouldn’t happen,” Musk said. Musk also voiced support for an effort to reinstate Huang, earlier, saying he would sign a petition seeking the former CEO's return. “A petition is underway to reinstate Jensen and I’m signing it too,” he wrote on X. However, Musk did not clarify whether he was referring to an initiative involving Nvidia employees. Some employees at the chipmaker have also called for Huang's return, news outlet WIRED reported on Friday, citing internal correspondence reviewed by the publication. According to the report, an engineer had posted a suggestion to Nvidia's internal ""suggestion box"" ahead of Huang's resignation, urging the company's board to consider employee sentiment before taking any action. Th","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:57:18 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/elon-musk-praises-jensen-huang-warns-nvidia-could-lose-critical-deals-without-him-101794670072655.html,2026-11-15 03:31:54
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Peoria bomb threat: Police continue search for more explosives at BioUrja plant as evacuation order remains,Peoria bomb threat: Police continue search for more explosives at BioUrja plant as evacuation order remains,"Peoria bomb threat: Police continue search for more explosives at BioUrja plant as evacuation order remains Police and the FBI continue searching Peoria's BioUrja plant for explosives after one bomb was found, while nearby residents remain evacuated. Police and federal investigators are continuing to search the BioUrja Renewables plant in Peoria,Illinois, for possible additional explosives after a bomb was discovered at the facility on Friday, November 13. The explosive device was rendered safe around 9:12pm, but authorities have not cleared the site, and an evacuation order covering a one-mile radius remains in effect as of Saturday, November 14. The FBI is assisting local authorities with the investigation. However, officials have not confirmed how many additional devices, if any, could be at the facility. A social mediapostby JLR Investigates, an investigative reporter, has also claimed that the FBI is searching for three more bombs in the Peoria area. The post stated, ""FBI are looking for 3 more bombs planted in the Peoria Illinois area. We are watching LIVE on KICK."" However, the claim about three additionalbomb threatshas not been confirmed by law enforcement officials. The investigation began Friday after BioUrja Renewables reported receiving a bomb threat. According to Peoria Police Chief Brad Dixon, the company contacted police at 1:08pm A suspicious package was found at around 2pm, and investigators determined it was a credible threat by 6:45pm. Also Read:Bomb confirmed at Illinois BioUrja ethanol plant as Peoria evacuation continues, mayor says Bombtechnicians later rendered the device safe at approximately 9:12pm. Despite that development, the search did not end. Dixon said the facility was large and would req","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:34:45 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/peoria-bomb-threat-police-continue-search-for-more-explosives-at-biourja-plant-as-evacuation-order-remains-101794674711354.html,2026-11-15 03:31:54
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy blames FAA nationwide ground stop on ‘contractor error or faulty equipment’,Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy blames FAA nationwide ground stop on ‘contractor error or faulty equipment’,"Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy blames FAA nationwide ground stop on ‘contractor error or faulty equipment’ Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said a contractor’s work on a router may have caused Friday’s FAA outage, and he said it was not a cyberattack. Transportation SecretarySean Duffyon Saturday suggested that anFAAcontractor might be to blame for Friday’s telecommunications outage, as per his remarks at a press briefing at Transportation Department headquarters. The outagegrounded flightsacross the country and led to thousands of cancellations. According to Duffy, “in at least one of our remote FAA locations, a contractor was doing routine maintenance to switch telecommunication lines from old copper wire, and they were bringing it over to fiber.” Duffy named the contractor as L3Harris. “That contractor that does the work for us is L3Harris. They’re our legacy provider,” he said. He added that officials are still trying to figure out what went wrong. “Was it user error or installation error from L3Harris, or did they install a faulty router? We haven’t determined what the fault was,” Duffy said, as perHuff Post. Also read:US flights grounded nationwide: A look back at the last major FAA shutdown in 2023 Duffy explained what caused the FAA Nationwide Ground Stop on Friday. “Either through contractor error or a faulty piece of equipment, that router that was being replaced as we switched from copper to fiber, it started flooding other routers in our air traffic control system. So specifically, we had over 1,000 connection attempts every four to five seconds. And what that did was give us issues with communication with airplanes, and it also caused some disruption with radar feeds.” He said the airspace was shut down for sa","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:27:54 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/transportation-secretary-sean-duffy-explains-what-caused-faa-nationwide-ground-stop-contractor-error-or-faulty-equipment-101794675054311.html,2026-11-15 03:31:54
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,AI tools Jensen Huang championed now star in memes of his downfall,AI tools Jensen Huang championed now star in memes of his downfall,"AI tools Jensen Huang championed now star in memes of his downfall Online content creators are capitalizing on Huang's scandalous week by posting scores of AI-generated memes making light of his extramarital affairs. Once artificial intelligence’s leading hype-man,Jensen Huangis now the face of an AI-driven meme craze. Online content creators are capitalizing on the formerNvidiaCorp. chief executive’s scandalous week by posting scores of AI-generated memes making light of his extramarital affairs. In the videos, Huang can be seen dancing to viral TikTok trends or appearing in scenes from iconic movies, such as Love Actually, alongside Alice Huang, the suspected Chinese spy whose affair with Huang contributed to his ouster from the company he led for three decades. “There’s a sense of irony for some people that, in a way, Huang is being targeted by tools powered by his own creations,” said Henry Ajder, an expert in AI and deepfakes. While unable to quantify the number of Huang-inspired memes, Ajder said he was struck by the sheer volume of content, generated quickly across the main social platforms. It’s not unusual for real-world scandals to be turned into online memes, but the number, variety and uncanny realism of the Huang-related posts stand out. One video made by a 43-year-old, London-based content creator known as @adventureruben_ shows AI-generated Huang dancing to Jason Derulo’s viral hit Mi Chico in the parking lot outside of Nvidia’s headquarters. He is accompanied by AI stand-ins for Alice Huang; Kimberly Powell, the Nvidia executive who also reportedly had a relationship with Huang; and his wife, Lori Huang. The clip also incongruously includes Susan Dell, wife of billionaire ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:19:57 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/ai-tools-jensen-huang-championed-now-star-in-memes-of-his-downfall-101794674629164.html,2026-11-15 03:31:55
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"FAA administrator Bryan Bedford says nationwide ground stop for ‘the right reasons,' rules out foul play","FAA administrator Bryan Bedford says nationwide ground stop for ‘the right reasons,' rules out foul play","FAA administrator Bryan Bedford says nationwide ground stop for ‘the right reasons,' rules out foul play FAA Administrator Bryan Bedford said the nationwide ground stop was for the right reasons, apologized for the disruption, and ruled out foul play. Bryan Bedford, the administrator of theFederal Aviation Administration, said at a press conference on Saturday afternoon that the nationwide ground stop since Friday afternoon was ""for the right reasons."" Apologising for the inconvenience travellers faced, Bedford simultaneously ruled out foul play behind the unprecedented outage. ""We see zero evidence of anything nefarious and zeroevidenceof anything AI-related,"" Bedford said, adding that passengers whose travel was disrupted by the outage will get a full refund. Bedford said that the agency's systems remain stable, though there are delays and cancellations that have spilled on to Saturday, as well. He said that between 4,000 and 5,000 scheduledflightson Saturday will likely be cancelled even as operations return to normal. Over 10,000 flights were delayed or cancelled on Friday. “As we went into Friday, we had 50,000 flights scheduled to operate,"" Bedford said. ""When we went into the ground stop at approximately 3:45 p.m. East Coast time yesterday, we had completed about 30,000 of those flights, either on the ground or in the air. ""So, we had 20,000 more flights to complete over the course of the four-hour ground stop. We were ultimately able to recover about 8,000 of those 20,000 flights. 12,000 we were unable to recover."" Also read:FAA outage update: Sean Duffy assures passengers ‘it is safe to fly’ as US flight operations slowly returning to normal Explaining the impact of the ground stop on the flights affected, Bedford","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:52:37 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/faa-administrator-bryan-bedford-says-nationwide-ground-stop-for-the-right-reasons-rules-out-foul-play-101794672619693.html,2026-11-15 03:31:55
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Zelensky says Ukraine's neutrality won't be enshrined in Constitution amid push from Russia,Zelensky says Ukraine's neutrality won't be enshrined in Constitution amid push from Russia,"Zelensky says Ukraine's neutrality won't be enshrined in Constitution amid push from Russia Zelenskyy said that Ukraine was not currently part of NATO but would not make neutrality a constitutional requirement. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has ruled out amending the country's Constitution to establish a neutral status, arguing that such a move would fail to provide Ukraine with lasting security guarantees. Zelenskyy told Interfax on Friday that Ukraine was not currently part of NATO but would not make neutrality a constitutional requirement. He also reiterated that Kyiv intended to join the European Union (EU), adding that its membership plans had been made clear at every level. ""If Putin expects Ukraine to have its neutrality enshrined, that won't happen. We're not in NATO right now anyway. If neutrality generally means that we're not in NATO, then we're already in that status. So what will ensure our long-term security? If they assume we won't be in the EU, well, we actually will be – that's been made clear at every level. For now, Ukraine is not a member of any alliance. And enshrining neutrality means you're amending your country's Constitution, and Ukraine won't go down that path,"" Zelenskyy told reporters on Friday, according to an Interfax-Ukraine correspondent. The Ukrainian president also described discussions about a new European security framework before the end of the war as dangerous. He said the US had raised the possibility of developing a different security arrangement for Europe and the rest of the world after the conflict. However, Zelenskyy stressed that the issue should not become the central focus of ongoing negotiations. He pointed to what he describ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:38:48 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/zelensky-says-ukraine-neutrality-wont-be-enshrined-in-constitution-amid-push-from-russia-101794666632077.html,2026-11-15 03:31:55
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,FAA outage update: Sean Duffy assures passengers ‘it is safe to fly’ as US flight operations slowly returning to normal,FAA outage update: Sean Duffy assures passengers ‘it is safe to fly’ as US flight operations slowly returning to normal,"FAA outage update: Sean Duffy assures passengers ‘it is safe to fly’ as US flight operations slowly returning to normal US flight operations resumed after technical problems disrupted FAA radar and communications systems, causing thousands of cancellations and delays. Air travel across the United States is gradually recovering following a nationwide Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) ground stop that disrupted thousands of flights on Friday. Transportation SecretarySean Duffyhas assured passengers that flight operations are resuming safely, although delays and cancellations are expected to continue as airlines work to restore normal schedules. In a statement posted on X on Saturday morning, Duffy said, “Operations are slowly returning to normal this morning. Planes are pushing back, taxiing, and taking off, and it is safe to fly.” The disruption began Friday afternoon after technical problems affected radar and telecommunications systems used by air traffic controllers. Inconsistent radar information and communication difficulties prompted the FAA to suspend departures nationwide as a precautionary safety measure. Also Read:Workday outage disrupts thousands of businesses worldwide: Walmart, Target workers face payroll and HR access issues The nationwide ground stop was lifted at approximately 8:15 p.m. Eastern Time on Friday, allowing airlines to gradually restart services. However, the operational impact continued into Saturday, with aircraft and flight crews displaced across the country. FlightAware figures cited by ABC News showed more than 12,500 cancellations across Friday and Saturday by Saturday morning, alongside thousands of delays. Duffy acknowledged that passengers should expect continued inconvenience while airlines reorgani","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:09:08 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/faa-outage-update-sean-duffy-assures-passengers-it-is-safe-to-fly-as-us-flight-operations-slowly-returning-to-normal-101794670065660.html,2026-11-15 03:31:55
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Trump, Putin and Xi to meet in China’s Shenzhen on Nov 19; evoke comparisons with 1945 Yalta conference","Trump, Putin and Xi to meet in China’s Shenzhen on Nov 19; evoke comparisons with 1945 Yalta conference","Trump, Putin and Xi to meet in China’s Shenzhen on Nov 19; evoke comparisons with 1945 Yalta conference The meeting would bring the leaders of the three major powers together on the sidelines of Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation forum. Russian President Vladimir Putin, Chinese President Xi Jinping and US President Donald Trump are set to hold a trilateral meeting in China's Shenzhen on November 19 on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) summit, the Kremlin confirmed, Reuters reported, citing Russian news agency RIA on Saturday. The meeting would bring the leaders of the three major powers together on the sidelines of the regional summit. The APEC leaders’ meeting is scheduled to take place on November 18-19 Earlier,the White House had confirmedthe meeting saying that nuclear arms control will be a central topic alongside regional conflicts, including the war in Iran. Reuters noted that the proposed meeting has drawn comparisons, particularly in Russia, with the 1945 Yalta Conference, where the US, Britain and the Soviet Union formalised spheres of influence and helped shape the post-World War II world order. The conference has since become synonymous with major powers striking deals that affect smaller countries. Held in February 1945 in Yalta, the conference brought together then-US President Franklin D Roosevelt, British PM Winston Churchill and Soviet leader Joseph Stalin to discuss the post-war future of Europe. Over time, the Yalta Conference became shorthand for agreements between major powers that shape the geopolitical future of smaller nations, often without their meaningful participation. The prospect of an updated version of Yalta has generated excitement among Russian na","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:08:37 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-russia-china-vladimir-putin-xi-jinping-donald-trump-to-hold-trilateral-meeting-in-china-shenzhen-on-november-19-kremlin-apec-yalta-101794669752710.html,2026-11-15 03:31:55
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Elon Musk warns Nvidia will lose 'critical' deals without Jensen Huang,Elon Musk warns Nvidia will lose 'critical' deals without Jensen Huang,"Elon Musk warns Nvidia will lose 'critical' deals without Jensen Huang Musk said Nvidia could lose critical deals following the exit of rHuang, arguing that many agreements depended on personal trust rather than written contracts. Elon Musk said chipmaker Nvidia would lose ""critical"" deals without its now ousted CEOJensen Huang, in a post on X on Saturday. Musk said that while Huang drove supply chain ""brilliantly"" atNvidia, many such deals were “a handshake with Jensen, not a written contract.” For decades, Huang personally cultivated relationships with some of the world's most important semiconductor manufacturers and technology suppliers, particularly in Asia. These relationships were not simply conventional buyer-supplier arrangements. They were partnerships built on credibility, long-term commitments and a shared belief in future growth. The relationship between NVIDIA and Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company (TSMC) is a powerful example. Huang and TSMC built a relationship spanning nearly three decades. In an interview with Dwarkesh Patel, Huang acknowledged that NVIDIA and TSMC did not have a formal legal contract, describing the relationship as one built on mutual trust and dependability. This is an extraordinary achievement in an industry where billions of dollars in manufacturing capacity, advanced packaging and infrastructure investments are at stake. Huang's personal credibility also helped persuade suppliers to make enormous investments ahead of demand. His ability to communicate NVIDIA's future requirements gave partners the confidence to expand capacity and align their businesses with NVIDIA's ambitious product roadmap. However, corporate relationships built around one individual c","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:37:45 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/elon-musk-warns-nvidia-will-lose-critical-deals-without-jensen-huang-101794668617377.html,2026-11-15 03:31:55
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Workday outage disrupts thousands of businesses worldwide: Walmart, Target workers face payroll and HR access issues","Workday outage disrupts thousands of businesses worldwide: Walmart, Target workers face payroll and HR access issues","Workday outage disrupts thousands of businesses worldwide: Walmart, Target workers face payroll and HR access issues A technical failure at Workday left customers like Walmart and Target unable to access payroll, timekeeping, leave requests, benefits and other HR functions. A major technical failure atWorkday, one of the world's leading human resources and payroll software providers, disrupted workplace services on Friday, November 13, leaving employees at affected organisations unable to access essential HR functions. From checking salary information and recording working hours to requesting leave and completing benefits paperwork, several routine workplace activities suddenly became inaccessible. The disruption raised concerns among employees and employers alike, particularly because Workday's platform is deeply integrated into the daily operations of thousands of organisations worldwide. The company says its software is used by more than 11,500 organisations, making the incident a significant reminder of how heavily modern workplaces depend on centralised digital infrastructure. The technical problems began on Friday afternoon, with outage reports rising rapidly as employees encountered difficulties accessing their workplace accounts, FOX Local reported. According toDowndetector, the online service-monitoring platform, nearly 3,000 reports of problems with Workday were recorded during the disruption. Many users attempting to log in encountered error messages indicating that the service was unavailable. Also Read:Blue Jays star Anthony Santander apologises after sharing anti-Muslim posts targeting Abdul El-Sayed: ‘this content caused hurt’ Theoutageaffected access to several important workplace functions. Employees at affected organisations re","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:04:54 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/workday-outage-disrupts-11-500-businesses-worldwide-walmart-target-workers-face-payroll-and-hr-access-issues-101794666114407.html,2026-11-15 03:31:55
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Is Putin weaponising winter? Macron warns Europe against Trump's push for 'unjust peace' in Ukraine,Is Putin weaponising winter? Macron warns Europe against Trump's push for 'unjust peace' in Ukraine,"Is Putin weaponising winter? Macron warns Europe against Trump's push for 'unjust peace' in Ukraine France's President Emmanuel Macron said on Saturday that countries seeking to limit aid to Ukraine want to impose an 'unjust peace', warning that it can be a 'recipe for another war' France's President Emmanuel Macron said on Saturday that countries seeking to limit aid to Ukraine want to impose an 'unjust peace', warning that it can be a 'recipe for another war' France's President Emmanuel Macron said on Saturday that countries seeking to limit aid to Ukraine want to impose an ""unjust peace"", warning that it can be a ""recipe for another war"". The remarks from the French leader are being seen as a dig at the United States, as the Trump administration floats Ukraine giving up the Donbas region for a Nato membership or Nato-like security guarantees. On Saturday, Macron wrote a lengthy post on X, formerly known as Twitter. It came at a time when theUS is mediating talks between Russia and Ukrainein a bid to end the war that was started by Moscow back in 2022. ""Those who want to ration aid to Ukraine wish underneath it all to force an unjust peace on it"", and, by extension, all of Europe, Macron said. ""That is the spirit of defeat. That is a recipe for another war. That cannot be France's position,"" he added. During a meeting ofEuropean leaders on Friday in Dublin, the continent chose five nations: France, Germany, Italy, the UK and Poland – to send representatives to the talks. ""Europe must take full part"" in the work to bring about a ""fair and lasting peace"" in Ukraine, Macron said in the Saturday post. ""What happens in Ukraine concerns us directly... Helping Ukraine defend itself is protecting France and the French,"" he added. The French President said tha","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:05:47 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/is-putin-weaponising-winter-macron-warns-europe-against-trumps-push-for-unjust-peace-in-ukraine-14060050.html,2026-11-15 03:31:56
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Pope Leo XIV denounces humiliation of enslaved Africans, acknowledges Church’s role in slave trade","Pope Leo XIV denounces humiliation of enslaved Africans, acknowledges Church’s role in slave trade","Pope Leo XIV denounces humiliation of enslaved Africans, acknowledges Church’s role in slave trade Pope Leo XIV on Saturday denounced the ”suffering and humiliation” endured by African enslaved people as he made a tangible show of remorse in Peru Pope Leo XIV on Saturday denounced the ”suffering and humiliation” endured by African enslaved people as he made a tangible show of remorse in Peru Pope Leo XIV on Saturday denounced the ”suffering and humiliation” endured by African enslaved people as he made a tangible show of remorse in Peru following his historic apology for the Holy See’s own role in legitimising the African slave trade in the Americas. The US-born Leo, whose own family tree includes enslaved people and slave owners, delivered the remarks in the northern Peruvian city of Zana, a UNESCO-recognised memorial site of slavery and center of the Afro-Peruvian community today. Zana is part of Leo’s former diocese of Chiclayo, and the former Robert Prevost came here often to pray before the relics of a 16th century saint, including the night before his ordination as a bishop. He knows the city and the history of African-descended Peruvians well, and the continued discrimination that Afro-Peruvians face today. In remarks to the community Saturday, Leo said Zana ”preserves the memory of generations of Africans who were torn from their homes and subjected to slavery.” ”Many endured great suffering and humiliation. Dear brothers and sisters of African descent, today I want to express my affection and closeness to you,” he said. ”Thank you for all that you contribute to the life of this church.” Zana, a historic town in Chiclayo province, was recognized by Unesco in 2017 as a ”site of memory of slavery and African cul","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:41:43 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/pope-leo-xiv-denounces-humiliation-of-enslaved-africans-acknowledges-churchs-role-in-slave-trade-14060040.html,2026-11-15 03:31:57
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Eisenkot dismisses Netanyahu's call for unity govt, slams 'racist' campaign against Arab Israelis","Eisenkot dismisses Netanyahu's call for unity govt, slams 'racist' campaign against Arab Israelis","Eisenkot dismisses Netanyahu's call for unity govt, slams 'racist' campaign against Arab Israelis Israel's Prime Minister-designate Gadi Eisenkot slammed the country's current Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu over his public appeal for a unity government, calling it a 'media stunt' Israel's Prime Minister-designate Gadi Eisenkot slammed the country's current Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu over his public appeal for a unity government, calling it a 'media stunt' Israel's Prime Minister-designate Gadi Eisenkot slammed the country's current Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu over his public appeal for a unity government, calling it a ""media stunt"". Eisenkot, the leader of the Yasher Party, is currently tasked with forming the next government. On Saturday, he said that the negotiating teams from his party and Netanyahu's Likud were scheduled to meet on Sunday. However, in a post on X, formerly known as Twitter, he went on to accuse Netanyahu of calling for national unity while continuing to sow divisions and incite against political opponents. He went on to point to the Israeli caretaker prime minister's speech at the opening of the new Knesset as an example. Eisenkot made it clear that Netanyahu's Likud could only join a national emergency government under his leadership if the party accepted his stated principles and distanced itself from extremist political forces. He went on to accuse Netanyahu of attempting to obstruct the formation of a new government and efforts to replace Knesset Speaker Amir Ohana, a Likud member. Eisenkot went on to condemn a “racist and aggressive campaign of delegitimisation” against the country’s Arab citizens at a time when Netanyahu has been accusing Arab parties of electoral fraud, without providing any evidence. It is per","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:20:14 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/eisenkot-dismisses-netanyahus-call-for-unity-govt-slams-racist-campaign-against-arab-israelis-14060047.html,2026-11-15 03:31:57
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,‘Indians rise and shine wherever they go’: Piyush Goyal lauds diaspora during Egypt visit,‘Indians rise and shine wherever they go’: Piyush Goyal lauds diaspora during Egypt visit,"‘Indians rise and shine wherever they go’: Piyush Goyal lauds diaspora during Egypt visit Union Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal has praised the Indian diaspora in Egypt for its contributions to strengthening bilateral relations. Union Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal has praised the Indian diaspora in Egypt for its contributions to strengthening bilateral relations. Union Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal has praised the Indian diaspora in Egypt for its contributions to strengthening bilateral relations, saying Indians carry the country's values wherever they go and play an important role in bringing nations closer. During an interaction with Indian diaspora in Cairo on Saturday, Goyal highlighted the historical and cultural connections between India and Egypt, while underlining the diaspora's contribution to fostering closer people-to-people ties. ""Wherever Indians go, they rise and shine!It was wonderful to interact with members of the Indian diaspora,"" Goyal said in a post on X, after attending an event organised by the Indian Community Association in Egypt. He further added, ""India and Egypt share deep historical connections & common traditions. It is heartening to see how much Egypt values the Indian community and the meaningful contributions they are making to their Karmabhoomi."" Goyal said the Indian diaspora carries ""India's values"" and plays a key role in bringing the two countries closer. ""This is what makes our diaspora so special. They carry India's values with them and make a difference wherever they go.I spoke about the many opportunities to further strengthen India-Egypt cooperation and how our diaspora can play an important role in bringing the two countries close","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:00:46 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/indian-diaspora/indians-rise-and-shine-wherever-they-go-piyush-goyal-lauds-diaspora-during-egypt-visit-14060045.html,2026-11-15 03:31:57
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Zelenskyy accuses SpaceX of lying about Starshield restrictions; is this a 'pressure tactic'?,Zelenskyy accuses SpaceX of lying about Starshield restrictions; is this a 'pressure tactic'?,"Zelenskyy accuses SpaceX of lying about Starshield restrictions; is this a 'pressure tactic'? Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has accused SpaceX of being dishonest about restrictions on Ukraine's Starshield satellite system as the war in the region escalates. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has accused SpaceX of being dishonest about restrictions on Ukraine's Starshield satellite system as the war in the region escalates. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has accused SpaceX of being dishonest about restrictions on Ukraine's Starshield satellite system as the war in the region escalates. On Friday, the Ukrainian leader said that the decision to impose speed limits appears to be “political” rather than “technical”. Speaking to reporters,Zelenskyy emphasised that the restrictions are affecting Ukrainian drone operationsand have been in place for the past five days. He noted that with the restriction on Starshield, these drones could no longer fly at speeds of more than 161km/h (100mph). As a result of this, the incoming jet-powered Russian Shahed drones could no longer be intercepted. Zelenskyy pointed out that Ukraine's own mid-range strikes against Russian military targets in occupied territory were also severely impacted due to these restrictions. While speaking to journalists at the presidential palace in Kyiv, Zelenskyy said he had asked his military leadership to raise the issue with Elon Musk’s company SpaceX, as well as with the Pentagon and the US State Department. There was “no clear explanation” as to why Ukraine’s operations were being throttled. Zelenskyy said thatSpaceX had told Kyivthat there were “no restrictions”. The claim, Zelenskyy suggested, was untrue, with problems detected across the “entire fron","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:22:40 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/zelenskyy-accuses-spacex-of-lying-about-starshield-restrictions-is-this-a-pressure-tactic-14060043.html,2026-11-15 03:31:57
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Starship makes historic return as SpaceX catches spacecraft midair, booster explodes","Starship makes historic return as SpaceX catches spacecraft midair, booster explodes","Starship makes historic return as SpaceX catches spacecraft midair, booster explodes SpaceX’s Starship made a triumphant return to Earth on Saturday, caught in midair by giant mechanical arms where its journey began 22 hours earlier. SpaceX’s Starship made a triumphant return to Earth on Saturday, caught in midair by giant mechanical arms where its journey began 22 hours earlier. SpaceX’s Starship made a triumphant return to Earth on Saturday, caught in midair by giant mechanical arms where its journey began 22 hours earlier. It was the grand finale that Elon Musk and his team hoped for — the first-ever capture of a Starship flying back from space. But with the first-stage booster exploding shortly after Friday’s liftoff from Texas, the company fell short of its desired double catch, still the goal for accelerating moon and Mars travel. Wreckage remained in the Gulf of Mexico, cordoned off by buoys, as the stainless steel, bullet-shaped spacecraft lowered itself upright at the launch pad. The dramatic, sci-fi-like capture helped blot out the booster’s messy miss. Cameras panned the spacecraft up and down as it hung high above the ground, supported by the arms of the launch tower. ”Can you believe it?” SpaceX commentator Dan Huot shouted, dragging out each word. ”Look at her! Baby, she’s back!” Soon afterward, Musk congratulated his ”incredible team.” SpaceX officials said Saturday’s catch demonstrates the full reusability of Starship, crucial for rapid and low-cost recycling. Although Friday’s booster recovery failed, the company had already made three previous booster catches, validating the technique. NASA welcomed Saturday’s news. The space agency is paying billions of dollars for Starship to land Arte","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:52:03 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/starship-makes-historic-return-as-spacex-catches-spacecraft-midair-booster-explodes-14060041.html,2026-11-15 03:31:58
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"India backs UN resolution on Palestinian rights over natural resources, 151 countries vote in favour","India backs UN resolution on Palestinian rights over natural resources, 151 countries vote in favour","India backs UN resolution on Palestinian rights over natural resources, 151 countries vote in favour India has voted in favour of a United Nations General Assembly draft resolution reaffirming the rights of Palestinians over their natural resources in the occupied territories, including East Jerusalem India has voted in favour of a United Nations General Assembly draft resolution reaffirming the rights of Palestinians over their natural resources in the occupied territories, including East Jerusalem India has voted in favour of a United Nations General Assembly draft resolution reaffirming the rights of Palestinians over their natural resources in the occupied territories, including East Jerusalem. The resolution also upholds the rights of the Arab population in the occupied Syrian Golan over its natural resources. The Uruguay-sponsored draft received overwhelming support in the General Assembly’s Second Committee during its 81st session on Wednesday. A total of 151 countries voted in favour, while seven, including the United States and Israel, opposed it. Eleven countries abstained. The draft will now move to the full General Assembly for consideration and final adoption later in the session. Its passage in the committee reflects broad international support for Palestinian rights over land, water and other resources in territories under occupation. The resolution urges Israel to stop policies and activities that could change the character, status or demographic composition of the Occupied Palestinian Territory, including East Jerusalem. It also calls on Israel to meet its obligations under international humanitarian law. The text raises concerns over the exploitation and depletion of natural resources, along with environmental damage caused by activities in occupied areas","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:53:58 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/india-backs-un-resolution-on-palestinian-rights-over-natural-resources-151-countries-vote-in-favour-14060036.html,2026-11-15 03:31:58
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Trump asks Supreme Court to curb judges' power to strike down federal policies nationwide,Trump asks Supreme Court to curb judges' power to strike down federal policies nationwide,"Trump asks Supreme Court to curb judges' power to strike down federal policies nationwide The Justice Department wants courts to limit relief under the Administrative Procedure Act to the parties who bring a case, potentially allowing disputed regulations to remain in force elsewhere. The Justice Department wants courts to limit relief under the Administrative Procedure Act to the parties who bring a case, potentially allowing disputed regulations to remain in force elsewhere. US President Donald Trump is seeking to further restrict the ability of federal judges to block his administration’s policies nationwide, asking the Supreme Court to limit a separate judicial power that survived a major ruling in his favour last year. An appeal filed by the Justice Department urges the justices to narrow the authority courts have long exercised under the Administrative Procedure Act (APA), a 1946 law governing the functioning of federal agencies. The administration argues that when judges find an agency regulation unlawful, they should be able to block its enforcement only against the specific parties who brought the lawsuit, rather than invalidate it nationwide. According to the administration, courts should not be able to shut down an agency’s regulation entirely, instead limiting any relief granted only to the specific plaintiffs in a given case. Aditya Bamzai, a University of Virginia expert in administrative law, said a win for Trump in the case could let the US government continue to enforce rules broadly on all but the plaintiffs in a given case, potentially for years as litigation plays out, even after judges have deemed them unlawful. Siding with Trump ”would give more flexibility to the executive branch,” Bamzai said. ”Whether you like or dislike that flexi","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:49:21 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/united-states/trump-asks-supreme-court-to-curb-judges-power-to-strike-down-federal-policies-nationwide-14060034.html,2026-11-15 03:31:58
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Putin's grandson registered under mother's surname as father's name echoes Ukraine's Zelenskyy: Report,Putin's grandson registered under mother's surname as father's name echoes Ukraine's Zelenskyy: Report,"Putin's grandson registered under mother's surname as father's name echoes Ukraine's Zelenskyy: Report Putin’s daughter Katerina Tikhonova reportedly named her son Adrian, but the child was registered under her surname rather than that of his father, ballet dancer Igor Zelensky. Putin’s daughter Katerina Tikhonova reportedly named her son Adrian, but the child was registered under her surname rather than that of his father, ballet dancer Igor Zelensky. Russian President Vladimir Putin’s family has reportedly added another grandchild, but the boy’s surname has become a talking point because his presumed father shares a name with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy. Putin’s younger daughter, Katerina Tikhonova, gave birth to a son named Adrian in Moscow on August 15, 2025, according to leaked civil registry records obtained by the independent Russian investigative outlet Agentstvo. The child’s presumed father is ballet dancer Igor Zelensky who is not related to the Ukrainian president. The records show that the boy was registered as Adrian Igorevich Tikhonov, taking the masculine form of his mother’s surname instead of his father’s. The choice has attracted attention because of the political significance of the Zelensky name amid Russia’s war against Ukraine. The Daily Beastdescribed the situation as an ironic predicament for Putin, suggesting that the Russian president’s grandson would otherwise have carried the surname of the Ukrainian leader who has become the face of his country’s resistance to Moscow. However, there is no confirmed evidence that Putin or his family deliberately chose the maternal surname because of its association with Zelenskyy. The timing of the child’s official registration has also raised questions. Although the first docu","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:11:56 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/putins-grandson-registered-under-mothers-surname-as-fathers-name-echoes-ukraines-zelenskyy-14060028.html,2026-11-15 03:31:58
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"No cyberattack, no AI: FAA identifies equipment fault behind US flight chaos, more cancellations likely","No cyberattack, no AI: FAA identifies equipment fault behind US flight chaos, more cancellations likely","No cyberattack, no AI: FAA identifies equipment fault behind US flight chaos, more cancellations likely FAA Administrator Bryan Bedford apologised to passengers affected by the disruption, saying investigators had identified the fault and found no evidence of a cyberattack or involvement of artificial intelligence FAA Administrator Bryan Bedford apologised to passengers affected by the disruption, saying investigators had identified the fault and found no evidence of a cyberattack or involvement of artificial intelligence Air travel across the United States continued to face major disruption on Saturday, even after authorities lifted a nationwide flight suspension triggered by a communications failure in the air traffic control system. Federal officials have warned that thousands of additional flights could be cancelled as airlines struggle to restore normal operations and reposition aircraft and crew. The Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) said around12,000 flights were cancelledon Friday (US time), while another 4,000 to 5,000 cancellations were expected on Saturday out of approximately 41,000 scheduled services. FAA Administrator Bryan Bedford apologised to passengers affected by the disruption, saying investigators had identified the fault and found no evidence of a cyberattack or involvement of artificial intelligence. ""We've identified the fault, and I want to reiterate we see zero evidence of anything nefarious and zero evidence of anything AI-related,"" Bedford said. Thenationwide ground stop, which lasted around four hours, was lifted at 8:15 pm Eastern Time on Friday. However, officials cautioned that the recovery would take longer, with passengers likely to face further delays and cancellations. Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said the disruption was linked to maintena","Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:01:13 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/united-states/no-cyberattack-no-ai-faa-identifies-equipment-fault-behind-us-flight-chaos-more-cancellations-likely-14060030.html,2026-11-15 03:31:58
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"After midterm rout of Republicans, Democrats face battle over how to govern and confront Trump","After midterm rout of Republicans, Democrats face battle over how to govern and confront Trump","After midterm rout of Republicans, Democrats face battle over how to govern and confront Trump A sweeping electoral victory has exposed divisions between moderates and progressives over economic priorities, cooperation with Trump and the direction of the party ahead of the 2028 presidential race. A sweeping electoral victory has exposed divisions between moderates and progressives over economic priorities, cooperation with Trump and the direction of the party ahead of the 2028 presidential race. Fresh from their sweeping victory in the November 3 midterm elections, Democrats gathered in Denver this week with a shared pledge to tackle the rising cost of living but sharply differing views on how to deliver on that promise. The party's first major gathering since its electoral triumph exposed disagreements over its political direction, the lessons of the result and how aggressively it should confront President Donald Trump. Despite the celebratory atmosphere following their decisive defeat of Republicans, tensions between the party's moderate leadership and its increasingly assertive progressive wing were evident throughout the conference. There was also a growing concern among party members that internal disagreements could undermine the opportunity created by their electoral success. The gathering provided an early indication of the contest likely to define the Democratic Party's future, as senior leaders and potential contenders for the 2028 presidential nomination debated how to translate their midterm victory into a governing programme while addressing longstanding ideological and generational differences. Organised by Majority Democrats, a group that advocates for younger Democratic leaders and opposes left-wing activism, the conference became a platform for compet","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:25:24 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/united-states/after-midterm-rout-of-republicans-democrats-face-battle-over-how-to-govern-and-confront-trump-14060024.html,2026-11-15 03:31:58
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"India-US ties ‘global’, Pakistan relationship ‘regional’: Blinken backs India’s right to defend itself","India-US ties ‘global’, Pakistan relationship ‘regional’: Blinken backs India’s right to defend itself","India-US ties ‘global’, Pakistan relationship ‘regional’: Blinken backs India’s right to defend itself The former US Secretary of State called Washington's ties with New Delhi global and its relationship with Islamabad regional, while stressing India's right to respond to terrorism and discussing conflicts in Iran and West Asia. The former US Secretary of State called Washington's ties with New Delhi global and its relationship with Islamabad regional, while stressing India's right to respond to terrorism and discussing conflicts in Iran and West Asia. Former US Secretary of State Antony Blinken on Saturday said Washington must uphold a zero-tolerance approach towards terrorism and respect India's right to defend itself against attacks. He also underlined the distinction between America's relationships with New Delhi and Islamabad, describing them as fundamentally different in nature. Speaking at the Hindustan Times Leadership Summit 2026 in New Delhi, Blinken said India had emerged as a global force, with its partnership with the United States extending across international issues and shared strategic interests. In contrast, he characterised the US relationship with Pakistan as primarily regional, although he acknowledged that cooperation with Islamabad remained important in certain areas, particularly counter-terrorism. ”India is a global force,” Blinken said, adding that the relationship and shared interests between Washington and New Delhi were ”really global in nature”. ""The relations with Pakistan are regional, and there are still going to be important areas where we need to do things with them, particularly, for example, when it comes to counter-terrorism, but these are fundamentally different relationships,"" he said during a conversation with Jawed Ashraf, chairman of the India Trade Promotio","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:36:20 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/india-us-ties-global-pakistan-relationship-regional-blinken-backs-indias-right-to-defend-itself-14060020.html,2026-11-15 03:31:58
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"‘No justice, no peace’: Protests sweep France over police bill, rising living costs","‘No justice, no peace’: Protests sweep France over police bill, rising living costs","‘No justice, no peace’: Protests sweep France over police bill, rising living costs Demonstrators, students and unions have taken to the streets over wages, alleged police brutality and a proposed law granting officers greater legal protection when using firearms. Demonstrators, students and unions have taken to the streets over wages, alleged police brutality and a proposed law granting officers greater legal protection when using firearms. Protesters raised the French flag atop a statue in Paris on Saturday as demonstrations swept across France, reflecting growing public anger over the rising cost of living, wages and a proposed law that could expand legal protections for police officers using firearms. France, the European Union's second-largest economy, has witnessed more than a month of high-school blockades and street demonstrations, with protesters demanding better wages and challenging government policies ahead of next year's presidential election, which will mark the end of Emmanuel Macron's presidency. Although most demonstrations have remained peaceful, some have been accompanied by violence involving fringe groups and allegations of police brutality including incidents involving young teenagers. Thousands gathered at Paris's Place de la République on Saturday afternoon, marking the fifth consecutive weekend of protests. ""No justice, no peace,"" one demonstrator shouted through a megaphone. Among those marching in the capital were members of the Yellow Vest movement, students, trade union representatives and civil rights activists. Benjamin Ball, a member of the Yellow Vest movement, toldAFPthat the government's response to public demands had been inadequate. ""The government has only given us crumbs, and we want the whole bak","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:18:47 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/no-justice-no-peace-protests-sweep-france-over-police-bill-rising-living-costs-14060016.html,2026-11-15 03:31:58
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,US flight chaos: FAA lifts nationwide ground stop after major air traffic communications failure,US flight chaos: FAA lifts nationwide ground stop after major air traffic communications failure,"US flight chaos: FAA lifts nationwide ground stop after major air traffic communications failure Air travel across the United States is gradually resuming after a major communications failure in the air traffic control system forced authorities to ground flights nationwide Air travel across the United States is gradually resuming after a major communications failure in the air traffic control system forced authorities to ground flights nationwide Air travel across the United States is gradually resuming after a major communications failure in the air traffic control system forced authorities to ground flights nationwide, leaving tens of thousands of passengers stranded and disrupting thousands of journeys. The Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) lifted thenationwide ground stopon Friday at 8:15 pm Eastern Time (1:15 am GMT on Saturday). However, Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy cautioned that it would take time for airlines to restore normal schedules, with delays and cancellations likely to continue for several days. More than 16,000 flights are likely to be cancelled by Saturday across the country, according to the aviation regulator. Delta Air Lines and American Airlines each reported more than 2,200 cancellations, while United Airlines recorded around 1,800. Duffy said tens of thousands of travellers had been affected by the disruption. The four-hour nationwide grounding was among the most significant interruptions to US aviation since the September 11, 2001, attacks. According to Duffy, the technical failure began at around 3:36 pm on Friday, when air traffic control centres experienced instability in their radar and communications systems. He explained that switches and routers within the network became overloaded with data, resultin","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:06:11 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/united-states/us-flight-chaos-faa-lifts-nationwide-ground-stop-after-major-air-traffic-communications-failure-14060015.html,2026-11-15 03:31:59
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Pakistan nominates climate minister for SCO dialogue in Delhi, first ministerial visit since May 2023","Pakistan nominates climate minister for SCO dialogue in Delhi, first ministerial visit since May 2023","Pakistan nominates climate minister for SCO dialogue in Delhi, first ministerial visit since May 2023 Pakistan's Climate Minister Musadik Masood Malik has been nominated to attend the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) Civilizational Dialogue, scheduled to take place in New Delhi from November 20 to 22 Pakistan's Climate Minister Musadik Masood Malik has been nominated to attend the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) Civilizational Dialogue, scheduled to take place in New Delhi from November 20 to 22 A Pakistani minister is likely to visit India later this month for a regional diplomatic gathering, which could mark the first ministerial-level visit from Islamabad to New Delhi in more than three years. Pakistan's Climate Minister Musadik Masood Malik has been nominated to attend the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) Civilizational Dialogue, scheduled to take place in New Delhi from November 20 to 22, Pakistan's Foreign Ministry spokesperson said on Saturday. If the visit goes ahead, it will be the first time a Pakistani minister has travelled to India since May 2023, when then Foreign Minister Bilawal Bhutto Zardari visited Goa to attend an SCO meeting of foreign ministers. The proposed visit comes amid strained relations between the two neighbours, which deteriorated further following the Pahalgam terror attack in Jammu and Kashmir in April 2025 and the subsequent military confrontation between the two countries. Announcing Malik's nomination, Pakistan's Foreign Ministry said Islamabad remained committed to encouraging dialogue among civilisations and strengthening people-to-people contacts under the SCO framework. It added that these efforts would be pursued in a spirit of mutual respect. A day earlier, India had confirmed that invitations had been extended to a","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:57:53 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/pakistan-nominates-climate-minister-for-sco-dialogue-in-delhi-first-ministerial-visit-since-may-2023-14060011.html,2026-11-15 03:31:59
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,‘Would Ukraine withdraw from Donbas?’ Zelenskyy says US raised Nato membership-for-territory deal,‘Would Ukraine withdraw from Donbas?’ Zelenskyy says US raised Nato membership-for-territory deal,"‘Would Ukraine withdraw from Donbas?’ Zelenskyy says US raised Nato membership-for-territory deal Zelenskyy said the United States had asked for the first time whether Ukraine would withdraw from parts of the Donbas region in eastern Ukraine that Russia does not control if Kyiv were admitted to NATO. He reiterated that Kyiv would not surrender its territory. Zelenskyy said the United States had asked for the first time whether Ukraine would withdraw from parts of the Donbas region in eastern Ukraine that Russia does not control if Kyiv were admitted to NATO. He reiterated that Kyiv would not surrender its territory. US negotiators have suggested that Ukraine could withdraw from its eastern Donbas region in return for securing Nato membership, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has said, following the latest round of US-mediated peace negotiations with Russia in Abu Dhabi. Zelenskyy said Russia was ""betting everything"" on this winter's campaign in its war with Ukraine, while warning that the Kremlin's demands to redraw Europe's security architecture are ""dangerous"" and could lead to more wars. Zelenskyy spoke to the media Friday after visits to Denmark and Ireland, where he met with European leaders following two days of US-brokered Ukraine-Russia talks in Abu Dhabi. The talks ended with no breakthrough in Europe's worst war since World War II, but all sides agreed that European officials should be included in future negotiations. ""The Americans raised a question: 'What if Ukraine joins Nato? Would Ukraine withdraw from Donbas?' This was the first time this had been raised,"" Zelenskyy said in the comments kept under embargo until Saturday. He added that the proposal had brought Nato membership back into the negotiations, although reaching an agreement would be particularly difficult given Russian President Vladimir Putin's re","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:57:03 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/would-ukraine-withdraw-from-donbas-us-floats-nato-membership-in-possible-territorial-trade-off-14060006.html,2026-11-15 03:31:59
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"US set to lose measles elimination status after surge in infections, vaccine hesitancy: Reports","US set to lose measles elimination status after surge in infections, vaccine hesitancy: Reports","US set to lose measles elimination status after surge in infections, vaccine hesitancy: Reports The United States is set to lose its measles elimination status, marking a major setback for the country's public health system and reversing an achievement it had maintained for more than two decades The United States is set to lose its measles elimination status, marking a major setback for the country's public health system and reversing an achievement it had maintained for more than two decades The United States is set to lose its measles elimination status, marking a major setback for the country's public health system and reversing an achievement it had maintained for more than two decades. International health experts have reportedly concluded that the highly contagious virus has been spreading continuously in the country for more than a year. According to reports byThe Washington PostandAxios, the Pan American Health Organization (PAHO) has determined that the US no longer qualifies as a country that has eliminated the continuous transmission of measles. The official announcement is still awaited. The decision follows a sharp rise in measles infections since early 2025, with outbreaks spreading across several states. Public health experts have linked the resurgence to declining vaccination coverage, growing public distrust of vaccines and concerns over the federal government's approach to immunisation. An expert panel convened by PAHO reportedly reached the decision after a three-day meeting in Washington, DC. The assessment found that the same strain of measles had continued circulating in the US for more than 12 consecutive months. Under international health standards, a country is considered to have eliminated measles when it stops the continuous transmission of","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:04:55 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/united-states/us-set-to-lose-measles-elimination-status-after-surge-in-infections-vaccine-hesitancy-reports-14060004.html,2026-11-15 03:31:59
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,A New 'Yalta'? Why a Trump-Xi-Putin summit may struggle to deliver a global breakthrough,A New 'Yalta'? Why a Trump-Xi-Putin summit may struggle to deliver a global breakthrough,"A New 'Yalta'? Why a Trump-Xi-Putin summit may struggle to deliver a global breakthrough The proposed meeting brings together three leaders with competing priorities, raising fears that a deal on Ukraine, nuclear arms or global influence could sideline smaller nations and reshape the world order without their involvement. The proposed meeting brings together three leaders with competing priorities, raising fears that a deal on Ukraine, nuclear arms or global influence could sideline smaller nations and reshape the world order without their involvement. The leaders of the United States, China and Russia could come together next week for an unprecedented trilateral meeting to discuss some of the world's most pressing challenges including the wars in Ukraine and Iran, nuclear weapons and artificial intelligence. However, expectations of a major diplomatic breakthrough from the rare gathering remain low. Negotiations over a proposed meeting between US President Donald Trump, Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin are continuing until the last moment, with no agreement yet on the agenda or the format of the discussions,Reuterscited two people familiar with the preparations as saying. The meeting is nevertheless expected to take place in Shenzhen, where the three leaders will attend the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) forum. Each leader is approaching the proposed encounter with different priorities. Putin is looking to use the opportunity to secure a settlement to the four-year-old war in Ukraine on terms favourable to Moscow. Trump, meanwhile, who has faced political setbacks following his Republican Party's recent electoral losses, sees the gathering as an opportunity to make diplomatic history, potentially by advancing a three-way understanding on nuclear arms","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:31:46 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/a-new-yalta-why-a-trump-xi-putin-summit-may-struggle-to-deliver-a-global-breakthrough-14059993.html,2026-11-15 03:31:59
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"China border 'more alive', requires sustained troop deployment, says Jaishankar","China border 'more alive', requires sustained troop deployment, says Jaishankar","China border 'more alive', requires sustained troop deployment, says Jaishankar External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar says India's border infrastructure and military deployment capabilities have improved significantly over the past decade, particularly after the 2020 Galwan clashes. External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar says India's border infrastructure and military deployment capabilities have improved significantly over the past decade, particularly after the 2020 Galwan clashes. India's border with China has become ""more alive"" in recent years and now demands a significantly larger and sustained deployment of troops, External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar said on Saturday, highlighting the government's efforts to strengthen infrastructure and military preparedness along the frontier. Speaking at an interactive session at the HT Leadership Summit, Jaishankar said India's ability to deploy troops along the Line of Actual Control (LAC) had improved considerably since the deadly clashes in Galwan Valley in eastern Ladakh in 2020. He also pointed to the expansion of military infrastructure and capabilities along the border. His remarks at an interactive session at the HT Leadership Summit came amid ongoing efforts by New Delhi and Beijing to normalise their relations, which came under severe strain following the over four-year border face-off in Eastern Ladakh. ”Just think about the last few years. How often do you now read – a new tunnel has been built, some new bridge has been built, another airfield has been commissioned. You’re getting this news with greater and greater frequency,” he said. ”What has happened today is the border with China has become more alive in a way. It has required a much greater commitment of troops on a sustained basis.” ”The ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:31:05 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/india/china-border-more-alive-requires-sustained-troop-deployment-says-jaishankar-14059994.html,2026-11-15 03:32:00
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Hasina's return to Bangladesh: Law Minister says legal process complete, puts ball in India's court","Hasina's return to Bangladesh: Law Minister says legal process complete, puts ball in India's court","Hasina's return to Bangladesh: Law Minister says legal process complete, puts ball in India's court As Bangladesh grapples with questions surrounding the possible return of ousted former PM Sheikh Hasina, Law Minister Asaduzzaman said on Saturday that she would return to the country through 'legal means' As Bangladesh grapples with questions surrounding the possible return of ousted former PM Sheikh Hasina, Law Minister Asaduzzaman said on Saturday that she would return to the country through 'legal means' Will she, or will she not? As Bangladesh grapples with questions surrounding the possible return of ousted former prime minister Sheikh Hasina, Law Minister Asaduzzaman said on Saturday that she would return to the country through “legal means”, adding that Dhaka had completed all the necessary steps from its side. “Sheikh Hasina will return to Bangladesh through legal means. We have completed everything required from our side as part of the legal process,” the minister said, as reported by Bangladeshi media outletProthom Alo. Days ago, Hasina had reportedlysought the issuance of a Bangladeshi passportso that she could return to the country by December. The Bangladesh government, however, rejected the demand, saying, “We don't issue passports to terrorists.” Dhaka has been pressing New Delhi to extradite Hasina under the extradition treaty signed between the two countries in 2013. The agreement provides for the reciprocal surrender of individuals charged with or convicted of offences punishable by at least one year of imprisonment. However, Article 6 of the treaty provides an exception for political offences, stating that extradition can be refused if the offence is considered to be of a political character. Speaking to journalists after an event at the Bangladesh-China Fri","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:08:34 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/hasinas-return-to-bangladesh-law-minister-says-legal-process-complete-puts-ball-in-indias-court-14059987.html,2026-11-15 03:32:00
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,UK: Indian-origin man sentenced to 30 years in prison for grooming 70 minors online,UK: Indian-origin man sentenced to 30 years in prison for grooming 70 minors online,"UK: Indian-origin man sentenced to 30 years in prison for grooming 70 minors online An Indian-origin man who groomed at least 70 girls and coerced them to send sexually explicit videos and images of themselves was sentenced to 30 years in prison in the United Kingdom. An Indian-origin man who groomed at least 70 girls and coerced them to send sexually explicit videos and images of themselves was sentenced to 30 years in prison in the United Kingdom. An Indian-origin man who groomed at least 70 girls and coerced them to send sexually explicit videos and images of themselves was sentenced to 30 years in prison in the United Kingdom. 27-year-old Bilal Kazi targeted his victims, who were between the ages of 10 and 17, using social media apps like Snapchat, Wink and even Roblox. According to the authorities, he committed the crimes between August 2021 and August 2025. Kazi, who came from India, was studying at the University of Chester. According to the BBC, he posed as a 14-year-old White British teenage boy and made his victims believe that he was in a relationship with them. He was eventually jailed after pleading guilty to 37 charges, including making indecent images, blackmail and inciting a child to engage in sexual activity. The court ruled that Kazi must serve a minimum of 20 years in prison before being eligible for parole and will be on the sex offenders register for life. Once he is eligible for parole, he will be on licence for eight years. In a personal impact statement read out at Chester Crown Court earlier, one victim said she had struggled with anxiety as Kazi, who later moved to Birmingham, had ""taken away a sense of privacy and security,"" BBC reported. ""I am doing my best to move forward, but the effects are still with me,"" s","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:22:58 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/uk-indian-origin-man-sentenced-to-30-years-in-prison-for-grooming-70-minors-online-14059976.html,2026-11-15 03:32:00
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"US asked if Ukraine would give up Donbas in return for Nato membership, says Zelenskyy","US asked if Ukraine would give up Donbas in return for Nato membership, says Zelenskyy","US asked if Ukraine would give up Donbas in return for Nato membership, says Zelenskyy Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has said the EU and Nato are essential to Europe’s security, while revealing that the US had raised the possibility of Ukraine surrendering territory in Donbas in exchange for Nato membership Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has said the EU and Nato are essential to Europe’s security, while revealing that the US had raised the possibility of Ukraine surrendering territory in Donbas in exchange for Nato membership Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said the United States asked whether Ukraine would withdraw from Donbas in return for Nato membership, a question he said had never been put to Kyiv before. His remarks come days before the leaders of the US, China and Russia are due to meet in Shenzhen on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit, an unprecedented gathering of the heads of the world’s biggest nuclear powers. Zelenskyy further said that theEuropean Union and Natoare the only source of genuine security on the continent, cautioning that Russia’s attempt to alter Europe’s security architecture could lead to fresh conflict. Speaking to reporters on Friday, in remarks embargoed until Saturday, he said such moves were dangerous because they were precisely the kind of thing that “lead to wars or escalations”. “Real security in Europe means the EU and Nato. That’s it,” he said. “There is no other security in Europe.” “The Americans raised a question: ‘What if Ukraine joins Nato? Would Ukraine withdraw from Donbas?’ This was the first time this had been raised,” he said. Kyiv’s government, he said, is in talks on “specific security guarantees from Nato and the EU”. If Western countries confirmed them, he would put the matter to the","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:00:02 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-asked-if-ukraine-would-give-up-donbas-in-return-for-nato-membership-says-zelenskyy-14059985.html,2026-11-15 03:32:00
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Microsoft says services fully restored after global outage hit governments, banks and airlines","Microsoft says services fully restored after global outage hit governments, banks and airlines","Microsoft says services fully restored after global outage hit governments, banks and airlines Microsoft says services are fully restored after a Thursday outage that disrupted Outlook, Teams and Copilot across more than 70 countries and territories, with the company blaming a network capacity upgrade rather than a cyber incident Microsoft says services are fully restored after a Thursday outage that disrupted Outlook, Teams and Copilot across more than 70 countries and territories, with the company blaming a network capacity upgrade rather than a cyber incident Microsoft said on Saturday that all services had been restored after a sweeping outage that left users around the world without access to core workplace tools for hours. “We have completed our efforts to address the underlying issue of the incident and restored service to the remaining impacted customers and regions,” the company said in an update on X. The Redmond, Washington-based company apologised on Friday for thedisruption. It said the outage was “not related to cyber” or artificial intelligence agents, and that the incident “was introduced by an issue during an earlier network capacity upgrade that surfaced” after a recent network change. Problems began to surface around midday on Thursday in the US. Within an hour, the online tracker Downdetector had logged outage reports from 74 countries and territories. Users reported disruption to Microsoft 365 services, including Outlook, Teams and the AI assistant Copilot. Governments, courts, healthcare services, businesses, airlines and banks in many places were affected. The governments of Japan, Singapore and Australia said the hours-long episode had hit some of their operations. The total number of people affected was not clear. Microsoft says more than 430 million people use its Microsoft 3","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:07:41 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/tech/microsoft-says-services-fully-restored-after-global-outage-hit-governments-banks-and-airlines-14059984.html,2026-11-15 03:32:00
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Indian student jailed for 30 years in UK for grooming 70 girls online,Indian student jailed for 30 years in UK for grooming 70 girls online,"Indian student jailed for 30 years in UK for grooming 70 girls online An Indian student who posed online as a teenage boy called “Reece” has been jailed for 30 years in England, after a police inquiry traced 70 of his victims across 28 UK forces An Indian student who posed online as a teenage boy called “Reece” has been jailed for 30 years in England, after a police inquiry traced 70 of his victims across 28 UK forces Bilal Kazi, a 27-year-old Indian student whom UK authorities have labelled a “serial online groomer”, will spend 30 years behind bars for coercing and exploiting children over the internet. He was sentenced at Chester Crown Court in north-west England on Friday, having admitted a series of online child sexual abuse offences. The inquiry that brought him to court was vast. Police identified 180 potential victims and eventually confirmed 70, aged between 11 and 17 at the time, spread across 28 of the UK’s 45 police forces. The court heard that Kazi hid behind a false identity on social media and gaming platforms to gain the confidence of girls aged between 10 and 15. Investigators found he used one method throughout. On Snapchat, Roblox and Wink, he presented himself as “Reece”, a white British teenage boy, using photographs of an unidentified youth. Many of the girls were soon convinced they were in a genuine relationship. Once trust was established, prosecutors said, he pressed them to film or photograph themselves performing sexual acts. Those who balked at further demands were blackmailed with threats to circulate the explicit images. The first victim began chatting to Kazi on Snapchat aged 13, believing he was her age, police said. The exchanges swiftly became sexual. In July 2021, she told him she w","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:47:59 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/indian-student-jailed-for-30-years-in-uk-for-grooming-70-girls-online-14059980.html,2026-11-15 03:32:00
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"'I don't pay my tax dollars for...': El-Sayed questions US's aid to countries like Pakistan, Egypt","'I don't pay my tax dollars for...': El-Sayed questions US's aid to countries like Pakistan, Egypt","'I don't pay my tax dollars for...': El-Sayed questions US's aid to countries like Pakistan, Egypt US Senator-elect from Michigan, Abdul El-Sayed, urged Washington to reconsider its financial and military assistance to countries that tend to violate international law, taking examples of Pakistan and Egypt, Saudi Arabia, etc. US Senator-elect from Michigan, Abdul El-Sayed, urged Washington to reconsider its financial and military assistance to countries that tend to violate international law, taking examples of Pakistan and Egypt, Saudi Arabia, etc. US Senator-elect from Michigan, Abdul El-Sayed, urged Washington to reconsider its financial and military assistance to countries that tend to violate international law, taking examples of Pakistan and Egypt, Saudi Arabia, etc. Emphasising that the taxpayers' money is at stake, the progressive Democratic leader said that there shouldn't be ""unconditional foreign aid"" to any country. ""I don't pay my tax dollars so the government of Egypt gets tanks, or the government of Pakistan, or the government of Saudi Arabia,"" El-Sayed said in an interview with PBS NewsHour. ""I don't believe that we should be doing unconditional foreign military aid as a matter of course,"" he added. This is not the first time the senator-elect has shared his thoughts on the matter. In an interview with ABC News earlier this week, El-Sayed said that American taxpayers’ money should not be used to support countries accused of violating international law. He insisted that the US need to ensure that its own actions are consistent with international law, adding that the issue should not be limited to Israel only. “How do we make sure that we’re holding ourselves accountable to international law? And it’s not just about Israel. I take the same approach to Egypt, where my family immigrate","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:26:27 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/i-dont-pay-my-tax-dollars-for-el-sayed-questions-uss-aid-to-countries-like-pakistan-egypt-14059958.html,2026-11-15 03:32:00
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Canada, Philippines conclude FTA negotiations, deal expected in 2027: Carney","Canada, Philippines conclude FTA negotiations, deal expected in 2027: Carney","Canada, Philippines conclude FTA negotiations, deal expected in 2027: Carney Carney announces the conclusion of negotiations for two trade agreements during his visit to Manila, with both expected to be signed in 2027. Carney announces the conclusion of negotiations for two trade agreements during his visit to Manila, with both expected to be signed in 2027. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney has announced the conclusion of free trade negotiations with the Philippines and the talks for a broader trade agreement with the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (Asean), marking a major step in Canada's efforts to diversify its economic partnerships beyond the United States. Both agreements are expected to be signed in 2027, as Ottawa looks to reduce its dependence on a single trading partner and strengthen its presence in one of the world's fastest-growing economic regions, as per the statement. The announcements came as Carney met Philippine President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. on the sidelines of the 49th Asean Summit in Manila, where he represented Canada as Guest of the Chair. The proposed Asean-Canada Free Trade Agreement (ACAFTA), covering a regional market of nearly 700 million people and an economy worth close to $6 trillion, is expected to add nearly $2 billion to Canada's gross domestic product (GDP) and create around 14,000 jobs once implemented. The agreement is also expected to strengthen Canada's integration into Asian supply chains, particularly in agriculture and manufacturing. The statement added that Ottawa has also announced $5 million in assistance to help Asean economies prepare for the agreement's ratification and ensure they benefit from it once it comes into force. The Phili","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:11:34 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/canada-philippines-conclude-fta-negotiations-deal-expected-in-2027-carney-14059966.html,2026-11-15 03:32:00
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Israel’s spy chief flies to Washington as Trump rebuffs Netanyahu on resuming Iran war,Israel’s spy chief flies to Washington as Trump rebuffs Netanyahu on resuming Iran war,"Israel’s spy chief flies to Washington as Trump rebuffs Netanyahu on resuming Iran war The head of Israel’s Mossad is in Washington for talks on the Iran war, just as Trump declares the US no longer needs a deal with Tehran and Netanyahu lobbies for a return to fighting The head of Israel’s Mossad is in Washington for talks on the Iran war, just as Trump declares the US no longer needs a deal with Tehran and Netanyahu lobbies for a return to fighting Israel’s Mossad chief, Roman Gofman, has travelled to Washington for talks with senior Trump administration officials on the war with Iran, according to sources cited byThe Jerusalem Post. The visit comes as Trump takes a harder line on a negotiated settlement and Netanyahu presses him to return to the fighting. On November 12, Trump declared that Washington had no need of an agreement with Iran. “Those days have long since passed,” he wrote on Truth Social, adding that the US already held “Hundreds of Billions of Dollars” of Iran’s money and “their Strait”. He also redirected Vice President JD Vance, who has been involved in attempts to end the conflict, towards what he called “Massive Corruption and Crime” in Democrat-run cities and states. “CORRUPTION is in the Democrat Leadership’s blood!” the president wrote. The remarks marked a notable departure from the preceding month, when Trump had seemed keener to conclude a deal and end the eight-month conflict. Netanyahu has been pressing for the opposite course.Axiosreported that Trump has lately refused his requests to resume hostilities. In a call on October 31 on US negotiations with Iran, Netanyahu is reported to have urged an immediate strike once the midterm elections were over. Trump turned the idea down,Axiossaid, preferring to keep to the","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:58:27 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/israels-spy-chief-flies-to-washington-as-trump-rebuffs-netanyahu-on-resuming-iran-war-14059971.html,2026-11-15 03:32:01
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Protesters take to French streets again, with 'licence to kill' bill in the spotlight","Protesters take to French streets again, with 'licence to kill' bill in the spotlight","Protesters take to French streets again, with 'licence to kill' bill in the spotlight France braces for a fifth consecutive Saturday of protests, with demonstrators airing grievances from the cost of living to a contested police bill, ahead of next year’s presidential elections France braces for a fifth consecutive Saturday of protests, with demonstrators airing grievances from the cost of living to a contested police bill, ahead of next year’s presidential elections France is set for another day of demonstrations on Saturday, with protesters voicing a mix of grievances, from rising prices to opposition to a new police bill, in the latest round of rallies to sweep the country. The European Union’s second-largest economy has been rocked for more than a month by high school blockades and cost-of-living protests. They come ahead of presidential elections next year that the far right regards as its best chance of taking power. Most of the rallies have passed off peacefully, though some have seen isolated violence and accusations of police brutality. Protesters were due to take to the streets for the fifth consecutive Saturday. The main march in Paris was set to begin at 1:00 pm (1200 GMT), alongside dozens of other gatherings nationwide. In the capital, the Yellow Vest movement was expected to joinhigh-school students, unions and other activists campaigning for children’s rights or against a bill giving police greater protection when they use their weapons. “Society’s in bad shape,” said Claire Bourdille, of a collective fighting violence against children and teenagers. “We can’t focus on one cause more than another.” In recent months, activists have pressed for stronger protection of children against sexual abuse. Other demonstrators will be marching a","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:31:04 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/world-france-protests-police-weapons-bill-unions-strike-14059968.html,2026-11-15 03:32:01
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Kaja Kallas pitches herself for EU envoy role in Ukraine peace talks, says ‘Russians do not want me’","Kaja Kallas pitches herself for EU envoy role in Ukraine peace talks, says ‘Russians do not want me’","Kaja Kallas pitches herself for EU envoy role in Ukraine peace talks, says ‘Russians do not want me’ The EU foreign policy chief has argued that her institutional role makes her a natural choice to represent the bloc in negotiations with Russia. The EU foreign policy chief has argued that her institutional role makes her a natural choice to represent the bloc in negotiations with Russia. European Union foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas has made a strong pitch for herself to become the bloc’s special envoy in negotiations aimed at ending Russia’s war in Ukraine, adding that her position makes her the appropriate choice for the high-stakes diplomatic role. However, acknowledging Moscow’s opposition to her appointment, Kallas said, “Russians do not want me” at the negotiating table because of her strong views on the conflict. Speaking on Friday at an informal summit of EU leaders in Dublin, Ireland, Kallas questioned why Russia should have a say in deciding who represents the European Union. “But do we have a say in who is representing Russia? No, we do not. Really, we have to have a strong team,” she said. Kallas argued that EU leaders had already designated her as the bloc’s representative on security and foreign policy when they appointed her High Representative in June 2024,reported by Euro news. She added that the appointment was made with the understanding that negotiations with Moscow would eventually take place during her five-year tenure. “If the leaders want to change that agreement, of course, they may, because it is the leaders’ decision, but I think we should focus our energy actually on the substance,” she added. The EU foreign policy chief also cautioned against replicating the United States’ approach to n","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:48:55 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/kaja-kallas-pitches-herself-for-eu-envoy-role-in-ukraine-peace-talks-says-russians-do-not-want-me-14059948.html,2026-11-15 03:32:01
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Finland rejects Russia's reported 'proposal' to reverse its Nato membership,Finland rejects Russia's reported 'proposal' to reverse its Nato membership,"Finland rejects Russia's reported 'proposal' to reverse its Nato membership Finland on Friday rejected Russia's reported demand that it withdraw its membership from Nato as part of negotiations to end the war in Ukraine. Finland on Friday rejected Russia's reported demand that it withdraw its membership from Nato as part of negotiations to end the war in Ukraine. Finland on Friday rejected Russia's reported demand that it withdraw its membership from Nato as part of negotiations to end the war in Ukraine. German news outlet Bild first reported that Russian negotiators had presented an unofficial proposal during the Abu Dhabi talks seeking to reverse Finland's Nato membership and restrict the alliance's military presence in Eastern Europe. However, Russia quickly denied the report and insisted that no such demands were made. In the midst of this, Finnish ministers made it clear that the country's membership was never open for negotiations in the first place. Finnish Defence Minister Antti Häkkänen said the reported demand was unacceptable and stressed that Finland's membership was not a subject for peace negotiations. ""Such matters are not open to negotiation under any circumstances. Even suggesting something like that is absolutely outrageous,"" Häkkänen told reporters, according to the Helsinki Times. He admitted that Russia was attempting to expand the negotiations beyond Ukraine to secure restrictions on European defence arrangements. Meanwhile, the country's Foreign Minister Elina Valtonen also rejected any suggestion that Moscow should influence Finland's Nato membership. ""It is clear that this is a decision for Finland and the alliance alone to make,"" she said. Prime Minister Petteri Orp","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:29:46 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/finland-rejects-russias-reported-proposal-to-reverse-its-nato-membership-14059942.html,2026-11-15 03:32:01
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Jensen Huang misled Nvidia’s top executives about Alice Huang relationship: Report,Jensen Huang misled Nvidia’s top executives about Alice Huang relationship: Report,"Jensen Huang misled Nvidia’s top executives about Alice Huang relationship: Report Jensen Huang misled senior Nvidia leaders, including general counsel Tim Teter and chief marketing officer Alison Wagonfeld, about his relationship with Alice Huang, Jensen Huang misled senior Nvidia leaders, including general counsel Tim Teter and chief marketing officer Alison Wagonfeld, about his relationship with Alice Huang, Jensen Huang’s resignation as Nvidia’s chief executive on Thursday has been followed by a troubling detail: he misled several of the company’s senior figures about his relationship with Chinese businesswoman Alice Huang, with whom he had an affair. General counsel Tim Teter and chief marketing officer Alison Wagonfeld were among those given the misleading account, two sources familiar with the matter and internal correspondence toldReuters. The agency reviewed several exchanges from October, on condition that it would not quote from the messages verbatim. In both the autumn of 2025 and October 2026, press queries drew the attention of some Nvidia leaders to Huang’s relationship with Megaspeed International andAlice Huang. On each occasion, the people said, he described his interactions as appropriate. They spoke on condition of anonymity. In two separate messages that month, Huang toldNvidia leaders, Teter and Wagonfeld among them, that the interactions amounted to standard business dealings with customers. In further messages, he stressed the routine nature of his contact with Megaspeed. Huang also discussed taking legal action against theNew York Timesafter it published an article in October last year that drew attention to his public meetings with Alice Huang, the people said. The article led him to contact so","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:25:04 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/jensen-huang-misled-nvidias-top-executives-about-alice-huang-relationship-report-14059950.html,2026-11-15 03:32:01
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,US lawmakers seek SpaceX records over satellite service disruptions in Ukraine,US lawmakers seek SpaceX records over satellite service disruptions in Ukraine,"US lawmakers seek SpaceX records over satellite service disruptions in Ukraine US Democratic senators have asked Elon Musk and SpaceX to preserve all records concerning restrictions on Ukraine's use of Starlink and Starshield, citing national security concerns and seeking answers over disruptions to the satellite services US Democratic senators have asked Elon Musk and SpaceX to preserve all records concerning restrictions on Ukraine's use of Starlink and Starshield, citing national security concerns and seeking answers over disruptions to the satellite services Democratic US senators have told Elon Musk to preserve all records related to his company SpaceX's restrictions on Ukraine's use of its Starlink and Starshield satellite services. Ukrainian forces say Starshield, the military-grade version of Starlink, is vital for frontline communications and drone operations in their defense against Russian drone and missile attacks. But in mid-October, Ukrainian officials complained that the service had been restricted without explanation or warning, limiting their military's ability to conduct complicated strike missions against Russian forces and slowing interceptor drones used to shoot down Russian attack drones. ""The October and November restrictions now raise the disturbing possibility that these vulnerabilities persist even within systems on which the U.S. government relies,"" Senators Jeanne Shaheen of New Hampshire and Chris Coons of Delaware said in a letter to Musk. They gave Musk until November 30 to provide written confirmation that ""all appropriate preservation measures have been implemented."" The lawmakers sought SpaceX's records since September 1, including all communications related to Starlink and Starshield in Ukraine as well as communications between Musk, SpaceX executives and the","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:27:34 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-lawmakers-seek-spacex-records-over-satellite-service-disruptions-in-ukraine-14059945.html,2026-11-15 03:32:01
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"US to keep Nvidia spy probe off table at Trump-Xi meeting, officials say","US to keep Nvidia spy probe off table at Trump-Xi meeting, officials say","US to keep Nvidia spy probe off table at Trump-Xi meeting, officials say Donald Trump is not expected to raise the Alice Huang case with Xi Jinping when they meet in Shenzhen next week, US officials said, days after Jensen Huang quit as Nvidia chief executive Donald Trump is not expected to raise the Alice Huang case with Xi Jinping when they meet in Shenzhen next week, US officials said, days after Jensen Huang quit as Nvidia chief executive President Donald Trump is not expected to broach the case of Alice Huang, a businesswoman whose ties to former Nvidia chief executive Jensen Huang have raised national security concerns, when he meets Chinese President Xi Jinping next week, US officials said on Friday. The two leaders are due to hold talks on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation forum in Shenzhen, China, during afour-day Asia trip. The meeting falls only days afterJensen Huangstepped down as Nvidia’s chief executive on Thursday, ending a dramatic fall from the heights of the chip industry. Semiconductors have been a major flashpoint in relations between Washington and Beijing, but the officials said the president was not expected, for now, to take up the latest matter with Xi. “When it comes to some of these national security matters and examinations and investigations that are going on in the US, it’s probably not something that we’re going to read the Chinese in on at this moment,” a senior administration official told reporters. A second US official said, “I don’t expect the president to raise it, the Alice Huang issue.” Both were responding to a reporter’s question on whether Trump would put the allegations involving Alice Huang to Xi. On Tuesday, the independent members of Nvidia’s board said they had r","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:53:06 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-to-keep-nvidia-spy-probe-off-table-at-trump-xi-meeting-officials-say-14059940.html,2026-11-15 03:32:01
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Investigation launched after explosive device found near Dublin office building,Investigation launched after explosive device found near Dublin office building,"Investigation launched after explosive device found near Dublin office building Irish police on Friday launched an investigation after an explosive device was discovered at an office building in central Dublin Irish police on Friday launched an investigation after an explosive device was discovered at an office building in central Dublin Irish police on Friday launched an investigation after an explosive device was discovered at an office building in central Dublin, close to the venue where world leaders attended a dinner during a summit a day earlier. The Irish Defence Forces' Explosive Ordnance Disposal (EOD) team made the device safe after police received a report of a suspicious object at the building on Merrion Square on Friday afternoon. Describing the device as ""crude but viable"", police said Explosive Ordnance Disposal (EOD) team had been called in following an initial assessment by Garda, Ireland's police force. ""Based ​on initial Garda (police) assessment the defence forces and the EOD team ​were requested to attend the scene. The EOD team has made what is a crude but viable device safe,"" Reuters reported, ciitng as police said in a statement. ""An investigation is under way,"" the statement added, without providing further details about the device or when it may have been planted. The incident came a day after leaders attending the European Political Community (EPC) summit gathered for dinner at the National Gallery of Ireland, located on another side of Merrion Square. French President Emmanuel Macron, British Prime Minister Andy Burnham and Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney, who attended as a guest, were among those present at the dinner. Security had been tightened ac","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:50:52 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/investigation-launched-after-explosive-device-found-near-dublin-office-building-14059930.html,2026-11-15 03:32:01
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Rubio hits out at international law as tool of 'global elite' in sharp warning to ICC,Rubio hits out at international law as tool of 'global elite' in sharp warning to ICC,"Rubio hits out at international law as tool of 'global elite' in sharp warning to ICC Marco Rubio, the US Secretary of State, accused critics of “weaponising” international law and warned the International Criminal Court against trying to enforce rules Washington does not recognise Marco Rubio, the US Secretary of State, accused critics of “weaponising” international law and warned the International Criminal Court against trying to enforce rules Washington does not recognise Marco Rubio, the US Secretary of State, on Friday delivered a blunt warning to the International Criminal Court (ICC), accusing the Hague-based tribunal of attempting to impose rules that Washington does not accept and denouncing what he called the “weaponization of international law”. Speaking at the Federalist Society National Lawyers Convention, Rubio warned the court against “quoting laws to men with swords”. The address, which drew a standing ovation from the conservative group, was his first major speech in the United States since the Republican Party suffered heavy losses in the midterm elections earlier this month. Rubio said international law had been invoked against “nearly every major foreign policy decision” taken by the Trump administration, citing the boat strikes in the Caribbean and the capture of Venezuelan leader Nicolas Maduro among them. Such law, he argued, was far from neutral. He described it as an “instrument” that the global elite used to further their own interests. Turning to the ICC, Rubio called it answerable to no one, yet “armed with the power to investigate, to prosecute, to persecute and to jail our citizens, according to laws we neither consent nor control”. He then invoked history. “If they’re foolish enough to try to enforce their paper decrees on","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:30:09 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/united-states/rubio-hits-out-at-international-law-as-tool-of-global-elite-in-sharp-warning-to-icc-14059935.html,2026-11-15 03:32:01
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Elon Musk backs campaign to bring Jensen Huang back as Nvidia weighs new CEO,Elon Musk backs campaign to bring Jensen Huang back as Nvidia weighs new CEO,"Elon Musk backs campaign to bring Jensen Huang back as Nvidia weighs new CEO Elon Musk has backed an employee-led campaign to reinstate Jensen Huang as Nvidia CEO, as the chipmaker considers potential successors, including former Nvidia executive and Arm chief Rene Haas Elon Musk has backed an employee-led campaign to reinstate Jensen Huang as Nvidia CEO, as the chipmaker considers potential successors, including former Nvidia executive and Arm chief Rene Haas Elon Musk has backed a campaign calling for Jensen Huang to return as Nvidia chief executive, as the chipmaker’s board weighs potential successors. Arm Holdings CEO Rene Haas is reportedly among those being considered for the role. Huang resignedabruptly on Thursday after reports of extramarital affairs, one of them with a woman suspected of ties to Chinese intelligence. His exit has plunged Nvidia into turmoil and unsettled the artificial intelligence industry that he helped build and finance. Huang, married to his wife Lori for more than four decades, confessed on Sunday to an affair, reportedly with Alice Huang, a former senior executive at the Singapore-based data centre firm Megaspeed. In a post on X, Musk, the billionaire owner of Tesla and SpaceX, said a petition was circulating to bring Huang back and that he would sign it. It was unclear whether he was referring to an employee initiative reported separately by the technology publication Wired. Wired reported that a long-time Nvidia engineer had posted an internal message urging colleagues to ensure employees’ views were heard before the board made a decision. The post had attracted more than 1,600 comments, according to internal correspondence reviewed by the publication, with several employees calling for a way to bring back ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:42:37 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/elon-musk-backs-campaign-to-bring-jensen-huang-back-as-nvidia-weighs-new-ceo-14059931.html,2026-11-15 03:32:01
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Trump, Xi and Putin to hold unprecedented trilateral meeting at APEC summit in China","Trump, Xi and Putin to hold unprecedented trilateral meeting at APEC summit in China","Trump, Xi and Putin to hold unprecedented trilateral meeting at APEC summit in China US, China and Russia leaders to hold historic talks amid tensions over Iran, Ukraine and nuclear weapons US, China and Russia leaders to hold historic talks amid tensions over Iran, Ukraine and nuclear weapons US President Donald Trump, Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin are expected to hold an unprecedented trilateral meeting on Thursday, on the sidelines of next week Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) summit in Shenzhen, China. The proposed gathering will bring together the leaders of the world's three major nuclear powers at a time of strained international relations, with the war involving Iran, the ongoing Russia-Ukraine conflict and the future of nuclear arms control among the key issues shaping global diplomacy. The White House confirmed the plans on Friday, AP reported. However, expectations of major diplomatic breakthroughs remain low, with analysts suggesting that the meeting could carry greater symbolic significance than produce concrete agreements. Trump is expected to discuss the Iran war with Xi and Putin, but Washington does not plan to raise the Ukraine conflict during the talks, a senior US official told reporters, according to AP. The meeting also comes after Trump sought to improve ties with both Beijing and Moscow. His engagement with Xi has continued despite disagreements over Iran and trade, while his efforts to establish a working relationship with Putin have persisted despite Russia's nearly five-year-old war against Ukraine. The proposed meeting is expected to provide an opening for discussions on nuclear arms control","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:25:06 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/trump-xi-and-putin-to-hold-unprecedented-trilateral-meeting-at-apec-summit-in-china-14059913.html,2026-11-15 03:32:01
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"US Flight Outage Live Updates: FAA lifts nationwide groundstop, departures resume","US Flight Outage Live Updates: FAA lifts nationwide groundstop, departures resume","US Flight Outage Live Updates: FAA lifts nationwide groundstop, departures resume US Flight Outage Live: The US Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) declared a nationwide ground stop for all the flights that are due to take off in the US on Friday, affecting over 11,000 flights across the country.","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:34:32 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/united-states/us-flight-outage-live-updates-faa-issues-nationwide-groundstop-thousands-of-flights-affected-liveblog-14059916.html,2026-11-15 03:32:02
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Canada cancels, delays flights to and from US as FAA issues nationwide ground stop","Canada cancels, delays flights to and from US as FAA issues nationwide ground stop","Canada cancels, delays flights to and from US as FAA issues nationwide ground stop After the US Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) issued a ground stop on all flights departing the United States, major Canadian airports are halting international flights from entering American airspace. After the US Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) issued a ground stop on all flights departing the United States, major Canadian airports are halting international flights from entering American airspace. After the US Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) issued a ground stop on all flights departing the United States, major Canadian airports are halting international flights from entering American airspace. In a statement posted on its social media platform, Toronto Pearson International Airport said flights were “impacted” and “there are currently no scheduled US-bound departures or arrivals at this time.” Meanwhile, Vancouver International Airport told Canadian news outlet Global News that it was aware of a “nationwide technology issue” that forced the ground stop. “As a result, YVR is seeing delays for US-bound departures as well as some international flights that would fly over the US. Domestic flights within Canada are not impacted,” it said. Edmonton International Airport told Global News in a statement that it has seven flights bound for the US that are set to depart by the end of the day. “As this is an evolving situation, passengers travelling to the United States today should check directly with their airline for the latest information on their flight before coming to the airport,” a spokesperson told the Canadian news outlet. Montreal-Trudeau International Airport said in a statement that “all flights to and from the US are suspended until further notice.” In a ","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:02:02 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/canada-cancels-delays-flights-to-and-from-us-as-faa-issues-nationwide-ground-stop-14059915.html,2026-11-15 03:32:02
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Bessent blames Lutnick's Commerce Department over delay in curbing Nvidia chip exports to China,Bessent blames Lutnick's Commerce Department over delay in curbing Nvidia chip exports to China,"Bessent blames Lutnick's Commerce Department over delay in curbing Nvidia chip exports to China The Treasury secretary said several US agencies had backed adding Megaspeed to an export control list months ago, but the Commerce Department was responsible for acting on the proposal. The Treasury secretary said several US agencies had backed adding Megaspeed to an export control list months ago, but the Commerce Department was responsible for acting on the proposal. US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent on Friday criticised the Commerce Department for delaying restrictions on exports of certain Nvidia chips to China, saying several other government agencies had supported action against a company linked to the chipmaker. Speaking toCNBC, Bessent said the Treasury, State and Defence departments, along with the US Trade Representative, had favoured placing Singapore-based Megaspeed International on an export control list for months. However, he said the Commerce Department was responsible for taking the decision. “I am frustrated when President Trump made it very clear China should not receive any Nvidia chips above H100s,” he said, referring to an older generation of the company’s advanced AI chips. Commerce “has the pen, and you will have to ask them about their internal processes.” The remarks amounted to an unusually public criticism of the department, which oversees US export controls on sensitive, high-tech goods. The dispute comes amid scrutiny of Nvidia's relationship with Megaspeed, whose website prominently advertises its partnership with the chipmaker. The company's links to Nvidia have also emerged as a major issue following the resignation of CEO Jensen Huang. Huang stepped down on Thursday after revelations of an affair with former Megaspeed exec","Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:32:24 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/bessent-blames-lutnicks-commerce-department-over-delay-in-curbing-nvidia-chip-exports-to-china-14059908.html,2026-11-15 03:32:02
